ecs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:216:**Chunk 3 — view report (S3).** Red: `describe` absent; `inspect.view` stub. Green: `describe` (row → `StoredView`), `view-report.ts` (describe + pull → report), TC-2.1–2.3 + describe null/shape legs. ~6 tests.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:222:Per-story: `pnpm verify` (lint, typecheck, default suites). Story 4 and epic close: `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all` — process suite must report `ran`. Red manifests regenerated per chunk per house discipline; no Epic 01–03 test amendments expected (additive surfaces only — list-opts default behavior is unchanged, existing `listMessages` callers see identical results).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:265:    planSummary: \"Extended the messages surface per DD-2/DD-3: listMessages gained optional {from, to, limit, includeDeleted} bounds in source-event-order coordinates (defaults preserve all existing callers; bad bounds refused as caller_error/invalid_bounds before any read), the store gained a bounded read plus an unfiltered by-id read, and a new messages.show composes the canonical full-block record (deleted flag always present and honest) with the owner report's queue-joined FormReportEntry rows via the same reportMessageForms read messages.report serves — never synthesized. Deleted records are excluded by default, listed flagged under includeDeleted, and show on a deleted id returns ok+flag (audit), missing id returns message_not_found. CLI gained lhc messages list/show in a new cli/messages-read.ts thin wrapper (numeric conversion at the argv boundary, semantic validation left in the SDK so refusal JSON has parity); sdk.ts exports MessageDetail/MessageListOptions. Tests: 8 default-suite tests in test/messages-read.test.ts covering TC-3.1–3.3 plus the DD-6 read-only delta legs (observable-state snapshot deep-equal around every read mode) and a zero-provider capture assert; 2 process-suite scenarios in test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts covering TC-3.4 spawned-CLI deep-equal parity across default/bounded/include-deleted/refused list options and live/deleted/missing show targets. Default suite 290→298; verify-all (process suite ran) 335 passing.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:269:        reason: \"MessageListOptions + bounds validation on listMessages (invalid_bounds caller errors), MessageDetail shape, new show() composing the by-id record read with reportMessageForms({messageId}) per DD-2, MessageRecord.deleted audit marker\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:275:        reason: \"added invalid_bounds caller_error code for bad listing bounds (recorded spec deviation, additive)\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:281:        reason: \"parse --from/--to/--limit/--include-deleted flags, route messages list (integer conversion at the boundary) and messages show (--message-id required), HELP grammar updated\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:290:        reason: \"TC-3.4 spawned-CLI list/show JSON parity with in-process SDK results (process suite, 2 scenarios)\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:305:        - \"messages-read :: show on a missing id is message_not_found\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:307:        - \"cli-process-inspect :: messages list mirrors the SDK across default, bounded, include-deleted, and refused options\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:308:        - \"cli-process-inspect :: messages show mirrors the SDK for live, deleted, and missing targets\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:334:      - \"tech-design §Interface Definitions pins 'Error codes: no additions', but no existing ErrorCode names a bad-bounds refusal; added the additive caller_error code `invalid_bounds` (comment-documented in shared/errors.ts), mirroring the accepted Epic 03 'additive error codes' deviation precedent. The test plan's pinned assertion (from > to → caller_error class) holds unchanged.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/streams/001-story-lead.stdout.log:3:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\\"action\\\":\\\"run-implement\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"No bounded child response exists yet, and the durable record is awaiting the first story-lead action. The story file and test plan provide enough requirements to start the implementation slice for TC-3.1 through TC-3.4.\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":{\\\"promptAddendum\\\":\\\"Implement Story 1 message read surface only. Use the story file and test plan as requirements. Target `src/domains/messages/index.ts`, `src/cli/messages-read.ts`, `src/sdk.ts`, `test/messages-read.test.ts`, and `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` as needed. Cover bounded list options `{ from?, to?, limit?, includeDeleted? }`, deleted default/audit behavior, full-record `messages.show` with owner report form join, SDK export, and CLI JSON parity. Do not add search behavior or placeholders. Run `pnpm verify` and report exact pass/fail evidence plus any remaining blockers. Do not commit.\\\"}}\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/streams/001-story-lead.stdout.log:7:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\\"action\\\":\\\"run-verify\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Implementation reports ready-for-verification, but acceptance requires an independent verifier pass; run the story gate verification against the implementor artifact before any acceptance recommendation.\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":{\\\"artifactRefs\\\":[\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/003-implementor.json\\\"],\\\"focus\\\":\\\"Verify TC-3.1 through TC-3.4, read-only/zero-provider legs, CLI JSON parity, deleted audit behavior, full tool-result content in show, and the recorded invalid_bounds spec deviation.\\\",\\\"provider\\\":\\\"codex\\\"},\\\"selfNote\\\":\\\"Next planner turn: accept only if verifier outcome is pass with no open findings; otherwise route quick-fix or ruling based on verifier evidence.\\\"}\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:10:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,500p' packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# Epic 04: Inspection — Tech Design\\n\\n**Epic:** `epic.md` (23 ACs / 17 TCs) · **Tech arch:** `../01-tech-arch.md` · **Test plan:** `test-plan.md`\\n**Inherits:** Epic 01–03 technical world — storage/transaction rules, error model, `OpResult`, verification tiers, process-suite accounting, CLI conventions. Nothing re-stated here that those designs pin; this document covers what Epic 04 adds.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nThe last epic of the v1 PRD, and the smallest: no migration, no new tables, no derivations, no provider use, no new algorithms. Four read surfaces and a lifecycle exercise. The design problem is not mechanism — it is *composition discipline*: every report assembles other domains' surfaces without touching their tables, and where a report describes another surface's output (`loadCost` vs `pull`), the design makes agreement structural rather than tested-into-existence (the materialize parity-by-construction pattern, reused).\\n\\nThe second design problem is the dependency posture: this epic consumes Epic 03's surfaces, which finished building days before this design. The epic's handoff gate requires the deviation check below.\\n\\n## Spec Validation\\n\\nDesigned from the epic; issues found and resolved during design:\\n\\n| # | Issue | Resolution | Status |\\n|---|-------|-----------|--------|\\n| 1 | **Handoff gate (epic Assumptions):** Epic 02/03 final deviation tables vs the contracts this epic consumes | Reviewed all recorded deviations (Epic 02 impl log; Epic 03 impl log: `ViewProfileOverride[]` config typing, `view_boundary` strftime seed, `ViewCompactParams` nested partial, additive error codes, sweep-absent literal superseded by Story 3). None alter consumed shapes: `ViewStatus`, `PullResult`, `thread_view`/`thread_view_band`/`view_boundary` DDL, `messages.report`/`turns.report`, `FormReportEntry`, `MessageRecord.forms` all match spec as built. One *favorable* drift: Epic 02's AC-4.7 ruling attached `forms` to message reads (built for this consumer), so Flow 3's join is thinner than the epic assumed | Gate PASSED — recorded here |\\n| 2 | AC-1.1 needs counts (events, messages by kind, tokens) that no surface exposes as counts; inspect may not read tables directly; epic sanctions only one surface addition (`describe`) | Overview composes *list* reads (`listEvents`, `listMessages`, `listTurns`, `listChunks`) and counts in inspect. Cost is linear in thread size — acceptable at v1 scale (NFR allows thread-proportional reads). Count-only surface ops are a deferred optimization, not a v1 need | Resolved — composition, no new surfaces |\\n| 3 | Epic Data Contracts leave list-option names to tech design | Pinned: `{ from?, to?, limit?, includeDeleted? }` — `from`/`to` are source-event-order bounds (reports name `sourceEventOrder`, so drill-down uses the coordinate the operator already holds), `limit` caps count after bounds | Resolved — DD-3 |\\n| 4 | AC-2.3 equality (`loadCost` totals what pull serves) could be a fragile re-implementation of pull's costing | `inspect.view` *invokes* `threadView.pull` through the surface and measures its output — parity by construction; the TC's independent leg runs a second pull in the test and re-measures. Same pattern as Epic 03's materialize | Resolved — DD-4 |\\n| 5 | TC-5.x suite placement left open by epic (TD question 5) | TC-5.1–5.3 default suite (in-process, deterministic, fast); TC-5.4 process suite (spawned CLI). The epic's lean (\\\"TC-5.1 likely default\\\") extended after checking runtimes: replay + teardown legs spawn nothing | Resolved — DD-8 |\\n\\n## System View\\n\\n```\\n                    ┌─────────────── inspect (NEW) ───────────────┐\\n                    │  overview()      view()       health()      │\\n                    └───┬─────┬─────────┬──┬───────────┬──────────┘\\n                        │     │         │  │           │\\n        ┌───────────────┘     │         │  └───────┐   └────────┐\\n        ▼                     ▼         ▼          ▼            ▼\\n   threads.resolve      intake-stream  thread-view  messages.report\\n   listThreads          .listEvents    .describe(NEW) turns.report\\n                                       .pull        .listQueuedWork\\n                        messages.listMessages(+opts)\\n                        messages.show (NEW)          turns.listTurns/listChunks\\n```\\n\\n`inspect` sits at the top of the domain graph: pure consumer, imports five surfaces, nothing imports it except `sdk.ts` and `cli/`. No cycles — unlike Epic 03's sanctioned intake→thread-view cycle, this addition is acyclic by construction. `check-boundaries` gains the domain with no exception entries.\\n\\n### External Contracts (consumed, as built)\\n\\n| Contract | Source | Used by |\\n|----------|--------|---------|\\n| `listEvents` → ordered `EventRecord[]` | intake-stream (E01) | overview (count, span) |\\n| `listMessages` → `MessageRecord[]` with `forms?` attached | messages (E01 + E02 AC-4.7) | overview, list/show |\\n| `report(ref, {messageId?})` → `FormReportEntry[]` (queue join) | messages/turns (E02) | health, show |\\n| `listTurns` / `listChunks` / `listQueuedWork` | turns (E01/E02) | overview, health |\\n| `status` → `ViewStatus` | thread-view (E03) | overview (visibility, derivation counts) |\\n| `pull` → `PullResult` | thread-view (E03) | view (loadCost by construction) |\\n| `thread_view` row + bands (storage, in-domain) | thread-view (E03) | `describe` only |\\n\\n## Module Boundaries\\n\\n### Placement\\n\\n```\\nsrc/\\n  domains/\\n    inspect/\\n      index.ts          ← NEW surface: overview, view, health\\n      internal/\\n        overview.ts     ← compose counts from list reads\\n        view-report.ts  ← describe + pull → ViewContentsReport\\n        health.ts       ← report joins → HealthReport\\n    thread-view/\\n      index.ts          ← gains describe() (read-only, ~30 lines)\\n    messages/\\n      index.ts          ← listMessages gains opts; gains show()\\n  shared/\\n    inspect.ts          ← NEW: InspectOverview, ViewContentsReport, HealthReport shapes\\n  cli/\\n    inspect.ts          ← NEW: lhc inspect overview|view|health\\n    messages-read.ts    ← NEW: lhc messages list|show (mutations stay in messages-mutate.ts)\\n  sdk.ts                ← gains inspect namespace; threadView.describe; messages.show/list opts\\n```\\n\\n### Module Responsibility Matrix\\n\\n| Module | Owns | Must NOT own |\\n|--------|------|--------------|\\n| `inspect/index.ts` + internal | Report assembly, counting, shaping | Any table read, any write, any provider call, any derivation interpretation beyond the owners' reported states |\\n| `thread-view/describe` | Exposing stored view row (arrangement, gaps, config, source state) | Recomputing anything; mutating; reading the record |\\n| `messages/show` | Single-record read (full blocks) + `report(messageId)` composition | View-form shortening (show returns the record — full tool results, never boundary-shortened) |\\n| `messages/listMessages` opts | Bounds, limit, deleted filter | Default-including deleted (audit is opt-in) |\\n| `cli/inspect.ts`, `cli/messages-read.ts` | argv → SDK → JSON stdout | Any logic beyond arg mapping (CLI parity is structural: same code path as SDK) |\\n\\nDesign decisions:\\n\\n- **DD-1 (describe placement):** `describe` lives in thread-view because the stored view row is thread-view's table; inspect consuming it through the surface keeps the must-not-own rule airtight. Absent view → `ok` with `null`, mirroring `status`'s never-compacted behavior.\\n- **DD-2 (show composes report):** `show` = internal single-message read (same store read as `listMessages`, by id, full blocks) + `messages.report(ref, {messageId})` for the queue-joined forms. No new join machinery; `FormReportEntry` is the forms shape `show` returns.\\n- **DD-3 (list options):** `{ from?, to?, limit?, includeDeleted? }`, bounds in source event order. Existing callers unaffected (opts optional, default behavior unchanged: all visible messages).\\n- **DD-4 (loadCost by construction):** `view-report.ts` calls `describe` (stored bands: entries, gaps, config, stored token counts) and `pull` (served messages). `loadCost.bandTokens` = sum of stored band counts; `loadCost.tailTokens` = estimator over pull's tail messages (band-absent entries); `total` = sum. Pull is the single costing authority for the tail — AC-2.2's boundary-aware shortening is inherited, not re-implemented.\\n- **DD-5 (overview's view section):** composed from `status` (boundary, zone, derivation counts, view health) + `describe` (viewId, createdAt, compactPoint, coveredFrom) — both already exist; overview adds no view logic.\\n- **DD-6 (read-only, structurally tested):** the architecture-risk test snapshots observable state (work-item rows via `listQueuedWork`/reports, boundary position via `status`, view identity via `describe`, event/message counts) before and after every inspect/describe/show/list call and asserts deep equality. Read-only is asserted as absence-of-delta, not absence-of-write-code.\\n- **DD-7 (no migration):** schema terminal at v6. The one index temptation (message kind counts) is declined — counts come from list reads (Spec Validation #2); if profiling ever demands an index, that is a v7 proposal.\\n- **DD-8 (suite placement):** TC-5.1–5.3 default suite; TC-5.4 process suite. The lifecycle script is a shared fixture helper (`test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts`) both suites drive, so the spawned leg replays the same sequence rather than a re-described one.\\n\\n## Storage\\n\\nNone. No tables, no migration, no new indexes (DD-7). The only storage *read* this epic adds is `describe`'s in-domain read of `thread_view` / `thread_view_band` / `view_boundary`, all Epic 03 tables.\\n\\n## Flow-by-Flow Design\\n\\n### Flow 1: Overview\\n\\n`overview(ref)`: resolve thread (registry metadata) → `listEvents` (count, first/last order) → `listMessages({includeDeleted: true})` (visible/deleted split, kind counts, visible token sum — deleted detected per the read contract's flag) → `listTurns` (open/closed counts) → `listChunks` (count; unchunked = closed turns minus chunk-member turns) → `status` + `describe` (derivation counts, visibility, view summary). Each piece independent; fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted-with-record, compacted, and mid-rebuild shapes fall out of the same composition path: absent pieces are zeros/nulls; no shape-specific branch is allowed except normalizing null sections.\\n\\nWorked example (compacted fixture, abridged):\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"thread\\\": { \\\"id\\\": \\\"th_…\\\", \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"…\\\" },\\n  \\\"events\\\": { \\\"count\\\": 412, \\\"span\\\": { \\\"first\\\": 1, \\\"last\\\": 412 } },\\n  \\\"messages\\\": { \\\"visible\\\": 187, \\\"byKind\\\": { \\\"user_prompt\\\": 14, \\\"assistant_text\\\": 41, \\\"tool_call\\\": 66, \\\"tool_result\\\": 64, \\\"assistant_thinking\\\": 2 }, \\\"deleted\\\": 2, \\\"visibleTokens\\\": 96342 },\\n  \\\"turns\\\": { \\\"open\\\": 0, \\\"closed\\\": 14 },\\n  \\\"chunks\\\": { \\\"count\\\": 4, \\\"unchunkedTurns\\\": 2 },\\n  \\\"derivation\\\": { \\\"ready\\\": 118, \\\"pending\\\": 3, \\\"retrying\\\": 1, \\\"failed\\\": 2, \\\"blocked\\\": 0 },\\n  \\\"view\\\": { \\\"viewId\\\": \\\"v391\\\", \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"…\\\", \\\"compactPoint\\\": 391, \\\"coveredFrom\\\": 12 },\\n  \\\"visibility\\\": { \\\"boundaryPosition\\\": 398, \\\"zoneTokens\\\": 18204 }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Flow 2: View Contents Report\\n\\n```\\ninspect.view ──► threadView.describe ──► stored arrangement/gaps/config/band tokens/source state\\n      │\\n      └────────► threadView.pull ──► served messages\\n                      │\\n                      ├─ band entries → cross-check count only (arrangement is describe's)\\n                      └─ tail entries → estimator → tailTokens (as served: short forms short)\\nloadCost = { bandTokens: Σ stored, tailTokens: measured, total: sum }\\n```\\n\\nNever-compacted: `describe` → null ⇒ `meta: null`, bands empty, whole pull output is tail, parity contract unchanged (AC-2.4). The report never recomputes selection, rendering, or boundary state — stored snapshot + live pull are the only sources (AC-2.1's \\\"not recomputed\\\" is structural).\\n\\n### Flow 3: Message Listing and Show\\n\\n`listMessages(ref, opts)`: existing read + WHERE bounds on `source_event_order`, LIMIT, deleted filter (default excluded; `includeDeleted` includes flagged). `show(ref, messageId)`: by-id read, full blocks verbatim from the record, `deleted` flag honest, forms from `report({messageId})`. Not-found → `message_not_found` (existing code). Deleted + show → `ok` with flagged record (AC-3.3: audit, never not-found).\\n\\n### Flow 4: Health\\n\\n`health(ref)`: `messages.report` + `turns.report` (full, not-ready included) + `listQueuedWork` both owners. Compose: counts by owner/kind/state from report entries' states; `failures[]` from `failed`/`blocked` entries (reason, attempts, lastError off `FormReportEntry`); `repairPreview[]` = failed-and-not-blocked subjects (reported, never requeued — AC-4.3); `queue` = queued/claimed counts from the live-item joins, consistent by construction with the same entries' states (AC-4.5). Rebuild visibility (AC-4.4) is two health calls bracketing a drain — no new mechanism, the cascade's pending states simply show.\\n\\n### Flow 5: Lifecycle Exercise\\n\\nScripted in `test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts`: phases named `create | intake | drain | status | compact1 | pull1 | inspect1 | mutate | rebuild | health2 | compact2 | pull2 | materialize`. Each phase returns its results to the driving test; checkpoint assertions live in the test, not the script. Teardown leg (TC-5.3) re-creates the SDK between named phase groups using the same script with a `freshSdk` hook. Receipt-vs-health cross-check (AC-5.2): `compact2`'s receipt sweep section against the `health2` snapshot taken immediately before — field-level equality on the failed/requeued sets.\\n\\n## Interface Definitions\\n\\n`src/shared/inspect.ts` (load-bearing shapes; field comments carry AC refs in source):\\n\\n```typescript\\nexport interface InspectOverview {\\n  thread: { id: string; createdAt: string; metadata?: Record<string, string> };\\n  events: { count: number; span: { first: number; last: number } | null };\\n  messages: { visible: number; byKind: Record<string, number>; deleted: number; visibleTokens: number };\\n  turns: { open: number; closed: number };\\n  chunks: { count: number; unchunkedTurns: number };\\n  derivation: { ready: number; pending: number; retrying: number; failed: number; blocked: number };\\n  view: { viewId: string; createdAt: string; compactPoint: number; coveredFrom: number } | null;\\n  visibility: { boundaryPosition: number; zoneTokens: number };\\n}\\n\\nexport interface ViewContentsReport {\\n  meta: { viewId: string; createdAt: string; profile: string | null;\\n          config: { lowerBound: number; percentages: Record<string, number> };\\n          compactPoint: number; coveredFrom: number } | null;\\n  bands: Array<{ band: Band; entries: Array<{ subjectKind: \\\"chunk\\\" | \\\"turn\\\"; subjectId: string;\\n          formUsed: string; degraded: boolean }>; storedTokens: number }>;\\n  gaps: Array<{ band: Band; subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\\n  tail: { messageCount: number; tokens: number };          // as served (AC-2.2)\\n  loadCost: { bandTokens: number; tailTokens: number; total: number }; // = pull (AC-2.3)\\n  sourceState: { maxEventOrder: number; formCounts: Record<string, number> }; // provenance verbatim (AC-2.5)\\n}\\n\\nexport interface HealthReport {\\n  owners: Array<{ owner: \\\"messages\\\" | \\\"turns\\\"; kind: string;\\n          counts: { ready: number; pending: number; retrying: number; failed: number; blocked: number } }>;\\n  failures: Array<{ owner: string; subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: string;\\n          reason: string; attempts: number; lastError?: string }>;\\n  repairPreview: Array<{ owner: string; subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: string }>;\\n  queue: { queued: number; claimed: number };\\n}\\n```\\n\\nSurface signatures:\\n\\n```typescript\\n// inspect\\noverview(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<InspectOverview>>;\\nview(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<ViewContentsReport>>;\\nhealth(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<HealthReport>>;\\n// thread-view addition\\ndescribe(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<StoredView | null>>;   // StoredView mirrors the row: id, createdAt, compactPoint, coveredFrom, profileName, config, arrangement, gaps, sourceState, bands (band → storedTokens)\\n// messages additions\\nlistMessages(ref: ThreadRef, opts?: { from?: number; to?: number; limit?: number; includeDeleted?: boolean }): Promise<OpResult<MessageRecord[]>>;\\nshow(ref: ThreadRef, messageId: string): Promise<OpResult<MessageDetail>>;  // MessageRecord (full blocks, deleted flag) + forms: FormReportEntry[]\\n```\\n\\nCLI grammar (JSON stdout, existing error classes, exit conventions inherited):\\n\\n```\\nlhc inspect overview --thread <ref>\\nlhc inspect view     --thread <ref>\\nlhc inspect health   --thread <ref>\\nlhc messages list    --thread <ref> [--from <n>] [--to <n>] [--limit <n>] [--include-deleted]\\nlhc messages show    --thread <ref> --message-id <id>\\n```\\n\\nError codes: no additions. `thread_not_found`, `message_not_found`, `caller_error` (bad bounds: `from > to`, `limit < 1`), `state_corruption`, `system_error` — all existing.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\nInherited wholesale from Epics 01–03: real temp SQLite, no mocks anywhere but the provider seam (unused here beyond fixture prep), default + process suites, zero-provider assertion extended to all inspect/show/list/describe operations. New emphasis — the **read-only delta assert** (DD-6) is this epic's architecture-risk centerpiece: every new operation runs under a before/after observable-state snapshot in one shared helper. Direct table-read prevention is static: `check-boundaries` forbids cross-domain internal imports, and this epic adds a source check that `domains/inspect/**` contains no raw SQL table-name access to other domains' tables. Test files: `inspect-overview.test.ts`, `inspect-view.test.ts`, `messages-read.test.ts`, `inspect-health.test.ts`, `lifecycle.test.ts`, `cli-process-inspect.test.ts` (process suite). Full TC mapping, fixture extensions, and Red/Green detail: `test-plan.md`.\\n\\n## Work Breakdown\\n\\nStory chunks follow the epic's four stories; per-chunk Red/Green and counts in the test plan.\\n\\n| Chunk | Story | Builds | Risk concentration |\\n|-------|-------|--------|--------------------|\\n| 1 | S1 Message reads | list opts, show, `cli/messages-read.ts` | Bounds semantics; deleted default; show returning record-not-view forms |\\n| 2 | S2 Inspect domain | surface + overview + health, `shared/inspect.ts`, `cli/inspect.ts`, fixture mutation-states extension | Count correctness vs fixture ground truth; health composition staying on surfaces |\\n| 3 | S3 View report | `describe`, `view-report.ts` | Parity-by-construction wiring; never-compacted nulls |\\n| 4 | S4 Lifecycle | `lifecycle.ts` script + 4 TC legs | Checkpoint ordering; receipt-vs-health equality; teardown continuity |\\n\\nSequencing: 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 (3 needs Epic 03 storage live — already landed; 4 needs 1–3).\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\nNone blocking. Deferred items: count-only surface ops if thread scale ever makes overview's list-composition measurable (Spec Validation #2); message search (post-v1, PRD-recorded).\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:12:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,500p' packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/01-message-read-surface.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# Story 1: Message Read Surface\\n\\n### Summary\\n<!-- Jira: Summary field -->\\nComplete message listing and single-message viewing with deleted-audit support and CLI parity.\\n\\n### Description\\n<!-- Jira: Description field -->\\n**User Profile:** The operator audits threads from the CLI; agents inside a harness use the same reads mid-task.\\n\\n**Objective:** Provide the drill-down floor for every report that names message subjects.\\n\\n**Scope In:** `messages.list` bounded listing options, `messages.show`, forms join, deleted-message audit option, `lhc messages list`, `lhc messages show`, SDK/CLI JSON parity.\\n\\n**Scope Out:** Message search is deferred post-v1. No search behavior, search placeholder, ranking, FTS, or result-granularity decision ships in this story.\\n\\n**Dependencies:** Built Epic 01 message record/read-back behavior and Epic 02 report/deleted-message contracts.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\\n- **AC-3.1**: Listing returns messages in record order with kind, block summary, token estimate, turn membership, and deleted status, with bounded-listing options (range/limit) so large threads list without loading everything.\\n\\n- **TC-3.1** (AC-3.1): List on the fixture → record order, kinds, token estimates, turn ids correct; range and limit options honored exactly.\\n\\n- **AC-3.2**: `messages.show` returns one message in full: every block with complete content (the record — full tool results, not view-shortened forms), token estimate, turn membership, and the message's derivation forms with their states and metadata (joined from the owner's report, including tool-outcome metadata where present).\\n\\n- **TC-3.2** (AC-3.2): Show on a drained tool-result message → full original content present, forms listed with states, outcome metadata present.\\n\\n- **AC-3.3**: Deleted messages are excluded by default and listable with an explicit include-deleted option, marked deleted — never silently mixed in. `show` on a deleted message returns the record marked deleted (audit is the point), never a not-found.\\n\\n- **TC-3.3** (AC-3.3): Delete one message → default list excludes it; include-deleted lists it marked; show on its id → record with deleted flag.\\n\\n- **AC-3.4**: CLI parity: `lhc messages list` and `lhc messages show` mirror the SDK operations — same options, same result JSON.\\n\\n- **TC-3.4** (AC-3.4): Spawned-CLI list and show on a fixture thread → JSON equals the in-process SDK results (process suite).\\n\\n### Technical Design\\n<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\\n#### Architecture Context\\n\\nThis story extends the existing messages surface. `listMessages` gains optional bounds and deleted-audit options while preserving default visible-message behavior for existing callers. `show` returns the canonical record content, not the view-shortened content, and composes form state from the owner report surface.\\n\\nThe CLI is a thin argv-to-SDK wrapper. JSON output must deep-equal the in-process SDK result.\\n\\n#### Build Strategy\\n\\nStrategy: simple-risk-reminders\\n\\nReason:\\n- One surface owns listing/showing behavior, but bounds semantics, deleted defaults, and CLI parity are easy to shortcut.\\n\\nRisk Reminders:\\n- `show` returns full record blocks, including full tool results.\\n- Deleted messages remain excluded by default and auditable on explicit request.\\n- Bounds use source-event-order coordinates: `{ from?, to?, limit?, includeDeleted? }`.\\n\\n#### Implementation Targets\\n\\n| Area | Files / Modules |\\n|------|-----------------|\\n| Message surface | `src/domains/messages/index.ts` |\\n| CLI | `src/cli/messages-read.ts` |\\n| SDK export | `src/sdk.ts` |\\n| Tests | `test/messages-read.test.ts`, `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` |\\n\\n#### Design References\\n\\n- [tech-design.md §Module Boundaries](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:54), lines 54-98\\n- [tech-design.md §Flow 3: Message Listing and Show](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:139), lines 139-142\\n- [tech-design.md §Interface Definitions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:189), lines 189-213\\n- [test-plan.md §Test Files](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:6), lines 6-18\\n- [test-plan.md §TC → Test Mapping](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:20), lines 20-40\\n- [test-plan.md §Chunk Red/Green Detail](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:56), lines 56-64\\n\\n#### Test Mapping\\n\\n| TC | Test File / Check | Test Description |\\n|----|-------------------|------------------|\\n| TC-3.1 | `test/messages-read.test.ts :: order, fields, bounds` | Record order, kind, token estimate, turn id, exact `from`/`to`/`limit` windows, and bad bounds error. |\\n| TC-3.2 | `test/messages-read.test.ts :: show full record + forms` | Drained tool-result message returns full content, form states, and outcome metadata. |\\n| TC-3.3 | `test/messages-read.test.ts :: deleted handling` | Default list excludes deleted; include-deleted marks it; show on deleted returns ok with flag; missing id returns not found. |\\n| TC-3.4 | `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts :: list/show parity` | Spawned CLI message list/show JSON deep-equals SDK results. |\\n\\n#### Architecture-Risk Tests\\n\\n| Risk | Test File / Check | Test Description | Why AC/TC Mapping Alone Would Miss It |\\n|------|-------------------|------------------|---------------------------------------|\\n| Read-only drift | `test/messages-read.test.ts` read-only legs | Before/after observable-state snapshots stay equal for list/show. | A read can satisfy shape assertions while still mutating queue, boundary, or view state. |\\n| CLI bypasses SDK | `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` process parity | Spawned commands compare serialized JSON against SDK results. | Private helper tests can pass while production CLI output diverges. |\\n\\n#### Technical Notes\\n\\n- `listMessages` option defaults must preserve existing callers: visible messages, unbounded, record order.\\n- `from` and `to` are source-event-order bounds; `limit` caps after bounds.\\n- `show` composes the by-id message read with `messages.report(ref, { messageId })`.\\n- Message search remains deferred post-v1 and gets no v1 placeholder behavior.\\n\\n#### Anti-Shim Requirements\\n\\n- Assert real full block content for tool-result messages, not only message id or metadata.\\n- Exercise the spawned `lhc messages` commands for process parity.\\n- Do not synthesize form state in `show`; use the owner report entries.\\n\\n#### Production Path Proof\\n\\n- Entrypoint: `messages.listMessages`, `messages.show`, `lhc messages list`, `lhc messages show`.\\n- Registration/default path: `src/sdk.ts` exposes the message operations; `src/cli/messages-read.ts` routes CLI commands to SDK calls.\\n- Evidence: process parity for CLI list/show and default-suite message read tests.\\n\\n#### Verification\\n\\n- Targeted: `pnpm verify`\\n- Story gate: `pnpm verify`\\n- Epic/process gate: `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all`\\n\\n#### Spec Deviations\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### Definition of Done\\n<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n- `messages.list` returns bounded, ordered message summaries with deleted filtering.\\n- `messages.show` returns full record content and owner-reported form state for one message.\\n- Deleted-message audit behavior matches Epic 02's deleted contract.\\n- CLI list/show options and JSON match SDK results.\\n- TC-3.1 through TC-3.4 pass with one primary owner in this story.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:14:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,500p' packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# Epic 04: Inspection — Test Plan\\n\\n**Epic:** `epic.md` (23 ACs / 17 TCs) · **Tech design:** `tech-design.md`\\nInherits Epic 01–03 test architecture: real temp SQLite per test, deterministic provider for fixture prep only, default suite (`pnpm verify`) + process suite (`LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all`), suite-accounting row, red manifest discipline.\\n\\n## Test Files\\n\\n| File | Suite | Covers |\\n|------|-------|--------|\\n| `test/messages-read.test.ts` | default | TC-3.1–3.3 + list/show read-only legs |\\n| `test/inspect-overview.test.ts` | default | TC-1.1–1.3 |\\n| `test/inspect-view.test.ts` | default | TC-2.1–2.3 + describe legs |\\n| `test/inspect-health.test.ts` | default | TC-4.1–4.3 |\\n| `test/lifecycle.test.ts` | default | TC-5.1–5.3 |\\n| `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` | process | TC-3.4, TC-5.4 |\\n| `test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts` | (helper) | the scripted sequence both suites drive |\\n\\nFixture: Epic 03's tool-heavy fixture reused; extended in place (Story 2) with a mutation-in-flight variant — one edit applied, drain *not* settled, so cleared-pending states are real production states, not hand-written rows (FC-fidelity rule carried from Epic 03 Story 0: states reached through intake → mutate → partial drain, never direct `derived_form` writes).\\n\\n## TC → Test Mapping\\n\\n| TC | Test (file :: name) | Assertion spine |\\n|----|--------------------|-----------------|\\n| TC-1.1 | inspect-overview :: full shape variants | fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted-with-record, compacted, and mid-rebuild all return the full shape with absent pieces as zeros/nulls; compacted fixture exact counts per section vs fixture ground truth |\\n| TC-1.2 | inspect-overview :: deleted accounting | delete one → visible−1, deleted=1, kind map excludes, tokens drop by its estimate, event count unchanged |\\n| TC-1.3 | inspect-overview :: purity | two calls, no writes between → deep-equal; read-only delta assert green; zero provider calls |\\n| TC-2.1 | inspect-view :: arrangement fidelity | entries/forms/degraded/gap reasons/config/provenance equal `describe` output equal stored row (degraded + gap fixture) |\\n| TC-2.2 | inspect-view :: loadCost parity on boundary-advanced fixture | tail costs short forms short; `total` = estimator over an independent `pull`'s messages |\\n| TC-2.3 | inspect-view :: never-compacted | `meta: null`, bands `[]`, tail spans record, parity holds |\\n| TC-3.1 | messages-read :: order, fields, bounds | record order; kind/tokens/turnId present; `from`/`to`/`limit` exact windows; `from > to` → `caller_error` |\\n| TC-3.2 | messages-read :: show full record + forms | drained tool-result: full content (not shortened), forms with states, outcome metadata present |\\n| TC-3.3 | messages-read :: deleted handling | default list excludes; `includeDeleted` marks; show on deleted → ok + flag; show on missing id → `message_not_found` |\\n| TC-3.4 | cli-process-inspect :: list/show parity | spawned `lhc messages list/show` JSON deep-equals in-process SDK results |\\n| TC-4.1 | inspect-health :: counts + queue consistency | mixed-state fixture: exact counts per owner/kind/state; queue section equals live-item counts from the same reports |\\n| TC-4.2 | inspect-health :: failure detail + preview | failed: reason/attempts/lastError exact; blocked excluded from preview; preview = failed∧¬blocked set exactly |\\n| TC-4.3 | inspect-health :: rebuild bracket | edit → health: cascade set pending with queued work visible (exact subjects per cascade contract); `drainSettled` → same set ready; disjoint forms untouched |\\n| TC-5.1 | lifecycle :: full sequence + checkpoints | every phase ok; post-compact pull = bands+tail; mutate → pending; drain → ready; compact2 reflects edit; receipt sweep section field-equals pre-compact health snapshot |\\n| TC-5.2 | lifecycle :: replay determinism | fresh thread, same script → hash-equal pull outputs and materialized file |\\n| TC-5.3 | lifecycle :: teardown continuity | `freshSdk` between phase groups → final pull/health/file identical to TC-5.1 run |\\n| TC-5.4 | cli-process-inspect :: checkpoint parity | spawned CLI overview/view/list at three checkpoints deep-equal in-process results at same checkpoints |\\n\\n## Architecture-Risk Tests\\n\\n| Risk | Test | Why it bites |\\n|------|------|--------------|\\n| Inspect quietly writes (work rows, boundary nudge, view touch) | **read-only delta assert**: shared helper snapshots observable state (queued work via owners, boundary/zone via status, view identity via describe, event/message counts) before/after *every* new operation; deep-equal after. Runs inside each TC file via wrapper | A single forgotten side effect makes \\\"inspect describes, never changes\\\" fiction; absence-of-delta is checkable, absence-of-write-code is not |\\n| Zero-provider on all new ops | suite-wide assert extended: overview/view/health/describe/show/list under a throwing provider config → all ok | The no-inference NFR stays structural through the last epic |\\n| `loadCost` drifts from served reality | TC-2.2's independent-pull leg + lifecycle TC-5.1 checkpoint (report at compact1 vs pull1) | Parity by construction can still break at the estimator seam; two independent measurements pin it |\\n| Health re-derives instead of composing | health tests assert composition through owner surfaces only: `check-boundaries` forbids cross-domain internal imports, an Epic 04 source check rejects raw SQL references to other domains' tables from `domains/inspect/**`, and the read-only delta assert separately catches writes | The must-not-own rule is the domain's entire contract |\\n| Lifecycle order bugs only visible cross-epic | TC-5.1's named-phase checkpoints; receipt-vs-health field equality | First sequence ever to run all surfaces in PI-extension order; seam drift between three separately-built epics surfaces here or in production |\\n\\n## Suite Accounting\\n\\nDefault suite grows ~26 tests across 5 files. Process suite grows TC-3.4 + TC-5.4 (2 spawned scenarios, ~6 assertions); accounting row carried: process suite `ran | not-ran` recorded per verify-all invocation, never silently skipped.\\n\\n## Chunk Red/Green Detail\\n\\n**Chunk 1 — message reads (S1).** Red: `show` absent from surface (structured not-implemented per house stub rule); list opts ignored — bounds test fails on full-list return. Green: opts → WHERE/LIMIT; show + report join; `cli/messages-read.ts`; TC-3.1–3.3 + read-only legs. ~8 tests.\\n\\n**Chunk 2 — inspect domain (S2).** Red: `inspect.*` stubs return not-implemented; fixture lacks mutation-variant (TC-4.3 unwritable → fixture work first). Green: `shared/inspect.ts` shapes; overview composition; health composition; `cli/inspect.ts`; delta-assert helper lands here and wraps Chunk 1's ops retroactively. TC-1.1–1.3, TC-4.1–4.3. ~11 tests.\\n\\n**Chunk 3 — view report (S3).** Red: `describe` absent; `inspect.view` stub. Green: `describe` (row → `StoredView`), `view-report.ts` (describe + pull → report), TC-2.1–2.3 + describe null/shape legs. ~6 tests.\\n\\n**Chunk 4 — lifecycle (S4).** Red: `lifecycle.ts` helper absent; all four TC files reference it. Green: script with named phases + `freshSdk` hook; TC-5.1–5.3 default; TC-5.4 process. ~7 tests (4 scenarios, multi-checkpoint).\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nPer-story: `pnpm verify` (lint, typecheck, default suites). Story 4 and epic close: `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all` — process suite must report `ran`. Red manifests regenerated per chunk per house discipline; no Epic 01–03 test amendments expected (additive surfaces only — list-opts default behavior is unchanged, existing `listMessages` callers see identical results).\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:18:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,500p' packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/003-implementor.json\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"{\\\"command\\\":\\\"story-implement\\\",\\\"version\\\":1,\\\"status\\\":\\\"ok\\\",\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"ready-for-verification\\\",\\\"result\\\":{\\\"resultId\\\":\\\"c8832ff2-5185-4a79-8568-2d0b818a3622\\\",\\\"provider\\\":\\\"claude-code\\\",\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-fable-5\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"story_implementor\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"92b30fef-4ad7-45bb-a8e9-4c6f66be56bf\\\",\\\"continuation\\\":{\\\"provider\\\":\\\"claude-code\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"92b30fef-4ad7-45bb-a8e9-4c6f66be56bf\\\",\\\"storyId\\\":\\\"01-message-read-surface\\\"},\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"ready-for-verification\\\",\\\"story\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"01-message-read-surface\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Story 1: Message Read Surface\\\"},\\\"planSummary\\\":\\\"Extended the messages surface per DD-2/DD-3: listMessages gained optional {from, to, limit, includeDeleted} bounds in source-event-order coordinates (defaults preserve all existing callers; bad bounds refused as caller_error/invalid_bounds before any read), the store gained a bounded read plus an unfiltered by-id read, and a new messages.show composes the canonical full-block record (deleted flag always present and honest) with the owner report's queue-joined FormReportEntry rows via the same reportMessageForms read messages.report serves — never synthesized. Deleted records are excluded by default, listed flagged under includeDeleted, and show on a deleted id returns ok+flag (audit), missing id returns message_not_found. CLI gained lhc messages list/show in a new cli/messages-read.ts thin wrapper (numeric conversion at the argv boundary, semantic validation left in the SDK so refusal JSON has parity); sdk.ts exports MessageDetail/MessageListOptions. Tests: 8 default-suite tests in test/messages-read.test.ts covering TC-3.1–3.3 plus the DD-6 read-only delta legs (observable-state snapshot deep-equal around every read mode) and a zero-provider capture assert; 2 process-suite scenarios in test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts covering TC-3.4 spawned-CLI deep-equal parity across default/bounded/include-deleted/refused list options and live/deleted/missing show targets. Default suite 290→298; verify-all (process suite ran) 335 passing.\\\",\\\"changedFiles\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"MessageListOptions + bounds validation on listMessages (invalid_bounds caller errors), MessageDetail shape, new show() composing the by-id record read with reportMessageForms({messageId}) per DD-2, MessageRecord.deleted audit marker\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/store.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"readMessages gained MessageReadOptions (deleted filter opt-out, source-event-order bounds, LIMIT after bounds); new readMessageById full-block unfiltered read with honest deleted flag; shared recordFromRow mapper\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"packages/lhc/src/shared/errors.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"added invalid_bounds caller_error code for bad listing bounds (recorded spec deviation, additive)\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"packages/lhc/src/cli/messages-read.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"new thin argv-to-SDK wrappers runMessagesList/runMessagesShow per tech-design §Placement (mutations stay in messages-mutate.ts)\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"parse --from/--to/--limit/--include-deleted flags, route messages list (integer conversion at the boundary) and messages show (--message-id required), HELP grammar updated\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"export MessageDetail and MessageListOptions types; show rides the existing messages namespace export\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"packages/lhc/test/messages-read.test.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"TC-3.1–3.3 plus read-only delta and zero-provider architecture-risk legs (default suite, 8 tests)\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"packages/lhc/test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"TC-3.4 spawned-CLI list/show JSON parity with in-process SDK results (process suite, 2 scenarios)\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"packages/lhc/vitest.config.ts\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"register cli-process-inspect.test.ts in the process-suite-only exclude list\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"recorded sha256 hashes of the two new story test files per house red-manifest discipline\\\"}],\\\"tests\\\":{\\\"added\\\":[\\\"messages-read :: returns messages in record order with kind, token estimate, and turn membership\\\",\\\"messages-read :: honors from/to/limit windows exactly in source-event-order coordinates\\\",\\\"messages-read :: refuses bad bounds as caller errors and returns no partial window\\\",\\\"messages-read :: a drained tool-result message comes back with full content, form states, and outcome metadata\\\",\\\"messages-read :: a drained prompt shows its smoothing form alongside the full record\\\",\\\"messages-read :: default list excludes a deleted message; include-deleted lists it marked; show returns it flagged\\\",\\\"messages-read :: show on a missing id is message_not_found\\\",\\\"messages-read :: list and show in every mode leave observable state unchanged and call no provider\\\",\\\"cli-process-inspect :: messages list mirrors the SDK across default, bounded, include-deleted, and refused options\\\",\\\"cli-process-inspect :: messages show mirrors the SDK for live, deleted, and missing targets\\\"],\\\"modified\\\":[],\\\"removed\\\":[],\\\"totalAfterStory\\\":298,\\\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\\\":8},\\\"gatesRun\\\":[{\\\"command\\\":\\\"pnpm verify\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"pass\\\"},{\\\"command\\\":\\\"LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"pass\\\"}],\\\"selfReview\\\":{\\\"passesRun\\\":0,\\\"findingsFixed\\\":[\\\"cli-process show-parity loop carried an unused expected-ok field that contradicted the deleted-target behavior (show on deleted is ok) — removed in favor of SDK-derived status expectations plus pinned deleted-ok/missing-refused assertions so the loop cannot both-sides-drift\\\",\\\"invalidBounds helper initially returned a wrapped OpResult that validateListOptions unwrapped via .error — flattened to return ErrorResult directly\\\"],\\\"findingsSurfaced\\\":[\\\"Bounded listing still loads all message_block rows before windowing (the pre-existing grouped-blocks read); linear in thread size, consistent with the v1 NFR and tech-design Spec Validation #2's deferred-optimization stance\\\",\\\"--from/--to/--limit/--include-deleted live in the shared CLI flag table, so unrelated commands parse-and-ignore them — matches the existing house pattern for --message-id/--turn-id and keeps strict unknown-flag rejection intact\\\",\\\"Non-integer numeric CLI values (e.g. --from abc) are refused at the adapter with the missing_flag code, following the --max-items precedent; integer-but-bad bounds flow to the SDK so refusal JSON keeps CLI/SDK parity\\\"]},\\\"openQuestions\\\":[],\\\"specDeviations\\\":[\\\"tech-design §Interface Definitions pins 'Error codes: no additions', but no existing ErrorCode names a bad-bounds refusal; added the additive caller_error code `invalid_bounds` (comment-documented in shared/errors.ts), mirroring the accepted Epic 03 'additive error codes' deviation precedent. The test plan's pinned assertion (from > to → caller_error class) holds unchanged.\\\"],\\\"recommendedNextStep\\\":\\\"Run story verification, then proceed to Story 2 (inspect domain): its shared read-only delta-assert helper should absorb this story's local observableState snapshot and wrap list/show retroactively per the chunk plan.\\\"},\\\"errors\\\":[],\\\"warnings\\\":[],\\\"artifacts\\\":[{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"result-envelope\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/003-implementor.json\\\"}],\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-06-12T12:47:33.794Z\\\",\\\"finishedAt\\\":\\\"2026-06-12T13:00:53.924Z\\\"}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:29:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/lhc/src/cli/messages-read.ts | sed -n '1,500p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t// `lhc messages list` and `lhc messages show` (Epic 04 Story 1) per tech\\n     2\\t// design §Placement: the message read command surface, mirroring the SDK\\n     3\\t// operations one-for-one (AC-3.4). Thin argv-to-SDK wrappers — semantic\\n     4\\t// option validation (from > to, limit < 1) stays in the SDK so the CLI's\\n     5\\t// result JSON deep-equals the in-process result, refusals included.\\n     6\\timport * as messages from \\\"../domains/messages/index.js\\\";\\n     7\\timport type { MessageListOptions } from \\\"../domains/messages/index.js\\\";\\n     8\\timport type { ThreadRef } from \\\"../domains/threads/index.js\\\";\\n     9\\timport { renderResult, type CliResult } from \\\"./render.js\\\";\\n    10\\t\\n    11\\texport async function runMessagesList(\\n    12\\t  threadRef: ThreadRef,\\n    13\\t  opts: MessageListOptions,\\n    14\\t): Promise<CliResult> {\\n    15\\t  return renderResult(await messages.listMessages(threadRef, opts));\\n    16\\t}\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\texport async function runMessagesShow(\\n    19\\t  threadRef: ThreadRef,\\n    20\\t  flags: { messageId: string },\\n    21\\t): Promise<CliResult> {\\n    22\\t  return renderResult(await messages.show(threadRef, flags.messageId));\\n    23\\t}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:31:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_12\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts | sed -n '1,500p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\timport { existsSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\n     2\\timport { runInTransaction, type OperationContext } from \\\"../../shared/context.js\\\";\\n     3\\timport type { FormKind, FormReportEntry, WorkHandler } from \\\"../../shared/derivation.js\\\";\\n     4\\timport { storageFailure, type ErrorResult, type OpResult } from \\\"../../shared/errors.js\\\";\\n     5\\timport {\\n     6\\t  enqueue,\\n     7\\t  hasLiveItem,\\n     8\\t  listItems,\\n     9\\t  type WorkItemRecord,\\n    10\\t  type WorkKind,\\n    11\\t} from \\\"../../tech-utils/work-queue/index.js\\\";\\n    12\\timport type { EventKind, EventRecord } from \\\"../intake-stream/index.js\\\";\\n    13\\timport {\\n    14\\t  openThreadDatabase,\\n    15\\t  resolveThreadRef,\\n    16\\t  type ThreadRef,\\n    17\\t} from \\\"../threads/index.js\\\";\\n    18\\timport type { DerivedForm } from \\\"../../shared/derivation.js\\\";\\n    19\\timport {\\n    20\\t  findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary,\\n    21\\t  readMessageFormRow,\\n    22\\t  readMessageForms,\\n    23\\t  reportMessageForms,\\n    24\\t} from \\\"./internal/forms.js\\\";\\n    25\\timport { messageWorkHandlers } from \\\"./internal/handlers.js\\\";\\n    26\\timport { projectEvent } from \\\"./internal/project.js\\\";\\n    27\\timport {\\n    28\\t  cascadeFromMessage,\\n    29\\t  cascadeMessageDelete,\\n    30\\t  cascadeTurnDelete,\\n    31\\t  type CascadeClear,\\n    32\\t  type CascadeOutcome,\\n    33\\t} from \\\"./internal/cascade.js\\\";\\n    34\\timport {\\n    35\\t  applyMessageEdit,\\n    36\\t  insertMessage,\\n    37\\t  markMessageDeleted,\\n    38\\t  markTurnMessagesDeleted,\\n    39\\t  readMessageById,\\n    40\\t  readMessages,\\n    41\\t  readMutableMessage,\\n    42\\t} from \\\"./internal/store.js\\\";\\n    43\\t\\n    44\\texport type BlockType = \\\"text\\\" | \\\"tool_call\\\" | \\\"tool_result\\\";\\n    45\\t\\n    46\\texport interface Block {\\n    47\\t  blockType: BlockType;\\n    48\\t  content: Record<string, unknown>; // per-kind shape as projected, verbatim source content\\n    49\\t}\\n    50\\t\\n    51\\texport interface MessageRecord {\\n    52\\t  messageId: string;\\n    53\\t  sourceEventOrder: number;\\n    54\\t  kind: Exclude<EventKind, \\\"turn_end\\\">;\\n    55\\t  blocks: Block[];\\n    56\\t  tokenEstimate: number;\\n    57\\t  actor: string;\\n    58\\t  harness: string;\\n    59\\t  turnId?: string;\\n    60\\t  // The message's derived forms as stored (Epic 02 Story 2): present only\\n    61\\t  // for messages that are derivation sources — kinds with no derivable form\\n    62\\t  // carry no rows and no key (AC-2.7). Stored state returned verbatim,\\n    63\\t  // never re-derived on read.\\n    64\\t  forms?: DerivedForm[];\\n    65\\t  // The deleted-audit marker (Epic 04 AC-3.3): present (true) only on\\n    66\\t  // deleted records, which only the includeDeleted listing and the show\\n    67\\t  // read ever surface — a default list never carries the key.\\n    68\\t  deleted?: boolean;\\n    69\\t}\\n    70\\t\\n    71\\t// The event as the walk holds it after recording: the validated input plus\\n    72\\t// its server-stamped order and timestamp.\\n    73\\texport type RecordedEvent = EventRecord;\\n    74\\t\\n    75\\texport type MessageCreated = {\\n    76\\t  messageId: string;\\n    77\\t  kind: Exclude<EventKind, \\\"turn_end\\\">;\\n    78\\t  // Carried for tool activity only: the pairing key the queue sites need —\\n    79\\t  // tool_result projection runs the AC-2.8 late-result lookup against it.\\n    80\\t  toolCallId?: string;\\n    81\\t} | null;\\n    82\\t\\n    83\\t// Cross-domain surface, called by intake-stream inside the batch transaction\\n    84\\t// (the first such call through the operation context; turns.applyEvent\\n    85\\t// follows the pattern in Story 4). Synchronous and throwing by design: a\\n    86\\t// projection failure propagates to the pipeline's catch and rejects the\\n    87\\t// whole batch — recorded events without messages is the stranded state the\\n    88\\t// transaction exists to prevent. Returns null for turn_end (no message).\\n    89\\t// turnId is the membership stamp, settled by the pipeline before this call:\\n    90\\t// the turn open *after* this event's transition (so a prompt belongs to the\\n    91\\t// turn it just opened), or null in a gap — written once, never updated.\\n    92\\texport function createFromEvent(\\n    93\\t  ctx: OperationContext,\\n    94\\t  event: RecordedEvent,\\n    95\\t  turnId: string | null,\\n    96\\t): MessageCreated {\\n    97\\t  const projected = projectEvent(event);\\n    98\\t  if (projected === null) return null;\\n    99\\t  const kind = event.eventKind as Exclude<EventKind, \\\"turn_end\\\">;\\n   100\\t  const messageId = `m${event.eventOrder}`;\\n   101\\t  insertMessage(ctx.db, {\\n   102\\t    messageId,\\n   103\\t    sourceEventOrder: event.eventOrder,\\n   104\\t    kind,\\n   105\\t    tokenEstimate: projected.tokenEstimate,\\n   106\\t    actor: event.actor,\\n   107\\t    harness: event.harness,\\n   108\\t    turnId,\\n   109\\t    blocks: projected.blocks,\\n   110\\t  });\\n   111\\t  if (event.eventKind === \\\"tool_call\\\" || event.eventKind === \\\"tool_result\\\") {\\n   112\\t    return { messageId, kind, toolCallId: event.payload.toolCallId };\\n   113\\t  }\\n   114\\t  return { messageId, kind };\\n   115\\t}\\n   116\\t\\n   117\\t// The kind gate, exact by design: a prompt queues prompt_smoothing, a tool\\n   118\\t// call queues tool_call_summary (Epic 02 Story 2's additive extension), a\\n   119\\t// tool result queues tool_result_summary, nothing else queues anything —\\n   120\\t// text, thinking, and note messages are not derivation sources (Epic 01\\n   121\\t// AC-2.8/TC-2.9; Epic 02 AC-2.2/AC-2.7). Cross-domain surface, called by\\n   122\\t// intake-stream inside the batch transaction for every recorded message, so\\n   123\\t// the item commits (or rolls back) with the batch.\\n   124\\tconst MESSAGE_WORK_KINDS: Partial<Record<EventKind, WorkKind>> = {\\n   125\\t  user_prompt: \\\"prompt_smoothing\\\",\\n   126\\t  tool_call: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n   127\\t  tool_result: \\\"tool_result_summary\\\",\\n   128\\t};\\n   129\\t\\n   130\\t// Which derived form each message-owned kind produces — the owning domain's\\n   131\\t// knowledge, handed to the meaning-blind enqueue so the form's pending row\\n   132\\t// rides the same transaction (DD-5).\\n   133\\tconst MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS: Partial<Record<WorkKind, FormKind>> = {\\n   134\\t  prompt_smoothing: \\\"smoothed_prompt\\\",\\n   135\\t  tool_call_summary: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n   136\\t  tool_result_summary: \\\"tool_result_summary\\\",\\n   137\\t};\\n   138\\t\\n   139\\t// Message-owned work handlers, merged into the SDK's dispatch map at\\n   140\\t// construction (DD-6): prompt smoothing and the two tool-activity summaries.\\n   141\\texport const workHandlers: Readonly<Partial<Record<WorkKind, WorkHandler>>> =\\n   142\\t  messageWorkHandlers;\\n   143\\t\\n   144\\texport function queueMessageWork(\\n   145\\t  ctx: OperationContext,\\n   146\\t  message: MessageCreated,\\n   147\\t): WorkItemRecord[] {\\n   148\\t  if (message === null) return [];\\n   149\\t  const items: WorkItemRecord[] = [];\\n   150\\t  const kind = MESSAGE_WORK_KINDS[message.kind];\\n   151\\t  if (kind !== undefined) {\\n   152\\t    const form = MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS[kind];\\n   153\\t    if (form === undefined) {\\n   154\\t      // Every queuing kind names its form above; a miss is a wiring bug.\\n   155\\t      throw new Error(`no derived form mapped for message work kind ${kind}`);\\n   156\\t    }\\n   157\\t    items.push(\\n   158\\t      enqueue(ctx, {\\n   159\\t        owner: \\\"messages\\\",\\n   160\\t        kind,\\n   161\\t        sourceRef: { messageId: message.messageId },\\n   162\\t        forms: [{ subjectKind: \\\"message\\\", subjectId: message.messageId, form }],\\n   163\\t      }),\\n   164\\t    );\\n   165\\t  }\\n   166\\t  // Late-result repair (AC-2.8): a tool result landing after its call's\\n   167\\t  // summary already derived with outcome \\\"unknown\\\" means the summary's\\n   168\\t  // source — the call+result pair — completed underneath it; clear and\\n   169\\t  // regenerate at the next source version, in this same batch transaction.\\n   170\\t  // One indexed lookup; pending summaries (metadata NULL) never match, so\\n   171\\t  // the common call-and-result-in-one-batch case never triggers, and the\\n   172\\t  // version-scoped item id keeps the requeue idempotent.\\n   173\\t  if (message.kind === \\\"tool_result\\\" && message.toolCallId !== undefined) {\\n   174\\t    const stale = findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary(ctx.db, message.toolCallId);\\n   175\\t    if (stale !== undefined) {\\n   176\\t      items.push(\\n   177\\t        enqueue(ctx, {\\n   178\\t          owner: \\\"messages\\\",\\n   179\\t          kind: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n   180\\t          sourceRef: { messageId: stale.messageId },\\n   181\\t          sourceVersion: stale.sourceVersion + 1,\\n   182\\t          forms: [\\n   183\\t            {\\n   184\\t              subjectKind: \\\"message\\\",\\n   185\\t              subjectId: stale.messageId,\\n   186\\t              form: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n   187\\t            },\\n   188\\t          ],\\n   189\\t        }),\\n   190\\t      );\\n   191\\t    }\\n   192\\t  }\\n   193\\t  return items;\\n   194\\t}\\n   195\\t\\n   196\\tfunction threadNotFound(filePath: string): { ok: false; error: ErrorResult } {\\n   197\\t  return {\\n   198\\t    ok: false,\\n   199\\t    error: {\\n   200\\t      errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n   201\\t      code: \\\"thread_not_found\\\",\\n   202\\t      reason: `no thread file exists at ${filePath}`,\\n   203\\t    },\\n   204\\t  };\\n   205\\t}\\n   206\\t\\n   207\\t// Bounded-listing options (Epic 04 Story 1, DD-3): from/to are\\n   208\\t// source-event-order bounds, limit caps the count after bounds,\\n   209\\t// includeDeleted is the audit opt-in. All optional — existing callers see\\n   210\\t// identical results (visible messages, unbounded, record order).\\n   211\\texport interface MessageListOptions {\\n   212\\t  from?: number;\\n   213\\t  to?: number;\\n   214\\t  limit?: number;\\n   215\\t  includeDeleted?: boolean;\\n   216\\t}\\n   217\\t\\n   218\\tfunction invalidBounds(reason: string): ErrorResult {\\n   219\\t  return { errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\", code: \\\"invalid_bounds\\\", reason };\\n   220\\t}\\n   221\\t\\n   222\\t// Bounds mistakes are operational caller errors returned as results (tech\\n   223\\t// design §Interface Definitions: from > to, limit < 1) — never a silent\\n   224\\t// empty list a caller could mistake for an empty window.\\n   225\\tfunction validateListOptions(opts: MessageListOptions): ErrorResult | undefined {\\n   226\\t  const integers: ReadonlyArray<readonly [string, number | undefined]> = [\\n   227\\t    [\\\"from\\\", opts.from],\\n   228\\t    [\\\"to\\\", opts.to],\\n   229\\t    [\\\"limit\\\", opts.limit],\\n   230\\t  ];\\n   231\\t  for (const [name, value] of integers) {\\n   232\\t    if (value !== undefined && !Number.isInteger(value)) {\\n   233\\t      return invalidBounds(`${name} must be an integer, got ${value}`);\\n   234\\t    }\\n   235\\t  }\\n   236\\t  if (opts.from !== undefined && opts.to !== undefined && opts.from > opts.to) {\\n   237\\t    return invalidBounds(`from (${opts.from}) must not exceed to (${opts.to})`);\\n   238\\t  }\\n   239\\t  if (opts.limit !== undefined && opts.limit < 1) {\\n   240\\t    return invalidBounds(`limit must be at least 1, got ${opts.limit}`);\\n   241\\t  }\\n   242\\t  return undefined;\\n   243\\t}\\n   244\\t\\n   245\\texport async function listMessages(\\n   246\\t  thread: ThreadRef,\\n   247\\t  opts?: MessageListOptions,\\n   248\\t): Promise<OpResult<MessageRecord[]>> {\\n   249\\t  if (opts !== undefined) {\\n   250\\t    const badBounds = validateListOptions(opts);\\n   251\\t    if (badBounds !== undefined) return { ok: false, error: badBounds };\\n   252\\t  }\\n   253\\t  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n   254\\t  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n   255\\t  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n   256\\t  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n   257\\t\\n   258\\t  // openThreadDatabase verifies the file is a real thread file and migrates\\n   259\\t  // a pre-Story-3 one before the read, so a thread recorded under an earlier\\n   260\\t  // story lists cleanly (F-03-001) and a non-thread file is rejected\\n   261\\t  // unmutated (F-03-002).\\n   262\\t  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n   263\\t  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n   264\\t  const db = opened.value;\\n   265\\t  try {\\n   266\\t    // Form read-back rides the message read (AC-2.1): each record carries\\n   267\\t    // its stored derived forms, attached from one grouped query — the\\n   268\\t    // production path for \\\"readable alongside the message\\\".\\n   269\\t    const formsByMessage = readMessageForms(db);\\n   270\\t    const records = readMessages(db, opts ?? {}).map((record) => {\\n   271\\t      const forms = formsByMessage.get(record.messageId);\\n   272\\t      return forms === undefined ? record : { ...record, forms };\\n   273\\t    });\\n   274\\t    return { ok: true, value: records };\\n   275\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n   276\\t    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n   277\\t    return storageFailure(`message read-back failed: ${reason}`);\\n   278\\t  } finally {\\n   279\\t    db.close();\\n   280\\t  }\\n   281\\t}\\n   282\\t\\n   283\\t// The single-message view (Epic 04 AC-3.2): the canonical record — every\\n   284\\t// block with complete content, full tool results, never the view-shortened\\n   285\\t// forms — plus the message's derivation forms with their states and\\n   286\\t// mechanically stamped metadata, joined from the owner's report read.\\n   287\\texport interface MessageDetail extends Omit<MessageRecord, \\\"forms\\\"> {\\n   288\\t  // Always present and honest (AC-3.3): show on a deleted message returns\\n   289\\t  // the record flagged — audit is the point — never a not-found.\\n   290\\t  deleted: boolean;\\n   291\\t  // The owner report's queue-joined entries (DD-2), never synthesized here:\\n   292\\t  // the same `reportMessageForms` read messages.report serves, scoped by id.\\n   293\\t  forms: FormReportEntry[];\\n   294\\t}\\n   295\\t\\n   296\\texport async function show(\\n   297\\t  thread: ThreadRef,\\n   298\\t  messageId: string,\\n   299\\t): Promise<OpResult<MessageDetail>> {\\n   300\\t  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n   301\\t  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n   302\\t  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n   303\\t  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n   304\\t\\n   305\\t  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n   306\\t  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n   307\\t  const db = opened.value;\\n   308\\t  try {\\n   309\\t    const record = readMessageById(db, messageId);\\n   310\\t    if (record === undefined) {\\n   311\\t      return {\\n   312\\t        ok: false,\\n   313\\t        error: {\\n   314\\t          errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n   315\\t          code: \\\"message_not_found\\\",\\n   316\\t          reason: `no message ${messageId} exists in this thread`,\\n   317\\t        },\\n   318\\t      };\\n   319\\t    }\\n   320\\t    const forms = reportMessageForms(db, { messageId });\\n   321\\t    return { ok: true, value: { ...record, forms } };\\n   322\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n   323\\t    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n   324\\t    return storageFailure(`message show failed: ${reason}`);\\n   325\\t  } finally {\\n   326\\t    db.close();\\n   327\\t  }\\n   328\\t}\\n   329\\t\\n   330\\texport async function listQueuedWork(\\n   331\\t  thread: ThreadRef,\\n   332\\t): Promise<OpResult<WorkItemRecord[]>> {\\n   333\\t  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n   334\\t  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n   335\\t  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n   336\\t  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n   337\\t\\n   338\\t  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n   339\\t  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n   340\\t  const db = opened.value;\\n   341\\t  try {\\n   342\\t    return { ok: true, value: listItems(db, \\\"messages\\\") };\\n   343\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n   344\\t    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n   345\\t    return storageFailure(`queued-work read-back failed: ${reason}`);\\n   346\\t  } finally {\\n   347\\t    db.close();\\n   348\\t  }\\n   349\\t}\\n   350\\t\\n   351\\t// ── report and repair (Epic 02 Story 4, Flow 4) ──────────────────\\n   352\\t\\n   353\\t// This owner's repair report: every message-owned form's durable state\\n   354\\t// joined with live queue detail in one query — the five operational\\n   355\\t// situations (waiting, retrying, ready, failed, blocked) read from the rows\\n   356\\t// without any queue API. Needs no provider; reads degrade, never block.\\n   357\\texport async function report(\\n   358\\t  thread: ThreadRef,\\n   359\\t  opts?: { notReady?: boolean; messageId?: string },\\n   360\\t): Promise<OpResult<FormReportEntry[]>> {\\n   361\\t  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n   362\\t  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n   363\\t  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n   364\\t  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n   365\\t\\n   366\\t  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n   367\\t  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n   368\\t  const db = opened.value;\\n   369\\t  try {\\n   370\\t    return { ok: true, value: reportMessageForms(db, opts ?? {}) };\\n   371\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n   372\\t    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n   373\\t    return storageFailure(`report read failed: ${reason}`);\\n   374\\t  } finally {\\n   375\\t    db.close();\\n   376\\t  }\\n   377\\t}\\n   378\\t\\n   379\\texport type RequeueOutcome = { workItemId: string } | { noop: \\\"already_queued\\\" };\\n   380\\t\\n   381\\t// Which work kind rebuilds each message-owned form — MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS\\n   382\\t// inverted; the requeue's join from the named form back to its queue site.\\n   383\\tconst MESSAGE_FORM_KINDS: Partial<Record<FormKind, WorkKind>> = {\\n   384\\t  smoothed_prompt: \\\"prompt_smoothing\\\",\\n   385\\t  tool_call_summary: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n   386\\t  tool_result_summary: \\\"tool_result_summary\\\",\\n   387\\t};\\n   388\\t\\n   389\\t// Explicit re-queue through the owning surface (AC-4.4): the public,\\n   390\\t// supported rebuild act. Refused for blocked forms with the form's stored\\n   391\\t// damage reason (AC-4.6) and for missing rows; a no-op against work already\\n   392\\t// queued or in flight at the form's current source version (AC-4.5).\\n   393\\t// Otherwise the form clears to pending and re-enqueues at the next source\\n   394\\t// version — the same enqueue path intake uses, poke-on-commit included, so\\n   395\\t// background mode processes the repair with no further call. The no-op check\\n   396\\t// and the enqueue commit in one transaction (anti-shim: a split would\\n   397\\t// reintroduce the duplicate-work race).\\n   398\\texport async function requeue(\\n   399\\t  thread: ThreadRef,\\n   400\\t  target: { messageId: string; form: FormKind },\\n   401\\t): Promise<OpResult<RequeueOutcome>> {\\n   402\\t  const kind = MESSAGE_FORM_KINDS[target.form];\\n   403\\t  if (kind === undefined) {\\n   404\\t    return {\\n   405\\t      ok: false,\\n   406\\t      error: {\\n   407\\t        errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n   408\\t        code: \\\"message_not_found\\\",\\n   409\\t        reason: `form ${target.form} is not message-owned; messages.requeue repairs smoothed_prompt, tool_call_summary, tool_result_summary`,\\n   410\\t      },\\n   411\\t    };\\n   412\\t  }\\n   413\\t  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n   414\\t  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n   415\\t  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n   416\\t  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n   417\\t\\n   418\\t  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n   419\\t  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n   420\\t  const db = opened.value;\\n   421\\t  try {\\n   422\\t    const meta = db\\n   423\\t      .prepare(`SELECT thread_id FROM thread_metadata WHERE id = 1`)\\n   424\\t      .get() as { thread_id: string } | undefined;\\n   425\\t    const threadId = meta?.thread_id ?? \\\"\\\";\\n   426\\t    return runInTransaction(db, () => new Date(), threadId, (ctx): OpResult<RequeueOutcome> => {\\n   427\\t      const row = readMessageFormRow(ctx.db, target.messageId, target.form);\\n   428\\t      if (row === undefined) {\\n   429\\t        return {\\n   430\\t          ok: false,\\n   431\\t          error: {\\n   432\\t            errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n   433\\t            code: \\\"message_not_found\\\",\\n   434\\t            reason: `no derived form ${target.form} exists for message ${target.messageId}`,\\n   435\\t          },\\n   436\\t        };\\n   437\\t      }\\n   438\\t      if (row.state === \\\"blocked\\\") {\\n   439\\t        // The refusal carries the form's stored reason — the damage named at\\n   440\\t        // blocking time, not a generic string (AC-4.6).\\n   441\\t        return {\\n   442\\t          ok: false,\\n   443\\t          error: {\\n   444\\t            errorClass: \\\"state_corruption\\\",\\n   445\\t            code: \\\"source_damaged\\\",\\n   446\\t            reason: row.reason ?? `form ${target.form} for message ${target.messageId} is blocked`,\\n   447\\t          },\\n   448\\t        };\\n   449\\t      }\\n   450\\t      const sourceRef = { messageId: target.messageId };\\n   451\\t      if (hasLiveItem(ctx.db, kind, sourceRef, row.sourceVersion)) {\\n   452\\t        return { ok: true, value: { noop: \\\"already_queued\\\" } };\\n   453\\t      }\\n   454\\t      const item = enqueue(ctx, {\\n   455\\t        owner: \\\"messages\\\",\\n   456\\t        kind,\\n   457\\t        sourceRef,\\n   458\\t        sourceVersion: row.sourceVersion + 1,\\n   459\\t        forms: [{ subjectKind: \\\"message\\\", subjectId: target.messageId, form: target.form }],\\n   460\\t      });\\n   461\\t      return { ok: true, value: { workItemId: item.workItemId } };\\n   462\\t    });\\n   463\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n   464\\t    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n   465\\t    return storageFailure(`requeue failed: ${reason}`);\\n   466\\t  } finally {\\n   467\\t    db.close();\\n   468\\t  }\\n   469\\t}\\n   470\\t\\n   471\\t// ── mutations (Epic 02 Story 5, Flow 5) ──────────────────────────\\n   472\\t\\n   473\\t// The mutation result contract (tech design §Interfaces): what changed in\\n   474\\t// the record, which dependent forms cleared, which dropped (delete only),\\n   475\\t// what replacement work queued, and which still-queued old items the cascade\\n   476\\t// tidied away (issue 1). Shared by edit and the Story 6 deletes.\\n   477\\texport interface MutationResult {\\n   478\\t  changed: { messageIds: string[]; turnIds: string[] };\\n   479\\t  cleared: CascadeClear[];\\n   480\\t  dropped: CascadeClear[];\\n   481\\t  queued: Array<{ workItemId: string; kind: WorkKind }>;\\n   482\\t  superseded: string[];\\n   483\\t}\\n   484\\t\\n   485\\t// The record's first sanctioned mutation (AC-5.1–5.5): change a closed-turn\\n   486\\t// message's content and blocks, re-stamp the token estimate, and walk the\\n   487\\t// full dependent chain — clear to pending, supersede queued old work,\\n   488\\t// enqueue replacements at the next source version — in one transaction.\\n   489\\t// Synchronous and local by contract: everything above commits before this\\n   490\\t// returns; the re-queued rebuilds run through the normal drain (background\\n   491\\t// mode needs no further call — the enqueue pokes ride the commit). Events\\n   492\\t// are never touched (projection-level mutation, DD-12), and no generated\\n   493\\t// thread-view is either — visibility arrives at the next compact/rebuild.\\n   494\\t// Refusals read through the deleted-filtered view and enforce the closed-turn\\n   495\\t// target boundary: only a message in a closed turn is editable, so an\\n   496\\t// open-turn *or* a turnless (no-membership) gap target is refused turn_open —\\n   497\\t// the boundary's one stable code — a missing or deleted message is\\n   498\\t// message_not_found, and a refusal changes nothing.\\n   499\\texport async function edit(\\n   500\\t  thread: ThreadRef,\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:32:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/store.ts | sed -n '1,500p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t// Message and block row operations. Writes run on the caller's handle inside\\n     2\\t// the batch transaction (insert failures propagate so the pipeline rejects\\n     3\\t// the whole batch); reads run on a fresh handle per operation. The mutation\\n     4\\t// half (Epic 02 Story 5) — the edit's validation read and content apply —\\n     5\\t// also lives here: row-level mechanics, no policy.\\n     6\\timport type { DatabaseSync } from \\\"node:sqlite\\\";\\n     7\\timport { estimateTokens } from \\\"../../../tech-utils/token-counting/index.js\\\";\\n     8\\timport type { Block, MessageRecord } from \\\"../index.js\\\";\\n     9\\t\\n    10\\texport interface MessageRow {\\n    11\\t  messageId: string;\\n    12\\t  sourceEventOrder: number;\\n    13\\t  kind: MessageRecord[\\\"kind\\\"];\\n    14\\t  tokenEstimate: number;\\n    15\\t  actor: string;\\n    16\\t  harness: string;\\n    17\\t  // Membership stamp, settled at intake: the turn open after this event's\\n    18\\t  // transition, or null in a gap. Written once here, never updated — a null\\n    19\\t  // gap stamp stays null forever (AC-3.8), a closed turn's members never\\n    20\\t  // change (AC-3.7).\\n    21\\t  turnId: string | null;\\n    22\\t  blocks: Block[];\\n    23\\t}\\n    24\\t\\n    25\\texport function insertMessage(db: DatabaseSync, row: MessageRow): void {\\n    26\\t  db.prepare(\\n    27\\t    `INSERT INTO message (message_id, source_event_order, kind, token_estimate, actor, harness, turn_id)\\n    28\\t     VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)`,\\n    29\\t  ).run(\\n    30\\t    row.messageId,\\n    31\\t    row.sourceEventOrder,\\n    32\\t    row.kind,\\n    33\\t    row.tokenEstimate,\\n    34\\t    row.actor,\\n    35\\t    row.harness,\\n    36\\t    row.turnId,\\n    37\\t  );\\n    38\\t\\n    39\\t  const insertBlock = db.prepare(\\n    40\\t    `INSERT INTO message_block (message_id, block_index, block_type, content)\\n    41\\t     VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)`,\\n    42\\t  );\\n    43\\t  for (const [index, block] of row.blocks.entries()) {\\n    44\\t    insertBlock.run(row.messageId, index, block.blockType, JSON.stringify(block.content));\\n    45\\t  }\\n    46\\t}\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t// The mutation operations' validation read (Flows 5/6): the live\\n    49\\t// (deleted-filtered) message joined to its turn's status. A deleted target\\n    50\\t// misses here and refuses as message_not_found — the filtered view is the\\n    51\\t// refusal's read by design (never a distinct error for deleted; double\\n    52\\t// delete reads the same way, AC-6.7). turnStatus is null for a gap message\\n    53\\t// (no membership); the closed-turn target boundary refuses it the same as\\n    54\\t// an open turn. initiatesTurn carries the prompt-protection fact (AC-6.3):\\n    55\\t// a turn opens on its prompt's event, so the member whose source event\\n    56\\t// order equals the turn's opened-at order is the turn's initiating prompt.\\n    57\\texport interface MutableMessageView {\\n    58\\t  messageId: string;\\n    59\\t  kind: string;\\n    60\\t  turnId: string | null;\\n    61\\t  turnStatus: \\\"open\\\" | \\\"closed\\\" | null;\\n    62\\t  initiatesTurn: boolean;\\n    63\\t}\\n    64\\t\\n    65\\texport function readMutableMessage(\\n    66\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\n    67\\t  messageId: string,\\n    68\\t): MutableMessageView | undefined {\\n    69\\t  const row = db\\n    70\\t    .prepare(\\n    71\\t      `SELECT m.message_id, m.kind, m.turn_id, m.source_event_order,\\n    72\\t              t.status AS turn_status, t.opened_at_event_order\\n    73\\t       FROM message m LEFT JOIN turns t ON t.turn_id = m.turn_id\\n    74\\t       WHERE m.message_id = ? AND m.deleted_at IS NULL`,\\n    75\\t    )\\n    76\\t    .get(messageId) as unknown as\\n    77\\t    | {\\n    78\\t        message_id: string;\\n    79\\t        kind: string;\\n    80\\t        turn_id: string | null;\\n    81\\t        source_event_order: number | bigint;\\n    82\\t        turn_status: string | null;\\n    83\\t        opened_at_event_order: number | bigint | null;\\n    84\\t      }\\n    85\\t    | undefined;\\n    86\\t  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\n    87\\t  return {\\n    88\\t    messageId: row.message_id,\\n    89\\t    kind: row.kind,\\n    90\\t    turnId: row.turn_id,\\n    91\\t    turnStatus: row.turn_status as MutableMessageView[\\\"turnStatus\\\"],\\n    92\\t    initiatesTurn:\\n    93\\t      row.opened_at_event_order !== null &&\\n    94\\t      Number(row.source_event_order) === Number(row.opened_at_event_order),\\n    95\\t  };\\n    96\\t}\\n    97\\t\\n    98\\t// The delete's record apply (Flow 6): a projection-level tombstone — the\\n    99\\t// deleted_at stamp every read filters on. The source events are never\\n   100\\t// touched (record-never-destroyed, DD-12); event read-back keeps showing\\n   101\\t// them. The bulk variant is turns.deleteTurn's member stamp, scoped to live\\n   102\\t// rows so a turn whose messages were individually deleted first still\\n   103\\t// deletes cleanly (membership walk on live rows); it returns the stamped\\n   104\\t// ids in record order for the mutation result and the cascade's drop set.\\n   105\\texport function markMessageDeleted(\\n   106\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\n   107\\t  messageId: string,\\n   108\\t  deletedAt: string,\\n   109\\t): void {\\n   110\\t  db.prepare(`UPDATE message SET deleted_at = ? WHERE message_id = ?`).run(\\n   111\\t    deletedAt,\\n   112\\t    messageId,\\n   113\\t  );\\n   114\\t}\\n   115\\t\\n   116\\texport function markTurnMessagesDeleted(\\n   117\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\n   118\\t  turnId: string,\\n   119\\t  deletedAt: string,\\n   120\\t): string[] {\\n   121\\t  const rows = db\\n   122\\t    .prepare(\\n   123\\t      `UPDATE message SET deleted_at = ?\\n   124\\t       WHERE turn_id = ? AND deleted_at IS NULL\\n   125\\t       RETURNING message_id, source_event_order`,\\n   126\\t    )\\n   127\\t    .all(deletedAt, turnId) as unknown as Array<{\\n   128\\t    message_id: string;\\n   129\\t    source_event_order: number | bigint;\\n   130\\t  }>;\\n   131\\t  return rows\\n   132\\t    .sort((a, b) => Number(a.source_event_order) - Number(b.source_event_order))\\n   133\\t    .map((row) => row.message_id);\\n   134\\t}\\n   135\\t\\n   136\\t// The edit's record apply (AC-5.1): the new content lands in each block's\\n   137\\t// content-bearing field — the same field per block type the projection wrote\\n   138\\t// and counted (internal/project.ts) — and the token estimate re-stamps from\\n   139\\t// the same estimator, so placement arithmetic stays current after edits.\\n   140\\t// Events are untouched: this is projection-level mutation; the log keeps the\\n   141\\t// original (DD-12).\\n   142\\texport function applyMessageEdit(db: DatabaseSync, messageId: string, content: string): void {\\n   143\\t  const blocks = db\\n   144\\t    .prepare(\\n   145\\t      `SELECT block_index, block_type, content FROM message_block\\n   146\\t       WHERE message_id = ? ORDER BY block_index`,\\n   147\\t    )\\n   148\\t    .all(messageId) as unknown as Array<{\\n   149\\t    block_index: number | bigint;\\n   150\\t    block_type: string;\\n   151\\t    content: string;\\n   152\\t  }>;\\n   153\\t  const update = db.prepare(\\n   154\\t    `UPDATE message_block SET content = ? WHERE message_id = ? AND block_index = ?`,\\n   155\\t  );\\n   156\\t  let tokenEstimate = estimateTokens(content);\\n   157\\t  for (const block of blocks) {\\n   158\\t    const parsed = JSON.parse(block.content) as Record<string, unknown>;\\n   159\\t    switch (block.block_type) {\\n   160\\t      case \\\"text\\\":\\n   161\\t        parsed[\\\"text\\\"] = content;\\n   162\\t        break;\\n   163\\t      case \\\"tool_result\\\":\\n   164\\t        parsed[\\\"content\\\"] = content;\\n   165\\t        break;\\n   166\\t      case \\\"tool_call\\\":\\n   167\\t        // Arguments are the call's counted content; the edit's string lands\\n   168\\t        // verbatim as the new arguments value, mirroring projection's\\n   169\\t        // serialized-arguments estimate.\\n   170\\t        parsed[\\\"arguments\\\"] = content;\\n   171\\t        tokenEstimate = estimateTokens(JSON.stringify(content));\\n   172\\t        break;\\n   173\\t      default:\\n   174\\t        throw new Error(`message ${messageId} carries unknown block type ${block.block_type}`);\\n   175\\t    }\\n   176\\t    update.run(JSON.stringify(parsed), messageId, Number(block.block_index));\\n   177\\t  }\\n   178\\t  db.prepare(`UPDATE message SET token_estimate = ? WHERE message_id = ?`).run(\\n   179\\t    tokenEstimate,\\n   180\\t    messageId,\\n   181\\t  );\\n   182\\t}\\n   183\\t\\n   184\\tinterface RawMessageRow {\\n   185\\t  message_id: string;\\n   186\\t  source_event_order: number | bigint;\\n   187\\t  kind: string;\\n   188\\t  token_estimate: number | bigint;\\n   189\\t  actor: string;\\n   190\\t  harness: string;\\n   191\\t  turn_id: string | null;\\n   192\\t  deleted_at: string | null;\\n   193\\t}\\n   194\\t\\n   195\\tinterface RawBlockRow {\\n   196\\t  message_id: string;\\n   197\\t  block_type: string;\\n   198\\t  content: string;\\n   199\\t}\\n   200\\t\\n   201\\tfunction recordFromRow(row: RawMessageRow, blocks: Block[]): MessageRecord {\\n   202\\t  const record: MessageRecord = {\\n   203\\t    messageId: row.message_id,\\n   204\\t    sourceEventOrder: Number(row.source_event_order),\\n   205\\t    kind: row.kind as MessageRecord[\\\"kind\\\"],\\n   206\\t    blocks,\\n   207\\t    tokenEstimate: Number(row.token_estimate),\\n   208\\t    actor: row.actor,\\n   209\\t    harness: row.harness,\\n   210\\t  };\\n   211\\t  if (row.turn_id !== null) record.turnId = row.turn_id;\\n   212\\t  // The deleted marker (Epic 04 AC-3.3): present only on deleted rows, which\\n   213\\t  // only the includeDeleted read surfaces — never silently mixed in.\\n   214\\t  if (row.deleted_at !== null) record.deleted = true;\\n   215\\t  return record;\\n   216\\t}\\n   217\\t\\n   218\\t// Bounds in source-event-order coordinates (Epic 04 DD-3): the coordinate\\n   219\\t// the reports name, so drill-down uses what the operator already holds.\\n   220\\t// limit caps the count after bounds. Defaults preserve every existing\\n   221\\t// caller: visible messages, unbounded, record order.\\n   222\\texport interface MessageReadOptions {\\n   223\\t  from?: number;\\n   224\\t  to?: number;\\n   225\\t  limit?: number;\\n   226\\t  includeDeleted?: boolean;\\n   227\\t}\\n   228\\t\\n   229\\texport function readMessages(\\n   230\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\n   231\\t  opts: MessageReadOptions = {},\\n   232\\t): MessageRecord[] {\\n   233\\t  const blockRows = db\\n   234\\t    .prepare(\\n   235\\t      `SELECT message_id, block_type, content FROM message_block\\n   236\\t       ORDER BY message_id, block_index`,\\n   237\\t    )\\n   238\\t    .all() as unknown as RawBlockRow[];\\n   239\\t  const blocksByMessage = new Map<string, Block[]>();\\n   240\\t  for (const row of blockRows) {\\n   241\\t    const blocks = blocksByMessage.get(row.message_id) ?? [];\\n   242\\t    blocks.push({\\n   243\\t      blockType: row.block_type as Block[\\\"blockType\\\"],\\n   244\\t      content: JSON.parse(row.content) as Record<string, unknown>,\\n   245\\t    });\\n   246\\t    blocksByMessage.set(row.message_id, blocks);\\n   247\\t  }\\n   248\\t\\n   249\\t  // The deleted-read filter (tech design §Mechanics): message reads surface\\n   250\\t  // live projection rows only; a deleted message's source events stay\\n   251\\t  // readable through the Epic 01 event read-back, the one unfiltered surface.\\n   252\\t  // includeDeleted is the Epic 04 audit opt-in: deleted rows return flagged.\\n   253\\t  const conditions: string[] = [];\\n   254\\t  const params: number[] = [];\\n   255\\t  if (opts.includeDeleted !== true) conditions.push(\\\"deleted_at IS NULL\\\");\\n   256\\t  if (opts.from !== undefined) {\\n   257\\t    conditions.push(\\\"source_event_order >= ?\\\");\\n   258\\t    params.push(opts.from);\\n   259\\t  }\\n   260\\t  if (opts.to !== undefined) {\\n   261\\t    conditions.push(\\\"source_event_order <= ?\\\");\\n   262\\t    params.push(opts.to);\\n   263\\t  }\\n   264\\t  if (opts.limit !== undefined) params.push(opts.limit);\\n   265\\t  const messageRows = db\\n   266\\t    .prepare(\\n   267\\t      `SELECT message_id, source_event_order, kind, token_estimate, actor, harness, turn_id, deleted_at\\n   268\\t       FROM message${conditions.length > 0 ? ` WHERE ${conditions.join(\\\" AND \\\")}` : \\\"\\\"}\\n   269\\t       ORDER BY source_event_order${opts.limit !== undefined ? \\\" LIMIT ?\\\" : \\\"\\\"}`,\\n   270\\t    )\\n   271\\t    .all(...params) as unknown as RawMessageRow[];\\n   272\\t  return messageRows.map((row) =>\\n   273\\t    recordFromRow(row, blocksByMessage.get(row.message_id) ?? []),\\n   274\\t  );\\n   275\\t}\\n   276\\t\\n   277\\t// The show operation's by-id read (Epic 04 Flow 3): the canonical record —\\n   278\\t// full blocks verbatim, never view-shortened — with the deleted flag honest.\\n   279\\t// Deliberately unfiltered on deleted_at: show on a deleted message is the\\n   280\\t// audit read (AC-3.3), never a not-found.\\n   281\\texport function readMessageById(\\n   282\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\n   283\\t  messageId: string,\\n   284\\t): (MessageRecord & { deleted: boolean }) | undefined {\\n   285\\t  const row = db\\n   286\\t    .prepare(\\n   287\\t      `SELECT message_id, source_event_order, kind, token_estimate, actor, harness, turn_id, deleted_at\\n   288\\t       FROM message WHERE message_id = ?`,\\n   289\\t    )\\n   290\\t    .get(messageId) as unknown as RawMessageRow | undefined;\\n   291\\t  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\n   292\\t  const blockRows = db\\n   293\\t    .prepare(\\n   294\\t      `SELECT message_id, block_type, content FROM message_block\\n   295\\t       WHERE message_id = ? ORDER BY block_index`,\\n   296\\t    )\\n   297\\t    .all(messageId) as unknown as RawBlockRow[];\\n   298\\t  const blocks = blockRows.map((block) => ({\\n   299\\t    blockType: block.block_type as Block[\\\"blockType\\\"],\\n   300\\t    content: JSON.parse(block.content) as Record<string, unknown>,\\n   301\\t  }));\\n   302\\t  return { ...recordFromRow(row, blocks), deleted: row.deleted_at !== null };\\n   303\\t}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:35:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_15\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/lhc/src/shared/errors.ts | sed -n '1,220p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\texport type ErrorClass = \\\"caller_error\\\" | \\\"state_corruption\\\" | \\\"system_error\\\";\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\texport type ErrorCode =\\n     4\\t  | \\\"path_exists\\\"\\n     5\\t  | \\\"thread_not_found\\\"\\n     6\\t  | \\\"invalid_thread_ref\\\" // empty/blank file path or otherwise unusable reference\\n     7\\t  | \\\"invalid_event\\\"\\n     8\\t  | \\\"empty_batch\\\"\\n     9\\t  | \\\"empty_stdin\\\" // CLI adapter only, emitted before any SDK call\\n    10\\t  | \\\"turn_state_corrupt\\\"\\n    11\\t  | \\\"storage_failure\\\"\\n    12\\t  // Epic 02 (tech design §Interfaces, issue 4):\\n    13\\t  | \\\"turn_open\\\" // caller_error — mutation against an open turn\\n    14\\t  | \\\"message_initiates_turn\\\" // caller_error — delete refused toward turns.delete\\n    15\\t  | \\\"message_not_found\\\" // caller_error\\n    16\\t  | \\\"turn_not_found\\\" // caller_error\\n    17\\t  | \\\"unknown_work_kind\\\" // state_corruption — unregistered kind at dispatch\\n    18\\t  | \\\"provider_not_configured\\\" // caller_error — CLI drain without --provider / LHC_PROVIDER (DD-11)\\n    19\\t  | \\\"provider_failure\\\" // system_error — exhausted retries; form.reason carries detail\\n    20\\t  | \\\"source_damaged\\\" // state_corruption — handler found corrupt source; form blocked\\n    21\\t  // Epic 03 (tech design §Interface Definitions): the surface-skeleton stub\\n    22\\t  // contract — machine-readable, never a throw on the thread-view surface.\\n    23\\t  | \\\"not_implemented\\\" // system_error — operation's story has not landed yet\\n    24\\t  // Epic 03 Story 2 (AC-2.2/2.3): compact-time config rejection — unlike SDK\\n    25\\t  // construction (programmer error, throws), a bad compact invocation is an\\n    26\\t  // operational caller error returned as a result.\\n    27\\t  | \\\"unknown_profile\\\" // caller_error — named profile not configured\\n    28\\t  | \\\"invalid_view_config\\\" // caller_error — band sum / bound violation, named\\n    29\\t  // Epic 03 Story 5: materialize accepts pi-session only; an unknown format\\n    30\\t  // is a caller error naming the accepted values (story Scope).\\n    31\\t  | \\\"unknown_format\\\" // caller_error — materialize format not supported\\n    32\\t  // Epic 04 Story 1: bounded listing — a bad bounds option (from > to,\\n    33\\t  // limit < 1, non-integer) is an operational caller error returned as a\\n    34\\t  // result, mirroring the compact-params precedent (additive code, the\\n    35\\t  // Epic 03 deviation pattern).\\n    36\\t  | \\\"invalid_bounds\\\"; // caller_error — listMessages bounds option rejected\\n    37\\t\\n    38\\texport interface ErrorResult {\\n    39\\t  errorClass: ErrorClass;\\n    40\\t  code: ErrorCode;\\n    41\\t  reason: string; // human-readable; machine logic switches on code\\n    42\\t  eventIndex?: number; // present on batch validation failures\\n    43\\t}\\n    44\\t\\n    45\\t// Expected operational failures — caller errors, corruption, environment\\n    46\\t// failures — are always returned as OpResult errors, never thrown.\\n    47\\t// Programmer bugs inside lhc may still throw; callers are not expected\\n    48\\t// to handle throws as contract outcomes.\\n    49\\texport type OpResult<T> =\\n    50\\t  | { ok: true; value: T }\\n    51\\t  | { ok: false; error: ErrorResult };\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\t// Infrastructure failures (SQLite, fs) are expected operational outcomes,\\n    54\\t// caught at the operation boundary and wrapped with the underlying detail.\\n    55\\texport function storageFailure(reason: string): { ok: false; error: ErrorResult } {\\n    56\\t  return {\\n    57\\t    ok: false,\\n    58\\t    error: { errorClass: \\\"system_error\\\", code: \\\"storage_failure\\\", reason },\\n    59\\t  };\\n    60\\t}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:36:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_16\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts | sed -n '1,360p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\timport { parseArgs } from \\\"node:util\\\";\\n     2\\timport * as intakeStream from \\\"../domains/intake-stream/index.js\\\";\\n     3\\timport * as messages from \\\"../domains/messages/index.js\\\";\\n     4\\timport * as threads from \\\"../domains/threads/index.js\\\";\\n     5\\timport * as turns from \\\"../domains/turns/index.js\\\";\\n     6\\timport type { MessageEventInput } from \\\"../domains/intake-stream/index.js\\\";\\n     7\\timport type { ThreadRef } from \\\"../domains/threads/index.js\\\";\\n     8\\timport type { OpResult } from \\\"../shared/errors.js\\\";\\n     9\\timport { renderCliError, renderResult, type CliResult } from \\\"./render.js\\\";\\n    10\\timport { runMessagesDelete, runMessagesEdit } from \\\"./messages-mutate.js\\\";\\n    11\\timport { runMessagesList, runMessagesShow } from \\\"./messages-read.js\\\";\\n    12\\timport { runTurnsDelete } from \\\"./turns-mutate.js\\\";\\n    13\\timport {\\n    14\\t  runMessagesReport,\\n    15\\t  runMessagesRequeue,\\n    16\\t  runTurnsReport,\\n    17\\t  runTurnsRequeue,\\n    18\\t  runWorkDrain,\\n    19\\t} from \\\"./work.js\\\";\\n    20\\timport { runViewCommand } from \\\"./view.js\\\";\\n    21\\t\\n    22\\t// Stdin seam: in-process tests inject a reader; the binary reads the real\\n    23\\t// process stdin. null means interactive (TTY) — distinct from empty input\\n    24\\t// only in how it arises; both are refused with empty_stdin before any SDK\\n    25\\t// call (the SDK itself can never return that code).\\n    26\\texport type StdinReader = () => Promise<string | null>;\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\tasync function readProcessStdin(): Promise<string | null> {\\n    29\\t  if (process.stdin.isTTY) return null;\\n    30\\t  process.stdin.setEncoding(\\\"utf8\\\");\\n    31\\t  let data = \\\"\\\";\\n    32\\t  for await (const chunk of process.stdin) data += String(chunk);\\n    33\\t  return data;\\n    34\\t}\\n    35\\t\\n    36\\tfunction stdinCallerError(code: \\\"empty_stdin\\\" | \\\"invalid_event\\\", reason: string): OpResult<never> {\\n    37\\t  return { ok: false, error: { errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\", code, reason } };\\n    38\\t}\\n    39\\t\\n    40\\tconst HELP = `lhc — Long Horizon Context CLI\\n    41\\t\\n    42\\tUsage:\\n    43\\t  lhc threads new-thread --file-path <p> [--title <t>] [--registry <r>]\\n    44\\t  lhc threads resolve --thread-id <id> [--registry <r>]\\n    45\\t  lhc threads list [--registry <r>]\\n    46\\t  lhc intake-stream message-events (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n    47\\t  lhc intake-stream list-events (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n    48\\t  lhc messages list (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--from <n>] [--to <n>]\\n    49\\t                    [--limit <n>] [--include-deleted] [--registry <r>]\\n    50\\t  lhc messages show (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) --message-id <id> [--registry <r>]\\n    51\\t  lhc messages list-queued-work (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n    52\\t  lhc messages report (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--not-ready] [--message-id <id>] [--registry <r>]\\n    53\\t  lhc messages requeue (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) --message-id <id> --form <form> [--registry <r>]\\n    54\\t  lhc messages edit (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) --message <id> --content <text> [--registry <r>]\\n    55\\t  lhc messages delete (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) --message <id> [--registry <r>]\\n    56\\t  lhc turns list (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n    57\\t  lhc turns list-chunks (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n    58\\t  lhc turns list-queued-work (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n    59\\t  lhc turns report (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--not-ready] [--turn-id <id>] [--chunk-id <id>] [--registry <r>]\\n    60\\t  lhc turns requeue (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) --subject-kind (turn|chunk) --subject-id <id> --form <form> [--registry <r>]\\n    61\\t  lhc turns delete (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) --turn <id> [--registry <r>]\\n    62\\t  lhc work drain (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--max-items <n>] [--provider <name>] [--registry <r>]\\n    63\\t  lhc view pull (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--json] [--registry <r>]\\n    64\\t  lhc view status (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--json] [--registry <r>]\\n    65\\t  lhc view compact (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--profile <name>]\\n    66\\t                   [--lower-bound <n>] [--full <n>] [--smooth <n>] [--detailed <n>] [--brief <n>]\\n    67\\t                   [--no-sweep] [--json] [--registry <r>]\\n    68\\t  lhc view sweep (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--json] [--registry <r>]\\n    69\\t  lhc view materialize (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) --out <path> [--format pi-session] [--registry <r>]\\n    70\\t\\n    71\\tEvery command prints the SDK result (value or error) as JSON and exits 0 on\\n    72\\tsuccess, 1 on failure. message-events reads an events JSON array on stdin.\\n    73\\tView commands need no provider; output is always JSON (--json accepted).\\n    74\\tTwo exceptions on success: view pull prints the message array itself, and\\n    75\\tview materialize prints the written path; their failures stay structured.\\n    76\\t`;\\n    77\\t\\n    78\\tinterface ParsedFlags {\\n    79\\t  threadId?: string;\\n    80\\t  filePath?: string;\\n    81\\t  title?: string;\\n    82\\t  registryPath?: string;\\n    83\\t  maxItems?: string;\\n    84\\t  provider?: string;\\n    85\\t  notReady?: boolean;\\n    86\\t  messageId?: string;\\n    87\\t  turnId?: string;\\n    88\\t  chunkId?: string;\\n    89\\t  form?: string;\\n    90\\t  subjectKind?: string;\\n    91\\t  subjectId?: string;\\n    92\\t  content?: string;\\n    93\\t  from?: string;\\n    94\\t  to?: string;\\n    95\\t  limit?: string;\\n    96\\t  includeDeleted?: boolean;\\n    97\\t}\\n    98\\t\\n    99\\t// strict parse rejects unknown/misspelled flags so they are named back to the\\n   100\\t// caller, never silently dropped — the CLI boundary matching the SDK's\\n   101\\t// closed-contract strictness. The failure is returned as data (not thrown) so\\n   102\\t// runCli can render it as the structured usage error.\\n   103\\ttype ParseFlagsResult =\\n   104\\t  | { ok: true; flags: ParsedFlags }\\n   105\\t  | { ok: false; unknownFlag: string };\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\tfunction parseFlags(args: readonly string[]): ParseFlagsResult {\\n   108\\t  let values;\\n   109\\t  try {\\n   110\\t    ({ values } = parseArgs({\\n   111\\t      args: [...args],\\n   112\\t      options: {\\n   113\\t        \\\"thread-id\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n   114\\t        \\\"file-path\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n   115\\t        title: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n   116\\t        registry: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n   117\\t        \\\"max-items\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n   118\\t        provider: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n   119\\t        \\\"not-ready\\\": { type: \\\"boolean\\\" },\\n   120\\t        \\\"message-id\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n   121\\t        \\\"turn-id\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n   122\\t        \\\"chunk-id\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n   123\\t        form: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n   124\\t        \\\"subject-kind\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n   125\\t        \\\"subject-id\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n   126\\t        // `--message` / `--turn` are the mutation commands' spellings\\n   127\\t        // (story/tech design); they parse into the same slots as\\n   128\\t        // `--message-id` / `--turn-id`.\\n   129\\t        message: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n   130\\t        turn: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n   131\\t        content: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n   132\\t        // Epic 04 Story 1: the bounded-listing options (lhc messages list).\\n   133\\t        from: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n   134\\t        to: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n   135\\t        limit: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n   136\\t        \\\"include-deleted\\\": { type: \\\"boolean\\\" },\\n   137\\t      },\\n   138\\t      strict: true,\\n   139\\t      allowPositionals: true,\\n   140\\t    }));\\n   141\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n   142\\t    const message = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n   143\\t    // parseArgs names the offending option in single quotes (e.g. Unknown\\n   144\\t    // option '--file-pth'); surface that token, falling back to the message.\\n   145\\t    const named = /'([^']+)'/.exec(message);\\n   146\\t    return { ok: false, unknownFlag: named?.[1] ?? message };\\n   147\\t  }\\n   148\\t  const flags: ParsedFlags = {};\\n   149\\t  if (typeof values[\\\"thread-id\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.threadId = values[\\\"thread-id\\\"];\\n   150\\t  if (typeof values[\\\"file-path\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.filePath = values[\\\"file-path\\\"];\\n   151\\t  if (typeof values.title === \\\"string\\\") flags.title = values.title;\\n   152\\t  if (typeof values.registry === \\\"string\\\") flags.registryPath = values.registry;\\n   153\\t  if (typeof values[\\\"max-items\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.maxItems = values[\\\"max-items\\\"];\\n   154\\t  if (typeof values.provider === \\\"string\\\") flags.provider = values.provider;\\n   155\\t  if (values[\\\"not-ready\\\"] === true) flags.notReady = true;\\n   156\\t  if (typeof values[\\\"message-id\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.messageId = values[\\\"message-id\\\"];\\n   157\\t  if (typeof values.message === \\\"string\\\") flags.messageId = values.message;\\n   158\\t  if (typeof values.content === \\\"string\\\") flags.content = values.content;\\n   159\\t  if (typeof values[\\\"turn-id\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.turnId = values[\\\"turn-id\\\"];\\n   160\\t  if (typeof values.turn === \\\"string\\\") flags.turnId = values.turn;\\n   161\\t  if (typeof values[\\\"chunk-id\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.chunkId = values[\\\"chunk-id\\\"];\\n   162\\t  if (typeof values.form === \\\"string\\\") flags.form = values.form;\\n   163\\t  if (typeof values[\\\"subject-kind\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.subjectKind = values[\\\"subject-kind\\\"];\\n   164\\t  if (typeof values[\\\"subject-id\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.subjectId = values[\\\"subject-id\\\"];\\n   165\\t  if (typeof values.from === \\\"string\\\") flags.from = values.from;\\n   166\\t  if (typeof values.to === \\\"string\\\") flags.to = values.to;\\n   167\\t  if (typeof values.limit === \\\"string\\\") flags.limit = values.limit;\\n   168\\t  if (values[\\\"include-deleted\\\"] === true) flags.includeDeleted = true;\\n   169\\t  return { ok: true, flags };\\n   170\\t}\\n   171\\t\\n   172\\t// The read commands take a thread reference but no stdin; a missing reference\\n   173\\t// is a usage error named before any SDK call, matching the intake commands.\\n   174\\tfunction requireThreadRef(flags: ParsedFlags, command: string): CliResult | undefined {\\n   175\\t  if (flags.threadId === undefined && flags.filePath === undefined) {\\n   176\\t    return renderCliError(\\n   177\\t      \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n   178\\t      \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n   179\\t      `${command} requires --thread-id or --file-path`,\\n   180\\t    );\\n   181\\t  }\\n   182\\t  return undefined;\\n   183\\t}\\n   184\\t\\n   185\\tfunction threadRefFrom(flags: ParsedFlags): ThreadRef {\\n   186\\t  if (flags.threadId !== undefined) {\\n   187\\t    return flags.registryPath !== undefined\\n   188\\t      ? { threadId: flags.threadId, registryPath: flags.registryPath }\\n   189\\t      : { threadId: flags.threadId };\\n   190\\t  }\\n   191\\t  return { filePath: flags.filePath ?? \\\"\\\" };\\n   192\\t}\\n   193\\t\\n   194\\texport async function runCli(\\n   195\\t  argv: readonly string[],\\n   196\\t  readStdin: StdinReader = readProcessStdin,\\n   197\\t): Promise<CliResult> {\\n   198\\t  if (argv.length === 0) {\\n   199\\t    return renderCliError(\\\"caller_error\\\", \\\"unknown_command\\\", \\\"no command given; run lhc --help\\\");\\n   200\\t  }\\n   201\\t  if (argv[0] === \\\"--help\\\" || argv[0] === \\\"-h\\\") {\\n   202\\t    return { exitCode: 0, stdout: HELP, stderr: \\\"\\\" };\\n   203\\t  }\\n   204\\t\\n   205\\t  const [group, command, ...rest] = argv;\\n   206\\t  // The view group parses its own flag surface (band overrides, --out,\\n   207\\t  // --format) — routed before the shared parse so its flags never widen the\\n   208\\t  // other commands' accepted set.\\n   209\\t  if (group === \\\"view\\\") {\\n   210\\t    return runViewCommand(command, rest);\\n   211\\t  }\\n   212\\t  const key = command === undefined ? group : `${group} ${command}`;\\n   213\\t  const parsed = parseFlags(command === undefined ? [] : rest);\\n   214\\t  if (!parsed.ok) {\\n   215\\t    return renderCliError(\\n   216\\t      \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n   217\\t      \\\"unknown_flag\\\",\\n   218\\t      `unknown flag: ${parsed.unknownFlag}; run lhc --help`,\\n   219\\t    );\\n   220\\t  }\\n   221\\t  const flags = parsed.flags;\\n   222\\t\\n   223\\t  switch (key) {\\n   224\\t    case \\\"threads new-thread\\\": {\\n   225\\t      // Guard here: an empty path reaching node:sqlite opens a temp database\\n   226\\t      // instead of failing, so the adapter refuses before any SDK call.\\n   227\\t      if (flags.filePath === undefined) {\\n   228\\t        return renderCliError(\\\"caller_error\\\", \\\"missing_flag\\\", \\\"threads new-thread requires --file-path\\\");\\n   229\\t      }\\n   230\\t      const input: Parameters<typeof threads.newThread>[0] = {\\n   231\\t        filePath: flags.filePath,\\n   232\\t      };\\n   233\\t      if (flags.title !== undefined) input.title = flags.title;\\n   234\\t      if (flags.registryPath !== undefined) input.registryPath = flags.registryPath;\\n   235\\t      return renderResult(await threads.newThread(input));\\n   236\\t    }\\n   237\\t    case \\\"threads resolve\\\": {\\n   238\\t      if (flags.threadId === undefined) {\\n   239\\t        return renderCliError(\\\"caller_error\\\", \\\"missing_flag\\\", \\\"threads resolve requires --thread-id\\\");\\n   240\\t      }\\n   241\\t      const input: Parameters<typeof threads.resolve>[0] = {\\n   242\\t        threadId: flags.threadId,\\n   243\\t      };\\n   244\\t      if (flags.registryPath !== undefined) input.registryPath = flags.registryPath;\\n   245\\t      return renderResult(await threads.resolve(input));\\n   246\\t    }\\n   247\\t    case \\\"threads list\\\": {\\n   248\\t      return renderResult(\\n   249\\t        await threads.listThreads(\\n   250\\t          flags.registryPath !== undefined ? { registryPath: flags.registryPath } : undefined,\\n   251\\t        ),\\n   252\\t      );\\n   253\\t    }\\n   254\\t    case \\\"intake-stream message-events\\\": {\\n   255\\t      if (flags.threadId === undefined && flags.filePath === undefined) {\\n   256\\t        return renderCliError(\\n   257\\t          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n   258\\t          \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n   259\\t          \\\"intake-stream message-events requires --thread-id or --file-path\\\",\\n   260\\t        );\\n   261\\t      }\\n   262\\t      const text = await readStdin();\\n   263\\t      if (text === null || text.trim() === \\\"\\\") {\\n   264\\t        return renderResult(\\n   265\\t          stdinCallerError(\\n   266\\t            \\\"empty_stdin\\\",\\n   267\\t            \\\"message-events expects an events JSON array on stdin; stdin was a TTY or empty\\\",\\n   268\\t          ),\\n   269\\t        );\\n   270\\t      }\\n   271\\t      let parsed: unknown;\\n   272\\t      try {\\n   273\\t        parsed = JSON.parse(text);\\n   274\\t      } catch (cause) {\\n   275\\t        const detail = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n   276\\t        return renderResult(\\n   277\\t          stdinCallerError(\\\"invalid_event\\\", `stdin is not valid JSON: ${detail}`),\\n   278\\t        );\\n   279\\t      }\\n   280\\t      if (!Array.isArray(parsed)) {\\n   281\\t        return renderResult(\\n   282\\t          stdinCallerError(\\\"invalid_event\\\", \\\"stdin must be a JSON array of events\\\"),\\n   283\\t        );\\n   284\\t      }\\n   285\\t      return renderResult(\\n   286\\t        await intakeStream.messageEvents(\\n   287\\t          threadRefFrom(flags),\\n   288\\t          parsed as readonly MessageEventInput[],\\n   289\\t        ),\\n   290\\t      );\\n   291\\t    }\\n   292\\t    case \\\"intake-stream list-events\\\": {\\n   293\\t      if (flags.threadId === undefined && flags.filePath === undefined) {\\n   294\\t        return renderCliError(\\n   295\\t          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n   296\\t          \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n   297\\t          \\\"intake-stream list-events requires --thread-id or --file-path\\\",\\n   298\\t        );\\n   299\\t      }\\n   300\\t      return renderResult(await intakeStream.listEvents(threadRefFrom(flags)));\\n   301\\t    }\\n   302\\t    case \\\"messages list\\\": {\\n   303\\t      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"messages list\\\");\\n   304\\t      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n   305\\t      // Numeric flags convert here (the argv boundary); semantic bounds\\n   306\\t      // checks (from > to, limit < 1) stay in the SDK so refusal JSON has\\n   307\\t      // CLI/SDK parity.\\n   308\\t      const listOpts: { from?: number; to?: number; limit?: number; includeDeleted?: boolean } =\\n   309\\t        {};\\n   310\\t      if (flags.includeDeleted === true) listOpts.includeDeleted = true;\\n   311\\t      const numericFlags = [\\n   312\\t        [\\\"from\\\", flags.from],\\n   313\\t        [\\\"to\\\", flags.to],\\n   314\\t        [\\\"limit\\\", flags.limit],\\n   315\\t      ] as const;\\n   316\\t      for (const [name, raw] of numericFlags) {\\n   317\\t        if (raw === undefined) continue;\\n   318\\t        const value = Number(raw);\\n   319\\t        if (!Number.isInteger(value)) {\\n   320\\t          return renderCliError(\\n   321\\t            \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n   322\\t            \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n   323\\t            `--${name} must be an integer, got ${raw}`,\\n   324\\t          );\\n   325\\t        }\\n   326\\t        listOpts[name] = value;\\n   327\\t      }\\n   328\\t      return runMessagesList(threadRefFrom(flags), listOpts);\\n   329\\t    }\\n   330\\t    case \\\"messages show\\\": {\\n   331\\t      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"messages show\\\");\\n   332\\t      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n   333\\t      if (flags.messageId === undefined) {\\n   334\\t        return renderCliError(\\n   335\\t          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n   336\\t          \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n   337\\t          \\\"messages show requires --message-id\\\",\\n   338\\t        );\\n   339\\t      }\\n   340\\t      return runMessagesShow(threadRefFrom(flags), { messageId: flags.messageId });\\n   341\\t    }\\n   342\\t    case \\\"messages list-queued-work\\\":\\n   343\\t      return (\\n   344\\t        requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"messages list-queued-work\\\") ??\\n   345\\t        renderResult(await messages.listQueuedWork(threadRefFrom(flags)))\\n   346\\t      );\\n   347\\t    case \\\"messages report\\\": {\\n   348\\t      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"messages report\\\");\\n   349\\t      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n   350\\t      const reportFlags: { notReady?: boolean; messageId?: string } = {};\\n   351\\t      if (flags.notReady === true) reportFlags.notReady = true;\\n   352\\t      if (flags.messageId !== undefined) reportFlags.messageId = flags.messageId;\\n   353\\t      return runMessagesReport(threadRefFrom(flags), reportFlags);\\n   354\\t    }\\n   355\\t    case \\\"messages requeue\\\": {\\n   356\\t      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"messages requeue\\\");\\n   357\\t      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n   358\\t      if (flags.messageId === undefined || flags.form === undefined) {\\n   359\\t        return renderCliError(\\n   360\\t          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:44:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_20\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/lhc/test/messages-read.test.ts | sed -n '1,500p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t// Story 1 (Epic 04), default suite: TC-3.1–3.3 — the message read surface.\\n     2\\t// Bounded listing in source-event-order coordinates (DD-3), show returning\\n     3\\t// the canonical record (full blocks, never view-shortened) composed with the\\n     4\\t// owner report's form entries (DD-2), and the deleted-audit contract\\n     5\\t// (excluded by default, listable flagged on request, show never not-found).\\n     6\\t// Plus the architecture-risk legs: every read leaves observable state\\n     7\\t// unchanged (read-only delta, DD-6) and calls no provider.\\n     8\\timport { afterEach, beforeEach, describe, expect, it } from \\\"vitest\\\";\\n     9\\timport {\\n    10\\t  createSdk,\\n    11\\t  intakeStream,\\n    12\\t  messages,\\n    13\\t  threadView,\\n    14\\t  turns,\\n    15\\t  type Lhc,\\n    16\\t  type MessageEventInput,\\n    17\\t} from \\\"../src/index.js\\\";\\n    18\\timport {\\n    19\\t  createProviderDouble,\\n    20\\t  readDerivedForms,\\n    21\\t  tempStore,\\n    22\\t  validEvent,\\n    23\\t  type TempStore,\\n    24\\t} from \\\"./fixtures/index.js\\\";\\n    25\\t\\n    26\\t// Long enough that any view-form shortening would be visible: show must\\n    27\\t// return this verbatim (AC-3.2's record-not-view contract).\\n    28\\tconst TOOL_RESULT_CONTENT = [\\n    29\\t  \\\"contents of notes.txt — full record content:\\\",\\n    30\\t  \\\"line 1: the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog\\\",\\n    31\\t  \\\"line 2: detailed tool output that a boundary-shortened form would drop\\\",\\n    32\\t  \\\"line 3: trailing detail proving the record came back complete\\\",\\n    33\\t].join(\\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\tinterface ReadFixture {\\n    36\\t  filePath: string;\\n    37\\t  sdk: Lhc;\\n    38\\t  double: ReturnType<typeof createProviderDouble>;\\n    39\\t}\\n    40\\t\\n    41\\t// Two closed turns through real intake, fully drained against the\\n    42\\t// deterministic double so m1's smoothing and m3/m4's tool summaries sit\\n    43\\t// ready with mechanically stamped outcome metadata. Messages: m1 prompt,\\n    44\\t// m2 text, m3 call, m4 result (turn 1; turn_end is event 5, no message);\\n    45\\t// m6 prompt, m7 text (turn 2). Source event orders 1,2,3,4,6,7.\\n    46\\tasync function readFixture(store: TempStore): Promise<ReadFixture> {\\n    47\\t  const double = createProviderDouble();\\n    48\\t  const sdk = createSdk({ provider: double, mode: \\\"manual\\\" });\\n    49\\t  const filePath = store.threadPath();\\n    50\\t  const created = await sdk.threads.newThread({\\n    51\\t    filePath,\\n    52\\t    registryPath: store.registryPath,\\n    53\\t  });\\n    54\\t  if (!created.ok) throw new Error(`fixture thread creation failed: ${created.error.reason}`);\\n    55\\t  const batches: MessageEventInput[][] = [\\n    56\\t    [\\n    57\\t      validEvent(\\\"user_prompt\\\", { payload: { text: \\\"please read notes.txt\\\" } }),\\n    58\\t      validEvent(\\\"assistant_text\\\", { payload: { text: \\\"reading it now\\\" } }),\\n    59\\t      validEvent(\\\"tool_call\\\", {\\n    60\\t        payload: {\\n    61\\t          toolCallId: \\\"call-read-1\\\",\\n    62\\t          toolName: \\\"read_file\\\",\\n    63\\t          arguments: { path: \\\"notes.txt\\\" },\\n    64\\t        },\\n    65\\t      }),\\n    66\\t      validEvent(\\\"tool_result\\\", {\\n    67\\t        payload: { toolCallId: \\\"call-read-1\\\", content: TOOL_RESULT_CONTENT, isError: false },\\n    68\\t      }),\\n    69\\t      validEvent(\\\"turn_end\\\"),\\n    70\\t    ],\\n    71\\t    [\\n    72\\t      validEvent(\\\"user_prompt\\\", { payload: { text: \\\"summarize what you read\\\" } }),\\n    73\\t      validEvent(\\\"assistant_text\\\", { payload: { text: \\\"here is the summary\\\" } }),\\n    74\\t      validEvent(\\\"turn_end\\\"),\\n    75\\t    ],\\n    76\\t  ];\\n    77\\t  for (const batch of batches) {\\n    78\\t    const sent = await sdk.intakeStream.messageEvents({ filePath }, batch);\\n    79\\t    if (!sent.ok) throw new Error(`fixture batch failed: ${sent.error.reason}`);\\n    80\\t  }\\n    81\\t  const drained = await sdk.work.drain({ filePath });\\n    82\\t  if (!drained.ok) throw new Error(`fixture drain failed: ${drained.error.reason}`);\\n    83\\t  if (drained.value.remaining !== 0) {\\n    84\\t    throw new Error(`fixture drain left ${drained.value.remaining} items behind`);\\n    85\\t  }\\n    86\\t  return { filePath, sdk, double };\\n    87\\t}\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\tfunction idsOf(result: { ok: boolean }): string[] {\\n    90\\t  if (!result.ok) throw new Error(\\\"expected an ok list result\\\");\\n    91\\t  return (result as { ok: true; value: Array<{ messageId: string }> }).value.map(\\n    92\\t    (record) => record.messageId,\\n    93\\t  );\\n    94\\t}\\n    95\\t\\n    96\\t// The DD-6 observable-state snapshot: queued work through both owners, view\\n    97\\t// boundary/zone through status, derived-form rows, and the event log. A read\\n    98\\t// that mutates any of these fails the before/after deep-equal.\\n    99\\tasync function observableState(filePath: string): Promise<Record<string, unknown>> {\\n   100\\t  return {\\n   101\\t    events: await intakeStream.listEvents({ filePath }),\\n   102\\t    messageWork: await messages.listQueuedWork({ filePath }),\\n   103\\t    turnWork: await turns.listQueuedWork({ filePath }),\\n   104\\t    viewStatus: await threadView.status({ filePath }),\\n   105\\t    forms: readDerivedForms(filePath),\\n   106\\t  };\\n   107\\t}\\n   108\\t\\n   109\\tlet store: TempStore;\\n   110\\tbeforeEach(() => {\\n   111\\t  store = tempStore();\\n   112\\t});\\n   113\\tafterEach(() => {\\n   114\\t  store.cleanup();\\n   115\\t});\\n   116\\t\\n   117\\tdescribe(\\\"TC-3.1 / AC-3.1: listing order, fields, and bounds\\\", () => {\\n   118\\t  it(\\\"returns messages in record order with kind, token estimate, and turn membership\\\", async () => {\\n   119\\t    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\n   120\\t    const listed = await messages.listMessages({ filePath });\\n   121\\t    expect(listed.ok).toBe(true);\\n   122\\t    if (!listed.ok) return;\\n   123\\t    expect(listed.value.map((m) => m.messageId)).toEqual([\\n   124\\t      \\\"m1\\\",\\n   125\\t      \\\"m2\\\",\\n   126\\t      \\\"m3\\\",\\n   127\\t      \\\"m4\\\",\\n   128\\t      \\\"m6\\\",\\n   129\\t      \\\"m7\\\",\\n   130\\t    ]);\\n   131\\t    expect(listed.value.map((m) => m.sourceEventOrder)).toEqual([1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7]);\\n   132\\t    expect(listed.value.map((m) => m.kind)).toEqual([\\n   133\\t      \\\"user_prompt\\\",\\n   134\\t      \\\"assistant_text\\\",\\n   135\\t      \\\"tool_call\\\",\\n   136\\t      \\\"tool_result\\\",\\n   137\\t      \\\"user_prompt\\\",\\n   138\\t      \\\"assistant_text\\\",\\n   139\\t    ]);\\n   140\\t    expect(listed.value.map((m) => m.turnId)).toEqual([\\\"t1\\\", \\\"t1\\\", \\\"t1\\\", \\\"t1\\\", \\\"t2\\\", \\\"t2\\\"]);\\n   141\\t    for (const record of listed.value) {\\n   142\\t      expect(record.tokenEstimate).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n   143\\t      expect(record.deleted).toBeUndefined();\\n   144\\t    }\\n   145\\t  });\\n   146\\t\\n   147\\t  it(\\\"honors from/to/limit windows exactly in source-event-order coordinates\\\", async () => {\\n   148\\t    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\n   149\\t    const windows: Array<[Parameters<typeof messages.listMessages>[1], string[]]> = [\\n   150\\t      [{ from: 2, to: 4 }, [\\\"m2\\\", \\\"m3\\\", \\\"m4\\\"]],\\n   151\\t      [{ from: 6 }, [\\\"m6\\\", \\\"m7\\\"]],\\n   152\\t      [{ to: 2 }, [\\\"m1\\\", \\\"m2\\\"]],\\n   153\\t      [{ limit: 3 }, [\\\"m1\\\", \\\"m2\\\", \\\"m3\\\"]],\\n   154\\t      [{ from: 2, limit: 2 }, [\\\"m2\\\", \\\"m3\\\"]],\\n   155\\t      [{ from: 4, to: 4 }, [\\\"m4\\\"]],\\n   156\\t      [{ from: 5, to: 5 }, []], // the turn_end order: an event, never a message\\n   157\\t    ];\\n   158\\t    for (const [opts, expected] of windows) {\\n   159\\t      expect(idsOf(await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, opts))).toEqual(expected);\\n   160\\t    }\\n   161\\t  });\\n   162\\t\\n   163\\t  it(\\\"refuses bad bounds as caller errors and returns no partial window\\\", async () => {\\n   164\\t    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\n   165\\t    const badBounds = [{ from: 5, to: 2 }, { limit: 0 }, { limit: -1 }, { from: 1.5 }];\\n   166\\t    for (const opts of badBounds) {\\n   167\\t      const refused = await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, opts);\\n   168\\t      expect(refused.ok).toBe(false);\\n   169\\t      if (refused.ok) continue;\\n   170\\t      expect(refused.error.errorClass).toBe(\\\"caller_error\\\");\\n   171\\t      expect(refused.error.code).toBe(\\\"invalid_bounds\\\");\\n   172\\t    }\\n   173\\t  });\\n   174\\t});\\n   175\\t\\n   176\\tdescribe(\\\"TC-3.2 / AC-3.2: show returns the full record with owner-reported forms\\\", () => {\\n   177\\t  it(\\\"a drained tool-result message comes back with full content, form states, and outcome metadata\\\", async () => {\\n   178\\t    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\n   179\\t    const shown = await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\"m4\\\");\\n   180\\t    expect(shown.ok).toBe(true);\\n   181\\t    if (!shown.ok) return;\\n   182\\t    const detail = shown.value;\\n   183\\t    expect(detail.messageId).toBe(\\\"m4\\\");\\n   184\\t    expect(detail.kind).toBe(\\\"tool_result\\\");\\n   185\\t    expect(detail.turnId).toBe(\\\"t1\\\");\\n   186\\t    expect(detail.deleted).toBe(false);\\n   187\\t    expect(detail.tokenEstimate).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n   188\\t    // The record, not the view: the complete original tool result verbatim.\\n   189\\t    expect(detail.blocks).toHaveLength(1);\\n   190\\t    expect(detail.blocks[0]?.blockType).toBe(\\\"tool_result\\\");\\n   191\\t    expect(detail.blocks[0]?.content[\\\"content\\\"]).toBe(TOOL_RESULT_CONTENT);\\n   192\\t    expect(detail.blocks[0]?.content[\\\"toolCallId\\\"]).toBe(\\\"call-read-1\\\");\\n   193\\t    // Forms with states and tool-outcome metadata, joined from the owner.\\n   194\\t    expect(detail.forms).toHaveLength(1);\\n   195\\t    const summary = detail.forms[0];\\n   196\\t    expect(summary?.form).toBe(\\\"tool_result_summary\\\");\\n   197\\t    expect(summary?.state).toBe(\\\"ready\\\");\\n   198\\t    expect(summary?.content).toBeDefined();\\n   199\\t    expect(summary?.metadata?.outcome).toBe(\\\"succeeded\\\");\\n   200\\t    // Anti-shim: the forms ARE the owner report's entries for this message,\\n   201\\t    // never a synthesized join (DD-2).\\n   202\\t    const report = await messages.report({ filePath }, { messageId: \\\"m4\\\" });\\n   203\\t    expect(report.ok).toBe(true);\\n   204\\t    if (!report.ok) return;\\n   205\\t    expect(detail.forms).toEqual(report.value);\\n   206\\t  });\\n   207\\t\\n   208\\t  it(\\\"a drained prompt shows its smoothing form alongside the full record\\\", async () => {\\n   209\\t    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\n   210\\t    const shown = await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\"m1\\\");\\n   211\\t    expect(shown.ok).toBe(true);\\n   212\\t    if (!shown.ok) return;\\n   213\\t    expect(shown.value.blocks[0]?.content[\\\"text\\\"]).toBe(\\\"please read notes.txt\\\");\\n   214\\t    expect(shown.value.forms.map((form) => [form.form, form.state])).toEqual([\\n   215\\t      [\\\"smoothed_prompt\\\", \\\"ready\\\"],\\n   216\\t    ]);\\n   217\\t  });\\n   218\\t});\\n   219\\t\\n   220\\tdescribe(\\\"TC-3.3 / AC-3.3: deleted messages are audit-visible, never silently mixed\\\", () => {\\n   221\\t  it(\\\"default list excludes a deleted message; include-deleted lists it marked; show returns it flagged\\\", async () => {\\n   222\\t    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\n   223\\t    const deleted = await messages.deleteMessage({ filePath }, { messageId: \\\"m2\\\" });\\n   224\\t    expect(deleted.ok).toBe(true);\\n   225\\t\\n   226\\t    const defaultList = await messages.listMessages({ filePath });\\n   227\\t    expect(idsOf(defaultList)).toEqual([\\\"m1\\\", \\\"m3\\\", \\\"m4\\\", \\\"m6\\\", \\\"m7\\\"]);\\n   228\\t\\n   229\\t    const audited = await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, { includeDeleted: true });\\n   230\\t    expect(audited.ok).toBe(true);\\n   231\\t    if (!audited.ok) return;\\n   232\\t    expect(audited.value.map((m) => m.messageId)).toEqual([\\n   233\\t      \\\"m1\\\",\\n   234\\t      \\\"m2\\\",\\n   235\\t      \\\"m3\\\",\\n   236\\t      \\\"m4\\\",\\n   237\\t      \\\"m6\\\",\\n   238\\t      \\\"m7\\\",\\n   239\\t    ]);\\n   240\\t    for (const record of audited.value) {\\n   241\\t      if (record.messageId === \\\"m2\\\") expect(record.deleted).toBe(true);\\n   242\\t      else expect(record.deleted).toBeUndefined();\\n   243\\t    }\\n   244\\t\\n   245\\t    // Show on the deleted message is the audit read: the record, flagged —\\n   246\\t    // never a not-found.\\n   247\\t    const shown = await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\"m2\\\");\\n   248\\t    expect(shown.ok).toBe(true);\\n   249\\t    if (!shown.ok) return;\\n   250\\t    expect(shown.value.deleted).toBe(true);\\n   251\\t    expect(shown.value.blocks[0]?.content[\\\"text\\\"]).toBe(\\\"reading it now\\\");\\n   252\\t  });\\n   253\\t\\n   254\\t  it(\\\"show on a missing id is message_not_found\\\", async () => {\\n   255\\t    const { filePath } = await readFixture(store);\\n   256\\t    const missing = await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\"m99\\\");\\n   257\\t    expect(missing.ok).toBe(false);\\n   258\\t    if (missing.ok) return;\\n   259\\t    expect(missing.error.errorClass).toBe(\\\"caller_error\\\");\\n   260\\t    expect(missing.error.code).toBe(\\\"message_not_found\\\");\\n   261\\t  });\\n   262\\t});\\n   263\\t\\n   264\\tdescribe(\\\"architecture risk: reads are read-only and provider-free (DD-6)\\\", () => {\\n   265\\t  it(\\\"list and show in every mode leave observable state unchanged and call no provider\\\", async () => {\\n   266\\t    const { filePath, double } = await readFixture(store);\\n   267\\t    const captured = double.captureInputs();\\n   268\\t    const before = await observableState(filePath);\\n   269\\t\\n   270\\t    await messages.listMessages({ filePath });\\n   271\\t    await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, { from: 2, to: 4, limit: 2 });\\n   272\\t    await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, { includeDeleted: true });\\n   273\\t    await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, { from: 9, to: 1 }); // refused, must not write either\\n   274\\t    await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\"m4\\\");\\n   275\\t    await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\"m99\\\"); // not-found, must not write either\\n   276\\t\\n   277\\t    const after = await observableState(filePath);\\n   278\\t    expect(after).toEqual(before);\\n   279\\t    expect(captured).toHaveLength(0);\\n   280\\t  });\\n   281\\t});\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/004-verify.stdout.log:46:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_21\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba packages/lhc/test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts | sed -n '1,500p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t// Story 1 (Epic 04), process-boundary suite: TC-3.4 — `lhc messages list`\\n     2\\t// and `lhc messages show` through the spawned dist/cli.js have full JSON\\n     3\\t// parity with the in-process SDK operations: same options, same result JSON,\\n     4\\t// refusals included. Reads are non-mutating, so one fixture thread serves\\n     5\\t// both sides — the spawned output deep-equals the SDK result on the same\\n     6\\t// file (the production-path proof: cli/messages-read.ts routes to the SDK,\\n     7\\t// any divergence is a bypass). Reads need no provider; the binary runs with\\n     8\\t// LHC_PROVIDER unset. Runs under verify-all only (LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1).\\n     9\\t// TC-5.4's checkpoint parity joins this file in Story 4.\\n    10\\timport { spawnSync } from \\\"node:child_process\\\";\\n    11\\timport { mkdtempSync, rmSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\n    12\\timport { tmpdir } from \\\"node:os\\\";\\n    13\\timport path from \\\"node:path\\\";\\n    14\\timport { fileURLToPath } from \\\"node:url\\\";\\n    15\\timport { afterEach, beforeEach, describe, expect, it } from \\\"vitest\\\";\\n    16\\timport {\\n    17\\t  createSdk,\\n    18\\t  messages,\\n    19\\t  resolveNamedProvider,\\n    20\\t  threads,\\n    21\\t  type MessageListOptions,\\n    22\\t} from \\\"../src/index.js\\\";\\n    23\\timport { validEvent } from \\\"./fixtures/index.js\\\";\\n    24\\t\\n    25\\tconst pkgRoot = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \\\"..\\\");\\n    26\\tconst cliPath = path.join(pkgRoot, \\\"dist\\\", \\\"cli.js\\\");\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\tfunction runBinary(args: string[]): { status: number | null; stdout: string; stderr: string } {\\n    29\\t  const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [cliPath, ...args], {\\n    30\\t    encoding: \\\"utf8\\\",\\n    31\\t    env: { ...process.env, LHC_PROVIDER: undefined },\\n    32\\t  });\\n    33\\t  return { status: result.status, stdout: result.stdout, stderr: result.stderr };\\n    34\\t}\\n    35\\t\\n    36\\tlet dir: string;\\n    37\\tbeforeEach(() => {\\n    38\\t  dir = mkdtempSync(path.join(tmpdir(), \\\"lhc-proc-inspect-\\\"));\\n    39\\t});\\n    40\\tafterEach(() => {\\n    41\\t  rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });\\n    42\\t});\\n    43\\t\\n    44\\t// Two closed turns (m1 prompt, m2 text, m3 call, m4 result; m6 prompt,\\n    45\\t// m7 text), drained in-process against the registry's deterministic\\n    46\\t// provider, then m2 deleted — so the parity sweep covers live, bounded,\\n    47\\t// deleted-included, and deleted-shown reads on one record.\\n    48\\tasync function seedThread(): Promise<string> {\\n    49\\t  const filePath = path.join(dir, \\\"inspect-parity.sqlite\\\");\\n    50\\t  const created = await threads.newThread({\\n    51\\t    filePath,\\n    52\\t    registryPath: path.join(dir, \\\"registry.sqlite\\\"),\\n    53\\t  });\\n    54\\t  if (!created.ok) throw new Error(`fixture thread creation failed: ${created.error.reason}`);\\n    55\\t  const provider = resolveNamedProvider(\\\"deterministic\\\");\\n    56\\t  if (provider === undefined) throw new Error(\\\"deterministic provider not registered\\\");\\n    57\\t  const sdk = createSdk({ provider, mode: \\\"manual\\\" });\\n    58\\t  const batches = [\\n    59\\t    [\\n    60\\t      validEvent(\\\"user_prompt\\\", { payload: { text: \\\"please read notes.txt\\\" } }),\\n    61\\t      validEvent(\\\"assistant_text\\\", { payload: { text: \\\"reading it now\\\" } }),\\n    62\\t      validEvent(\\\"tool_call\\\", {\\n    63\\t        payload: {\\n    64\\t          toolCallId: \\\"call-parity-1\\\",\\n    65\\t          toolName: \\\"read_file\\\",\\n    66\\t          arguments: { path: \\\"notes.txt\\\" },\\n    67\\t        },\\n    68\\t      }),\\n    69\\t      validEvent(\\\"tool_result\\\", {\\n    70\\t        payload: {\\n    71\\t          toolCallId: \\\"call-parity-1\\\",\\n    72\\t          content: \\\"contents of notes.txt: full parity-fixture tool output\\\",\\n    73\\t          isError: false,\\n    74\\t        },\\n    75\\t      }),\\n    76\\t      validEvent(\\\"turn_end\\\"),\\n    77\\t    ],\\n    78\\t    [\\n    79\\t      validEvent(\\\"user_prompt\\\", { payload: { text: \\\"summarize what you read\\\" } }),\\n    80\\t      validEvent(\\\"assistant_text\\\", { payload: { text: \\\"here is the summary\\\" } }),\\n    81\\t      validEvent(\\\"turn_end\\\"),\\n    82\\t    ],\\n    83\\t  ];\\n    84\\t  for (const batch of batches) {\\n    85\\t    const sent = await sdk.intakeStream.messageEvents({ filePath }, batch);\\n    86\\t    if (!sent.ok) throw new Error(`fixture batch failed: ${sent.error.reason}`);\\n    87\\t  }\\n    88\\t  const drained = await sdk.work.drain({ filePath });\\n    89\\t  if (!drained.ok || drained.value.remaining !== 0) {\\n    90\\t    throw new Error(\\\"fixture drain did not settle\\\");\\n    91\\t  }\\n    92\\t  const deleted = await messages.deleteMessage({ filePath }, { messageId: \\\"m2\\\" });\\n    93\\t  if (!deleted.ok) throw new Error(`fixture delete failed: ${deleted.error.reason}`);\\n    94\\t  return filePath;\\n    95\\t}\\n    96\\t\\n    97\\tdescribe(\\\"TC-3.4 / AC-3.4: spawned-CLI message list/show parity with the SDK\\\", () => {\\n    98\\t  it(\\\"messages list mirrors the SDK across default, bounded, include-deleted, and refused options\\\", async () => {\\n    99\\t    const filePath = await seedThread();\\n   100\\t    const cases: Array<{ args: string[]; opts: MessageListOptions; ok: boolean }> = [\\n   101\\t      { args: [], opts: {}, ok: true },\\n   102\\t      { args: [\\\"--from\\\", \\\"2\\\", \\\"--to\\\", \\\"4\\\"], opts: { from: 2, to: 4 }, ok: true },\\n   103\\t      { args: [\\\"--limit\\\", \\\"2\\\"], opts: { limit: 2 }, ok: true },\\n   104\\t      { args: [\\\"--include-deleted\\\"], opts: { includeDeleted: true }, ok: true },\\n   105\\t      {\\n   106\\t        args: [\\\"--from\\\", \\\"3\\\", \\\"--limit\\\", \\\"2\\\", \\\"--include-deleted\\\"],\\n   107\\t        opts: { from: 3, limit: 2, includeDeleted: true },\\n   108\\t        ok: true,\\n   109\\t      },\\n   110\\t      // The refusal leg: bad bounds carry the same structured error through\\n   111\\t      // the process boundary, exit 1.\\n   112\\t      { args: [\\\"--from\\\", \\\"5\\\", \\\"--to\\\", \\\"2\\\"], opts: { from: 5, to: 2 }, ok: false },\\n   113\\t    ];\\n   114\\t    for (const parity of cases) {\\n   115\\t      const viaSdk = await messages.listMessages({ filePath }, parity.opts);\\n   116\\t      expect(viaSdk.ok).toBe(parity.ok);\\n   117\\t      const viaCli = runBinary([\\\"messages\\\", \\\"list\\\", \\\"--file-path\\\", filePath, ...parity.args]);\\n   118\\t      expect(viaCli.status).toBe(parity.ok ? 0 : 1);\\n   119\\t      expect(JSON.parse(viaCli.stdout)).toEqual(viaSdk);\\n   120\\t    }\\n   121\\t  });\\n   122\\t\\n   123\\t  it(\\\"messages show mirrors the SDK for live, deleted, and missing targets\\\", async () => {\\n   124\\t    const filePath = await seedThread();\\n   125\\t    for (const messageId of [\\n   126\\t      \\\"m4\\\", // live drained tool result, forms attached\\n   127\\t      \\\"m2\\\", // deleted: ok + flag — the audit read\\n   128\\t      \\\"m99\\\", // missing: message_not_found, exit 1\\n   129\\t    ]) {\\n   130\\t      const viaSdk = await messages.show({ filePath }, messageId);\\n   131\\t      const viaCli = runBinary([\\n   132\\t        \\\"messages\\\",\\n   133\\t        \\\"show\\\",\\n   134\\t        \\\"--file-path\\\",\\n   135\\t        filePath,\\n   136\\t        \\\"--message-id\\\",\\n   137\\t        messageId,\\n   138\\t      ]);\\n   139\\t      expect(viaCli.status).toBe(viaSdk.ok ? 0 : 1);\\n   140\\t      expect(JSON.parse(viaCli.stdout)).toEqual(viaSdk);\\n   141\\t    }\\n   142\\t    // The deleted target succeeds with the flag; the missing one refuses —\\n   143\\t    // pinned here so the loop's parity can't both-sides-drift.\\n   144\\t    const deletedShown = await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\"m2\\\");\\n   145\\t    expect(deletedShown.ok).toBe(true);\\n   146\\t    if (deletedShown.ok) expect(deletedShown.value.deleted).toBe(true);\\n   147\\t    const missing = await messages.show({ filePath }, \\\"m99\\\");\\n   148\\t    expect(missing.ok).toBe(false);\\n   149\\t    if (!missing.ok) expect(missing.error.code).toBe(\\\"message_not_found\\\");\\n   150\\t  });\\n   151\\t});\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:25:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01543JZUD6uY8ku7okzcZdFX\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t# Story 1: Message Read Surface\\n2\\t\\n3\\t### Summary\\n4\\t<!-- Jira: Summary field -->\\n5\\tComplete message listing and single-message viewing with deleted-audit support and CLI parity.\\n6\\t\\n7\\t### Description\\n8\\t<!-- Jira: Description field -->\\n9\\t**User Profile:** The operator audits threads from the CLI; agents inside a harness use the same reads mid-task.\\n10\\t\\n11\\t**Objective:** Provide the drill-down floor for every report that names message subjects.\\n12\\t\\n13\\t**Scope In:** `messages.list` bounded listing options, `messages.show`, forms join, deleted-message audit option, `lhc messages list`, `lhc messages show`, SDK/CLI JSON parity.\\n14\\t\\n15\\t**Scope Out:** Message search is deferred post-v1. No search behavior, search placeholder, ranking, FTS, or result-granularity decision ships in this story.\\n16\\t\\n17\\t**Dependencies:** Built Epic 01 message record/read-back behavior and Epic 02 report/deleted-message contracts.\\n18\\t\\n19\\t### Acceptance Criteria\\n20\\t<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\\n21\\t- **AC-3.1**: Listing returns messages in record order with kind, block summary, token estimate, turn membership, and deleted status, with bounded-listing options (range/limit) so large threads list without loading everything.\\n22\\t\\n23\\t- **TC-3.1** (AC-3.1): List on the fixture → record order, kinds, token estimates, turn ids correct; range and limit options honored exactly.\\n24\\t\\n25\\t- **AC-3.2**: `messages.show` returns one message in full: every block with complete content (the record — full tool results, not view-shortened forms), token estimate, turn membership, and the message's derivation forms with their states and metadata (joined from the owner's report, including tool-outcome metadata where present).\\n26\\t\\n27\\t- **TC-3.2** (AC-3.2): Show on a drained tool-result message → full original content present, forms listed with states, outcome metadata present.\\n28\\t\\n29\\t- **AC-3.3**: Deleted messages are excluded by default and listable with an explicit include-deleted option, marked deleted — never silently mixed in. `show` on a deleted message returns the record marked deleted (audit is the point), never a not-found.\\n30\\t\\n31\\t- **TC-3.3** (AC-3.3): Delete one message → default list excludes it; include-deleted lists it marked; show on its id → record with deleted flag.\\n32\\t\\n33\\t- **AC-3.4**: CLI parity: `lhc messages list` and `lhc messages show` mirror the SDK operations — same options, same result JSON.\\n34\\t\\n35\\t- **TC-3.4** (AC-3.4): Spawned-CLI list and show on a fixture thread → JSON equals the in-process SDK results (process suite).\\n36\\t\\n37\\t### Technical Design\\n38\\t<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\\n39\\t#### Architecture Context\\n40\\t\\n41\\tThis story extends the existing messages surface. `listMessages` gains optional bounds and deleted-audit options while preserving default visible-message behavior for existing callers. `show` returns the canonical record content, not the view-shortened content, and composes form state from the owner report surface.\\n42\\t\\n43\\tThe CLI is a thin argv-to-SDK wrapper. JSON output must deep-equal the in-process SDK result.\\n44\\t\\n45\\t#### Build Strategy\\n46\\t\\n47\\tStrategy: simple-risk-reminders\\n48\\t\\n49\\tReason:\\n50\\t- One surface owns listing/showing behavior, but bounds semantics, deleted defaults, and CLI parity are easy to shortcut.\\n51\\t\\n52\\tRisk Reminders:\\n53\\t- `show` returns full record blocks, including full tool results.\\n54\\t- Deleted messages remain excluded by default and auditable on explicit request.\\n55\\t- Bounds use source-event-order coordinates: `{ from?, to?, limit?, includeDeleted? }`.\\n56\\t\\n57\\t#### Implementation Targets\\n58\\t\\n59\\t| Area | Files / Modules |\\n60\\t|------|-----------------|\\n61\\t| Message surface | `src/domains/messages/index.ts` |\\n62\\t| CLI | `src/cli/messages-read.ts` |\\n63\\t| SDK export | `src/sdk.ts` |\\n64\\t| Tests | `test/messages-read.test.ts`, `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` |\\n65\\t\\n66\\t#### Design References\\n67\\t\\n68\\t- [tech-design.md §Module Boundaries](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:54), lines 54-98\\n69\\t- [tech-design.md §Flow 3: Message Listing and Show](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:139), lines 139-142\\n70\\t- [tech-design.md §Interface Definitions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:189), lines 189-213\\n71\\t- [test-plan.md §Test Files](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:6), lines 6-18\\n72\\t- [test-plan.md §TC → Test Mapping](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:20), lines 20-40\\n73\\t- [test-plan.md §Chunk Red/Green Detail](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:56), lines 56-64\\n74\\t\\n75\\t#### Test Mapping\\n76\\t\\n77\\t| TC | Test File / Check | Test Description |\\n78\\t|----|-------------------|------------------|\\n79\\t| TC-3.1 | `test/messages-read.test.ts :: order, fields, bounds` | Record order, kind, token estimate, turn id, exact `from`/`to`/`limit` windows, and bad bounds error. |\\n80\\t| TC-3.2 | `test/messages-read.test.ts :: show full record + forms` | Drained tool-result message returns full content, form states, and outcome metadata. |\\n81\\t| TC-3.3 | `test/messages-read.test.ts :: deleted handling` | Default list excludes deleted; include-deleted marks it; show on deleted returns ok with flag; missing id returns not found. |\\n82\\t| TC-3.4 | `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts :: list/show parity` | Spawned CLI message list/show JSON deep-equals SDK results. |\\n83\\t\\n84\\t#### Architecture-Risk Tests\\n85\\t\\n86\\t| Risk | Test File / Check | Test Description | Why AC/TC Mapping Alone Would Miss It |\\n87\\t|------|-------------------|------------------|---------------------------------------|\\n88\\t| Read-only drift | `test/messages-read.test.ts` read-only legs | Before/after observable-state snapshots stay equal for list/show. | A read can satisfy shape assertions while still mutating queue, boundary, or view state. |\\n89\\t| CLI bypasses SDK | `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` process parity | Spawned commands compare serialized JSON against SDK results. | Private helper tests can pass while production CLI output diverges. |\\n90\\t\\n91\\t#### Technical Notes\\n92\\t\\n93\\t- `listMessages` option defaults must preserve existing callers: visible messages, unbounded, record order.\\n94\\t- `from` and `to` are source-event-order bounds; `limit` caps after bounds.\\n95\\t- `show` composes the by-id message read with `messages.report(ref, { messageId })`.\\n96\\t- Message search remains deferred post-v1 and gets no v1 placeholder behavior.\\n97\\t\\n98\\t#### Anti-Shim Requirements\\n99\\t\\n100\\t- Assert real full block content for tool-result messages, not only message id or metadata.\\n101\\t- Exercise the spawned `lhc messages` commands for process parity.\\n102\\t- Do not synthesize form state in `show`; use the owner report entries.\\n103\\t\\n104\\t#### Production Path Proof\\n105\\t\\n106\\t- Entrypoint: `messages.listMessages`, `messages.show`, `lhc messages list`, `lhc messages show`.\\n107\\t- Registration/default path: `src/sdk.ts` exposes the message operations; `src/cli/messages-read.ts` routes CLI commands to SDK calls.\\n108\\t- Evidence: process parity for CLI list/show and default-suite message read tests.\\n109\\t\\n110\\t#### Verification\\n111\\t\\n112\\t- Targeted: `pnpm verify`\\n113\\t- Story gate: `pnpm verify`\\n114\\t- Epic/process gate: `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all`\\n115\\t\\n116\\t#### Spec Deviations\\n117\\t\\n118\\tNone.\\n119\\t\\n120\\t### Definition of Done\\n121\\t<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n122\\t- `messages.list` returns bounded, ordered message summaries with deleted filtering.\\n123\\t- `messages.show` returns full record content and owner-reported form state for one message.\\n124\\t- Deleted-message audit behavior matches Epic 02's deleted contract.\\n125\\t- CLI list/show options and JSON match SDK results.\\n126\\t- TC-3.1 through TC-3.4 pass with one primary owner in this story.\\n127\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"92b30fef-4ad7-45bb-a8e9-4c6f66be56bf\",\"uuid\":\"35683720-7dbe-4350-bb66-29d4cc2e5cee\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-12T12:47:38.981Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/01-message-read-surface.md\",\"content\":\"# Story 1: Message Read Surface\\n\\n### Summary\\n<!-- Jira: Summary field -->\\nComplete message listing and single-message viewing with deleted-audit support and CLI parity.\\n\\n### Description\\n<!-- Jira: Description field -->\\n**User Profile:** The operator audits threads from the CLI; agents inside a harness use the same reads mid-task.\\n\\n**Objective:** Provide the drill-down floor for every report that names message subjects.\\n\\n**Scope In:** `messages.list` bounded listing options, `messages.show`, forms join, deleted-message audit option, `lhc messages list`, `lhc messages show`, SDK/CLI JSON parity.\\n\\n**Scope Out:** Message search is deferred post-v1. No search behavior, search placeholder, ranking, FTS, or result-granularity decision ships in this story.\\n\\n**Dependencies:** Built Epic 01 message record/read-back behavior and Epic 02 report/deleted-message contracts.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\\n- **AC-3.1**: Listing returns messages in record order with kind, block summary, token estimate, turn membership, and deleted status, with bounded-listing options (range/limit) so large threads list without loading everything.\\n\\n- **TC-3.1** (AC-3.1): List on the fixture → record order, kinds, token estimates, turn ids correct; range and limit options honored exactly.\\n\\n- **AC-3.2**: `messages.show` returns one message in full: every block with complete content (the record — full tool results, not view-shortened forms), token estimate, turn membership, and the message's derivation forms with their states and metadata (joined from the owner's report, including tool-outcome metadata where present).\\n\\n- **TC-3.2** (AC-3.2): Show on a drained tool-result message → full original content present, forms listed with states, outcome metadata present.\\n\\n- **AC-3.3**: Deleted messages are excluded by default and listable with an explicit include-deleted option, marked deleted — never silently mixed in. `show` on a deleted message returns the record marked deleted (audit is the point), never a not-found.\\n\\n- **TC-3.3** (AC-3.3): Delete one message → default list excludes it; include-deleted lists it marked; show on its id → record with deleted flag.\\n\\n- **AC-3.4**: CLI parity: `lhc messages list` and `lhc messages show` mirror the SDK operations — same options, same result JSON.\\n\\n- **TC-3.4** (AC-3.4): Spawned-CLI list and show on a fixture thread → JSON equals the in-process SDK results (process suite).\\n\\n### Technical Design\\n<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\\n#### Architecture Context\\n\\nThis story extends the existing messages surface. `listMessages` gains optional bounds and deleted-audit options while preserving default visible-message behavior for existing callers. `show` returns the canonical record content, not the view-shortened content, and composes form state from the owner report surface.\\n\\nThe CLI is a thin argv-to-SDK wrapper. JSON output must deep-equal the in-process SDK result.\\n\\n#### Build Strategy\\n\\nStrategy: simple-risk-reminders\\n\\nReason:\\n- One surface owns listing/showing behavior, but bounds semantics, deleted defaults, and CLI parity are easy to shortcut.\\n\\nRisk Reminders:\\n- `show` returns full record blocks, including full tool results.\\n- Deleted messages remain excluded by default and auditable on explicit request.\\n- Bounds use source-event-order coordinates: `{ from?, to?, limit?, includeDeleted? }`.\\n\\n#### Implementation Targets\\n\\n| Area | Files / Modules |\\n|------|-----------------|\\n| Message surface | `src/domains/messages/index.ts` |\\n| CLI | `src/cli/messages-read.ts` |\\n| SDK export | `src/sdk.ts` |\\n| Tests | `test/messages-read.test.ts`, `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` |\\n\\n#### Design References\\n\\n- [tech-design.md §Module Boundaries](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:54), lines 54-98\\n- [tech-design.md §Flow 3: Message Listing and Show](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:139), lines 139-142\\n- [tech-design.md §Interface Definitions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:189), lines 189-213\\n- [test-plan.md §Test Files](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:6), lines 6-18\\n- [test-plan.md §TC → Test Mapping](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:20), lines 20-40\\n- [test-plan.md §Chunk Red/Green Detail](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:56), lines 56-64\\n\\n#### Test Mapping\\n\\n| TC | Test File / Check | Test Description |\\n|----|-------------------|------------------|\\n| TC-3.1 | `test/messages-read.test.ts :: order, fields, bounds` | Record order, kind, token estimate, turn id, exact `from`/`to`/`limit` windows, and bad bounds error. |\\n| TC-3.2 | `test/messages-read.test.ts :: show full record + forms` | Drained tool-result message returns full content, form states, and outcome metadata. |\\n| TC-3.3 | `test/messages-read.test.ts :: deleted handling` | Default list excludes deleted; include-deleted marks it; show on deleted returns ok with flag; missing id returns not found. |\\n| TC-3.4 | `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts :: list/show parity` | Spawned CLI message list/show JSON deep-equals SDK results. |\\n\\n#### Architecture-Risk Tests\\n\\n| Risk | Test File / Check | Test Description | Why AC/TC Mapping Alone Would Miss It |\\n|------|-------------------|------------------|---------------------------------------|\\n| Read-only drift | `test/messages-read.test.ts` read-only legs | Before/after observable-state snapshots stay equal for list/show. | A read can satisfy shape assertions while still mutating queue, boundary, or view state. |\\n| CLI bypasses SDK | `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` process parity | Spawned commands compare serialized JSON against SDK results. | Private helper tests can pass while production CLI output diverges. |\\n\\n#### Technical Notes\\n\\n- `listMessages` option defaults must preserve existing callers: visible messages, unbounded, record order.\\n- `from` and `to` are source-event-order bounds; `limit` caps after bounds.\\n- `show` composes the by-id message read with `messages.report(ref, { messageId })`.\\n- Message search remains deferred post-v1 and gets no v1 placeholder behavior.\\n\\n#### Anti-Shim Requirements\\n\\n- Assert real full block content for tool-result messages, not only message id or metadata.\\n- Exercise the spawned `lhc messages` commands for process parity.\\n- Do not synthesize form state in `show`; use the owner report entries.\\n\\n#### Production Path Proof\\n\\n- Entrypoint: `messages.listMessages`, `messages.show`, `lhc messages list`, `lhc messages show`.\\n- Registration/default path: `src/sdk.ts` exposes the message operations; `src/cli/messages-read.ts` routes CLI commands to SDK calls.\\n- Evidence: process parity for CLI list/show and default-suite message read tests.\\n\\n#### Verification\\n\\n- Targeted: `pnpm verify`\\n- Story gate: `pnpm verify`\\n- Epic/process gate: `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all`\\n\\n#### Spec Deviations\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### Definition of Done\\n<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n- `messages.list` returns bounded, ordered message summaries with deleted filtering.\\n- `messages.show` returns full record content and owner-reported form state for one message.\\n- Deleted-message audit behavior matches Epic 02's deleted contract.\\n- CLI list/show options and JSON match SDK results.\\n- TC-3.1 through TC-3.4 pass with one primary owner in this story.\\n\",\"numLines\":127,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":127}}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:31:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01W67tcwY5B4grhTNdXULHv9\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t# Epic 04: Inspection — Tech Design\\n2\\t\\n3\\t**Epic:** `epic.md` (23 ACs / 17 TCs) · **Tech arch:** `../01-tech-arch.md` · **Test plan:** `test-plan.md`\\n4\\t**Inherits:** Epic 01–03 technical world — storage/transaction rules, error model, `OpResult`, verification tiers, process-suite accounting, CLI conventions. Nothing re-stated here that those designs pin; this document covers what Epic 04 adds.\\n5\\t\\n6\\t## Context\\n7\\t\\n8\\tThe last epic of the v1 PRD, and the smallest: no migration, no new tables, no derivations, no provider use, no new algorithms. Four read surfaces and a lifecycle exercise. The design problem is not mechanism — it is *composition discipline*: every report assembles other domains' surfaces without touching their tables, and where a report describes another surface's output (`loadCost` vs `pull`), the design makes agreement structural rather than tested-into-existence (the materialize parity-by-construction pattern, reused).\\n9\\t\\n10\\tThe second design problem is the dependency posture: this epic consumes Epic 03's surfaces, which finished building days before this design. The epic's handoff gate requires the deviation check below.\\n11\\t\\n12\\t## Spec Validation\\n13\\t\\n14\\tDesigned from the epic; issues found and resolved during design:\\n15\\t\\n16\\t| # | Issue | Resolution | Status |\\n17\\t|---|-------|-----------|--------|\\n18\\t| 1 | **Handoff gate (epic Assumptions):** Epic 02/03 final deviation tables vs the contracts this epic consumes | Reviewed all recorded deviations (Epic 02 impl log; Epic 03 impl log: `ViewProfileOverride[]` config typing, `view_boundary` strftime seed, `ViewCompactParams` nested partial, additive error codes, sweep-absent literal superseded by Story 3). None alter consumed shapes: `ViewStatus`, `PullResult`, `thread_view`/`thread_view_band`/`view_boundary` DDL, `messages.report`/`turns.report`, `FormReportEntry`, `MessageRecord.forms` all match spec as built. One *favorable* drift: Epic 02's AC-4.7 ruling attached `forms` to message reads (built for this consumer), so Flow 3's join is thinner than the epic assumed | Gate PASSED — recorded here |\\n19\\t| 2 | AC-1.1 needs counts (events, messages by kind, tokens) that no surface exposes as counts; inspect may not read tables directly; epic sanctions only one surface addition (`describe`) | Overview composes *list* reads (`listEvents`, `listMessages`, `listTurns`, `listChunks`) and counts in inspect. Cost is linear in thread size — acceptable at v1 scale (NFR allows thread-proportional reads). Count-only surface ops are a deferred optimization, not a v1 need | Resolved — composition, no new surfaces |\\n20\\t| 3 | Epic Data Contracts leave list-option names to tech design | Pinned: `{ from?, to?, limit?, includeDeleted? }` — `from`/`to` are source-event-order bounds (reports name `sourceEventOrder`, so drill-down uses the coordinate the operator already holds), `limit` caps count after bounds | Resolved — DD-3 |\\n21\\t| 4 | AC-2.3 equality (`loadCost` totals what pull serves) could be a fragile re-implementation of pull's costing | `inspect.view` *invokes* `threadView.pull` through the surface and measures its output — parity by construction; the TC's independent leg runs a second pull in the test and re-measures. Same pattern as Epic 03's materialize | Resolved — DD-4 |\\n22\\t| 5 | TC-5.x suite placement left open by epic (TD question 5) | TC-5.1–5.3 default suite (in-process, deterministic, fast); TC-5.4 process suite (spawned CLI). The epic's lean (\\\"TC-5.1 likely default\\\") extended after checking runtimes: replay + teardown legs spawn nothing | Resolved — DD-8 |\\n23\\t\\n24\\t## System View\\n25\\t\\n26\\t```\\n27\\t                    ┌─────────────── inspect (NEW) ───────────────┐\\n28\\t                    │  overview()      view()       health()      │\\n29\\t                    └───┬─────┬─────────┬──┬───────────┬──────────┘\\n30\\t                        │     │         │  │           │\\n31\\t        ┌───────────────┘     │         │  └───────┐   └────────┐\\n32\\t        ▼                     ▼         ▼          ▼            ▼\\n33\\t   threads.resolve      intake-stream  thread-view  messages.report\\n34\\t   listThreads          .listEvents    .describe(NEW) turns.report\\n35\\t                                       .pull        .listQueuedWork\\n36\\t                        messages.listMessages(+opts)\\n37\\t                        messages.show (NEW)          turns.listTurns/listChunks\\n38\\t```\\n39\\t\\n40\\t`inspect` sits at the top of the domain graph: pure consumer, imports five surfaces, nothing imports it except `sdk.ts` and `cli/`. No cycles — unlike Epic 03's sanctioned intake→thread-view cycle, this addition is acyclic by construction. `check-boundaries` gains the domain with no exception entries.\\n41\\t\\n42\\t### External Contracts (consumed, as built)\\n43\\t\\n44\\t| Contract | Source | Used by |\\n45\\t|----------|--------|---------|\\n46\\t| `listEvents` → ordered `EventRecord[]` | intake-stream (E01) | overview (count, span) |\\n47\\t| `listMessages` → `MessageRecord[]` with `forms?` attached | messages (E01 + E02 AC-4.7) | overview, list/show |\\n48\\t| `report(ref, {messageId?})` → `FormReportEntry[]` (queue join) | messages/turns (E02) | health, show |\\n49\\t| `listTurns` / `listChunks` / `listQueuedWork` | turns (E01/E02) | overview, health |\\n50\\t| `status` → `ViewStatus` | thread-view (E03) | overview (visibility, derivation counts) |\\n51\\t| `pull` → `PullResult` | thread-view (E03) | view (loadCost by construction) |\\n52\\t| `thread_view` row + bands (storage, in-domain) | thread-view (E03) | `describe` only |\\n53\\t\\n54\\t## Module Boundaries\\n55\\t\\n56\\t### Placement\\n57\\t\\n58\\t```\\n59\\tsrc/\\n60\\t  domains/\\n61\\t    inspect/\\n62\\t      index.ts          ← NEW surface: overview, view, health\\n63\\t      internal/\\n64\\t        overview.ts     ← compose counts from list reads\\n65\\t        view-report.ts  ← describe + pull → ViewContentsReport\\n66\\t        health.ts       ← report joins → HealthReport\\n67\\t    thread-view/\\n68\\t      index.ts          ← gains describe() (read-only, ~30 lines)\\n69\\t    messages/\\n70\\t      index.ts          ← listMessages gains opts; gains show()\\n71\\t  shared/\\n72\\t    inspect.ts          ← NEW: InspectOverview, ViewContentsReport, HealthReport shapes\\n73\\t  cli/\\n74\\t    inspect.ts          ← NEW: lhc inspect overview|view|health\\n75\\t    messages-read.ts    ← NEW: lhc messages list|show (mutations stay in messages-mutate.ts)\\n76\\t  sdk.ts                ← gains inspect namespace; threadView.describe; messages.show/list opts\\n77\\t```\\n78\\t\\n79\\t### Module Responsibility Matrix\\n80\\t\\n81\\t| Module | Owns | Must NOT own |\\n82\\t|--------|------|--------------|\\n83\\t| `inspect/index.ts` + internal | Report assembly, counting, shaping | Any table read, any write, any provider call, any derivation interpretation beyond the owners' reported states |\\n84\\t| `thread-view/describe` | Exposing stored view row (arrangement, gaps, config, source state) | Recomputing anything; mutating; reading the record |\\n85\\t| `messages/show` | Single-record read (full blocks) + `report(messageId)` composition | View-form shortening (show returns the record — full tool results, never boundary-shortened) |\\n86\\t| `messages/listMessages` opts | Bounds, limit, deleted filter | Default-including deleted (audit is opt-in) |\\n87\\t| `cli/inspect.ts`, `cli/messages-read.ts` | argv → SDK → JSON stdout | Any logic beyond arg mapping (CLI parity is structural: same code path as SDK) |\\n88\\t\\n89\\tDesign decisions:\\n90\\t\\n91\\t- **DD-1 (describe placement):** `describe` lives in thread-view because the stored view row is thread-view's table; inspect consuming it through the surface keeps the must-not-own rule airtight. Absent view → `ok` with `null`, mirroring `status`'s never-compacted behavior.\\n92\\t- **DD-2 (show composes report):** `show` = internal single-message read (same store read as `listMessages`, by id, full blocks) + `messages.report(ref, {messageId})` for the queue-joined forms. No new join machinery; `FormReportEntry` is the forms shape `show` returns.\\n93\\t- **DD-3 (list options):** `{ from?, to?, limit?, includeDeleted? }`, bounds in source event order. Existing callers unaffected (opts optional, default behavior unchanged: all visible messages).\\n94\\t- **DD-4 (loadCost by construction):** `view-report.ts` calls `describe` (stored bands: entries, gaps, config, stored token counts) and `pull` (served messages). `loadCost.bandTokens` = sum of stored band counts; `loadCost.tailTokens` = estimator over pull's tail messages (band-absent entries); `total` = sum. Pull is the single costing authority for the tail — AC-2.2's boundary-aware shortening is inherited, not re-implemented.\\n95\\t- **DD-5 (overview's view section):** composed from `status` (boundary, zone, derivation counts, view health) + `describe` (viewId, createdAt, compactPoint, coveredFrom) — both already exist; overview adds no view logic.\\n96\\t- **DD-6 (read-only, structurally tested):** the architecture-risk test snapshots observable state (work-item rows via `listQueuedWork`/reports, boundary position via `status`, view identity via `describe`, event/message counts) before and after every inspect/describe/show/list call and asserts deep equality. Read-only is asserted as absence-of-delta, not absence-of-write-code.\\n97\\t- **DD-7 (no migration):** schema terminal at v6. The one index temptation (message kind counts) is declined — counts come from list reads (Spec Validation #2); if profiling ever demands an index, that is a v7 proposal.\\n98\\t- **DD-8 (suite placement):** TC-5.1–5.3 default suite; TC-5.4 process suite. The lifecycle script is a shared fixture helper (`test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts`) both suites drive, so the spawned leg replays the same sequence rather than a re-described one.\\n99\\t\\n100\\t## Storage\\n101\\t\\n102\\tNone. No tables, no migration, no new indexes (DD-7). The only storage *read* this epic adds is `describe`'s in-domain read of `thread_view` / `thread_view_band` / `view_boundary`, all Epic 03 tables.\\n103\\t\\n104\\t## Flow-by-Flow Design\\n105\\t\\n106\\t### Flow 1: Overview\\n107\\t\\n108\\t`overview(ref)`: resolve thread (registry metadata) → `listEvents` (count, first/last order) → `listMessages({includeDeleted: true})` (visible/deleted split, kind counts, visible token sum — deleted detected per the read contract's flag) → `listTurns` (open/closed counts) → `listChunks` (count; unchunked = closed turns minus chunk-member turns) → `status` + `describe` (derivation counts, visibility, view summary). Each piece independent; fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted-with-record, compacted, and mid-rebuild shapes fall out of the same composition path: absent pieces are zeros/nulls; no shape-specific branch is allowed except normalizing null sections.\\n109\\t\\n110\\tWorked example (compacted fixture, abridged):\\n111\\t\\n112\\t```json\\n113\\t{\\n114\\t  \\\"thread\\\": { \\\"id\\\": \\\"th_…\\\", \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"…\\\" },\\n115\\t  \\\"events\\\": { \\\"count\\\": 412, \\\"span\\\": { \\\"first\\\": 1, \\\"last\\\": 412 } },\\n116\\t  \\\"messages\\\": { \\\"visible\\\": 187, \\\"byKind\\\": { \\\"user_prompt\\\": 14, \\\"assistant_text\\\": 41, \\\"tool_call\\\": 66, \\\"tool_result\\\": 64, \\\"assistant_thinking\\\": 2 }, \\\"deleted\\\": 2, \\\"visibleTokens\\\": 96342 },\\n117\\t  \\\"turns\\\": { \\\"open\\\": 0, \\\"closed\\\": 14 },\\n118\\t  \\\"chunks\\\": { \\\"count\\\": 4, \\\"unchunkedTurns\\\": 2 },\\n119\\t  \\\"derivation\\\": { \\\"ready\\\": 118, \\\"pending\\\": 3, \\\"retrying\\\": 1, \\\"failed\\\": 2, \\\"blocked\\\": 0 },\\n120\\t  \\\"view\\\": { \\\"viewId\\\": \\\"v391\\\", \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"…\\\", \\\"compactPoint\\\": 391, \\\"coveredFrom\\\": 12 },\\n121\\t  \\\"visibility\\\": { \\\"boundaryPosition\\\": 398, \\\"zoneTokens\\\": 18204 }\\n122\\t}\\n123\\t```\\n124\\t\\n125\\t### Flow 2: View Contents Report\\n126\\t\\n127\\t```\\n128\\tinspect.view ──► threadView.describe ──► stored arrangement/gaps/config/band tokens/source state\\n129\\t      │\\n130\\t      └────────► threadView.pull ──► served messages\\n131\\t                      │\\n132\\t                      ├─ band entries → cross-check count only (arrangement is describe's)\\n133\\t                      └─ tail entries → estimator → tailTokens (as served: short forms short)\\n134\\tloadCost = { bandTokens: Σ stored, tailTokens: measured, total: sum }\\n135\\t```\\n136\\t\\n137\\tNever-compacted: `describe` → null ⇒ `meta: null`, bands empty, whole pull output is tail, parity contract unchanged (AC-2.4). The report never recomputes selection, rendering, or boundary state — stored snapshot + live pull are the only sources (AC-2.1's \\\"not recomputed\\\" is structural).\\n138\\t\\n139\\t### Flow 3: Message Listing and Show\\n140\\t\\n141\\t`listMessages(ref, opts)`: existing read + WHERE bounds on `source_event_order`, LIMIT, deleted filter (default excluded; `includeDeleted` includes flagged). `show(ref, messageId)`: by-id read, full blocks verbatim from the record, `deleted` flag honest, forms from `report({messageId})`. Not-found → `message_not_found` (existing code). Deleted + show → `ok` with flagged record (AC-3.3: audit, never not-found).\\n142\\t\\n143\\t### Flow 4: Health\\n144\\t\\n145\\t`health(ref)`: `messages.report` + `turns.report` (full, not-ready included) + `listQueuedWork` both owners. Compose: counts by owner/kind/state from report entries' states; `failures[]` from `failed`/`blocked` entries (reason, attempts, lastError off `FormReportEntry`); `repairPreview[]` = failed-and-not-blocked subjects (reported, never requeued — AC-4.3); `queue` = queued/claimed counts from the live-item joins, consistent by construction with the same entries' states (AC-4.5). Rebuild visibility (AC-4.4) is two health calls bracketing a drain — no new mechanism, the cascade's pending states simply show.\\n146\\t\\n147\\t### Flow 5: Lifecycle Exercise\\n148\\t\\n149\\tScripted in `test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts`: phases named `create | intake | drain | status | compact1 | pull1 | inspect1 | mutate | rebuild | health2 | compact2 | pull2 | materialize`. Each phase returns its results to the driving test; checkpoint assertions live in the test, not the script. Teardown leg (TC-5.3) re-creates the SDK between named phase groups using the same script with a `freshSdk` hook. Receipt-vs-health cross-check (AC-5.2): `compact2`'s receipt sweep section against the `health2` snapshot taken immediately before — field-level equality on the failed/requeued sets.\\n150\\t\\n151\\t## Interface Definitions\\n152\\t\\n153\\t`src/shared/inspect.ts` (load-bearing shapes; field comments carry AC refs in source):\\n154\\t\\n155\\t```typescript\\n156\\texport interface InspectOverview {\\n157\\t  thread: { id: string; createdAt: string; metadata?: Record<string, string> };\\n158\\t  events: { count: number; span: { first: number; last: number } | null };\\n159\\t  messages: { visible: number; byKind: Record<string, number>; deleted: number; visibleTokens: number };\\n160\\t  turns: { open: number; closed: number };\\n161\\t  chunks: { count: number; unchunkedTurns: number };\\n162\\t  derivation: { ready: number; pending: number; retrying: number; failed: number; blocked: number };\\n163\\t  view: { viewId: string; createdAt: string; compactPoint: number; coveredFrom: number } | null;\\n164\\t  visibility: { boundaryPosition: number; zoneTokens: number };\\n165\\t}\\n166\\t\\n167\\texport interface ViewContentsReport {\\n168\\t  meta: { viewId: string; createdAt: string; profile: string | null;\\n169\\t          config: { lowerBound: number; percentages: Record<string, number> };\\n170\\t          compactPoint: number; coveredFrom: number } | null;\\n171\\t  bands: Array<{ band: Band; entries: Array<{ subjectKind: \\\"chunk\\\" | \\\"turn\\\"; subjectId: string;\\n172\\t          formUsed: string; degraded: boolean }>; storedTokens: number }>;\\n173\\t  gaps: Array<{ band: Band; subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\\n174\\t  tail: { messageCount: number; tokens: number };          // as served (AC-2.2)\\n175\\t  loadCost: { bandTokens: number; tailTokens: number; total: number }; // = pull (AC-2.3)\\n176\\t  sourceState: { maxEventOrder: number; formCounts: Record<string, number> }; // provenance verbatim (AC-2.5)\\n177\\t}\\n178\\t\\n179\\texport interface HealthReport {\\n180\\t  owners: Array<{ owner: \\\"messages\\\" | \\\"turns\\\"; kind: string;\\n181\\t          counts: { ready: number; pending: number; retrying: number; failed: number; blocked: number } }>;\\n182\\t  failures: Array<{ owner: string; subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: string;\\n183\\t          reason: string; attempts: number; lastError?: string }>;\\n184\\t  repairPreview: Array<{ owner: string; subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: string }>;\\n185\\t  queue: { queued: number; claimed: number };\\n186\\t}\\n187\\t```\\n188\\t\\n189\\tSurface signatures:\\n190\\t\\n191\\t```typescript\\n192\\t// inspect\\n193\\toverview(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<InspectOverview>>;\\n194\\tview(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<ViewContentsReport>>;\\n195\\thealth(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<HealthReport>>;\\n196\\t// thread-view addition\\n197\\tdescribe(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<StoredView | null>>;   // StoredView mirrors the row: id, createdAt, compactPoint, coveredFrom, profileName, config, arrangement, gaps, sourceState, bands (band → storedTokens)\\n198\\t// messages additions\\n199\\tlistMessages(ref: ThreadRef, opts?: { from?: number; to?: number; limit?: number; includeDeleted?: boolean }): Promise<OpResult<MessageRecord[]>>;\\n200\\tshow(ref: ThreadRef, messageId: string): Promise<OpResult<MessageDetail>>;  // MessageRecord (full blocks, deleted flag) + forms: FormReportEntry[]\\n201\\t```\\n202\\t\\n203\\tCLI grammar (JSON stdout, existing error classes, exit conventions inherited):\\n204\\t\\n205\\t```\\n206\\tlhc inspect overview --thread <ref>\\n207\\tlhc inspect view     --thread <ref>\\n208\\tlhc inspect health   --thread <ref>\\n209\\tlhc messages list    --thread <ref> [--from <n>] [--to <n>] [--limit <n>] [--include-deleted]\\n210\\tlhc messages show    --thread <ref> --message-id <id>\\n211\\t```\\n212\\t\\n213\\tError codes: no additions. `thread_not_found`, `message_not_found`, `caller_error` (bad bounds: `from > to`, `limit < 1`), `state_corruption`, `system_error` — all existing.\\n214\\t\\n215\\t## Testing Strategy\\n216\\t\\n217\\tInherited wholesale from Epics 01–03: real temp SQLite, no mocks anywhere but the provider seam (unused here beyond fixture prep), default + process suites, zero-provider assertion extended to all inspect/show/list/describe operations. New emphasis — the **read-only delta assert** (DD-6) is this epic's architecture-risk centerpiece: every new operation runs under a before/after observable-state snapshot in one shared helper. Direct table-read prevention is static: `check-boundaries` forbids cross-domain internal imports, and this epic adds a source check that `domains/inspect/**` contains no raw SQL table-name access to other domains' tables. Test files: `inspect-overview.test.ts`, `inspect-view.test.ts`, `messages-read.test.ts`, `inspect-health.test.ts`, `lifecycle.test.ts`, `cli-process-inspect.test.ts` (process suite). Full TC mapping, fixture extensions, and Red/Green detail: `test-plan.md`.\\n218\\t\\n219\\t## Work Breakdown\\n220\\t\\n221\\tStory chunks follow the epic's four stories; per-chunk Red/Green and counts in the test plan.\\n222\\t\\n223\\t| Chunk | Story | Builds | Risk concentration |\\n224\\t|-------|-------|--------|--------------------|\\n225\\t| 1 | S1 Message reads | list opts, show, `cli/messages-read.ts` | Bounds semantics; deleted default; show returning record-not-view forms |\\n226\\t| 2 | S2 Inspect domain | surface + overview + health, `shared/inspect.ts`, `cli/inspect.ts`, fixture mutation-states extension | Count correctness vs fixture ground truth; health composition staying on surfaces |\\n227\\t| 3 | S3 View report | `describe`, `view-report.ts` | Parity-by-construction wiring; never-compacted nulls |\\n228\\t| 4 | S4 Lifecycle | `lifecycle.ts` script + 4 TC legs | Checkpoint ordering; receipt-vs-health equality; teardown continuity |\\n229\\t\\n230\\tSequencing: 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 (3 needs Epic 03 storage live — already landed; 4 needs 1–3).\\n231\\t\\n232\\t## Open Questions\\n233\\t\\n234\\tNone blocking. Deferred items: count-only surface ops if thread scale ever makes overview's list-composition measurable (Spec Validation #2); message search (post-v1, PRD-recorded).\\n235\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"92b30fef-4ad7-45bb-a8e9-4c6f66be56bf\",\"uuid\":\"f0c4f02c-1a9d-4d21-a898-35152c0ce1fc\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-12T12:47:40.060Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"content\":\"# Epic 04: Inspection — Tech Design\\n\\n**Epic:** `epic.md` (23 ACs / 17 TCs) · **Tech arch:** `../01-tech-arch.md` · **Test plan:** `test-plan.md`\\n**Inherits:** Epic 01–03 technical world — storage/transaction rules, error model, `OpResult`, verification tiers, process-suite accounting, CLI conventions. Nothing re-stated here that those designs pin; this document covers what Epic 04 adds.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nThe last epic of the v1 PRD, and the smallest: no migration, no new tables, no derivations, no provider use, no new algorithms. Four read surfaces and a lifecycle exercise. The design problem is not mechanism — it is *composition discipline*: every report assembles other domains' surfaces without touching their tables, and where a report describes another surface's output (`loadCost` vs `pull`), the design makes agreement structural rather than tested-into-existence (the materialize parity-by-construction pattern, reused).\\n\\nThe second design problem is the dependency posture: this epic consumes Epic 03's surfaces, which finished building days before this design. The epic's handoff gate requires the deviation check below.\\n\\n## Spec Validation\\n\\nDesigned from the epic; issues found and resolved during design:\\n\\n| # | Issue | Resolution | Status |\\n|---|-------|-----------|--------|\\n| 1 | **Handoff gate (epic Assumptions):** Epic 02/03 final deviation tables vs the contracts this epic consumes | Reviewed all recorded deviations (Epic 02 impl log; Epic 03 impl log: `ViewProfileOverride[]` config typing, `view_boundary` strftime seed, `ViewCompactParams` nested partial, additive error codes, sweep-absent literal superseded by Story 3). None alter consumed shapes: `ViewStatus`, `PullResult`, `thread_view`/`thread_view_band`/`view_boundary` DDL, `messages.report`/`turns.report`, `FormReportEntry`, `MessageRecord.forms` all match spec as built. One *favorable* drift: Epic 02's AC-4.7 ruling attached `forms` to message reads (built for this consumer), so Flow 3's join is thinner than the epic assumed | Gate PASSED — recorded here |\\n| 2 | AC-1.1 needs counts (events, messages by kind, tokens) that no surface exposes as counts; inspect may not read tables directly; epic sanctions only one surface addition (`describe`) | Overview composes *list* reads (`listEvents`, `listMessages`, `listTurns`, `listChunks`) and counts in inspect. Cost is linear in thread size — acceptable at v1 scale (NFR allows thread-proportional reads). Count-only surface ops are a deferred optimization, not a v1 need | Resolved — composition, no new surfaces |\\n| 3 | Epic Data Contracts leave list-option names to tech design | Pinned: `{ from?, to?, limit?, includeDeleted? }` — `from`/`to` are source-event-order bounds (reports name `sourceEventOrder`, so drill-down uses the coordinate the operator already holds), `limit` caps count after bounds | Resolved — DD-3 |\\n| 4 | AC-2.3 equality (`loadCost` totals what pull serves) could be a fragile re-implementation of pull's costing | `inspect.view` *invokes* `threadView.pull` through the surface and measures its output — parity by construction; the TC's independent leg runs a second pull in the test and re-measures. Same pattern as Epic 03's materialize | Resolved — DD-4 |\\n| 5 | TC-5.x suite placement left open by epic (TD question 5) | TC-5.1–5.3 default suite (in-process, deterministic, fast); TC-5.4 process suite (spawned CLI). The epic's lean (\\\"TC-5.1 likely default\\\") extended after checking runtimes: replay + teardown legs spawn nothing | Resolved — DD-8 |\\n\\n## System View\\n\\n```\\n                    ┌─────────────── inspect (NEW) ───────────────┐\\n                    │  overview()      view()       health()      │\\n                    └───┬─────┬─────────┬──┬───────────┬──────────┘\\n                        │     │         │  │           │\\n        ┌───────────────┘     │         │  └───────┐   └────────┐\\n        ▼                     ▼         ▼          ▼            ▼\\n   threads.resolve      intake-stream  thread-view  messages.report\\n   listThreads          .listEvents    .describe(NEW) turns.report\\n                                       .pull        .listQueuedWork\\n                        messages.listMessages(+opts)\\n                        messages.show (NEW)          turns.listTurns/listChunks\\n```\\n\\n`inspect` sits at the top of the domain graph: pure consumer, imports five surfaces, nothing imports it except `sdk.ts` and `cli/`. No cycles — unlike Epic 03's sanctioned intake→thread-view cycle, this addition is acyclic by construction. `check-boundaries` gains the domain with no exception entries.\\n\\n### External Contracts (consumed, as built)\\n\\n| Contract | Source | Used by |\\n|----------|--------|---------|\\n| `listEvents` → ordered `EventRecord[]` | intake-stream (E01) | overview (count, span) |\\n| `listMessages` → `MessageRecord[]` with `forms?` attached | messages (E01 + E02 AC-4.7) | overview, list/show |\\n| `report(ref, {messageId?})` → `FormReportEntry[]` (queue join) | messages/turns (E02) | health, show |\\n| `listTurns` / `listChunks` / `listQueuedWork` | turns (E01/E02) | overview, health |\\n| `status` → `ViewStatus` | thread-view (E03) | overview (visibility, derivation counts) |\\n| `pull` → `PullResult` | thread-view (E03) | view (loadCost by construction) |\\n| `thread_view` row + bands (storage, in-domain) | thread-view (E03) | `describe` only |\\n\\n## Module Boundaries\\n\\n### Placement\\n\\n```\\nsrc/\\n  domains/\\n    inspect/\\n      index.ts          ← NEW surface: overview, view, health\\n      internal/\\n        overview.ts     ← compose counts from list reads\\n        view-report.ts  ← describe + pull → ViewContentsReport\\n        health.ts       ← report joins → HealthReport\\n    thread-view/\\n      index.ts          ← gains describe() (read-only, ~30 lines)\\n    messages/\\n      index.ts          ← listMessages gains opts; gains show()\\n  shared/\\n    inspect.ts          ← NEW: InspectOverview, ViewContentsReport, HealthReport shapes\\n  cli/\\n    inspect.ts          ← NEW: lhc inspect overview|view|health\\n    messages-read.ts    ← NEW: lhc messages list|show (mutations stay in messages-mutate.ts)\\n  sdk.ts                ← gains inspect namespace; threadView.describe; messages.show/list opts\\n```\\n\\n### Module Responsibility Matrix\\n\\n| Module | Owns | Must NOT own |\\n|--------|------|--------------|\\n| `inspect/index.ts` + internal | Report assembly, counting, shaping | Any table read, any write, any provider call, any derivation interpretation beyond the owners' reported states |\\n| `thread-view/describe` | Exposing stored view row (arrangement, gaps, config, source state) | Recomputing anything; mutating; reading the record |\\n| `messages/show` | Single-record read (full blocks) + `report(messageId)` composition | View-form shortening (show returns the record — full tool results, never boundary-shortened) |\\n| `messages/listMessages` opts | Bounds, limit, deleted filter | Default-including deleted (audit is opt-in) |\\n| `cli/inspect.ts`, `cli/messages-read.ts` | argv → SDK → JSON stdout | Any logic beyond arg mapping (CLI parity is structural: same code path as SDK) |\\n\\nDesign decisions:\\n\\n- **DD-1 (describe placement):** `describe` lives in thread-view because the stored view row is thread-view's table; inspect consuming it through the surface keeps the must-not-own rule airtight. Absent view → `ok` with `null`, mirroring `status`'s never-compacted behavior.\\n- **DD-2 (show composes report):** `show` = internal single-message read (same store read as `listMessages`, by id, full blocks) + `messages.report(ref, {messageId})` for the queue-joined forms. No new join machinery; `FormReportEntry` is the forms shape `show` returns.\\n- **DD-3 (list options):** `{ from?, to?, limit?, includeDeleted? }`, bounds in source event order. Existing callers unaffected (opts optional, default behavior unchanged: all visible messages).\\n- **DD-4 (loadCost by construction):** `view-report.ts` calls `describe` (stored bands: entries, gaps, config, stored token counts) and `pull` (served messages). `loadCost.bandTokens` = sum of stored band counts; `loadCost.tailTokens` = estimator over pull's tail messages (band-absent entries); `total` = sum. Pull is the single costing authority for the tail — AC-2.2's boundary-aware shortening is inherited, not re-implemented.\\n- **DD-5 (overview's view section):** composed from `status` (boundary, zone, derivation counts, view health) + `describe` (viewId, createdAt, compactPoint, coveredFrom) — both already exist; overview adds no view logic.\\n- **DD-6 (read-only, structurally tested):** the architecture-risk test snapshots observable state (work-item rows via `listQueuedWork`/reports, boundary position via `status`, view identity via `describe`, event/message counts) before and after every inspect/describe/show/list call and asserts deep equality. Read-only is asserted as absence-of-delta, not absence-of-write-code.\\n- **DD-7 (no migration):** schema terminal at v6. The one index temptation (message kind counts) is declined — counts come from list reads (Spec Validation #2); if profiling ever demands an index, that is a v7 proposal.\\n- **DD-8 (suite placement):** TC-5.1–5.3 default suite; TC-5.4 process suite. The lifecycle script is a shared fixture helper (`test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts`) both suites drive, so the spawned leg replays the same sequence rather than a re-described one.\\n\\n## Storage\\n\\nNone. No tables, no migration, no new indexes (DD-7). The only storage *read* this epic adds is `describe`'s in-domain read of `thread_view` / `thread_view_band` / `view_boundary`, all Epic 03 tables.\\n\\n## Flow-by-Flow Design\\n\\n### Flow 1: Overview\\n\\n`overview(ref)`: resolve thread (registry metadata) → `listEvents` (count, first/last order) → `listMessages({includeDeleted: true})` (visible/deleted split, kind counts, visible token sum — deleted detected per the read contract's flag) → `listTurns` (open/closed counts) → `listChunks` (count; unchunked = closed turns minus chunk-member turns) → `status` + `describe` (derivation counts, visibility, view summary). Each piece independent; fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted-with-record, compacted, and mid-rebuild shapes fall out of the same composition path: absent pieces are zeros/nulls; no shape-specific branch is allowed except normalizing null sections.\\n\\nWorked example (compacted fixture, abridged):\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"thread\\\": { \\\"id\\\": \\\"th_…\\\", \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"…\\\" },\\n  \\\"events\\\": { \\\"count\\\": 412, \\\"span\\\": { \\\"first\\\": 1, \\\"last\\\": 412 } },\\n  \\\"messages\\\": { \\\"visible\\\": 187, \\\"byKind\\\": { \\\"user_prompt\\\": 14, \\\"assistant_text\\\": 41, \\\"tool_call\\\": 66, \\\"tool_result\\\": 64, \\\"assistant_thinking\\\": 2 }, \\\"deleted\\\": 2, \\\"visibleTokens\\\": 96342 },\\n  \\\"turns\\\": { \\\"open\\\": 0, \\\"closed\\\": 14 },\\n  \\\"chunks\\\": { \\\"count\\\": 4, \\\"unchunkedTurns\\\": 2 },\\n  \\\"derivation\\\": { \\\"ready\\\": 118, \\\"pending\\\": 3, \\\"retrying\\\": 1, \\\"failed\\\": 2, \\\"blocked\\\": 0 },\\n  \\\"view\\\": { \\\"viewId\\\": \\\"v391\\\", \\\"createdAt\\\": \\\"…\\\", \\\"compactPoint\\\": 391, \\\"coveredFrom\\\": 12 },\\n  \\\"visibility\\\": { \\\"boundaryPosition\\\": 398, \\\"zoneTokens\\\": 18204 }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Flow 2: View Contents Report\\n\\n```\\ninspect.view ──► threadView.describe ──► stored arrangement/gaps/config/band tokens/source state\\n      │\\n      └────────► threadView.pull ──► served messages\\n                      │\\n                      ├─ band entries → cross-check count only (arrangement is describe's)\\n                      └─ tail entries → estimator → tailTokens (as served: short forms short)\\nloadCost = { bandTokens: Σ stored, tailTokens: measured, total: sum }\\n```\\n\\nNever-compacted: `describe` → null ⇒ `meta: null`, bands empty, whole pull output is tail, parity contract unchanged (AC-2.4). The report never recomputes selection, rendering, or boundary state — stored snapshot + live pull are the only sources (AC-2.1's \\\"not recomputed\\\" is structural).\\n\\n### Flow 3: Message Listing and Show\\n\\n`listMessages(ref, opts)`: existing read + WHERE bounds on `source_event_order`, LIMIT, deleted filter (default excluded; `includeDeleted` includes flagged). `show(ref, messageId)`: by-id read, full blocks verbatim from the record, `deleted` flag honest, forms from `report({messageId})`. Not-found → `message_not_found` (existing code). Deleted + show → `ok` with flagged record (AC-3.3: audit, never not-found).\\n\\n### Flow 4: Health\\n\\n`health(ref)`: `messages.report` + `turns.report` (full, not-ready included) + `listQueuedWork` both owners. Compose: counts by owner/kind/state from report entries' states; `failures[]` from `failed`/`blocked` entries (reason, attempts, lastError off `FormReportEntry`); `repairPreview[]` = failed-and-not-blocked subjects (reported, never requeued — AC-4.3); `queue` = queued/claimed counts from the live-item joins, consistent by construction with the same entries' states (AC-4.5). Rebuild visibility (AC-4.4) is two health calls bracketing a drain — no new mechanism, the cascade's pending states simply show.\\n\\n### Flow 5: Lifecycle Exercise\\n\\nScripted in `test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts`: phases named `create | intake | drain | status | compact1 | pull1 | inspect1 | mutate | rebuild | health2 | compact2 | pull2 | materialize`. Each phase returns its results to the driving test; checkpoint assertions live in the test, not the script. Teardown leg (TC-5.3) re-creates the SDK between named phase groups using the same script with a `freshSdk` hook. Receipt-vs-health cross-check (AC-5.2): `compact2`'s receipt sweep section against the `health2` snapshot taken immediately before — field-level equality on the failed/requeued sets.\\n\\n## Interface Definitions\\n\\n`src/shared/inspect.ts` (load-bearing shapes; field comments carry AC refs in source):\\n\\n```typescript\\nexport interface InspectOverview {\\n  thread: { id: string; createdAt: string; metadata?: Record<string, string> };\\n  events: { count: number; span: { first: number; last: number } | null };\\n  messages: { visible: number; byKind: Record<string, number>; deleted: number; visibleTokens: number };\\n  turns: { open: number; closed: number };\\n  chunks: { count: number; unchunkedTurns: number };\\n  derivation: { ready: number; pending: number; retrying: number; failed: number; blocked: number };\\n  view: { viewId: string; createdAt: string; compactPoint: number; coveredFrom: number } | null;\\n  visibility: { boundaryPosition: number; zoneTokens: number };\\n}\\n\\nexport interface ViewContentsReport {\\n  meta: { viewId: string; createdAt: string; profile: string | null;\\n          config: { lowerBound: number; percentages: Record<string, number> };\\n          compactPoint: number; coveredFrom: number } | null;\\n  bands: Array<{ band: Band; entries: Array<{ subjectKind: \\\"chunk\\\" | \\\"turn\\\"; subjectId: string;\\n          formUsed: string; degraded: boolean }>; storedTokens: number }>;\\n  gaps: Array<{ band: Band; subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\\n  tail: { messageCount: number; tokens: number };          // as served (AC-2.2)\\n  loadCost: { bandTokens: number; tailTokens: number; total: number }; // = pull (AC-2.3)\\n  sourceState: { maxEventOrder: number; formCounts: Record<string, number> }; // provenance verbatim (AC-2.5)\\n}\\n\\nexport interface HealthReport {\\n  owners: Array<{ owner: \\\"messages\\\" | \\\"turns\\\"; kind: string;\\n          counts: { ready: number; pending: number; retrying: number; failed: number; blocked: number } }>;\\n  failures: Array<{ owner: string; subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: string;\\n          reason: string; attempts: number; lastError?: string }>;\\n  repairPreview: Array<{ owner: string; subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: string }>;\\n  queue: { queued: number; claimed: number };\\n}\\n```\\n\\nSurface signatures:\\n\\n```typescript\\n// inspect\\noverview(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<InspectOverview>>;\\nview(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<ViewContentsReport>>;\\nhealth(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<HealthReport>>;\\n// thread-view addition\\ndescribe(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<StoredView | null>>;   // StoredView mirrors the row: id, createdAt, compactPoint, coveredFrom, profileName, config, arrangement, gaps, sourceState, bands (band → storedTokens)\\n// messages additions\\nlistMessages(ref: ThreadRef, opts?: { from?: number; to?: number; limit?: number; includeDeleted?: boolean }): Promise<OpResult<MessageRecord[]>>;\\nshow(ref: ThreadRef, messageId: string): Promise<OpResult<MessageDetail>>;  // MessageRecord (full blocks, deleted flag) + forms: FormReportEntry[]\\n```\\n\\nCLI grammar (JSON stdout, existing error classes, exit conventions inherited):\\n\\n```\\nlhc inspect overview --thread <ref>\\nlhc inspect view     --thread <ref>\\nlhc inspect health   --thread <ref>\\nlhc messages list    --thread <ref> [--from <n>] [--to <n>] [--limit <n>] [--include-deleted]\\nlhc messages show    --thread <ref> --message-id <id>\\n```\\n\\nError codes: no additions. `thread_not_found`, `message_not_found`, `caller_error` (bad bounds: `from > to`, `limit < 1`), `state_corruption`, `system_error` — all existing.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\nInherited wholesale from Epics 01–03: real temp SQLite, no mocks anywhere but the provider seam (unused here beyond fixture prep), default + process suites, zero-provider assertion extended to all inspect/show/list/describe operations. New emphasis — the **read-only delta assert** (DD-6) is this epic's architecture-risk centerpiece: every new operation runs under a before/after observable-state snapshot in one shared helper. Direct table-read prevention is static: `check-boundaries` forbids cross-domain internal imports, and this epic adds a source check that `domains/inspect/**` contains no raw SQL table-name access to other domains' tables. Test files: `inspect-overview.test.ts`, `inspect-view.test.ts`, `messages-read.test.ts`, `inspect-health.test.ts`, `lifecycle.test.ts`, `cli-process-inspect.test.ts` (process suite). Full TC mapping, fixture extensions, and Red/Green detail: `test-plan.md`.\\n\\n## Work Breakdown\\n\\nStory chunks follow the epic's four stories; per-chunk Red/Green and counts in the test plan.\\n\\n| Chunk | Story | Builds | Risk concentration |\\n|-------|-------|--------|--------------------|\\n| 1 | S1 Message reads | list opts, show, `cli/messages-read.ts` | Bounds semantics; deleted default; show returning record-not-view forms |\\n| 2 | S2 Inspect domain | surface + overview + health, `shared/inspect.ts`, `cli/inspect.ts`, fixture mutation-states extension | Count correctness vs fixture ground truth; health composition staying on surfaces |\\n| 3 | S3 View report | `describe`, `view-report.ts` | Parity-by-construction wiring; never-compacted nulls |\\n| 4 | S4 Lifecycle | `lifecycle.ts` script + 4 TC legs | Checkpoint ordering; receipt-vs-health equality; teardown continuity |\\n\\nSequencing: 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 (3 needs Epic 03 storage live — already landed; 4 needs 1–3).\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\nNone blocking. Deferred items: count-only surface ops if thread scale ever makes overview's list-composition measurable (Spec Validation #2); message search (post-v1, PRD-recorded).\\n\",\"numLines\":235,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":235}}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:39:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01KAv6UR79hps5jHzQQp1Ykb\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t# Epic 04: Inspection — Test Plan\\n2\\t\\n3\\t**Epic:** `epic.md` (23 ACs / 17 TCs) · **Tech design:** `tech-design.md`\\n4\\tInherits Epic 01–03 test architecture: real temp SQLite per test, deterministic provider for fixture prep only, default suite (`pnpm verify`) + process suite (`LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all`), suite-accounting row, red manifest discipline.\\n5\\t\\n6\\t## Test Files\\n7\\t\\n8\\t| File | Suite | Covers |\\n9\\t|------|-------|--------|\\n10\\t| `test/messages-read.test.ts` | default | TC-3.1–3.3 + list/show read-only legs |\\n11\\t| `test/inspect-overview.test.ts` | default | TC-1.1–1.3 |\\n12\\t| `test/inspect-view.test.ts` | default | TC-2.1–2.3 + describe legs |\\n13\\t| `test/inspect-health.test.ts` | default | TC-4.1–4.3 |\\n14\\t| `test/lifecycle.test.ts` | default | TC-5.1–5.3 |\\n15\\t| `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` | process | TC-3.4, TC-5.4 |\\n16\\t| `test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts` | (helper) | the scripted sequence both suites drive |\\n17\\t\\n18\\tFixture: Epic 03's tool-heavy fixture reused; extended in place (Story 2) with a mutation-in-flight variant — one edit applied, drain *not* settled, so cleared-pending states are real production states, not hand-written rows (FC-fidelity rule carried from Epic 03 Story 0: states reached through intake → mutate → partial drain, never direct `derived_form` writes).\\n19\\t\\n20\\t## TC → Test Mapping\\n21\\t\\n22\\t| TC | Test (file :: name) | Assertion spine |\\n23\\t|----|--------------------|-----------------|\\n24\\t| TC-1.1 | inspect-overview :: full shape variants | fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted-with-record, compacted, and mid-rebuild all return the full shape with absent pieces as zeros/nulls; compacted fixture exact counts per section vs fixture ground truth |\\n25\\t| TC-1.2 | inspect-overview :: deleted accounting | delete one → visible−1, deleted=1, kind map excludes, tokens drop by its estimate, event count unchanged |\\n26\\t| TC-1.3 | inspect-overview :: purity | two calls, no writes between → deep-equal; read-only delta assert green; zero provider calls |\\n27\\t| TC-2.1 | inspect-view :: arrangement fidelity | entries/forms/degraded/gap reasons/config/provenance equal `describe` output equal stored row (degraded + gap fixture) |\\n28\\t| TC-2.2 | inspect-view :: loadCost parity on boundary-advanced fixture | tail costs short forms short; `total` = estimator over an independent `pull`'s messages |\\n29\\t| TC-2.3 | inspect-view :: never-compacted | `meta: null`, bands `[]`, tail spans record, parity holds |\\n30\\t| TC-3.1 | messages-read :: order, fields, bounds | record order; kind/tokens/turnId present; `from`/`to`/`limit` exact windows; `from > to` → `caller_error` |\\n31\\t| TC-3.2 | messages-read :: show full record + forms | drained tool-result: full content (not shortened), forms with states, outcome metadata present |\\n32\\t| TC-3.3 | messages-read :: deleted handling | default list excludes; `includeDeleted` marks; show on deleted → ok + flag; show on missing id → `message_not_found` |\\n33\\t| TC-3.4 | cli-process-inspect :: list/show parity | spawned `lhc messages list/show` JSON deep-equals in-process SDK results |\\n34\\t| TC-4.1 | inspect-health :: counts + queue consistency | mixed-state fixture: exact counts per owner/kind/state; queue section equals live-item counts from the same reports |\\n35\\t| TC-4.2 | inspect-health :: failure detail + preview | failed: reason/attempts/lastError exact; blocked excluded from preview; preview = failed∧¬blocked set exactly |\\n36\\t| TC-4.3 | inspect-health :: rebuild bracket | edit → health: cascade set pending with queued work visible (exact subjects per cascade contract); `drainSettled` → same set ready; disjoint forms untouched |\\n37\\t| TC-5.1 | lifecycle :: full sequence + checkpoints | every phase ok; post-compact pull = bands+tail; mutate → pending; drain → ready; compact2 reflects edit; receipt sweep section field-equals pre-compact health snapshot |\\n38\\t| TC-5.2 | lifecycle :: replay determinism | fresh thread, same script → hash-equal pull outputs and materialized file |\\n39\\t| TC-5.3 | lifecycle :: teardown continuity | `freshSdk` between phase groups → final pull/health/file identical to TC-5.1 run |\\n40\\t| TC-5.4 | cli-process-inspect :: checkpoint parity | spawned CLI overview/view/list at three checkpoints deep-equal in-process results at same checkpoints |\\n41\\t\\n42\\t## Architecture-Risk Tests\\n43\\t\\n44\\t| Risk | Test | Why it bites |\\n45\\t|------|------|--------------|\\n46\\t| Inspect quietly writes (work rows, boundary nudge, view touch) | **read-only delta assert**: shared helper snapshots observable state (queued work via owners, boundary/zone via status, view identity via describe, event/message counts) before/after *every* new operation; deep-equal after. Runs inside each TC file via wrapper | A single forgotten side effect makes \\\"inspect describes, never changes\\\" fiction; absence-of-delta is checkable, absence-of-write-code is not |\\n47\\t| Zero-provider on all new ops | suite-wide assert extended: overview/view/health/describe/show/list under a throwing provider config → all ok | The no-inference NFR stays structural through the last epic |\\n48\\t| `loadCost` drifts from served reality | TC-2.2's independent-pull leg + lifecycle TC-5.1 checkpoint (report at compact1 vs pull1) | Parity by construction can still break at the estimator seam; two independent measurements pin it |\\n49\\t| Health re-derives instead of composing | health tests assert composition through owner surfaces only: `check-boundaries` forbids cross-domain internal imports, an Epic 04 source check rejects raw SQL references to other domains' tables from `domains/inspect/**`, and the read-only delta assert separately catches writes | The must-not-own rule is the domain's entire contract |\\n50\\t| Lifecycle order bugs only visible cross-epic | TC-5.1's named-phase checkpoints; receipt-vs-health field equality | First sequence ever to run all surfaces in PI-extension order; seam drift between three separately-built epics surfaces here or in production |\\n51\\t\\n52\\t## Suite Accounting\\n53\\t\\n54\\tDefault suite grows ~26 tests across 5 files. Process suite grows TC-3.4 + TC-5.4 (2 spawned scenarios, ~6 assertions); accounting row carried: process suite `ran | not-ran` recorded per verify-all invocation, never silently skipped.\\n55\\t\\n56\\t## Chunk Red/Green Detail\\n57\\t\\n58\\t**Chunk 1 — message reads (S1).** Red: `show` absent from surface (structured not-implemented per house stub rule); list opts ignored — bounds test fails on full-list return. Green: opts → WHERE/LIMIT; show + report join; `cli/messages-read.ts`; TC-3.1–3.3 + read-only legs. ~8 tests.\\n59\\t\\n60\\t**Chunk 2 — inspect domain (S2).** Red: `inspect.*` stubs return not-implemented; fixture lacks mutation-variant (TC-4.3 unwritable → fixture work first). Green: `shared/inspect.ts` shapes; overview composition; health composition; `cli/inspect.ts`; delta-assert helper lands here and wraps Chunk 1's ops retroactively. TC-1.1–1.3, TC-4.1–4.3. ~11 tests.\\n61\\t\\n62\\t**Chunk 3 — view report (S3).** Red: `describe` absent; `inspect.view` stub. Green: `describe` (row → `StoredView`), `view-report.ts` (describe + pull → report), TC-2.1–2.3 + describe null/shape legs. ~6 tests.\\n63\\t\\n64\\t**Chunk 4 — lifecycle (S4).** Red: `lifecycle.ts` helper absent; all four TC files reference it. Green: script with named phases + `freshSdk` hook; TC-5.1–5.3 default; TC-5.4 process. ~7 tests (4 scenarios, multi-checkpoint).\\n65\\t\\n66\\t## Verification\\n67\\t\\n68\\tPer-story: `pnpm verify` (lint, typecheck, default suites). Story 4 and epic close: `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all` — process suite must report `ran`. Red manifests regenerated per chunk per house discipline; no Epic 01–03 test amendments expected (additive surfaces only — list-opts default behavior is unchanged, existing `listMessages` callers see identical results).\\n69\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"92b30fef-4ad7-45bb-a8e9-4c6f66be56bf\",\"uuid\":\"15fefbcf-ffd3-490e-ab5c-95cb2f0d406d\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-12T12:47:40.647Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\",\"content\":\"# Epic 04: Inspection — Test Plan\\n\\n**Epic:** `epic.md` (23 ACs / 17 TCs) · **Tech design:** `tech-design.md`\\nInherits Epic 01–03 test architecture: real temp SQLite per test, deterministic provider for fixture prep only, default suite (`pnpm verify`) + process suite (`LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all`), suite-accounting row, red manifest discipline.\\n\\n## Test Files\\n\\n| File | Suite | Covers |\\n|------|-------|--------|\\n| `test/messages-read.test.ts` | default | TC-3.1–3.3 + list/show read-only legs |\\n| `test/inspect-overview.test.ts` | default | TC-1.1–1.3 |\\n| `test/inspect-view.test.ts` | default | TC-2.1–2.3 + describe legs |\\n| `test/inspect-health.test.ts` | default | TC-4.1–4.3 |\\n| `test/lifecycle.test.ts` | default | TC-5.1–5.3 |\\n| `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` | process | TC-3.4, TC-5.4 |\\n| `test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts` | (helper) | the scripted sequence both suites drive |\\n\\nFixture: Epic 03's tool-heavy fixture reused; extended in place (Story 2) with a mutation-in-flight variant — one edit applied, drain *not* settled, so cleared-pending states are real production states, not hand-written rows (FC-fidelity rule carried from Epic 03 Story 0: states reached through intake → mutate → partial drain, never direct `derived_form` writes).\\n\\n## TC → Test Mapping\\n\\n| TC | Test (file :: name) | Assertion spine |\\n|----|--------------------|-----------------|\\n| TC-1.1 | inspect-overview :: full shape variants | fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted-with-record, compacted, and mid-rebuild all return the full shape with absent pieces as zeros/nulls; compacted fixture exact counts per section vs fixture ground truth |\\n| TC-1.2 | inspect-overview :: deleted accounting | delete one → visible−1, deleted=1, kind map excludes, tokens drop by its estimate, event count unchanged |\\n| TC-1.3 | inspect-overview :: purity | two calls, no writes between → deep-equal; read-only delta assert green; zero provider calls |\\n| TC-2.1 | inspect-view :: arrangement fidelity | entries/forms/degraded/gap reasons/config/provenance equal `describe` output equal stored row (degraded + gap fixture) |\\n| TC-2.2 | inspect-view :: loadCost parity on boundary-advanced fixture | tail costs short forms short; `total` = estimator over an independent `pull`'s messages |\\n| TC-2.3 | inspect-view :: never-compacted | `meta: null`, bands `[]`, tail spans record, parity holds |\\n| TC-3.1 | messages-read :: order, fields, bounds | record order; kind/tokens/turnId present; `from`/`to`/`limit` exact windows; `from > to` → `caller_error` |\\n| TC-3.2 | messages-read :: show full record + forms | drained tool-result: full content (not shortened), forms with states, outcome metadata present |\\n| TC-3.3 | messages-read :: deleted handling | default list excludes; `includeDeleted` marks; show on deleted → ok + flag; show on missing id → `message_not_found` |\\n| TC-3.4 | cli-process-inspect :: list/show parity | spawned `lhc messages list/show` JSON deep-equals in-process SDK results |\\n| TC-4.1 | inspect-health :: counts + queue consistency | mixed-state fixture: exact counts per owner/kind/state; queue section equals live-item counts from the same reports |\\n| TC-4.2 | inspect-health :: failure detail + preview | failed: reason/attempts/lastError exact; blocked excluded from preview; preview = failed∧¬blocked set exactly |\\n| TC-4.3 | inspect-health :: rebuild bracket | edit → health: cascade set pending with queued work visible (exact subjects per cascade contract); `drainSettled` → same set ready; disjoint forms untouched |\\n| TC-5.1 | lifecycle :: full sequence + checkpoints | every phase ok; post-compact pull = bands+tail; mutate → pending; drain → ready; compact2 reflects edit; receipt sweep section field-equals pre-compact health snapshot |\\n| TC-5.2 | lifecycle :: replay determinism | fresh thread, same script → hash-equal pull outputs and materialized file |\\n| TC-5.3 | lifecycle :: teardown continuity | `freshSdk` between phase groups → final pull/health/file identical to TC-5.1 run |\\n| TC-5.4 | cli-process-inspect :: checkpoint parity | spawned CLI overview/view/list at three checkpoints deep-equal in-process results at same checkpoints |\\n\\n## Architecture-Risk Tests\\n\\n| Risk | Test | Why it bites |\\n|------|------|--------------|\\n| Inspect quietly writes (work rows, boundary nudge, view touch) | **read-only delta assert**: shared helper snapshots observable state (queued work via owners, boundary/zone via status, view identity via describe, event/message counts) before/after *every* new operation; deep-equal after. Runs inside each TC file via wrapper | A single forgotten side effect makes \\\"inspect describes, never changes\\\" fiction; absence-of-delta is checkable, absence-of-write-code is not |\\n| Zero-provider on all new ops | suite-wide assert extended: overview/view/health/describe/show/list under a throwing provider config → all ok | The no-inference NFR stays structural through the last epic |\\n| `loadCost` drifts from served reality | TC-2.2's independent-pull leg + lifecycle TC-5.1 checkpoint (report at compact1 vs pull1) | Parity by construction can still break at the estimator seam; two independent measurements pin it |\\n| Health re-derives instead of composing | health tests assert composition through owner surfaces only: `check-boundaries` forbids cross-domain internal imports, an Epic 04 source check rejects raw SQL references to other domains' tables from `domains/inspect/**`, and the read-only delta assert separately catches writes | The must-not-own rule is the domain's entire contract |\\n| Lifecycle order bugs only visible cross-epic | TC-5.1's named-phase checkpoints; receipt-vs-health field equality | First sequence ever to run all surfaces in PI-extension order; seam drift between three separately-built epics surfaces here or in production |\\n\\n## Suite Accounting\\n\\nDefault suite grows ~26 tests across 5 files. Process suite grows TC-3.4 + TC-5.4 (2 spawned scenarios, ~6 assertions); accounting row carried: process suite `ran | not-ran` recorded per verify-all invocation, never silently skipped.\\n\\n## Chunk Red/Green Detail\\n\\n**Chunk 1 — message reads (S1).** Red: `show` absent from surface (structured not-implemented per house stub rule); list opts ignored — bounds test fails on full-list return. Green: opts → WHERE/LIMIT; show + report join; `cli/messages-read.ts`; TC-3.1–3.3 + read-only legs. ~8 tests.\\n\\n**Chunk 2 — inspect domain (S2).** Red: `inspect.*` stubs return not-implemented; fixture lacks mutation-variant (TC-4.3 unwritable → fixture work first). Green: `shared/inspect.ts` shapes; overview composition; health composition; `cli/inspect.ts`; delta-assert helper lands here and wraps Chunk 1's ops retroactively. TC-1.1–1.3, TC-4.1–4.3. ~11 tests.\\n\\n**Chunk 3 — view report (S3).** Red: `describe` absent; `inspect.view` stub. Green: `describe` (row → `StoredView`), `view-report.ts` (describe + pull → report), TC-2.1–2.3 + describe null/shape legs. ~6 tests.\\n\\n**Chunk 4 — lifecycle (S4).** Red: `lifecycle.ts` helper absent; all four TC files reference it. Green: script with named phases + `freshSdk` hook; TC-5.1–5.3 default; TC-5.4 process. ~7 tests (4 scenarios, multi-checkpoint).\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nPer-story: `pnpm verify` (lint, typecheck, default suites). Story 4 and epic close: `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all` — process suite must report `ran`. Red manifests regenerated per chunk per house discipline; no Epic 01–03 test amendments expected (additive surfaces only — list-opts default behavior is unchanged, existing `listMessages` callers see identical results).\\n\",\"numLines\":69,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":69}}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:74:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01E6j7toYJUbmmfbnmnPjE1u\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\timport { existsSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\n2\\timport { runInTransaction, type OperationContext } from \\\"../../shared/context.js\\\";\\n3\\timport type { FormKind, FormReportEntry, WorkHandler } from \\\"../../shared/derivation.js\\\";\\n4\\timport { storageFailure, type ErrorResult, type OpResult } from \\\"../../shared/errors.js\\\";\\n5\\timport {\\n6\\t  enqueue,\\n7\\t  hasLiveItem,\\n8\\t  listItems,\\n9\\t  type WorkItemRecord,\\n10\\t  type WorkKind,\\n11\\t} from \\\"../../tech-utils/work-queue/index.js\\\";\\n12\\timport type { EventKind, EventRecord } from \\\"../intake-stream/index.js\\\";\\n13\\timport {\\n14\\t  openThreadDatabase,\\n15\\t  resolveThreadRef,\\n16\\t  type ThreadRef,\\n17\\t} from \\\"../threads/index.js\\\";\\n18\\timport type { DerivedForm } from \\\"../../shared/derivation.js\\\";\\n19\\timport {\\n20\\t  findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary,\\n21\\t  readMessageFormRow,\\n22\\t  readMessageForms,\\n23\\t  reportMessageForms,\\n24\\t} from \\\"./internal/forms.js\\\";\\n25\\timport { messageWorkHandlers } from \\\"./internal/handlers.js\\\";\\n26\\timport { projectEvent } from \\\"./internal/project.js\\\";\\n27\\timport {\\n28\\t  cascadeFromMessage,\\n29\\t  cascadeMessageDelete,\\n30\\t  cascadeTurnDelete,\\n31\\t  type CascadeClear,\\n32\\t  type CascadeOutcome,\\n33\\t} from \\\"./internal/cascade.js\\\";\\n34\\timport {\\n35\\t  applyMessageEdit,\\n36\\t  insertMessage,\\n37\\t  markMessageDeleted,\\n38\\t  markTurnMessagesDeleted,\\n39\\t  readMessages,\\n40\\t  readMutableMessage,\\n41\\t} from \\\"./internal/store.js\\\";\\n42\\t\\n43\\texport type BlockType = \\\"text\\\" | \\\"tool_call\\\" | \\\"tool_result\\\";\\n44\\t\\n45\\texport interface Block {\\n46\\t  blockType: BlockType;\\n47\\t  content: Record<string, unknown>; // per-kind shape as projected, verbatim source content\\n48\\t}\\n49\\t\\n50\\texport interface MessageRecord {\\n51\\t  messageId: string;\\n52\\t  sourceEventOrder: number;\\n53\\t  kind: Exclude<EventKind, \\\"turn_end\\\">;\\n54\\t  blocks: Block[];\\n55\\t  tokenEstimate: number;\\n56\\t  actor: string;\\n57\\t  harness: string;\\n58\\t  turnId?: string;\\n59\\t  // The message's derived forms as stored (Epic 02 Story 2): present only\\n60\\t  // for messages that are derivation sources — kinds with no derivable form\\n61\\t  // carry no rows and no key (AC-2.7). Stored state returned verbatim,\\n62\\t  // never re-derived on read.\\n63\\t  forms?: DerivedForm[];\\n64\\t}\\n65\\t\\n66\\t// The event as the walk holds it after recording: the validated input plus\\n67\\t// its server-stamped order and timestamp.\\n68\\texport type RecordedEvent = EventRecord;\\n69\\t\\n70\\texport type MessageCreated = {\\n71\\t  messageId: string;\\n72\\t  kind: Exclude<EventKind, \\\"turn_end\\\">;\\n73\\t  // Carried for tool activity only: the pairing key the queue sites need —\\n74\\t  // tool_result projection runs the AC-2.8 late-result lookup against it.\\n75\\t  toolCallId?: string;\\n76\\t} | null;\\n77\\t\\n78\\t// Cross-domain surface, called by intake-stream inside the batch transaction\\n79\\t// (the first such call through the operation context; turns.applyEvent\\n80\\t// follows the pattern in Story 4). Synchronous and throwing by design: a\\n81\\t// projection failure propagates to the pipeline's catch and rejects the\\n82\\t// whole batch — recorded events without messages is the stranded state the\\n83\\t// transaction exists to prevent. Returns null for turn_end (no message).\\n84\\t// turnId is the membership stamp, settled by the pipeline before this call:\\n85\\t// the turn open *after* this event's transition (so a prompt belongs to the\\n86\\t// turn it just opened), or null in a gap — written once, never updated.\\n87\\texport function createFromEvent(\\n88\\t  ctx: OperationContext,\\n89\\t  event: RecordedEvent,\\n90\\t  turnId: string | null,\\n91\\t): MessageCreated {\\n92\\t  const projected = projectEvent(event);\\n93\\t  if (projected === null) return null;\\n94\\t  const kind = event.eventKind as Exclude<EventKind, \\\"turn_end\\\">;\\n95\\t  const messageId = `m${event.eventOrder}`;\\n96\\t  insertMessage(ctx.db, {\\n97\\t    messageId,\\n98\\t    sourceEventOrder: event.eventOrder,\\n99\\t    kind,\\n100\\t    tokenEstimate: projected.tokenEstimate,\\n101\\t    actor: event.actor,\\n102\\t    harness: event.harness,\\n103\\t    turnId,\\n104\\t    blocks: projected.blocks,\\n105\\t  });\\n106\\t  if (event.eventKind === \\\"tool_call\\\" || event.eventKind === \\\"tool_result\\\") {\\n107\\t    return { messageId, kind, toolCallId: event.payload.toolCallId };\\n108\\t  }\\n109\\t  return { messageId, kind };\\n110\\t}\\n111\\t\\n112\\t// The kind gate, exact by design: a prompt queues prompt_smoothing, a tool\\n113\\t// call queues tool_call_summary (Epic 02 Story 2's additive extension), a\\n114\\t// tool result queues tool_result_summary, nothing else queues anything —\\n115\\t// text, thinking, and note messages are not derivation sources (Epic 01\\n116\\t// AC-2.8/TC-2.9; Epic 02 AC-2.2/AC-2.7). Cross-domain surface, called by\\n117\\t// intake-stream inside the batch transaction for every recorded message, so\\n118\\t// the item commits (or rolls back) with the batch.\\n119\\tconst MESSAGE_WORK_KINDS: Partial<Record<EventKind, WorkKind>> = {\\n120\\t  user_prompt: \\\"prompt_smoothing\\\",\\n121\\t  tool_call: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n122\\t  tool_result: \\\"tool_result_summary\\\",\\n123\\t};\\n124\\t\\n125\\t// Which derived form each message-owned kind produces — the owning domain's\\n126\\t// knowledge, handed to the meaning-blind enqueue so the form's pending row\\n127\\t// rides the same transaction (DD-5).\\n128\\tconst MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS: Partial<Record<WorkKind, FormKind>> = {\\n129\\t  prompt_smoothing: \\\"smoothed_prompt\\\",\\n130\\t  tool_call_summary: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n131\\t  tool_result_summary: \\\"tool_result_summary\\\",\\n132\\t};\\n133\\t\\n134\\t// Message-owned work handlers, merged into the SDK's dispatch map at\\n135\\t// construction (DD-6): prompt smoothing and the two tool-activity summaries.\\n136\\texport const workHandlers: Readonly<Partial<Record<WorkKind, WorkHandler>>> =\\n137\\t  messageWorkHandlers;\\n138\\t\\n139\\texport function queueMessageWork(\\n140\\t  ctx: OperationContext,\\n141\\t  message: MessageCreated,\\n142\\t): WorkItemRecord[] {\\n143\\t  if (message === null) return [];\\n144\\t  const items: WorkItemRecord[] = [];\\n145\\t  const kind = MESSAGE_WORK_KINDS[message.kind];\\n146\\t  if (kind !== undefined) {\\n147\\t    const form = MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS[kind];\\n148\\t    if (form === undefined) {\\n149\\t      // Every queuing kind names its form above; a miss is a wiring bug.\\n150\\t      throw new Error(`no derived form mapped for message work kind ${kind}`);\\n151\\t    }\\n152\\t    items.push(\\n153\\t      enqueue(ctx, {\\n154\\t        owner: \\\"messages\\\",\\n155\\t        kind,\\n156\\t        sourceRef: { messageId: message.messageId },\\n157\\t        forms: [{ subjectKind: \\\"message\\\", subjectId: message.messageId, form }],\\n158\\t      }),\\n159\\t    );\\n160\\t  }\\n161\\t  // Late-result repair (AC-2.8): a tool result landing after its call's\\n162\\t  // summary already derived with outcome \\\"unknown\\\" means the summary's\\n163\\t  // source — the call+result pair — completed underneath it; clear and\\n164\\t  // regenerate at the next source version, in this same batch transaction.\\n165\\t  // One indexed lookup; pending summaries (metadata NULL) never match, so\\n166\\t  // the common call-and-result-in-one-batch case never triggers, and the\\n167\\t  // version-scoped item id keeps the requeue idempotent.\\n168\\t  if (message.kind === \\\"tool_result\\\" && message.toolCallId !== undefined) {\\n169\\t    const stale = findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary(ctx.db, message.toolCallId);\\n170\\t    if (stale !== undefined) {\\n171\\t      items.push(\\n172\\t        enqueue(ctx, {\\n173\\t          owner: \\\"messages\\\",\\n174\\t          kind: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n175\\t          sourceRef: { messageId: stale.messageId },\\n176\\t          sourceVersion: stale.sourceVersion + 1,\\n177\\t          forms: [\\n178\\t            {\\n179\\t              subjectKind: \\\"message\\\",\\n180\\t              subjectId: stale.messageId,\\n181\\t              form: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n182\\t            },\\n183\\t          ],\\n184\\t        }),\\n185\\t      );\\n186\\t    }\\n187\\t  }\\n188\\t  return items;\\n189\\t}\\n190\\t\\n191\\tfunction threadNotFound(filePath: string): { ok: false; error: ErrorResult } {\\n192\\t  return {\\n193\\t    ok: false,\\n194\\t    error: {\\n195\\t      errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n196\\t      code: \\\"thread_not_found\\\",\\n197\\t      reason: `no thread file exists at ${filePath}`,\\n198\\t    },\\n199\\t  };\\n200\\t}\\n201\\t\\n202\\texport async function listMessages(\\n203\\t  thread: ThreadRef,\\n204\\t): Promise<OpResult<MessageRecord[]>> {\\n205\\t  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n206\\t  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n207\\t  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n208\\t  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n209\\t\\n210\\t  // openThreadDatabase verifies the file is a real thread file and migrates\\n211\\t  // a pre-Story-3 one before the read, so a thread recorded under an earlier\\n212\\t  // story lists cleanly (F-03-001) and a non-thread file is rejected\\n213\\t  // unmutated (F-03-002).\\n214\\t  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n215\\t  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n216\\t  const db = opened.value;\\n217\\t  try {\\n218\\t    // Form read-back rides the message read (AC-2.1): each record carries\\n219\\t    // its stored derived forms, attached from one grouped query — the\\n220\\t    // production path for \\\"readable alongside the message\\\".\\n221\\t    const formsByMessage = readMessageForms(db);\\n222\\t    const records = readMessages(db).map((record) => {\\n223\\t      const forms = formsByMessage.get(record.messageId);\\n224\\t      return forms === undefined ? record : { ...record, forms };\\n225\\t    });\\n226\\t    return { ok: true, value: records };\\n227\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n228\\t    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n229\\t    return storageFailure(`message read-back failed: ${reason}`);\\n230\\t  } finally {\\n231\\t    db.close();\\n232\\t  }\\n233\\t}\\n234\\t\\n235\\texport async function listQueuedWork(\\n236\\t  thread: ThreadRef,\\n237\\t): Promise<OpResult<WorkItemRecord[]>> {\\n238\\t  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n239\\t  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n240\\t  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n241\\t  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n242\\t\\n243\\t  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n244\\t  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n245\\t  const db = opened.value;\\n246\\t  try {\\n247\\t    return { ok: true, value: listItems(db, \\\"messages\\\") };\\n248\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n249\\t    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n250\\t    return storageFailure(`queued-work read-back failed: ${reason}`);\\n251\\t  } finally {\\n252\\t    db.close();\\n253\\t  }\\n254\\t}\\n255\\t\\n256\\t// ── report and repair (Epic 02 Story 4, Flow 4) ──────────────────\\n257\\t\\n258\\t// This owner's repair report: every message-owned form's durable state\\n259\\t// joined with live queue detail in one query — the five operational\\n260\\t// situations (waiting, retrying, ready, failed, blocked) read from the rows\\n261\\t// without any queue API. Needs no provider; reads degrade, never block.\\n262\\texport async function report(\\n263\\t  thread: ThreadRef,\\n264\\t  opts?: { notReady?: boolean; messageId?: string },\\n265\\t): Promise<OpResult<FormReportEntry[]>> {\\n266\\t  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n267\\t  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n268\\t  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n269\\t  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n270\\t\\n271\\t  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n272\\t  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n273\\t  const db = opened.value;\\n274\\t  try {\\n275\\t    return { ok: true, value: reportMessageForms(db, opts ?? {}) };\\n276\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n277\\t    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n278\\t    return storageFailure(`report read failed: ${reason}`);\\n279\\t  } finally {\\n280\\t    db.close();\\n281\\t  }\\n282\\t}\\n283\\t\\n284\\texport type RequeueOutcome = { workItemId: string } | { noop: \\\"already_queued\\\" };\\n285\\t\\n286\\t// Which work kind rebuilds each message-owned form — MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS\\n287\\t// inverted; the requeue's join from the named form back to its queue site.\\n288\\tconst MESSAGE_FORM_KINDS: Partial<Record<FormKind, WorkKind>> = {\\n289\\t  smoothed_prompt: \\\"prompt_smoothing\\\",\\n290\\t  tool_call_summary: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n291\\t  tool_result_summary: \\\"tool_result_summary\\\",\\n292\\t};\\n293\\t\\n294\\t// Explicit re-queue through the owning surface (AC-4.4): the public,\\n295\\t// supported rebuild act. Refused for blocked forms with the form's stored\\n296\\t// damage reason (AC-4.6) and for missing rows; a no-op against work already\\n297\\t// queued or in flight at the form's current source version (AC-4.5).\\n298\\t// Otherwise the form clears to pending and re-enqueues at the next source\\n299\\t// version — the same enqueue path intake uses, poke-on-commit included, so\\n300\\t// background mode processes the repair with no further call. The no-op check\\n301\\t// and the enqueue commit in one transaction (anti-shim: a split would\\n302\\t// reintroduce the duplicate-work race).\\n303\\texport async function requeue(\\n304\\t  thread: ThreadRef,\\n305\\t  target: { messageId: string; form: FormKind },\\n306\\t): Promise<OpResult<RequeueOutcome>> {\\n307\\t  const kind = MESSAGE_FORM_KINDS[target.form];\\n308\\t  if (kind === undefined) {\\n309\\t    return {\\n310\\t      ok: false,\\n311\\t      error: {\\n312\\t        errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n313\\t        code: \\\"message_not_found\\\",\\n314\\t        reason: `form ${target.form} is not message-owned; messages.requeue repairs smoothed_prompt, tool_call_summary, tool_result_summary`,\\n315\\t      },\\n316\\t    };\\n317\\t  }\\n318\\t  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n319\\t  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n320\\t  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n321\\t  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n322\\t\\n323\\t  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n324\\t  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n325\\t  const db = opened.value;\\n326\\t  try {\\n327\\t    const meta = db\\n328\\t      .prepare(`SELECT thread_id FROM thread_metadata WHERE id = 1`)\\n329\\t      .get() as { thread_id: string } | undefined;\\n330\\t    const threadId = meta?.thread_id ?? \\\"\\\";\\n331\\t    return runInTransaction(db, () => new Date(), threadId, (ctx): OpResult<RequeueOutcome> => {\\n332\\t      const row = readMessageFormRow(ctx.db, target.messageId, target.form);\\n333\\t      if (row === undefined) {\\n334\\t        return {\\n335\\t          ok: false,\\n336\\t          error: {\\n337\\t            errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n338\\t            code: \\\"message_not_found\\\",\\n339\\t            reason: `no derived form ${target.form} exists for message ${target.messageId}`,\\n340\\t          },\\n341\\t        };\\n342\\t      }\\n343\\t      if (row.state === \\\"blocked\\\") {\\n344\\t        // The refusal carries the form's stored reason — the damage named at\\n345\\t        // blocking time, not a generic string (AC-4.6).\\n346\\t        return {\\n347\\t          ok: false,\\n348\\t          error: {\\n349\\t            errorClass: \\\"state_corruption\\\",\\n350\\t            code: \\\"source_damaged\\\",\\n351\\t            reason: row.reason ?? `form ${target.form} for message ${target.messageId} is blocked`,\\n352\\t          },\\n353\\t        };\\n354\\t      }\\n355\\t      const sourceRef = { messageId: target.messageId };\\n356\\t      if (hasLiveItem(ctx.db, kind, sourceRef, row.sourceVersion)) {\\n357\\t        return { ok: true, value: { noop: \\\"already_queued\\\" } };\\n358\\t      }\\n359\\t      const item = enqueue(ctx, {\\n360\\t        owner: \\\"messages\\\",\\n361\\t        kind,\\n362\\t        sourceRef,\\n363\\t        sourceVersion: row.sourceVersion + 1,\\n364\\t        forms: [{ subjectKind: \\\"message\\\", subjectId: target.messageId, form: target.form }],\\n365\\t      });\\n366\\t      return { ok: true, value: { workItemId: item.workItemId } };\\n367\\t    });\\n368\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n369\\t    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n370\\t    return storageFailure(`requeue failed: ${reason}`);\\n371\\t  } finally {\\n372\\t    db.close();\\n373\\t  }\\n374\\t}\\n375\\t\\n376\\t// ── mutations (Epic 02 Story 5, Flow 5) ──────────────────────────\\n377\\t\\n378\\t// The mutation result contract (tech design §Interfaces): what changed in\\n379\\t// the record, which dependent forms cleared, which dropped (delete only),\\n380\\t// what replacement work queued, and which still-queued old items the cascade\\n381\\t// tidied away (issue 1). Shared by edit and the Story 6 deletes.\\n382\\texport interface MutationResult {\\n383\\t  changed: { messageIds: string[]; turnIds: string[] };\\n384\\t  cleared: CascadeClear[];\\n385\\t  dropped: CascadeClear[];\\n386\\t  queued: Array<{ workItemId: string; kind: WorkKind }>;\\n387\\t  superseded: string[];\\n388\\t}\\n389\\t\\n390\\t// The record's first sanctioned mutation (AC-5.1–5.5): change a closed-turn\\n391\\t// message's content and blocks, re-stamp the token estimate, and walk the\\n392\\t// full dependent chain — clear to pending, supersede queued old work,\\n393\\t// enqueue replacements at the next source version — in one transaction.\\n394\\t// Synchronous and local by contract: everything above commits before this\\n395\\t// returns; the re-queued rebuilds run through the normal drain (background\\n396\\t// mode needs no further call — the enqueue pokes ride the commit). Events\\n397\\t// are never touched (projection-level mutation, DD-12), and no generated\\n398\\t// thread-view is either — visibility arrives at the next compact/rebuild.\\n399\\t// Refusals read through the deleted-filtered view and enforce the closed-turn\\n400\\t// target boundary: only a message in a closed turn is editable, so an\\n401\\t// open-turn *or* a turnless (no-membership) gap target is refused turn_open —\\n402\\t// the boundary's one stable code — a missing or deleted message is\\n403\\t// message_not_found, and a refusal changes nothing.\\n404\\texport async function edit(\\n405\\t  thread: ThreadRef,\\n406\\t  input: { messageId: string; content: string },\\n407\\t): Promise<OpResult<MutationResult>> {\\n408\\t  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n409\\t  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n410\\t  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n411\\t  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n412\\t\\n413\\t  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n414\\t  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n415\\t  const db = opened.value;\\n416\\t  try {\\n417\\t    const meta = db\\n418\\t      .prepare(`SELECT thread_id FROM thread_metadata WHERE id = 1`)\\n419\\t      .get() as { thread_id: string } | undefined;\\n420\\t    const threadId = meta?.thread_id ?? \\\"\\\";\\n421\\t    return runInTransaction(db, () => new Date(), threadId, (ctx): OpResult<MutationResult> => {\\n422\\t      const target = readMutableMessage(ctx.db, input.messageId);\\n423\\t      if (target === undefined) {\\n424\\t        return {\\n425\\t          ok: false,\\n426\\t          error: {\\n427\\t            errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n428\\t            code: \\\"message_not_found\\\",\\n429\\t            reason: `no message ${input.messageId} exists in this thread`,\\n430\\t          },\\n431\\t        };\\n432\\t      }\\n433\\t      // The closed-turn target boundary (story scope; AC-5.1): the edit's\\n434\\t      // editable class is a message in a *closed* turn. Both failing cases —\\n435\\t      // an open turn and a turnless gap message (no membership) — refuse under\\n436\\t      // the one stable code; the reason distinguishes them so the open-turn\\n437\\t      // message reads exactly as before. A deleted/missing target never gets\\n438\\t      // here (it misses the filtered read above as message_not_found).\\n439\\t      if (target.turnStatus !== \\\"closed\\\") {\\n440\\t        return {\\n441\\t          ok: false,\\n442\\t          error: {\\n443\\t            errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n444\\t            code: \\\"turn_open\\\",\\n445\\t            reason:\\n446\\t              target.turnStatus === \\\"open\\\"\\n447\\t                ? `message ${input.messageId} belongs to open turn ${target.turnId ?? \\\"\\\"}; open-turn messages cannot be edited (v1 boundary)`\\n448\\t                : `message ${input.messageId} has no turn membership; only closed-turn messages can be edited (v1 boundary)`,\\n449\\t          },\\n450\\t        };\\n451\\t      }\\n452\\t      applyMessageEdit(ctx.db, input.messageId, input.content);\\n453\\t      const cascade = cascadeFromMessage(ctx, input.messageId);\\n454\\t      return {\\n455\\t        ok: true,\\n456\\t        value: {\\n457\\t          changed: { messageIds: [input.messageId], turnIds: [] },\\n458\\t          cleared: cascade.cleared,\\n459\\t          dropped: cascade.dropped,\\n460\\t          queued: cascade.queued,\\n461\\t          superseded: cascade.superseded,\\n462\\t        },\\n463\\t      };\\n464\\t    });\\n465\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n466\\t    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n467\\t    return storageFailure(`edit failed: ${reason}`);\\n468\\t  } finally {\\n469\\t    db.close();\\n470\\t  }\\n471\\t}\\n472\\t\\n473\\t// ── delete (Epic 02 Story 6, Flow 6) ─────────────────────────────\\n474\\t\\n475\\t// The record's removal mutation for one message (AC-6.1–6.3, 6.7):\\n476\\t// projection-level delete — the deleted_at stamp plus the delete cascade\\n477\\t// (own forms dropped, turn and chunk cleared and re-queued for minus-one\\n478\\t// composition) in one transaction. The source events are never touched;\\n479\\t// event read-back keeps returning them (the audit surface). Validation\\n480\\t// reads the same filtered view as edit, so a missing, deleted, or\\n481\\t// double-deleted target is message_not_found and an open-turn or turnless\\n482\\t// gap target is turn_open. The one delete-specific refusal is prompt\\n483\\t// protection: a turn is a prompt and what came back for it, so deleting the\\n484\\t// turn's initiating prompt is refused toward turns.deleteTurn — the error\\n485\\t// names the turn and that path (AC-6.3).\\n486\\texport async function deleteMessage(\\n487\\t  thread: ThreadRef,\\n488\\t  input: { messageId: string },\\n489\\t): Promise<OpResult<MutationResult>> {\\n490\\t  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n491\\t  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n492\\t  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n493\\t  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n494\\t\\n495\\t  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n496\\t  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n497\\t  const db = opened.value;\\n498\\t  try {\\n499\\t    const meta = db\\n500\\t      .prepare(`SELECT thread_id FROM thread_metadata WHERE id = 1`)\\n501\\t      .get() as { thread_id: string } | undefined;\\n502\\t    const threadId = meta?.thread_id ?? \\\"\\\";\\n503\\t    return runInTransaction(db, () => new Date(), threadId, (ctx): OpResult<MutationResult> => {\\n504\\t      const target = readMutableMessage(ctx.db, input.messageId);\\n505\\t      if (target === undefined) {\\n506\\t        return {\\n507\\t          ok: false,\\n508\\t          error: {\\n509\\t            errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n510\\t            code: \\\"message_not_found\\\",\\n511\\t            reason: `no message ${input.messageId} exists in this thread`,\\n512\\t          },\\n513\\t        };\\n514\\t      }\\n515\\t      if (target.turnStatus !== \\\"closed\\\") {\\n516\\t        return {\\n517\\t          ok: false,\\n518\\t          error: {\\n519\\t            errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n520\\t            code: \\\"turn_open\\\",\\n521\\t            reason:\\n522\\t              target.turnStatus === \\\"open\\\"\\n523\\t                ? `message ${input.messageId} belongs to open turn ${target.turnId ?? \\\"\\\"}; open-turn messages cannot be deleted (v1 boundary)`\\n524\\t                : `message ${input.messageId} has no turn membership; only closed-turn messages can be deleted (v1 boundary)`,\\n525\\t          },\\n526\\t        };\\n527\\t      }\\n528\\t      if (target.initiatesTurn) {\\n529\\t        return {\\n530\\t          ok: false,\\n531\\t          error: {\\n532\\t            errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n533\\t            code: \\\"message_initiates_turn\\\",\\n534\\t            reason: `message ${input.messageId} is the prompt that initiates turn ${target.turnId ?? \\\"\\\"}; a turn is a prompt and what came back for it — delete the whole exchange with turns.deleteTurn (lhc turns delete --turn-id ${target.turnId ?? \\\"\\\"})`,\\n535\\t          },\\n536\\t        };\\n537\\t      }\\n538\\t      markMessageDeleted(ctx.db, input.messageId, ctx.clock().toISOString());\\n539\\t      const cascade = cascadeMessageDelete(ctx, input.messageId);\\n540\\t      return {\\n541\\t        ok: true,\\n542\\t        value: {\\n543\\t          changed: { messageIds: [input.messageId], turnIds: [] },\\n544\\t          cleared: cascade.cleared,\\n545\\t          dropped: cascade.dropped,\\n546\\t          queued: cascade.queued,\\n547\\t          superseded: cascade.superseded,\\n548\\t        },\\n549\\t      };\\n550\\t    });\\n551\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n552\\t    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n553\\t    return storageFailure(`delete failed: ${reason}`);\\n554\\t  } finally {\\n555\\t    db.close();\\n556\\t  }\\n557\\t}\\n558\\t\\n559\\t// Cross-domain surface for turns.deleteTurn (DD-8: one cascade module, two\\n560\\t// callers), called inside the turn delete's transaction after the turn row\\n561\\t// is stamped. The messages domain owns the message-table write — the member\\n562\\t// stamp, scoped to live rows — and the shared cascade entry; the turns\\n563\\t// operation owns its own validation and turn-row stamp. Returns the cascade\\n564\\t// outcome plus the member ids stamped now (record order), which the turn\\n565\\t// delete reports as its changed messages.\\n566\\texport function applyTurnDeleteCascade(\\n567\\t  ctx: OperationContext,\\n568\\t  turnId: string,\\n569\\t): CascadeOutcome & { memberMessageIds: string[] } {\\n570\\t  const memberMessageIds = markTurnMessagesDeleted(\\n571\\t    ctx.db,\\n572\\t    turnId,\\n573\\t    ctx.clock().toISOString(),\\n574\\t  );\\n575\\t  return { ...cascadeTurnDelete(ctx, turnId, memberMessageIds), memberMessageIds };\\n576\\t}\\n577\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"92b30fef-4ad7-45bb-a8e9-4c6f66be56bf\",\"uuid\":\"ec9679cf-b502-47cc-9d54-98c9f1f63c07\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-12T12:47:53.583Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts\",\"content\":\"import { existsSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\nimport { runInTransaction, type OperationContext } from \\\"../../shared/context.js\\\";\\nimport type { FormKind, FormReportEntry, WorkHandler } from \\\"../../shared/derivation.js\\\";\\nimport { storageFailure, type ErrorResult, type OpResult } from \\\"../../shared/errors.js\\\";\\nimport {\\n  enqueue,\\n  hasLiveItem,\\n  listItems,\\n  type WorkItemRecord,\\n  type WorkKind,\\n} from \\\"../../tech-utils/work-queue/index.js\\\";\\nimport type { EventKind, EventRecord } from \\\"../intake-stream/index.js\\\";\\nimport {\\n  openThreadDatabase,\\n  resolveThreadRef,\\n  type ThreadRef,\\n} from \\\"../threads/index.js\\\";\\nimport type { DerivedForm } from \\\"../../shared/derivation.js\\\";\\nimport {\\n  findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary,\\n  readMessageFormRow,\\n  readMessageForms,\\n  reportMessageForms,\\n} from \\\"./internal/forms.js\\\";\\nimport { messageWorkHandlers } from \\\"./internal/handlers.js\\\";\\nimport { projectEvent } from \\\"./internal/project.js\\\";\\nimport {\\n  cascadeFromMessage,\\n  cascadeMessageDelete,\\n  cascadeTurnDelete,\\n  type CascadeClear,\\n  type CascadeOutcome,\\n} from \\\"./internal/cascade.js\\\";\\nimport {\\n  applyMessageEdit,\\n  insertMessage,\\n  markMessageDeleted,\\n  markTurnMessagesDeleted,\\n  readMessages,\\n  readMutableMessage,\\n} from \\\"./internal/store.js\\\";\\n\\nexport type BlockType = \\\"text\\\" | \\\"tool_call\\\" | \\\"tool_result\\\";\\n\\nexport interface Block {\\n  blockType: BlockType;\\n  content: Record<string, unknown>; // per-kind shape as projected, verbatim source content\\n}\\n\\nexport interface MessageRecord {\\n  messageId: string;\\n  sourceEventOrder: number;\\n  kind: Exclude<EventKind, \\\"turn_end\\\">;\\n  blocks: Block[];\\n  tokenEstimate: number;\\n  actor: string;\\n  harness: string;\\n  turnId?: string;\\n  // The message's derived forms as stored (Epic 02 Story 2): present only\\n  // for messages that are derivation sources — kinds with no derivable form\\n  // carry no rows and no key (AC-2.7). Stored state returned verbatim,\\n  // never re-derived on read.\\n  forms?: DerivedForm[];\\n}\\n\\n// The event as the walk holds it after recording: the validated input plus\\n// its server-stamped order and timestamp.\\nexport type RecordedEvent = EventRecord;\\n\\nexport type MessageCreated = {\\n  messageId: string;\\n  kind: Exclude<EventKind, \\\"turn_end\\\">;\\n  // Carried for tool activity only: the pairing key the queue sites need —\\n  // tool_result projection runs the AC-2.8 late-result lookup against it.\\n  toolCallId?: string;\\n} | null;\\n\\n// Cross-domain surface, called by intake-stream inside the batch transaction\\n// (the first such call through the operation context; turns.applyEvent\\n// follows the pattern in Story 4). Synchronous and throwing by design: a\\n// projection failure propagates to the pipeline's catch and rejects the\\n// whole batch — recorded events without messages is the stranded state the\\n// transaction exists to prevent. Returns null for turn_end (no message).\\n// turnId is the membership stamp, settled by the pipeline before this call:\\n// the turn open *after* this event's transition (so a prompt belongs to the\\n// turn it just opened), or null in a gap — written once, never updated.\\nexport function createFromEvent(\\n  ctx: OperationContext,\\n  event: RecordedEvent,\\n  turnId: string | null,\\n): MessageCreated {\\n  const projected = projectEvent(event);\\n  if (projected === null) return null;\\n  const kind = event.eventKind as Exclude<EventKind, \\\"turn_end\\\">;\\n  const messageId = `m${event.eventOrder}`;\\n  insertMessage(ctx.db, {\\n    messageId,\\n    sourceEventOrder: event.eventOrder,\\n    kind,\\n    tokenEstimate: projected.tokenEstimate,\\n    actor: event.actor,\\n    harness: event.harness,\\n    turnId,\\n    blocks: projected.blocks,\\n  });\\n  if (event.eventKind === \\\"tool_call\\\" || event.eventKind === \\\"tool_result\\\") {\\n    return { messageId, kind, toolCallId: event.payload.toolCallId };\\n  }\\n  return { messageId, kind };\\n}\\n\\n// The kind gate, exact by design: a prompt queues prompt_smoothing, a tool\\n// call queues tool_call_summary (Epic 02 Story 2's additive extension), a\\n// tool result queues tool_result_summary, nothing else queues anything —\\n// text, thinking, and note messages are not derivation sources (Epic 01\\n// AC-2.8/TC-2.9; Epic 02 AC-2.2/AC-2.7). Cross-domain surface, called by\\n// intake-stream inside the batch transaction for every recorded message, so\\n// the item commits (or rolls back) with the batch.\\nconst MESSAGE_WORK_KINDS: Partial<Record<EventKind, WorkKind>> = {\\n  user_prompt: \\\"prompt_smoothing\\\",\\n  tool_call: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n  tool_result: \\\"tool_result_summary\\\",\\n};\\n\\n// Which derived form each message-owned kind produces — the owning domain's\\n// knowledge, handed to the meaning-blind enqueue so the form's pending row\\n// rides the same transaction (DD-5).\\nconst MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS: Partial<Record<WorkKind, FormKind>> = {\\n  prompt_smoothing: \\\"smoothed_prompt\\\",\\n  tool_call_summary: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n  tool_result_summary: \\\"tool_result_summary\\\",\\n};\\n\\n// Message-owned work handlers, merged into the SDK's dispatch map at\\n// construction (DD-6): prompt smoothing and the two tool-activity summaries.\\nexport const workHandlers: Readonly<Partial<Record<WorkKind, WorkHandler>>> =\\n  messageWorkHandlers;\\n\\nexport function queueMessageWork(\\n  ctx: OperationContext,\\n  message: MessageCreated,\\n): WorkItemRecord[] {\\n  if (message === null) return [];\\n  const items: WorkItemRecord[] = [];\\n  const kind = MESSAGE_WORK_KINDS[message.kind];\\n  if (kind !== undefined) {\\n    const form = MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS[kind];\\n    if (form === undefined) {\\n      // Every queuing kind names its form above; a miss is a wiring bug.\\n      throw new Error(`no derived form mapped for message work kind ${kind}`);\\n    }\\n    items.push(\\n      enqueue(ctx, {\\n        owner: \\\"messages\\\",\\n        kind,\\n        sourceRef: { messageId: message.messageId },\\n        forms: [{ subjectKind: \\\"message\\\", subjectId: message.messageId, form }],\\n      }),\\n    );\\n  }\\n  // Late-result repair (AC-2.8): a tool result landing after its call's\\n  // summary already derived with outcome \\\"unknown\\\" means the summary's\\n  // source — the call+result pair — completed underneath it; clear and\\n  // regenerate at the next source version, in this same batch transaction.\\n  // One indexed lookup; pending summaries (metadata NULL) never match, so\\n  // the common call-and-result-in-one-batch case never triggers, and the\\n  // version-scoped item id keeps the requeue idempotent.\\n  if (message.kind === \\\"tool_result\\\" && message.toolCallId !== undefined) {\\n    const stale = findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary(ctx.db, message.toolCallId);\\n    if (stale !== undefined) {\\n      items.push(\\n        enqueue(ctx, {\\n          owner: \\\"messages\\\",\\n          kind: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n          sourceRef: { messageId: stale.messageId },\\n          sourceVersion: stale.sourceVersion + 1,\\n          forms: [\\n            {\\n              subjectKind: \\\"message\\\",\\n              subjectId: stale.messageId,\\n              form: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n            },\\n          ],\\n        }),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return items;\\n}\\n\\nfunction threadNotFound(filePath: string): { ok: false; error: ErrorResult } {\\n  return {\\n    ok: false,\\n    error: {\\n      errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n      code: \\\"thread_not_found\\\",\\n      reason: `no thread file exists at ${filePath}`,\\n    },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport async function listMessages(\\n  thread: ThreadRef,\\n): Promise<OpResult<MessageRecord[]>> {\\n  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n\\n  // openThreadDatabase verifies the file is a real thread file and migrates\\n  // a pre-Story-3 one before the read, so a thread recorded under an earlier\\n  // story lists cleanly (F-03-001) and a non-thread file is rejected\\n  // unmutated (F-03-002).\\n  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n  const db = opened.value;\\n  try {\\n    // Form read-back rides the message read (AC-2.1): each record carries\\n    // its stored derived forms, attached from one grouped query — the\\n    // production path for \\\"readable alongside the message\\\".\\n    const formsByMessage = readMessageForms(db);\\n    const records = readMessages(db).map((record) => {\\n      const forms = formsByMessage.get(record.messageId);\\n      return forms === undefined ? record : { ...record, forms };\\n    });\\n    return { ok: true, value: records };\\n  } catch (cause) {\\n    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n    return storageFailure(`message read-back failed: ${reason}`);\\n  } finally {\\n    db.close();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport async function listQueuedWork(\\n  thread: ThreadRef,\\n): Promise<OpResult<WorkItemRecord[]>> {\\n  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n\\n  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n  const db = opened.value;\\n  try {\\n    return { ok: true, value: listItems(db, \\\"messages\\\") };\\n  } catch (cause) {\\n    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n    return storageFailure(`queued-work read-back failed: ${reason}`);\\n  } finally {\\n    db.close();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// ── report and repair (Epic 02 Story 4, Flow 4) ──────────────────\\n\\n// This owner's repair report: every message-owned form's durable state\\n// joined with live queue detail in one query — the five operational\\n// situations (waiting, retrying, ready, failed, blocked) read from the rows\\n// without any queue API. Needs no provider; reads degrade, never block.\\nexport async function report(\\n  thread: ThreadRef,\\n  opts?: { notReady?: boolean; messageId?: string },\\n): Promise<OpResult<FormReportEntry[]>> {\\n  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n\\n  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n  const db = opened.value;\\n  try {\\n    return { ok: true, value: reportMessageForms(db, opts ?? {}) };\\n  } catch (cause) {\\n    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n    return storageFailure(`report read failed: ${reason}`);\\n  } finally {\\n    db.close();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport type RequeueOutcome = { workItemId: string } | { noop: \\\"already_queued\\\" };\\n\\n// Which work kind rebuilds each message-owned form — MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS\\n// inverted; the requeue's join from the named form back to its queue site.\\nconst MESSAGE_FORM_KINDS: Partial<Record<FormKind, WorkKind>> = {\\n  smoothed_prompt: \\\"prompt_smoothing\\\",\\n  tool_call_summary: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n  tool_result_summary: \\\"tool_result_summary\\\",\\n};\\n\\n// Explicit re-queue through the owning surface (AC-4.4): the public,\\n// supported rebuild act. Refused for blocked forms with the form's stored\\n// damage reason (AC-4.6) and for missing rows; a no-op against work already\\n// queued or in flight at the form's current source version (AC-4.5).\\n// Otherwise the form clears to pending and re-enqueues at the next source\\n// version — the same enqueue path intake uses, poke-on-commit included, so\\n// background mode processes the repair with no further call. The no-op check\\n// and the enqueue commit in one transaction (anti-shim: a split would\\n// reintroduce the duplicate-work race).\\nexport async function requeue(\\n  thread: ThreadRef,\\n  target: { messageId: string; form: FormKind },\\n): Promise<OpResult<RequeueOutcome>> {\\n  const kind = MESSAGE_FORM_KINDS[target.form];\\n  if (kind === undefined) {\\n    return {\\n      ok: false,\\n      error: {\\n        errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n        code: \\\"message_not_found\\\",\\n        reason: `form ${target.form} is not message-owned; messages.requeue repairs smoothed_prompt, tool_call_summary, tool_result_summary`,\\n      },\\n    };\\n  }\\n  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n\\n  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n  const db = opened.value;\\n  try {\\n    const meta = db\\n      .prepare(`SELECT thread_id FROM thread_metadata WHERE id = 1`)\\n      .get() as { thread_id: string } | undefined;\\n    const threadId = meta?.thread_id ?? \\\"\\\";\\n    return runInTransaction(db, () => new Date(), threadId, (ctx): OpResult<RequeueOutcome> => {\\n      const row = readMessageFormRow(ctx.db, target.messageId, target.form);\\n      if (row === undefined) {\\n        return {\\n          ok: false,\\n          error: {\\n            errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n            code: \\\"message_not_found\\\",\\n            reason: `no derived form ${target.form} exists for message ${target.messageId}`,\\n          },\\n        };\\n      }\\n      if (row.state === \\\"blocked\\\") {\\n        // The refusal carries the form's stored reason — the damage named at\\n        // blocking time, not a generic string (AC-4.6).\\n        return {\\n          ok: false,\\n          error: {\\n            errorClass: \\\"state_corruption\\\",\\n            code: \\\"source_damaged\\\",\\n            reason: row.reason ?? `form ${target.form} for message ${target.messageId} is blocked`,\\n          },\\n        };\\n      }\\n      const sourceRef = { messageId: target.messageId };\\n      if (hasLiveItem(ctx.db, kind, sourceRef, row.sourceVersion)) {\\n        return { ok: true, value: { noop: \\\"already_queued\\\" } };\\n      }\\n      const item = enqueue(ctx, {\\n        owner: \\\"messages\\\",\\n        kind,\\n        sourceRef,\\n        sourceVersion: row.sourceVersion + 1,\\n        forms: [{ subjectKind: \\\"message\\\", subjectId: target.messageId, form: target.form }],\\n      });\\n      return { ok: true, value: { workItemId: item.workItemId } };\\n    });\\n  } catch (cause) {\\n    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n    return storageFailure(`requeue failed: ${reason}`);\\n  } finally {\\n    db.close();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// ── mutations (Epic 02 Story 5, Flow 5) ──────────────────────────\\n\\n// The mutation result contract (tech design §Interfaces): what changed in\\n// the record, which dependent forms cleared, which dropped (delete only),\\n// what replacement work queued, and which still-queued old items the cascade\\n// tidied away (issue 1). Shared by edit and the Story 6 deletes.\\nexport interface MutationResult {\\n  changed: { messageIds: string[]; turnIds: string[] };\\n  cleared: CascadeClear[];\\n  dropped: CascadeClear[];\\n  queued: Array<{ workItemId: string; kind: WorkKind }>;\\n  superseded: string[];\\n}\\n\\n// The record's first sanctioned mutation (AC-5.1–5.5): change a closed-turn\\n// message's content and blocks, re-stamp the token estimate, and walk the\\n// full dependent chain — clear to pending, supersede queued old work,\\n// enqueue replacements at the next source version — in one transaction.\\n// Synchronous and local by contract: everything above commits before this\\n// returns; the re-queued rebuilds run through the normal drain (background\\n// mode needs no further call — the enqueue pokes ride the commit). Events\\n// are never touched (projection-level mutation, DD-12), and no generated\\n// thread-view is either — visibility arrives at the next compact/rebuild.\\n// Refusals read through the deleted-filtered view and enforce the closed-turn\\n// target boundary: only a message in a closed turn is editable, so an\\n// open-turn *or* a turnless (no-membership) gap target is refused turn_open —\\n// the boundary's one stable code — a missing or deleted message is\\n// message_not_found, and a refusal changes nothing.\\nexport async function edit(\\n  thread: ThreadRef,\\n  input: { messageId: string; content: string },\\n): Promise<OpResult<MutationResult>> {\\n  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n\\n  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n  const db = opened.value;\\n  try {\\n    const meta = db\\n      .prepare(`SELECT thread_id FROM thread_metadata WHERE id = 1`)\\n      .get() as { thread_id: string } | undefined;\\n    const threadId = meta?.thread_id ?? \\\"\\\";\\n    return runInTransaction(db, () => new Date(), threadId, (ctx): OpResult<MutationResult> => {\\n      const target = readMutableMessage(ctx.db, input.messageId);\\n      if (target === undefined) {\\n        return {\\n          ok: false,\\n          error: {\\n            errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n            code: \\\"message_not_found\\\",\\n            reason: `no message ${input.messageId} exists in this thread`,\\n          },\\n        };\\n      }\\n      // The closed-turn target boundary (story scope; AC-5.1): the edit's\\n      // editable class is a message in a *closed* turn. Both failing cases —\\n      // an open turn and a turnless gap message (no membership) — refuse under\\n      // the one stable code; the reason distinguishes them so the open-turn\\n      // message reads exactly as before. A deleted/missing target never gets\\n      // here (it misses the filtered read above as message_not_found).\\n      if (target.turnStatus !== \\\"closed\\\") {\\n        return {\\n          ok: false,\\n          error: {\\n            errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n            code: \\\"turn_open\\\",\\n            reason:\\n              target.turnStatus === \\\"open\\\"\\n                ? `message ${input.messageId} belongs to open turn ${target.turnId ?? \\\"\\\"}; open-turn messages cannot be edited (v1 boundary)`\\n                : `message ${input.messageId} has no turn membership; only closed-turn messages can be edited (v1 boundary)`,\\n          },\\n        };\\n      }\\n      applyMessageEdit(ctx.db, input.messageId, input.content);\\n      const cascade = cascadeFromMessage(ctx, input.messageId);\\n      return {\\n        ok: true,\\n        value: {\\n          changed: { messageIds: [input.messageId], turnIds: [] },\\n          cleared: cascade.cleared,\\n          dropped: cascade.dropped,\\n          queued: cascade.queued,\\n          superseded: cascade.superseded,\\n        },\\n      };\\n    });\\n  } catch (cause) {\\n    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n    return storageFailure(`edit failed: ${reason}`);\\n  } finally {\\n    db.close();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// ── delete (Epic 02 Story 6, Flow 6) ─────────────────────────────\\n\\n// The record's removal mutation for one message (AC-6.1–6.3, 6.7):\\n// projection-level delete — the deleted_at stamp plus the delete cascade\\n// (own forms dropped, turn and chunk cleared and re-queued for minus-one\\n// composition) in one transaction. The source events are never touched;\\n// event read-back keeps returning them (the audit surface). Validation\\n// reads the same filtered view as edit, so a missing, deleted, or\\n// double-deleted target is message_not_found and an open-turn or turnless\\n// gap target is turn_open. The one delete-specific refusal is prompt\\n// protection: a turn is a prompt and what came back for it, so deleting the\\n// turn's initiating prompt is refused toward turns.deleteTurn — the error\\n// names the turn and that path (AC-6.3).\\nexport async function deleteMessage(\\n  thread: ThreadRef,\\n  input: { messageId: string },\\n): Promise<OpResult<MutationResult>> {\\n  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n\\n  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n  const db = opened.value;\\n  try {\\n    const meta = db\\n      .prepare(`SELECT thread_id FROM thread_metadata WHERE id = 1`)\\n      .get() as { thread_id: string } | undefined;\\n    const threadId = meta?.thread_id ?? \\\"\\\";\\n    return runInTransaction(db, () => new Date(), threadId, (ctx): OpResult<MutationResult> => {\\n      const target = readMutableMessage(ctx.db, input.messageId);\\n      if (target === undefined) {\\n        return {\\n          ok: false,\\n          error: {\\n            errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n            code: \\\"message_not_found\\\",\\n            reason: `no message ${input.messageId} exists in this thread`,\\n          },\\n        };\\n      }\\n      if (target.turnStatus !== \\\"closed\\\") {\\n        return {\\n          ok: false,\\n          error: {\\n            errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n            code: \\\"turn_open\\\",\\n            reason:\\n              target.turnStatus === \\\"open\\\"\\n                ? `message ${input.messageId} belongs to open turn ${target.turnId ?? \\\"\\\"}; open-turn messages cannot be deleted (v1 boundary)`\\n                : `message ${input.messageId} has no turn membership; only closed-turn messages can be deleted (v1 boundary)`,\\n          },\\n        };\\n      }\\n      if (target.initiatesTurn) {\\n        return {\\n          ok: false,\\n          error: {\\n            errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n            code: \\\"message_initiates_turn\\\",\\n            reason: `message ${input.messageId} is the prompt that initiates turn ${target.turnId ?? \\\"\\\"}; a turn is a prompt and what came back for it — delete the whole exchange with turns.deleteTurn (lhc turns delete --turn-id ${target.turnId ?? \\\"\\\"})`,\\n          },\\n        };\\n      }\\n      markMessageDeleted(ctx.db, input.messageId, ctx.clock().toISOString());\\n      const cascade = cascadeMessageDelete(ctx, input.messageId);\\n      return {\\n        ok: true,\\n        value: {\\n          changed: { messageIds: [input.messageId], turnIds: [] },\\n          cleared: cascade.cleared,\\n          dropped: cascade.dropped,\\n          queued: cascade.queued,\\n          superseded: cascade.superseded,\\n        },\\n      };\\n    });\\n  } catch (cause) {\\n    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n    return storageFailure(`delete failed: ${reason}`);\\n  } finally {\\n    db.close();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// Cross-domain surface for turns.deleteTurn (DD-8: one cascade module, two\\n// callers), called inside the turn delete's transaction after the turn row\\n// is stamped. The messages domain owns the message-table write — the member\\n// stamp, scoped to live rows — and the shared cascade entry; the turns\\n// operation owns its own validation and turn-row stamp. Returns the cascade\\n// outcome plus the member ids stamped now (record order), which the turn\\n// delete reports as its changed messages.\\nexport function applyTurnDeleteCascade(\\n  ctx: OperationContext,\\n  turnId: string,\\n): CascadeOutcome & { memberMessageIds: string[] } {\\n  const memberMessageIds = markTurnMessagesDeleted(\\n    ctx.db,\\n    turnId,\\n    ctx.clock().toISOString(),\\n  );\\n  return { ...cascadeTurnDelete(ctx, turnId, memberMessageIds), memberMessageIds };\\n}\\n\",\"numLines\":577,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":577}}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:86:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01GdWDtgfvLgrooSVmSam3kK\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t// Message and block row operations. Writes run on the caller's handle inside\\n2\\t// the batch transaction (insert failures propagate so the pipeline rejects\\n3\\t// the whole batch); reads run on a fresh handle per operation. The mutation\\n4\\t// half (Epic 02 Story 5) — the edit's validation read and content apply —\\n5\\t// also lives here: row-level mechanics, no policy.\\n6\\timport type { DatabaseSync } from \\\"node:sqlite\\\";\\n7\\timport { estimateTokens } from \\\"../../../tech-utils/token-counting/index.js\\\";\\n8\\timport type { Block, MessageRecord } from \\\"../index.js\\\";\\n9\\t\\n10\\texport interface MessageRow {\\n11\\t  messageId: string;\\n12\\t  sourceEventOrder: number;\\n13\\t  kind: MessageRecord[\\\"kind\\\"];\\n14\\t  tokenEstimate: number;\\n15\\t  actor: string;\\n16\\t  harness: string;\\n17\\t  // Membership stamp, settled at intake: the turn open after this event's\\n18\\t  // transition, or null in a gap. Written once here, never updated — a null\\n19\\t  // gap stamp stays null forever (AC-3.8), a closed turn's members never\\n20\\t  // change (AC-3.7).\\n21\\t  turnId: string | null;\\n22\\t  blocks: Block[];\\n23\\t}\\n24\\t\\n25\\texport function insertMessage(db: DatabaseSync, row: MessageRow): void {\\n26\\t  db.prepare(\\n27\\t    `INSERT INTO message (message_id, source_event_order, kind, token_estimate, actor, harness, turn_id)\\n28\\t     VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)`,\\n29\\t  ).run(\\n30\\t    row.messageId,\\n31\\t    row.sourceEventOrder,\\n32\\t    row.kind,\\n33\\t    row.tokenEstimate,\\n34\\t    row.actor,\\n35\\t    row.harness,\\n36\\t    row.turnId,\\n37\\t  );\\n38\\t\\n39\\t  const insertBlock = db.prepare(\\n40\\t    `INSERT INTO message_block (message_id, block_index, block_type, content)\\n41\\t     VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)`,\\n42\\t  );\\n43\\t  for (const [index, block] of row.blocks.entries()) {\\n44\\t    insertBlock.run(row.messageId, index, block.blockType, JSON.stringify(block.content));\\n45\\t  }\\n46\\t}\\n47\\t\\n48\\t// The mutation operations' validation read (Flows 5/6): the live\\n49\\t// (deleted-filtered) message joined to its turn's status. A deleted target\\n50\\t// misses here and refuses as message_not_found — the filtered view is the\\n51\\t// refusal's read by design (never a distinct error for deleted; double\\n52\\t// delete reads the same way, AC-6.7). turnStatus is null for a gap message\\n53\\t// (no membership); the closed-turn target boundary refuses it the same as\\n54\\t// an open turn. initiatesTurn carries the prompt-protection fact (AC-6.3):\\n55\\t// a turn opens on its prompt's event, so the member whose source event\\n56\\t// order equals the turn's opened-at order is the turn's initiating prompt.\\n57\\texport interface MutableMessageView {\\n58\\t  messageId: string;\\n59\\t  kind: string;\\n60\\t  turnId: string | null;\\n61\\t  turnStatus: \\\"open\\\" | \\\"closed\\\" | null;\\n62\\t  initiatesTurn: boolean;\\n63\\t}\\n64\\t\\n65\\texport function readMutableMessage(\\n66\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\n67\\t  messageId: string,\\n68\\t): MutableMessageView | undefined {\\n69\\t  const row = db\\n70\\t    .prepare(\\n71\\t      `SELECT m.message_id, m.kind, m.turn_id, m.source_event_order,\\n72\\t              t.status AS turn_status, t.opened_at_event_order\\n73\\t       FROM message m LEFT JOIN turns t ON t.turn_id = m.turn_id\\n74\\t       WHERE m.message_id = ? AND m.deleted_at IS NULL`,\\n75\\t    )\\n76\\t    .get(messageId) as unknown as\\n77\\t    | {\\n78\\t        message_id: string;\\n79\\t        kind: string;\\n80\\t        turn_id: string | null;\\n81\\t        source_event_order: number | bigint;\\n82\\t        turn_status: string | null;\\n83\\t        opened_at_event_order: number | bigint | null;\\n84\\t      }\\n85\\t    | undefined;\\n86\\t  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\n87\\t  return {\\n88\\t    messageId: row.message_id,\\n89\\t    kind: row.kind,\\n90\\t    turnId: row.turn_id,\\n91\\t    turnStatus: row.turn_status as MutableMessageView[\\\"turnStatus\\\"],\\n92\\t    initiatesTurn:\\n93\\t      row.opened_at_event_order !== null &&\\n94\\t      Number(row.source_event_order) === Number(row.opened_at_event_order),\\n95\\t  };\\n96\\t}\\n97\\t\\n98\\t// The delete's record apply (Flow 6): a projection-level tombstone — the\\n99\\t// deleted_at stamp every read filters on. The source events are never\\n100\\t// touched (record-never-destroyed, DD-12); event read-back keeps showing\\n101\\t// them. The bulk variant is turns.deleteTurn's member stamp, scoped to live\\n102\\t// rows so a turn whose messages were individually deleted first still\\n103\\t// deletes cleanly (membership walk on live rows); it returns the stamped\\n104\\t// ids in record order for the mutation result and the cascade's drop set.\\n105\\texport function markMessageDeleted(\\n106\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\n107\\t  messageId: string,\\n108\\t  deletedAt: string,\\n109\\t): void {\\n110\\t  db.prepare(`UPDATE message SET deleted_at = ? WHERE message_id = ?`).run(\\n111\\t    deletedAt,\\n112\\t    messageId,\\n113\\t  );\\n114\\t}\\n115\\t\\n116\\texport function markTurnMessagesDeleted(\\n117\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\n118\\t  turnId: string,\\n119\\t  deletedAt: string,\\n120\\t): string[] {\\n121\\t  const rows = db\\n122\\t    .prepare(\\n123\\t      `UPDATE message SET deleted_at = ?\\n124\\t       WHERE turn_id = ? AND deleted_at IS NULL\\n125\\t       RETURNING message_id, source_event_order`,\\n126\\t    )\\n127\\t    .all(deletedAt, turnId) as unknown as Array<{\\n128\\t    message_id: string;\\n129\\t    source_event_order: number | bigint;\\n130\\t  }>;\\n131\\t  return rows\\n132\\t    .sort((a, b) => Number(a.source_event_order) - Number(b.source_event_order))\\n133\\t    .map((row) => row.message_id);\\n134\\t}\\n135\\t\\n136\\t// The edit's record apply (AC-5.1): the new content lands in each block's\\n137\\t// content-bearing field — the same field per block type the projection wrote\\n138\\t// and counted (internal/project.ts) — and the token estimate re-stamps from\\n139\\t// the same estimator, so placement arithmetic stays current after edits.\\n140\\t// Events are untouched: this is projection-level mutation; the log keeps the\\n141\\t// original (DD-12).\\n142\\texport function applyMessageEdit(db: DatabaseSync, messageId: string, content: string): void {\\n143\\t  const blocks = db\\n144\\t    .prepare(\\n145\\t      `SELECT block_index, block_type, content FROM message_block\\n146\\t       WHERE message_id = ? ORDER BY block_index`,\\n147\\t    )\\n148\\t    .all(messageId) as unknown as Array<{\\n149\\t    block_index: number | bigint;\\n150\\t    block_type: string;\\n151\\t    content: string;\\n152\\t  }>;\\n153\\t  const update = db.prepare(\\n154\\t    `UPDATE message_block SET content = ? WHERE message_id = ? AND block_index = ?`,\\n155\\t  );\\n156\\t  let tokenEstimate = estimateTokens(content);\\n157\\t  for (const block of blocks) {\\n158\\t    const parsed = JSON.parse(block.content) as Record<string, unknown>;\\n159\\t    switch (block.block_type) {\\n160\\t      case \\\"text\\\":\\n161\\t        parsed[\\\"text\\\"] = content;\\n162\\t        break;\\n163\\t      case \\\"tool_result\\\":\\n164\\t        parsed[\\\"content\\\"] = content;\\n165\\t        break;\\n166\\t      case \\\"tool_call\\\":\\n167\\t        // Arguments are the call's counted content; the edit's string lands\\n168\\t        // verbatim as the new arguments value, mirroring projection's\\n169\\t        // serialized-arguments estimate.\\n170\\t        parsed[\\\"arguments\\\"] = content;\\n171\\t        tokenEstimate = estimateTokens(JSON.stringify(content));\\n172\\t        break;\\n173\\t      default:\\n174\\t        throw new Error(`message ${messageId} carries unknown block type ${block.block_type}`);\\n175\\t    }\\n176\\t    update.run(JSON.stringify(parsed), messageId, Number(block.block_index));\\n177\\t  }\\n178\\t  db.prepare(`UPDATE message SET token_estimate = ? WHERE message_id = ?`).run(\\n179\\t    tokenEstimate,\\n180\\t    messageId,\\n181\\t  );\\n182\\t}\\n183\\t\\n184\\tinterface RawMessageRow {\\n185\\t  message_id: string;\\n186\\t  source_event_order: number | bigint;\\n187\\t  kind: string;\\n188\\t  token_estimate: number | bigint;\\n189\\t  actor: string;\\n190\\t  harness: string;\\n191\\t  turn_id: string | null;\\n192\\t}\\n193\\t\\n194\\tinterface RawBlockRow {\\n195\\t  message_id: string;\\n196\\t  block_type: string;\\n197\\t  content: string;\\n198\\t}\\n199\\t\\n200\\texport function readMessages(db: DatabaseSync): MessageRecord[] {\\n201\\t  const blockRows = db\\n202\\t    .prepare(\\n203\\t      `SELECT message_id, block_type, content FROM message_block\\n204\\t       ORDER BY message_id, block_index`,\\n205\\t    )\\n206\\t    .all() as unknown as RawBlockRow[];\\n207\\t  const blocksByMessage = new Map<string, Block[]>();\\n208\\t  for (const row of blockRows) {\\n209\\t    const blocks = blocksByMessage.get(row.message_id) ?? [];\\n210\\t    blocks.push({\\n211\\t      blockType: row.block_type as Block[\\\"blockType\\\"],\\n212\\t      content: JSON.parse(row.content) as Record<string, unknown>,\\n213\\t    });\\n214\\t    blocksByMessage.set(row.message_id, blocks);\\n215\\t  }\\n216\\t\\n217\\t  // The deleted-read filter (tech design §Mechanics): message reads surface\\n218\\t  // live projection rows only; a deleted message's source events stay\\n219\\t  // readable through the Epic 01 event read-back, the one unfiltered surface.\\n220\\t  const messageRows = db\\n221\\t    .prepare(\\n222\\t      `SELECT message_id, source_event_order, kind, token_estimate, actor, harness, turn_id\\n223\\t       FROM message WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY source_event_order`,\\n224\\t    )\\n225\\t    .all() as unknown as RawMessageRow[];\\n226\\t  return messageRows.map((row) => {\\n227\\t    const record: MessageRecord = {\\n228\\t      messageId: row.message_id,\\n229\\t      sourceEventOrder: Number(row.source_event_order),\\n230\\t      kind: row.kind as MessageRecord[\\\"kind\\\"],\\n231\\t      blocks: blocksByMessage.get(row.message_id) ?? [],\\n232\\t      tokenEstimate: Number(row.token_estimate),\\n233\\t      actor: row.actor,\\n234\\t      harness: row.harness,\\n235\\t    };\\n236\\t    if (row.turn_id !== null) record.turnId = row.turn_id;\\n237\\t    return record;\\n238\\t  });\\n239\\t}\\n240\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"92b30fef-4ad7-45bb-a8e9-4c6f66be56bf\",\"uuid\":\"9d3594a9-0090-4102-a497-9ca3911c9c67\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-12T12:47:58.863Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/store.ts\",\"content\":\"// Message and block row operations. Writes run on the caller's handle inside\\n// the batch transaction (insert failures propagate so the pipeline rejects\\n// the whole batch); reads run on a fresh handle per operation. The mutation\\n// half (Epic 02 Story 5) — the edit's validation read and content apply —\\n// also lives here: row-level mechanics, no policy.\\nimport type { DatabaseSync } from \\\"node:sqlite\\\";\\nimport { estimateTokens } from \\\"../../../tech-utils/token-counting/index.js\\\";\\nimport type { Block, MessageRecord } from \\\"../index.js\\\";\\n\\nexport interface MessageRow {\\n  messageId: string;\\n  sourceEventOrder: number;\\n  kind: MessageRecord[\\\"kind\\\"];\\n  tokenEstimate: number;\\n  actor: string;\\n  harness: string;\\n  // Membership stamp, settled at intake: the turn open after this event's\\n  // transition, or null in a gap. Written once here, never updated — a null\\n  // gap stamp stays null forever (AC-3.8), a closed turn's members never\\n  // change (AC-3.7).\\n  turnId: string | null;\\n  blocks: Block[];\\n}\\n\\nexport function insertMessage(db: DatabaseSync, row: MessageRow): void {\\n  db.prepare(\\n    `INSERT INTO message (message_id, source_event_order, kind, token_estimate, actor, harness, turn_id)\\n     VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)`,\\n  ).run(\\n    row.messageId,\\n    row.sourceEventOrder,\\n    row.kind,\\n    row.tokenEstimate,\\n    row.actor,\\n    row.harness,\\n    row.turnId,\\n  );\\n\\n  const insertBlock = db.prepare(\\n    `INSERT INTO message_block (message_id, block_index, block_type, content)\\n     VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)`,\\n  );\\n  for (const [index, block] of row.blocks.entries()) {\\n    insertBlock.run(row.messageId, index, block.blockType, JSON.stringify(block.content));\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// The mutation operations' validation read (Flows 5/6): the live\\n// (deleted-filtered) message joined to its turn's status. A deleted target\\n// misses here and refuses as message_not_found — the filtered view is the\\n// refusal's read by design (never a distinct error for deleted; double\\n// delete reads the same way, AC-6.7). turnStatus is null for a gap message\\n// (no membership); the closed-turn target boundary refuses it the same as\\n// an open turn. initiatesTurn carries the prompt-protection fact (AC-6.3):\\n// a turn opens on its prompt's event, so the member whose source event\\n// order equals the turn's opened-at order is the turn's initiating prompt.\\nexport interface MutableMessageView {\\n  messageId: string;\\n  kind: string;\\n  turnId: string | null;\\n  turnStatus: \\\"open\\\" | \\\"closed\\\" | null;\\n  initiatesTurn: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nexport function readMutableMessage(\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\n  messageId: string,\\n): MutableMessageView | undefined {\\n  const row = db\\n    .prepare(\\n      `SELECT m.message_id, m.kind, m.turn_id, m.source_event_order,\\n              t.status AS turn_status, t.opened_at_event_order\\n       FROM message m LEFT JOIN turns t ON t.turn_id = m.turn_id\\n       WHERE m.message_id = ? AND m.deleted_at IS NULL`,\\n    )\\n    .get(messageId) as unknown as\\n    | {\\n        message_id: string;\\n        kind: string;\\n        turn_id: string | null;\\n        source_event_order: number | bigint;\\n        turn_status: string | null;\\n        opened_at_event_order: number | bigint | null;\\n      }\\n    | undefined;\\n  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\n  return {\\n    messageId: row.message_id,\\n    kind: row.kind,\\n    turnId: row.turn_id,\\n    turnStatus: row.turn_status as MutableMessageView[\\\"turnStatus\\\"],\\n    initiatesTurn:\\n      row.opened_at_event_order !== null &&\\n      Number(row.source_event_order) === Number(row.opened_at_event_order),\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n// The delete's record apply (Flow 6): a projection-level tombstone — the\\n// deleted_at stamp every read filters on. The source events are never\\n// touched (record-never-destroyed, DD-12); event read-back keeps showing\\n// them. The bulk variant is turns.deleteTurn's member stamp, scoped to live\\n// rows so a turn whose messages were individually deleted first still\\n// deletes cleanly (membership walk on live rows); it returns the stamped\\n// ids in record order for the mutation result and the cascade's drop set.\\nexport function markMessageDeleted(\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\n  messageId: string,\\n  deletedAt: string,\\n): void {\\n  db.prepare(`UPDATE message SET deleted_at = ? WHERE message_id = ?`).run(\\n    deletedAt,\\n    messageId,\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nexport function markTurnMessagesDeleted(\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\n  turnId: string,\\n  deletedAt: string,\\n): string[] {\\n  const rows = db\\n    .prepare(\\n      `UPDATE message SET deleted_at = ?\\n       WHERE turn_id = ? AND deleted_at IS NULL\\n       RETURNING message_id, source_event_order`,\\n    )\\n    .all(deletedAt, turnId) as unknown as Array<{\\n    message_id: string;\\n    source_event_order: number | bigint;\\n  }>;\\n  return rows\\n    .sort((a, b) => Number(a.source_event_order) - Number(b.source_event_order))\\n    .map((row) => row.message_id);\\n}\\n\\n// The edit's record apply (AC-5.1): the new content lands in each block's\\n// content-bearing field — the same field per block type the projection wrote\\n// and counted (internal/project.ts) — and the token estimate re-stamps from\\n// the same estimator, so placement arithmetic stays current after edits.\\n// Events are untouched: this is projection-level mutation; the log keeps the\\n// original (DD-12).\\nexport function applyMessageEdit(db: DatabaseSync, messageId: string, content: string): void {\\n  const blocks = db\\n    .prepare(\\n      `SELECT block_index, block_type, content FROM message_block\\n       WHERE message_id = ? ORDER BY block_index`,\\n    )\\n    .all(messageId) as unknown as Array<{\\n    block_index: number | bigint;\\n    block_type: string;\\n    content: string;\\n  }>;\\n  const update = db.prepare(\\n    `UPDATE message_block SET content = ? WHERE message_id = ? AND block_index = ?`,\\n  );\\n  let tokenEstimate = estimateTokens(content);\\n  for (const block of blocks) {\\n    const parsed = JSON.parse(block.content) as Record<string, unknown>;\\n    switch (block.block_type) {\\n      case \\\"text\\\":\\n        parsed[\\\"text\\\"] = content;\\n        break;\\n      case \\\"tool_result\\\":\\n        parsed[\\\"content\\\"] = content;\\n        break;\\n      case \\\"tool_call\\\":\\n        // Arguments are the call's counted content; the edit's string lands\\n        // verbatim as the new arguments value, mirroring projection's\\n        // serialized-arguments estimate.\\n        parsed[\\\"arguments\\\"] = content;\\n        tokenEstimate = estimateTokens(JSON.stringify(content));\\n        break;\\n      default:\\n        throw new Error(`message ${messageId} carries unknown block type ${block.block_type}`);\\n    }\\n    update.run(JSON.stringify(parsed), messageId, Number(block.block_index));\\n  }\\n  db.prepare(`UPDATE message SET token_estimate = ? WHERE message_id = ?`).run(\\n    tokenEstimate,\\n    messageId,\\n  );\\n}\\n\\ninterface RawMessageRow {\\n  message_id: string;\\n  source_event_order: number | bigint;\\n  kind: string;\\n  token_estimate: number | bigint;\\n  actor: string;\\n  harness: string;\\n  turn_id: string | null;\\n}\\n\\ninterface RawBlockRow {\\n  message_id: string;\\n  block_type: string;\\n  content: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport function readMessages(db: DatabaseSync): MessageRecord[] {\\n  const blockRows = db\\n    .prepare(\\n      `SELECT message_id, block_type, content FROM message_block\\n       ORDER BY message_id, block_index`,\\n    )\\n    .all() as unknown as RawBlockRow[];\\n  const blocksByMessage = new Map<string, Block[]>();\\n  for (const row of blockRows) {\\n    const blocks = blocksByMessage.get(row.message_id) ?? [];\\n    blocks.push({\\n      blockType: row.block_type as Block[\\\"blockType\\\"],\\n      content: JSON.parse(row.content) as Record<string, unknown>,\\n    });\\n    blocksByMessage.set(row.message_id, blocks);\\n  }\\n\\n  // The deleted-read filter (tech design §Mechanics): message reads surface\\n  // live projection rows only; a deleted message's source events stay\\n  // readable through the Epic 01 event read-back, the one unfiltered surface.\\n  const messageRows = db\\n    .prepare(\\n      `SELECT message_id, source_event_order, kind, token_estimate, actor, harness, turn_id\\n       FROM message WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY source_event_order`,\\n    )\\n    .all() as unknown as RawMessageRow[];\\n  return messageRows.map((row) => {\\n    const record: MessageRecord = {\\n      messageId: row.message_id,\\n      sourceEventOrder: Number(row.source_event_order),\\n      kind: row.kind as MessageRecord[\\\"kind\\\"],\\n      blocks: blocksByMessage.get(row.message_id) ?? [],\\n      tokenEstimate: Number(row.token_estimate),\\n      actor: row.actor,\\n      harness: row.harness,\\n    };\\n    if (row.turn_id !== null) record.turnId = row.turn_id;\\n    return record;\\n  });\\n}\\n\",\"numLines\":240,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":240}}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:113:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01Dsjw18yoBSESYW6bwjiYUY\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\timport { parseArgs } from \\\"node:util\\\";\\n2\\timport * as intakeStream from \\\"../domains/intake-stream/index.js\\\";\\n3\\timport * as messages from \\\"../domains/messages/index.js\\\";\\n4\\timport * as threads from \\\"../domains/threads/index.js\\\";\\n5\\timport * as turns from \\\"../domains/turns/index.js\\\";\\n6\\timport type { MessageEventInput } from \\\"../domains/intake-stream/index.js\\\";\\n7\\timport type { ThreadRef } from \\\"../domains/threads/index.js\\\";\\n8\\timport type { OpResult } from \\\"../shared/errors.js\\\";\\n9\\timport { renderCliError, renderResult, type CliResult } from \\\"./render.js\\\";\\n10\\timport { runMessagesDelete, runMessagesEdit } from \\\"./messages-mutate.js\\\";\\n11\\timport { runTurnsDelete } from \\\"./turns-mutate.js\\\";\\n12\\timport {\\n13\\t  runMessagesReport,\\n14\\t  runMessagesRequeue,\\n15\\t  runTurnsReport,\\n16\\t  runTurnsRequeue,\\n17\\t  runWorkDrain,\\n18\\t} from \\\"./work.js\\\";\\n19\\timport { runViewCommand } from \\\"./view.js\\\";\\n20\\t\\n21\\t// Stdin seam: in-process tests inject a reader; the binary reads the real\\n22\\t// process stdin. null means interactive (TTY) — distinct from empty input\\n23\\t// only in how it arises; both are refused with empty_stdin before any SDK\\n24\\t// call (the SDK itself can never return that code).\\n25\\texport type StdinReader = () => Promise<string | null>;\\n26\\t\\n27\\tasync function readProcessStdin(): Promise<string | null> {\\n28\\t  if (process.stdin.isTTY) return null;\\n29\\t  process.stdin.setEncoding(\\\"utf8\\\");\\n30\\t  let data = \\\"\\\";\\n31\\t  for await (const chunk of process.stdin) data += String(chunk);\\n32\\t  return data;\\n33\\t}\\n34\\t\\n35\\tfunction stdinCallerError(code: \\\"empty_stdin\\\" | \\\"invalid_event\\\", reason: string): OpResult<never> {\\n36\\t  return { ok: false, error: { errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\", code, reason } };\\n37\\t}\\n38\\t\\n39\\tconst HELP = `lhc — Long Horizon Context CLI\\n40\\t\\n41\\tUsage:\\n42\\t  lhc threads new-thread --file-path <p> [--title <t>] [--registry <r>]\\n43\\t  lhc threads resolve --thread-id <id> [--registry <r>]\\n44\\t  lhc threads list [--registry <r>]\\n45\\t  lhc intake-stream message-events (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n46\\t  lhc intake-stream list-events (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n47\\t  lhc messages list (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n48\\t  lhc messages list-queued-work (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n49\\t  lhc messages report (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--not-ready] [--message-id <id>] [--registry <r>]\\n50\\t  lhc messages requeue (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) --message-id <id> --form <form> [--registry <r>]\\n51\\t  lhc messages edit (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) --message <id> --content <text> [--registry <r>]\\n52\\t  lhc messages delete (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) --message <id> [--registry <r>]\\n53\\t  lhc turns list (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n54\\t  lhc turns list-chunks (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n55\\t  lhc turns list-queued-work (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n56\\t  lhc turns report (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--not-ready] [--turn-id <id>] [--chunk-id <id>] [--registry <r>]\\n57\\t  lhc turns requeue (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) --subject-kind (turn|chunk) --subject-id <id> --form <form> [--registry <r>]\\n58\\t  lhc turns delete (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) --turn <id> [--registry <r>]\\n59\\t  lhc work drain (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--max-items <n>] [--provider <name>] [--registry <r>]\\n60\\t  lhc view pull (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--json] [--registry <r>]\\n61\\t  lhc view status (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--json] [--registry <r>]\\n62\\t  lhc view compact (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--profile <name>]\\n63\\t                   [--lower-bound <n>] [--full <n>] [--smooth <n>] [--detailed <n>] [--brief <n>]\\n64\\t                   [--no-sweep] [--json] [--registry <r>]\\n65\\t  lhc view sweep (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--json] [--registry <r>]\\n66\\t  lhc view materialize (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) --out <path> [--format pi-session] [--registry <r>]\\n67\\t\\n68\\tEvery command prints the SDK result (value or error) as JSON and exits 0 on\\n69\\tsuccess, 1 on failure. message-events reads an events JSON array on stdin.\\n70\\tView commands need no provider; output is always JSON (--json accepted).\\n71\\tTwo exceptions on success: view pull prints the message array itself, and\\n72\\tview materialize prints the written path; their failures stay structured.\\n73\\t`;\\n74\\t\\n75\\tinterface ParsedFlags {\\n76\\t  threadId?: string;\\n77\\t  filePath?: string;\\n78\\t  title?: string;\\n79\\t  registryPath?: string;\\n80\\t  maxItems?: string;\\n81\\t  provider?: string;\\n82\\t  notReady?: boolean;\\n83\\t  messageId?: string;\\n84\\t  turnId?: string;\\n85\\t  chunkId?: string;\\n86\\t  form?: string;\\n87\\t  subjectKind?: string;\\n88\\t  subjectId?: string;\\n89\\t  content?: string;\\n90\\t}\\n91\\t\\n92\\t// strict parse rejects unknown/misspelled flags so they are named back to the\\n93\\t// caller, never silently dropped — the CLI boundary matching the SDK's\\n94\\t// closed-contract strictness. The failure is returned as data (not thrown) so\\n95\\t// runCli can render it as the structured usage error.\\n96\\ttype ParseFlagsResult =\\n97\\t  | { ok: true; flags: ParsedFlags }\\n98\\t  | { ok: false; unknownFlag: string };\\n99\\t\\n100\\tfunction parseFlags(args: readonly string[]): ParseFlagsResult {\\n101\\t  let values;\\n102\\t  try {\\n103\\t    ({ values } = parseArgs({\\n104\\t      args: [...args],\\n105\\t      options: {\\n106\\t        \\\"thread-id\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n107\\t        \\\"file-path\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n108\\t        title: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n109\\t        registry: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n110\\t        \\\"max-items\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n111\\t        provider: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n112\\t        \\\"not-ready\\\": { type: \\\"boolean\\\" },\\n113\\t        \\\"message-id\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n114\\t        \\\"turn-id\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n115\\t        \\\"chunk-id\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n116\\t        form: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n117\\t        \\\"subject-kind\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n118\\t        \\\"subject-id\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n119\\t        // `--message` / `--turn` are the mutation commands' spellings\\n120\\t        // (story/tech design); they parse into the same slots as\\n121\\t        // `--message-id` / `--turn-id`.\\n122\\t        message: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n123\\t        turn: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n124\\t        content: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n125\\t      },\\n126\\t      strict: true,\\n127\\t      allowPositionals: true,\\n128\\t    }));\\n129\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n130\\t    const message = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n131\\t    // parseArgs names the offending option in single quotes (e.g. Unknown\\n132\\t    // option '--file-pth'); surface that token, falling back to the message.\\n133\\t    const named = /'([^']+)'/.exec(message);\\n134\\t    return { ok: false, unknownFlag: named?.[1] ?? message };\\n135\\t  }\\n136\\t  const flags: ParsedFlags = {};\\n137\\t  if (typeof values[\\\"thread-id\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.threadId = values[\\\"thread-id\\\"];\\n138\\t  if (typeof values[\\\"file-path\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.filePath = values[\\\"file-path\\\"];\\n139\\t  if (typeof values.title === \\\"string\\\") flags.title = values.title;\\n140\\t  if (typeof values.registry === \\\"string\\\") flags.registryPath = values.registry;\\n141\\t  if (typeof values[\\\"max-items\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.maxItems = values[\\\"max-items\\\"];\\n142\\t  if (typeof values.provider === \\\"string\\\") flags.provider = values.provider;\\n143\\t  if (values[\\\"not-ready\\\"] === true) flags.notReady = true;\\n144\\t  if (typeof values[\\\"message-id\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.messageId = values[\\\"message-id\\\"];\\n145\\t  if (typeof values.message === \\\"string\\\") flags.messageId = values.message;\\n146\\t  if (typeof values.content === \\\"string\\\") flags.content = values.content;\\n147\\t  if (typeof values[\\\"turn-id\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.turnId = values[\\\"turn-id\\\"];\\n148\\t  if (typeof values.turn === \\\"string\\\") flags.turnId = values.turn;\\n149\\t  if (typeof values[\\\"chunk-id\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.chunkId = values[\\\"chunk-id\\\"];\\n150\\t  if (typeof values.form === \\\"string\\\") flags.form = values.form;\\n151\\t  if (typeof values[\\\"subject-kind\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.subjectKind = values[\\\"subject-kind\\\"];\\n152\\t  if (typeof values[\\\"subject-id\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.subjectId = values[\\\"subject-id\\\"];\\n153\\t  return { ok: true, flags };\\n154\\t}\\n155\\t\\n156\\t// The read commands take a thread reference but no stdin; a missing reference\\n157\\t// is a usage error named before any SDK call, matching the intake commands.\\n158\\tfunction requireThreadRef(flags: ParsedFlags, command: string): CliResult | undefined {\\n159\\t  if (flags.threadId === undefined && flags.filePath === undefined) {\\n160\\t    return renderCliError(\\n161\\t      \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n162\\t      \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n163\\t      `${command} requires --thread-id or --file-path`,\\n164\\t    );\\n165\\t  }\\n166\\t  return undefined;\\n167\\t}\\n168\\t\\n169\\tfunction threadRefFrom(flags: ParsedFlags): ThreadRef {\\n170\\t  if (flags.threadId !== undefined) {\\n171\\t    return flags.registryPath !== undefined\\n172\\t      ? { threadId: flags.threadId, registryPath: flags.registryPath }\\n173\\t      : { threadId: flags.threadId };\\n174\\t  }\\n175\\t  return { filePath: flags.filePath ?? \\\"\\\" };\\n176\\t}\\n177\\t\\n178\\texport async function runCli(\\n179\\t  argv: readonly string[],\\n180\\t  readStdin: StdinReader = readProcessStdin,\\n181\\t): Promise<CliResult> {\\n182\\t  if (argv.length === 0) {\\n183\\t    return renderCliError(\\\"caller_error\\\", \\\"unknown_command\\\", \\\"no command given; run lhc --help\\\");\\n184\\t  }\\n185\\t  if (argv[0] === \\\"--help\\\" || argv[0] === \\\"-h\\\") {\\n186\\t    return { exitCode: 0, stdout: HELP, stderr: \\\"\\\" };\\n187\\t  }\\n188\\t\\n189\\t  const [group, command, ...rest] = argv;\\n190\\t  // The view group parses its own flag surface (band overrides, --out,\\n191\\t  // --format) — routed before the shared parse so its flags never widen the\\n192\\t  // other commands' accepted set.\\n193\\t  if (group === \\\"view\\\") {\\n194\\t    return runViewCommand(command, rest);\\n195\\t  }\\n196\\t  const key = command === undefined ? group : `${group} ${command}`;\\n197\\t  const parsed = parseFlags(command === undefined ? [] : rest);\\n198\\t  if (!parsed.ok) {\\n199\\t    return renderCliError(\\n200\\t      \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n201\\t      \\\"unknown_flag\\\",\\n202\\t      `unknown flag: ${parsed.unknownFlag}; run lhc --help`,\\n203\\t    );\\n204\\t  }\\n205\\t  const flags = parsed.flags;\\n206\\t\\n207\\t  switch (key) {\\n208\\t    case \\\"threads new-thread\\\": {\\n209\\t      // Guard here: an empty path reaching node:sqlite opens a temp database\\n210\\t      // instead of failing, so the adapter refuses before any SDK call.\\n211\\t      if (flags.filePath === undefined) {\\n212\\t        return renderCliError(\\\"caller_error\\\", \\\"missing_flag\\\", \\\"threads new-thread requires --file-path\\\");\\n213\\t      }\\n214\\t      const input: Parameters<typeof threads.newThread>[0] = {\\n215\\t        filePath: flags.filePath,\\n216\\t      };\\n217\\t      if (flags.title !== undefined) input.title = flags.title;\\n218\\t      if (flags.registryPath !== undefined) input.registryPath = flags.registryPath;\\n219\\t      return renderResult(await threads.newThread(input));\\n220\\t    }\\n221\\t    case \\\"threads resolve\\\": {\\n222\\t      if (flags.threadId === undefined) {\\n223\\t        return renderCliError(\\\"caller_error\\\", \\\"missing_flag\\\", \\\"threads resolve requires --thread-id\\\");\\n224\\t      }\\n225\\t      const input: Parameters<typeof threads.resolve>[0] = {\\n226\\t        threadId: flags.threadId,\\n227\\t      };\\n228\\t      if (flags.registryPath !== undefined) input.registryPath = flags.registryPath;\\n229\\t      return renderResult(await threads.resolve(input));\\n230\\t    }\\n231\\t    case \\\"threads list\\\": {\\n232\\t      return renderResult(\\n233\\t        await threads.listThreads(\\n234\\t          flags.registryPath !== undefined ? { registryPath: flags.registryPath } : undefined,\\n235\\t        ),\\n236\\t      );\\n237\\t    }\\n238\\t    case \\\"intake-stream message-events\\\": {\\n239\\t      if (flags.threadId === undefined && flags.filePath === undefined) {\\n240\\t        return renderCliError(\\n241\\t          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n242\\t          \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n243\\t          \\\"intake-stream message-events requires --thread-id or --file-path\\\",\\n244\\t        );\\n245\\t      }\\n246\\t      const text = await readStdin();\\n247\\t      if (text === null || text.trim() === \\\"\\\") {\\n248\\t        return renderResult(\\n249\\t          stdinCallerError(\\n250\\t            \\\"empty_stdin\\\",\\n251\\t            \\\"message-events expects an events JSON array on stdin; stdin was a TTY or empty\\\",\\n252\\t          ),\\n253\\t        );\\n254\\t      }\\n255\\t      let parsed: unknown;\\n256\\t      try {\\n257\\t        parsed = JSON.parse(text);\\n258\\t      } catch (cause) {\\n259\\t        const detail = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n260\\t        return renderResult(\\n261\\t          stdinCallerError(\\\"invalid_event\\\", `stdin is not valid JSON: ${detail}`),\\n262\\t        );\\n263\\t      }\\n264\\t      if (!Array.isArray(parsed)) {\\n265\\t        return renderResult(\\n266\\t          stdinCallerError(\\\"invalid_event\\\", \\\"stdin must be a JSON array of events\\\"),\\n267\\t        );\\n268\\t      }\\n269\\t      return renderResult(\\n270\\t        await intakeStream.messageEvents(\\n271\\t          threadRefFrom(flags),\\n272\\t          parsed as readonly MessageEventInput[],\\n273\\t        ),\\n274\\t      );\\n275\\t    }\\n276\\t    case \\\"intake-stream list-events\\\": {\\n277\\t      if (flags.threadId === undefined && flags.filePath === undefined) {\\n278\\t        return renderCliError(\\n279\\t          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n280\\t          \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n281\\t          \\\"intake-stream list-events requires --thread-id or --file-path\\\",\\n282\\t        );\\n283\\t      }\\n284\\t      return renderResult(await intakeStream.listEvents(threadRefFrom(flags)));\\n285\\t    }\\n286\\t    case \\\"messages list\\\":\\n287\\t      return (\\n288\\t        requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"messages list\\\") ??\\n289\\t        renderResult(await messages.listMessages(threadRefFrom(flags)))\\n290\\t      );\\n291\\t    case \\\"messages list-queued-work\\\":\\n292\\t      return (\\n293\\t        requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"messages list-queued-work\\\") ??\\n294\\t        renderResult(await messages.listQueuedWork(threadRefFrom(flags)))\\n295\\t      );\\n296\\t    case \\\"messages report\\\": {\\n297\\t      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"messages report\\\");\\n298\\t      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n299\\t      const reportFlags: { notReady?: boolean; messageId?: string } = {};\\n300\\t      if (flags.notReady === true) reportFlags.notReady = true;\\n301\\t      if (flags.messageId !== undefined) reportFlags.messageId = flags.messageId;\\n302\\t      return runMessagesReport(threadRefFrom(flags), reportFlags);\\n303\\t    }\\n304\\t    case \\\"messages requeue\\\": {\\n305\\t      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"messages requeue\\\");\\n306\\t      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n307\\t      if (flags.messageId === undefined || flags.form === undefined) {\\n308\\t        return renderCliError(\\n309\\t          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n310\\t          \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n311\\t          \\\"messages requeue requires --message-id and --form\\\",\\n312\\t        );\\n313\\t      }\\n314\\t      return runMessagesRequeue(threadRefFrom(flags), {\\n315\\t        messageId: flags.messageId,\\n316\\t        form: flags.form,\\n317\\t      });\\n318\\t    }\\n319\\t    case \\\"messages edit\\\": {\\n320\\t      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"messages edit\\\");\\n321\\t      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n322\\t      if (flags.messageId === undefined || flags.content === undefined) {\\n323\\t        return renderCliError(\\n324\\t          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n325\\t          \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n326\\t          \\\"messages edit requires --message (or --message-id) and --content\\\",\\n327\\t        );\\n328\\t      }\\n329\\t      return runMessagesEdit(threadRefFrom(flags), {\\n330\\t        messageId: flags.messageId,\\n331\\t        content: flags.content,\\n332\\t      });\\n333\\t    }\\n334\\t    case \\\"messages delete\\\": {\\n335\\t      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"messages delete\\\");\\n336\\t      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n337\\t      if (flags.messageId === undefined) {\\n338\\t        return renderCliError(\\n339\\t          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n340\\t          \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n341\\t          \\\"messages delete requires --message (or --message-id)\\\",\\n342\\t        );\\n343\\t      }\\n344\\t      return runMessagesDelete(threadRefFrom(flags), { messageId: flags.messageId });\\n345\\t    }\\n346\\t    case \\\"turns list\\\":\\n347\\t      return (\\n348\\t        requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"turns list\\\") ??\\n349\\t        renderResult(await turns.listTurns(threadRefFrom(flags)))\\n350\\t      );\\n351\\t    case \\\"turns list-chunks\\\":\\n352\\t      return (\\n353\\t        requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"turns list-chunks\\\") ??\\n354\\t        renderResult(await turns.listChunks(threadRefFrom(flags)))\\n355\\t      );\\n356\\t    case \\\"turns list-queued-work\\\":\\n357\\t      return (\\n358\\t        requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"turns list-queued-work\\\") ??\\n359\\t        renderResult(await turns.listQueuedWork(threadRefFrom(flags)))\\n360\\t      );\\n361\\t    case \\\"turns report\\\": {\\n362\\t      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"turns report\\\");\\n363\\t      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n364\\t      const reportFlags: { notReady?: boolean; turnId?: string; chunkId?: string } = {};\\n365\\t      if (flags.notReady === true) reportFlags.notReady = true;\\n366\\t      if (flags.turnId !== undefined) reportFlags.turnId = flags.turnId;\\n367\\t      if (flags.chunkId !== undefined) reportFlags.chunkId = flags.chunkId;\\n368\\t      return runTurnsReport(threadRefFrom(flags), reportFlags);\\n369\\t    }\\n370\\t    case \\\"turns requeue\\\": {\\n371\\t      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"turns requeue\\\");\\n372\\t      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n373\\t      if (\\n374\\t        flags.subjectKind === undefined ||\\n375\\t        flags.subjectId === undefined ||\\n376\\t        flags.form === undefined\\n377\\t      ) {\\n378\\t        return renderCliError(\\n379\\t          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n380\\t          \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n381\\t          \\\"turns requeue requires --subject-kind, --subject-id, and --form\\\",\\n382\\t        );\\n383\\t      }\\n384\\t      if (flags.subjectKind !== \\\"turn\\\" && flags.subjectKind !== \\\"chunk\\\") {\\n385\\t        return renderCliError(\\n386\\t          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n387\\t          \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n388\\t          `--subject-kind must be \\\"turn\\\" or \\\"chunk\\\", got ${flags.subjectKind}`,\\n389\\t        );\\n390\\t      }\\n391\\t      return runTurnsRequeue(threadRefFrom(flags), {\\n392\\t        subjectKind: flags.subjectKind,\\n393\\t        subjectId: flags.subjectId,\\n394\\t        form: flags.form,\\n395\\t      });\\n396\\t    }\\n397\\t    case \\\"turns delete\\\": {\\n398\\t      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"turns delete\\\");\\n399\\t      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n400\\t      if (flags.turnId === undefined) {\\n401\\t        return renderCliError(\\n402\\t          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n403\\t          \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n404\\t          \\\"turns delete requires --turn (or --turn-id)\\\",\\n405\\t        );\\n406\\t      }\\n407\\t      return runTurnsDelete(threadRefFrom(flags), { turnId: flags.turnId });\\n408\\t    }\\n409\\t    case \\\"work drain\\\": {\\n410\\t      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"work drain\\\");\\n411\\t      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n412\\t      const drainFlags: { provider?: string; maxItems?: number } = {};\\n413\\t      if (flags.provider !== undefined) drainFlags.provider = flags.provider;\\n414\\t      if (flags.maxItems !== undefined) {\\n415\\t        const maxItems = Number(flags.maxItems);\\n416\\t        if (!Number.isInteger(maxItems) || maxItems <= 0) {\\n417\\t          return renderCliError(\\n418\\t            \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n419\\t            \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n420\\t            `--max-items must be a positive integer, got ${flags.maxItems}`,\\n421\\t          );\\n422\\t        }\\n423\\t        drainFlags.maxItems = maxItems;\\n424\\t      }\\n425\\t      return runWorkDrain(threadRefFrom(flags), drainFlags);\\n426\\t    }\\n427\\t    default:\\n428\\t      return renderCliError(\\n429\\t        \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n430\\t        \\\"unknown_command\\\",\\n431\\t        `unknown command: ${key}; run lhc --help`,\\n432\\t      );\\n433\\t  }\\n434\\t}\\n435\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"92b30fef-4ad7-45bb-a8e9-4c6f66be56bf\",\"uuid\":\"f80f4160-d3bc-4acd-b3ff-10e9aeab2f52\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-12T12:48:08.201Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\",\"content\":\"import { parseArgs } from \\\"node:util\\\";\\nimport * as intakeStream from \\\"../domains/intake-stream/index.js\\\";\\nimport * as messages from \\\"../domains/messages/index.js\\\";\\nimport * as threads from \\\"../domains/threads/index.js\\\";\\nimport * as turns from \\\"../domains/turns/index.js\\\";\\nimport type { MessageEventInput } from \\\"../domains/intake-stream/index.js\\\";\\nimport type { ThreadRef } from \\\"../domains/threads/index.js\\\";\\nimport type { OpResult } from \\\"../shared/errors.js\\\";\\nimport { renderCliError, renderResult, type CliResult } from \\\"./render.js\\\";\\nimport { runMessagesDelete, runMessagesEdit } from \\\"./messages-mutate.js\\\";\\nimport { runTurnsDelete } from \\\"./turns-mutate.js\\\";\\nimport {\\n  runMessagesReport,\\n  runMessagesRequeue,\\n  runTurnsReport,\\n  runTurnsRequeue,\\n  runWorkDrain,\\n} from \\\"./work.js\\\";\\nimport { runViewCommand } from \\\"./view.js\\\";\\n\\n// Stdin seam: in-process tests inject a reader; the binary reads the real\\n// process stdin. null means interactive (TTY) — distinct from empty input\\n// only in how it arises; both are refused with empty_stdin before any SDK\\n// call (the SDK itself can never return that code).\\nexport type StdinReader = () => Promise<string | null>;\\n\\nasync function readProcessStdin(): Promise<string | null> {\\n  if (process.stdin.isTTY) return null;\\n  process.stdin.setEncoding(\\\"utf8\\\");\\n  let data = \\\"\\\";\\n  for await (const chunk of process.stdin) data += String(chunk);\\n  return data;\\n}\\n\\nfunction stdinCallerError(code: \\\"empty_stdin\\\" | \\\"invalid_event\\\", reason: string): OpResult<never> {\\n  return { ok: false, error: { errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\", code, reason } };\\n}\\n\\nconst HELP = `lhc — Long Horizon Context CLI\\n\\nUsage:\\n  lhc threads new-thread --file-path <p> [--title <t>] [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc threads resolve --thread-id <id> [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc threads list [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc intake-stream message-events (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc intake-stream list-events (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc messages list (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc messages list-queued-work (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc messages report (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--not-ready] [--message-id <id>] [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc messages requeue (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) --message-id <id> --form <form> [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc messages edit (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) --message <id> --content <text> [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc messages delete (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) --message <id> [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc turns list (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc turns list-chunks (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc turns list-queued-work (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc turns report (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--not-ready] [--turn-id <id>] [--chunk-id <id>] [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc turns requeue (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) --subject-kind (turn|chunk) --subject-id <id> --form <form> [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc turns delete (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) --turn <id> [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc work drain (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--max-items <n>] [--provider <name>] [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc view pull (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--json] [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc view status (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--json] [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc view compact (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--profile <name>]\\n                   [--lower-bound <n>] [--full <n>] [--smooth <n>] [--detailed <n>] [--brief <n>]\\n                   [--no-sweep] [--json] [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc view sweep (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) [--json] [--registry <r>]\\n  lhc view materialize (--thread-id <id> | --file-path <p>) --out <path> [--format pi-session] [--registry <r>]\\n\\nEvery command prints the SDK result (value or error) as JSON and exits 0 on\\nsuccess, 1 on failure. message-events reads an events JSON array on stdin.\\nView commands need no provider; output is always JSON (--json accepted).\\nTwo exceptions on success: view pull prints the message array itself, and\\nview materialize prints the written path; their failures stay structured.\\n`;\\n\\ninterface ParsedFlags {\\n  threadId?: string;\\n  filePath?: string;\\n  title?: string;\\n  registryPath?: string;\\n  maxItems?: string;\\n  provider?: string;\\n  notReady?: boolean;\\n  messageId?: string;\\n  turnId?: string;\\n  chunkId?: string;\\n  form?: string;\\n  subjectKind?: string;\\n  subjectId?: string;\\n  content?: string;\\n}\\n\\n// strict parse rejects unknown/misspelled flags so they are named back to the\\n// caller, never silently dropped — the CLI boundary matching the SDK's\\n// closed-contract strictness. The failure is returned as data (not thrown) so\\n// runCli can render it as the structured usage error.\\ntype ParseFlagsResult =\\n  | { ok: true; flags: ParsedFlags }\\n  | { ok: false; unknownFlag: string };\\n\\nfunction parseFlags(args: readonly string[]): ParseFlagsResult {\\n  let values;\\n  try {\\n    ({ values } = parseArgs({\\n      args: [...args],\\n      options: {\\n        \\\"thread-id\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n        \\\"file-path\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n        title: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n        registry: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n        \\\"max-items\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n        provider: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n        \\\"not-ready\\\": { type: \\\"boolean\\\" },\\n        \\\"message-id\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n        \\\"turn-id\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n        \\\"chunk-id\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n        form: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n        \\\"subject-kind\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n        \\\"subject-id\\\": { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n        // `--message` / `--turn` are the mutation commands' spellings\\n        // (story/tech design); they parse into the same slots as\\n        // `--message-id` / `--turn-id`.\\n        message: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n        turn: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n        content: { type: \\\"string\\\" },\\n      },\\n      strict: true,\\n      allowPositionals: true,\\n    }));\\n  } catch (cause) {\\n    const message = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n    // parseArgs names the offending option in single quotes (e.g. Unknown\\n    // option '--file-pth'); surface that token, falling back to the message.\\n    const named = /'([^']+)'/.exec(message);\\n    return { ok: false, unknownFlag: named?.[1] ?? message };\\n  }\\n  const flags: ParsedFlags = {};\\n  if (typeof values[\\\"thread-id\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.threadId = values[\\\"thread-id\\\"];\\n  if (typeof values[\\\"file-path\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.filePath = values[\\\"file-path\\\"];\\n  if (typeof values.title === \\\"string\\\") flags.title = values.title;\\n  if (typeof values.registry === \\\"string\\\") flags.registryPath = values.registry;\\n  if (typeof values[\\\"max-items\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.maxItems = values[\\\"max-items\\\"];\\n  if (typeof values.provider === \\\"string\\\") flags.provider = values.provider;\\n  if (values[\\\"not-ready\\\"] === true) flags.notReady = true;\\n  if (typeof values[\\\"message-id\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.messageId = values[\\\"message-id\\\"];\\n  if (typeof values.message === \\\"string\\\") flags.messageId = values.message;\\n  if (typeof values.content === \\\"string\\\") flags.content = values.content;\\n  if (typeof values[\\\"turn-id\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.turnId = values[\\\"turn-id\\\"];\\n  if (typeof values.turn === \\\"string\\\") flags.turnId = values.turn;\\n  if (typeof values[\\\"chunk-id\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.chunkId = values[\\\"chunk-id\\\"];\\n  if (typeof values.form === \\\"string\\\") flags.form = values.form;\\n  if (typeof values[\\\"subject-kind\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.subjectKind = values[\\\"subject-kind\\\"];\\n  if (typeof values[\\\"subject-id\\\"] === \\\"string\\\") flags.subjectId = values[\\\"subject-id\\\"];\\n  return { ok: true, flags };\\n}\\n\\n// The read commands take a thread reference but no stdin; a missing reference\\n// is a usage error named before any SDK call, matching the intake commands.\\nfunction requireThreadRef(flags: ParsedFlags, command: string): CliResult | undefined {\\n  if (flags.threadId === undefined && flags.filePath === undefined) {\\n    return renderCliError(\\n      \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n      \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n      `${command} requires --thread-id or --file-path`,\\n    );\\n  }\\n  return undefined;\\n}\\n\\nfunction threadRefFrom(flags: ParsedFlags): ThreadRef {\\n  if (flags.threadId !== undefined) {\\n    return flags.registryPath !== undefined\\n      ? { threadId: flags.threadId, registryPath: flags.registryPath }\\n      : { threadId: flags.threadId };\\n  }\\n  return { filePath: flags.filePath ?? \\\"\\\" };\\n}\\n\\nexport async function runCli(\\n  argv: readonly string[],\\n  readStdin: StdinReader = readProcessStdin,\\n): Promise<CliResult> {\\n  if (argv.length === 0) {\\n    return renderCliError(\\\"caller_error\\\", \\\"unknown_command\\\", \\\"no command given; run lhc --help\\\");\\n  }\\n  if (argv[0] === \\\"--help\\\" || argv[0] === \\\"-h\\\") {\\n    return { exitCode: 0, stdout: HELP, stderr: \\\"\\\" };\\n  }\\n\\n  const [group, command, ...rest] = argv;\\n  // The view group parses its own flag surface (band overrides, --out,\\n  // --format) — routed before the shared parse so its flags never widen the\\n  // other commands' accepted set.\\n  if (group === \\\"view\\\") {\\n    return runViewCommand(command, rest);\\n  }\\n  const key = command === undefined ? group : `${group} ${command}`;\\n  const parsed = parseFlags(command === undefined ? [] : rest);\\n  if (!parsed.ok) {\\n    return renderCliError(\\n      \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n      \\\"unknown_flag\\\",\\n      `unknown flag: ${parsed.unknownFlag}; run lhc --help`,\\n    );\\n  }\\n  const flags = parsed.flags;\\n\\n  switch (key) {\\n    case \\\"threads new-thread\\\": {\\n      // Guard here: an empty path reaching node:sqlite opens a temp database\\n      // instead of failing, so the adapter refuses before any SDK call.\\n      if (flags.filePath === undefined) {\\n        return renderCliError(\\\"caller_error\\\", \\\"missing_flag\\\", \\\"threads new-thread requires --file-path\\\");\\n      }\\n      const input: Parameters<typeof threads.newThread>[0] = {\\n        filePath: flags.filePath,\\n      };\\n      if (flags.title !== undefined) input.title = flags.title;\\n      if (flags.registryPath !== undefined) input.registryPath = flags.registryPath;\\n      return renderResult(await threads.newThread(input));\\n    }\\n    case \\\"threads resolve\\\": {\\n      if (flags.threadId === undefined) {\\n        return renderCliError(\\\"caller_error\\\", \\\"missing_flag\\\", \\\"threads resolve requires --thread-id\\\");\\n      }\\n      const input: Parameters<typeof threads.resolve>[0] = {\\n        threadId: flags.threadId,\\n      };\\n      if (flags.registryPath !== undefined) input.registryPath = flags.registryPath;\\n      return renderResult(await threads.resolve(input));\\n    }\\n    case \\\"threads list\\\": {\\n      return renderResult(\\n        await threads.listThreads(\\n          flags.registryPath !== undefined ? { registryPath: flags.registryPath } : undefined,\\n        ),\\n      );\\n    }\\n    case \\\"intake-stream message-events\\\": {\\n      if (flags.threadId === undefined && flags.filePath === undefined) {\\n        return renderCliError(\\n          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n          \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n          \\\"intake-stream message-events requires --thread-id or --file-path\\\",\\n        );\\n      }\\n      const text = await readStdin();\\n      if (text === null || text.trim() === \\\"\\\") {\\n        return renderResult(\\n          stdinCallerError(\\n            \\\"empty_stdin\\\",\\n            \\\"message-events expects an events JSON array on stdin; stdin was a TTY or empty\\\",\\n          ),\\n        );\\n      }\\n      let parsed: unknown;\\n      try {\\n        parsed = JSON.parse(text);\\n      } catch (cause) {\\n        const detail = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n        return renderResult(\\n          stdinCallerError(\\\"invalid_event\\\", `stdin is not valid JSON: ${detail}`),\\n        );\\n      }\\n      if (!Array.isArray(parsed)) {\\n        return renderResult(\\n          stdinCallerError(\\\"invalid_event\\\", \\\"stdin must be a JSON array of events\\\"),\\n        );\\n      }\\n      return renderResult(\\n        await intakeStream.messageEvents(\\n          threadRefFrom(flags),\\n          parsed as readonly MessageEventInput[],\\n        ),\\n      );\\n    }\\n    case \\\"intake-stream list-events\\\": {\\n      if (flags.threadId === undefined && flags.filePath === undefined) {\\n        return renderCliError(\\n          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n          \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n          \\\"intake-stream list-events requires --thread-id or --file-path\\\",\\n        );\\n      }\\n      return renderResult(await intakeStream.listEvents(threadRefFrom(flags)));\\n    }\\n    case \\\"messages list\\\":\\n      return (\\n        requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"messages list\\\") ??\\n        renderResult(await messages.listMessages(threadRefFrom(flags)))\\n      );\\n    case \\\"messages list-queued-work\\\":\\n      return (\\n        requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"messages list-queued-work\\\") ??\\n        renderResult(await messages.listQueuedWork(threadRefFrom(flags)))\\n      );\\n    case \\\"messages report\\\": {\\n      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"messages report\\\");\\n      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n      const reportFlags: { notReady?: boolean; messageId?: string } = {};\\n      if (flags.notReady === true) reportFlags.notReady = true;\\n      if (flags.messageId !== undefined) reportFlags.messageId = flags.messageId;\\n      return runMessagesReport(threadRefFrom(flags), reportFlags);\\n    }\\n    case \\\"messages requeue\\\": {\\n      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"messages requeue\\\");\\n      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n      if (flags.messageId === undefined || flags.form === undefined) {\\n        return renderCliError(\\n          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n          \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n          \\\"messages requeue requires --message-id and --form\\\",\\n        );\\n      }\\n      return runMessagesRequeue(threadRefFrom(flags), {\\n        messageId: flags.messageId,\\n        form: flags.form,\\n      });\\n    }\\n    case \\\"messages edit\\\": {\\n      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"messages edit\\\");\\n      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n      if (flags.messageId === undefined || flags.content === undefined) {\\n        return renderCliError(\\n          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n          \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n          \\\"messages edit requires --message (or --message-id) and --content\\\",\\n        );\\n      }\\n      return runMessagesEdit(threadRefFrom(flags), {\\n        messageId: flags.messageId,\\n        content: flags.content,\\n      });\\n    }\\n    case \\\"messages delete\\\": {\\n      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"messages delete\\\");\\n      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n      if (flags.messageId === undefined) {\\n        return renderCliError(\\n          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n          \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n          \\\"messages delete requires --message (or --message-id)\\\",\\n        );\\n      }\\n      return runMessagesDelete(threadRefFrom(flags), { messageId: flags.messageId });\\n    }\\n    case \\\"turns list\\\":\\n      return (\\n        requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"turns list\\\") ??\\n        renderResult(await turns.listTurns(threadRefFrom(flags)))\\n      );\\n    case \\\"turns list-chunks\\\":\\n      return (\\n        requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"turns list-chunks\\\") ??\\n        renderResult(await turns.listChunks(threadRefFrom(flags)))\\n      );\\n    case \\\"turns list-queued-work\\\":\\n      return (\\n        requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"turns list-queued-work\\\") ??\\n        renderResult(await turns.listQueuedWork(threadRefFrom(flags)))\\n      );\\n    case \\\"turns report\\\": {\\n      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"turns report\\\");\\n      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n      const reportFlags: { notReady?: boolean; turnId?: string; chunkId?: string } = {};\\n      if (flags.notReady === true) reportFlags.notReady = true;\\n      if (flags.turnId !== undefined) reportFlags.turnId = flags.turnId;\\n      if (flags.chunkId !== undefined) reportFlags.chunkId = flags.chunkId;\\n      return runTurnsReport(threadRefFrom(flags), reportFlags);\\n    }\\n    case \\\"turns requeue\\\": {\\n      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"turns requeue\\\");\\n      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n      if (\\n        flags.subjectKind === undefined ||\\n        flags.subjectId === undefined ||\\n        flags.form === undefined\\n      ) {\\n        return renderCliError(\\n          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n          \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n          \\\"turns requeue requires --subject-kind, --subject-id, and --form\\\",\\n        );\\n      }\\n      if (flags.subjectKind !== \\\"turn\\\" && flags.subjectKind !== \\\"chunk\\\") {\\n        return renderCliError(\\n          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n          \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n          `--subject-kind must be \\\"turn\\\" or \\\"chunk\\\", got ${flags.subjectKind}`,\\n        );\\n      }\\n      return runTurnsRequeue(threadRefFrom(flags), {\\n        subjectKind: flags.subjectKind,\\n        subjectId: flags.subjectId,\\n        form: flags.form,\\n      });\\n    }\\n    case \\\"turns delete\\\": {\\n      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"turns delete\\\");\\n      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n      if (flags.turnId === undefined) {\\n        return renderCliError(\\n          \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n          \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n          \\\"turns delete requires --turn (or --turn-id)\\\",\\n        );\\n      }\\n      return runTurnsDelete(threadRefFrom(flags), { turnId: flags.turnId });\\n    }\\n    case \\\"work drain\\\": {\\n      const missingRef = requireThreadRef(flags, \\\"work drain\\\");\\n      if (missingRef !== undefined) return missingRef;\\n      const drainFlags: { provider?: string; maxItems?: number } = {};\\n      if (flags.provider !== undefined) drainFlags.provider = flags.provider;\\n      if (flags.maxItems !== undefined) {\\n        const maxItems = Number(flags.maxItems);\\n        if (!Number.isInteger(maxItems) || maxItems <= 0) {\\n          return renderCliError(\\n            \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n            \\\"missing_flag\\\",\\n            `--max-items must be a positive integer, got ${flags.maxItems}`,\\n          );\\n        }\\n        drainFlags.maxItems = maxItems;\\n      }\\n      return runWorkDrain(threadRefFrom(flags), drainFlags);\\n    }\\n    default:\\n      return renderCliError(\\n        \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n        \\\"unknown_command\\\",\\n        `unknown command: ${key}; run lhc --help`,\\n      );\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"numLines\":435,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":435}}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:155:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01UmQaiZyw5c356iwfpkZLa2\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t// Message-domain reads for derivation (Flow 2): the handler's view of its\\n2\\t// source message and the call-id pairing reads — the only reach a\\n3\\t// message-level handler has beyond its own message (AC-2.5). Also the\\n4\\t// late-result repair lookup intake's projection step runs (AC-2.8): one\\n5\\t// indexed query by call id, never a scan (the v5 expression index on\\n6\\t// message_block covers it) and never a drain-time sweep or read-time join.\\n7\\t// Completion writes for message forms ride the work-queue util's `complete`\\n8\\t// (Story 1): UPDATE-only with the source-version check — no write path here.\\n9\\t// Read-back of message-owned form rows (the listMessages join) also lives\\n10\\t// here: stored state returned as stored — never re-derived on read.\\n11\\timport type { DatabaseSync } from \\\"node:sqlite\\\";\\n12\\timport type {\\n13\\t  DependencyGap,\\n14\\t  DerivedForm,\\n15\\t  DerivedFormMetadata,\\n16\\t  DerivedFormState,\\n17\\t  FormKind,\\n18\\t  FormReportEntry,\\n19\\t} from \\\"../../../shared/derivation.js\\\";\\n20\\timport { reportEntryFromRow, type RawReportRow } from \\\"../../../shared/report.js\\\";\\n21\\t\\n22\\texport interface MessageSource {\\n23\\t  messageId: string;\\n24\\t  kind: string;\\n25\\t  blocks: Array<{ blockType: string; content: Record<string, unknown> }>;\\n26\\t}\\n27\\t\\n28\\texport function readMessageSource(\\n29\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\n30\\t  messageId: string,\\n31\\t): MessageSource | undefined {\\n32\\t  const row = db\\n33\\t    .prepare(`SELECT kind FROM message WHERE message_id = ?`)\\n34\\t    .get(messageId) as unknown as { kind: string } | undefined;\\n35\\t  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\n36\\t  const blocks = db\\n37\\t    .prepare(\\n38\\t      `SELECT block_type, content FROM message_block\\n39\\t       WHERE message_id = ? ORDER BY block_index`,\\n40\\t    )\\n41\\t    .all(messageId) as unknown as Array<{ block_type: string; content: string }>;\\n42\\t  return {\\n43\\t    messageId,\\n44\\t    kind: row.kind,\\n45\\t    blocks: blocks.map((block) => ({\\n46\\t      blockType: block.block_type,\\n47\\t      content: JSON.parse(block.content) as Record<string, unknown>,\\n48\\t    })),\\n49\\t  };\\n50\\t}\\n51\\t\\n52\\tinterface RawFormRow {\\n53\\t  subject_id: string;\\n54\\t  form: string;\\n55\\t  state: string;\\n56\\t  content: string | null;\\n57\\t  reason: string | null;\\n58\\t  metadata: string | null;\\n59\\t  source_version: number | bigint;\\n60\\t  gaps: string | null;\\n61\\t  derived_at: string | null;\\n62\\t}\\n63\\t\\n64\\t// Every message-owned derived-form row, grouped by message id — the form\\n65\\t// read-back joined onto message reads (AC-2.1's \\\"readable alongside the\\n66\\t// message\\\"). Rows come back exactly as the queue landed them: state, content,\\n67\\t// reason, mechanically stamped metadata; nothing is derived at read time.\\n68\\texport function readMessageForms(db: DatabaseSync): Map<string, DerivedForm[]> {\\n69\\t  const rows = db\\n70\\t    .prepare(\\n71\\t      `SELECT subject_id, form, state, content, reason, metadata,\\n72\\t              source_version, gaps, derived_at\\n73\\t       FROM derived_form WHERE subject_kind = 'message'\\n74\\t       ORDER BY subject_id, form`,\\n75\\t    )\\n76\\t    .all() as unknown as RawFormRow[];\\n77\\t  const byMessage = new Map<string, DerivedForm[]>();\\n78\\t  for (const row of rows) {\\n79\\t    const record: DerivedForm = {\\n80\\t      subjectKind: \\\"message\\\",\\n81\\t      subjectId: row.subject_id,\\n82\\t      form: row.form as FormKind,\\n83\\t      state: row.state as DerivedFormState,\\n84\\t      sourceVersion: Number(row.source_version),\\n85\\t    };\\n86\\t    if (row.content !== null) record.content = row.content;\\n87\\t    if (row.reason !== null) record.reason = row.reason;\\n88\\t    if (row.metadata !== null) {\\n89\\t      record.metadata = JSON.parse(row.metadata) as DerivedFormMetadata;\\n90\\t    }\\n91\\t    if (row.gaps !== null) record.gaps = JSON.parse(row.gaps) as DependencyGap[];\\n92\\t    if (row.derived_at !== null) record.derivedAt = row.derived_at;\\n93\\t    const forms = byMessage.get(row.subject_id) ?? [];\\n94\\t    forms.push(record);\\n95\\t    byMessage.set(row.subject_id, forms);\\n96\\t  }\\n97\\t  return byMessage;\\n98\\t}\\n99\\t\\n100\\t// One form row by exact key — the requeue operation's refusal read (missing\\n101\\t// row, blocked state, current source version). State returned as stored.\\n102\\texport function readMessageFormRow(\\n103\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\n104\\t  messageId: string,\\n105\\t  form: FormKind,\\n106\\t): { state: DerivedFormState; reason?: string; sourceVersion: number } | undefined {\\n107\\t  const row = db\\n108\\t    .prepare(\\n109\\t      `SELECT state, reason, source_version FROM derived_form\\n110\\t       WHERE subject_kind = 'message' AND subject_id = ? AND form = ?`,\\n111\\t    )\\n112\\t    .get(messageId, form) as unknown as\\n113\\t    | { state: string; reason: string | null; source_version: number | bigint }\\n114\\t    | undefined;\\n115\\t  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\n116\\t  const view: { state: DerivedFormState; reason?: string; sourceVersion: number } = {\\n117\\t    state: row.state as DerivedFormState,\\n118\\t    sourceVersion: Number(row.source_version),\\n119\\t  };\\n120\\t  if (row.reason !== null) view.reason = row.reason;\\n121\\t  return view;\\n122\\t}\\n123\\t\\n124\\t// The message owner's report (Flow 4): one query — message-owned form rows\\n125\\t// LEFT JOINed with the live work_item still targeting each form at its\\n126\\t// current source version, if any (DD-1: only live rows exist; terminal\\n127\\t// outcomes already live on the form). No N+1, no in-memory assembly beyond\\n128\\t// row mapping. The form→kind CASE is the owner's own queue-site mapping\\n129\\t// (MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS) inverted.\\n130\\texport function reportMessageForms(\\n131\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\n132\\t  opts: { notReady?: boolean; messageId?: string } = {},\\n133\\t): FormReportEntry[] {\\n134\\t  const conditions = [\\\"df.subject_kind = 'message'\\\"];\\n135\\t  const params: string[] = [];\\n136\\t  if (opts.messageId !== undefined) {\\n137\\t    conditions.push(\\\"df.subject_id = ?\\\");\\n138\\t    params.push(opts.messageId);\\n139\\t  }\\n140\\t  // notReady is exact set equality by construction: every state but ready.\\n141\\t  if (opts.notReady === true) conditions.push(\\\"df.state <> 'ready'\\\");\\n142\\t  const rows = db\\n143\\t    .prepare(\\n144\\t      `SELECT df.subject_id, df.form, df.state, df.content, df.reason, df.metadata,\\n145\\t              df.source_version, df.gaps, df.derived_at,\\n146\\t              w.status AS queue_status, w.attempts AS queue_attempts,\\n147\\t              w.last_error AS queue_last_error, w.eligible_at AS queue_eligible_at\\n148\\t       FROM derived_form df\\n149\\t       LEFT JOIN work_item w\\n150\\t         ON w.status IN ('queued', 'claimed')\\n151\\t        AND w.kind = CASE df.form WHEN 'smoothed_prompt' THEN 'prompt_smoothing' ELSE df.form END\\n152\\t        AND json_extract(w.source_ref, '$.messageId') = df.subject_id\\n153\\t        AND COALESCE(json_extract(w.payload, '$.sourceVersion'), 1) = df.source_version\\n154\\t       WHERE ${conditions.join(\\\" AND \\\")}\\n155\\t       ORDER BY df.subject_id, df.form`,\\n156\\t    )\\n157\\t    .all(...params) as unknown as RawReportRow[];\\n158\\t  return rows.map((row) => reportEntryFromRow(\\\"message\\\", row));\\n159\\t}\\n160\\t\\n161\\t// The call-id pairing reads. Earliest-recorded block wins if a call id were\\n162\\t// ever repeated; in a well-formed record the pair is unique. Deleted messages\\n163\\t// are excluded (tech-design §Mechanics' deleted-read rule, epic-fix-001):\\n164\\t// composition inputs and derivation reads never see deleted records, so a\\n165\\t// tool_call whose paired result has been deleted reads no pair and derives\\n166\\t// outcome `unknown` — never the dead result's outcome.\\n167\\tfunction findPairedBlock(\\n168\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\n169\\t  blockType: \\\"tool_call\\\" | \\\"tool_result\\\",\\n170\\t  toolCallId: string,\\n171\\t): Record<string, unknown> | undefined {\\n172\\t  const row = db\\n173\\t    .prepare(\\n174\\t      `SELECT b.content FROM message_block b\\n175\\t       JOIN message m ON m.message_id = b.message_id AND m.deleted_at IS NULL\\n176\\t       WHERE b.block_type = ? AND json_extract(b.content, '$.toolCallId') = ?\\n177\\t       ORDER BY m.source_event_order LIMIT 1`,\\n178\\t    )\\n179\\t    .get(blockType, toolCallId) as unknown as { content: string } | undefined;\\n180\\t  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\n181\\t  return JSON.parse(row.content) as Record<string, unknown>;\\n182\\t}\\n183\\t\\n184\\texport function findPairedToolResult(\\n185\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\n186\\t  toolCallId: string,\\n187\\t): { content: string; isError: boolean } | undefined {\\n188\\t  const block = findPairedBlock(db, \\\"tool_result\\\", toolCallId);\\n189\\t  if (block === undefined) return undefined;\\n190\\t  return {\\n191\\t    content: typeof block[\\\"content\\\"] === \\\"string\\\" ? block[\\\"content\\\"] : \\\"\\\",\\n192\\t    isError: block[\\\"isError\\\"] === true,\\n193\\t  };\\n194\\t}\\n195\\t\\n196\\texport function findPairedToolCall(\\n197\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\n198\\t  toolCallId: string,\\n199\\t): { toolName: string } | undefined {\\n200\\t  const block = findPairedBlock(db, \\\"tool_call\\\", toolCallId);\\n201\\t  if (block === undefined) return undefined;\\n202\\t  return { toolName: typeof block[\\\"toolName\\\"] === \\\"string\\\" ? block[\\\"toolName\\\"] : \\\"\\\" };\\n203\\t}\\n204\\t\\n205\\t// AC-2.8's intake-time lookup: does the paired call's summary sit landed with\\n206\\t// outcome \\\"unknown\\\"? Pending rows carry NULL metadata and never match, so the\\n207\\t// common case — call and result in one batch, summary not yet run — never\\n208\\t// triggers a requeue. Returns the call's message id and the form's current\\n209\\t// source version (the requeue enqueues at version + 1: the pair is the\\n210\\t// summary's source, and a source completing follows clear-and-regenerate).\\n211\\texport function findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary(\\n212\\t  db: DatabaseSync,\\n213\\t  toolCallId: string,\\n214\\t): { messageId: string; sourceVersion: number } | undefined {\\n215\\t  const row = db\\n216\\t    .prepare(\\n217\\t      `SELECT df.subject_id, df.source_version FROM message_block b\\n218\\t       JOIN message m ON m.message_id = b.message_id AND m.deleted_at IS NULL\\n219\\t       JOIN derived_form df ON df.subject_kind = 'message'\\n220\\t         AND df.subject_id = b.message_id AND df.form = 'tool_call_summary'\\n221\\t       WHERE b.block_type = 'tool_call' AND json_extract(b.content, '$.toolCallId') = ?\\n222\\t         AND json_extract(df.metadata, '$.outcome') = 'unknown'\\n223\\t       LIMIT 1`,\\n224\\t    )\\n225\\t    .get(toolCallId) as unknown as\\n226\\t    | { subject_id: string; source_version: number | bigint }\\n227\\t    | undefined;\\n228\\t  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\n229\\t  return { messageId: row.subject_id, sourceVersion: Number(row.source_version) };\\n230\\t}\\n231\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"92b30fef-4ad7-45bb-a8e9-4c6f66be56bf\",\"uuid\":\"9f8462bf-a58a-44b2-97a9-ec741b8cfbc6\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-12T12:48:25.848Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/forms.ts\",\"content\":\"// Message-domain reads for derivation (Flow 2): the handler's view of its\\n// source message and the call-id pairing reads — the only reach a\\n// message-level handler has beyond its own message (AC-2.5). Also the\\n// late-result repair lookup intake's projection step runs (AC-2.8): one\\n// indexed query by call id, never a scan (the v5 expression index on\\n// message_block covers it) and never a drain-time sweep or read-time join.\\n// Completion writes for message forms ride the work-queue util's `complete`\\n// (Story 1): UPDATE-only with the source-version check — no write path here.\\n// Read-back of message-owned form rows (the listMessages join) also lives\\n// here: stored state returned as stored — never re-derived on read.\\nimport type { DatabaseSync } from \\\"node:sqlite\\\";\\nimport type {\\n  DependencyGap,\\n  DerivedForm,\\n  DerivedFormMetadata,\\n  DerivedFormState,\\n  FormKind,\\n  FormReportEntry,\\n} from \\\"../../../shared/derivation.js\\\";\\nimport { reportEntryFromRow, type RawReportRow } from \\\"../../../shared/report.js\\\";\\n\\nexport interface MessageSource {\\n  messageId: string;\\n  kind: string;\\n  blocks: Array<{ blockType: string; content: Record<string, unknown> }>;\\n}\\n\\nexport function readMessageSource(\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\n  messageId: string,\\n): MessageSource | undefined {\\n  const row = db\\n    .prepare(`SELECT kind FROM message WHERE message_id = ?`)\\n    .get(messageId) as unknown as { kind: string } | undefined;\\n  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\n  const blocks = db\\n    .prepare(\\n      `SELECT block_type, content FROM message_block\\n       WHERE message_id = ? ORDER BY block_index`,\\n    )\\n    .all(messageId) as unknown as Array<{ block_type: string; content: string }>;\\n  return {\\n    messageId,\\n    kind: row.kind,\\n    blocks: blocks.map((block) => ({\\n      blockType: block.block_type,\\n      content: JSON.parse(block.content) as Record<string, unknown>,\\n    })),\\n  };\\n}\\n\\ninterface RawFormRow {\\n  subject_id: string;\\n  form: string;\\n  state: string;\\n  content: string | null;\\n  reason: string | null;\\n  metadata: string | null;\\n  source_version: number | bigint;\\n  gaps: string | null;\\n  derived_at: string | null;\\n}\\n\\n// Every message-owned derived-form row, grouped by message id — the form\\n// read-back joined onto message reads (AC-2.1's \\\"readable alongside the\\n// message\\\"). Rows come back exactly as the queue landed them: state, content,\\n// reason, mechanically stamped metadata; nothing is derived at read time.\\nexport function readMessageForms(db: DatabaseSync): Map<string, DerivedForm[]> {\\n  const rows = db\\n    .prepare(\\n      `SELECT subject_id, form, state, content, reason, metadata,\\n              source_version, gaps, derived_at\\n       FROM derived_form WHERE subject_kind = 'message'\\n       ORDER BY subject_id, form`,\\n    )\\n    .all() as unknown as RawFormRow[];\\n  const byMessage = new Map<string, DerivedForm[]>();\\n  for (const row of rows) {\\n    const record: DerivedForm = {\\n      subjectKind: \\\"message\\\",\\n      subjectId: row.subject_id,\\n      form: row.form as FormKind,\\n      state: row.state as DerivedFormState,\\n      sourceVersion: Number(row.source_version),\\n    };\\n    if (row.content !== null) record.content = row.content;\\n    if (row.reason !== null) record.reason = row.reason;\\n    if (row.metadata !== null) {\\n      record.metadata = JSON.parse(row.metadata) as DerivedFormMetadata;\\n    }\\n    if (row.gaps !== null) record.gaps = JSON.parse(row.gaps) as DependencyGap[];\\n    if (row.derived_at !== null) record.derivedAt = row.derived_at;\\n    const forms = byMessage.get(row.subject_id) ?? [];\\n    forms.push(record);\\n    byMessage.set(row.subject_id, forms);\\n  }\\n  return byMessage;\\n}\\n\\n// One form row by exact key — the requeue operation's refusal read (missing\\n// row, blocked state, current source version). State returned as stored.\\nexport function readMessageFormRow(\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\n  messageId: string,\\n  form: FormKind,\\n): { state: DerivedFormState; reason?: string; sourceVersion: number } | undefined {\\n  const row = db\\n    .prepare(\\n      `SELECT state, reason, source_version FROM derived_form\\n       WHERE subject_kind = 'message' AND subject_id = ? AND form = ?`,\\n    )\\n    .get(messageId, form) as unknown as\\n    | { state: string; reason: string | null; source_version: number | bigint }\\n    | undefined;\\n  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\n  const view: { state: DerivedFormState; reason?: string; sourceVersion: number } = {\\n    state: row.state as DerivedFormState,\\n    sourceVersion: Number(row.source_version),\\n  };\\n  if (row.reason !== null) view.reason = row.reason;\\n  return view;\\n}\\n\\n// The message owner's report (Flow 4): one query — message-owned form rows\\n// LEFT JOINed with the live work_item still targeting each form at its\\n// current source version, if any (DD-1: only live rows exist; terminal\\n// outcomes already live on the form). No N+1, no in-memory assembly beyond\\n// row mapping. The form→kind CASE is the owner's own queue-site mapping\\n// (MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS) inverted.\\nexport function reportMessageForms(\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\n  opts: { notReady?: boolean; messageId?: string } = {},\\n): FormReportEntry[] {\\n  const conditions = [\\\"df.subject_kind = 'message'\\\"];\\n  const params: string[] = [];\\n  if (opts.messageId !== undefined) {\\n    conditions.push(\\\"df.subject_id = ?\\\");\\n    params.push(opts.messageId);\\n  }\\n  // notReady is exact set equality by construction: every state but ready.\\n  if (opts.notReady === true) conditions.push(\\\"df.state <> 'ready'\\\");\\n  const rows = db\\n    .prepare(\\n      `SELECT df.subject_id, df.form, df.state, df.content, df.reason, df.metadata,\\n              df.source_version, df.gaps, df.derived_at,\\n              w.status AS queue_status, w.attempts AS queue_attempts,\\n              w.last_error AS queue_last_error, w.eligible_at AS queue_eligible_at\\n       FROM derived_form df\\n       LEFT JOIN work_item w\\n         ON w.status IN ('queued', 'claimed')\\n        AND w.kind = CASE df.form WHEN 'smoothed_prompt' THEN 'prompt_smoothing' ELSE df.form END\\n        AND json_extract(w.source_ref, '$.messageId') = df.subject_id\\n        AND COALESCE(json_extract(w.payload, '$.sourceVersion'), 1) = df.source_version\\n       WHERE ${conditions.join(\\\" AND \\\")}\\n       ORDER BY df.subject_id, df.form`,\\n    )\\n    .all(...params) as unknown as RawReportRow[];\\n  return rows.map((row) => reportEntryFromRow(\\\"message\\\", row));\\n}\\n\\n// The call-id pairing reads. Earliest-recorded block wins if a call id were\\n// ever repeated; in a well-formed record the pair is unique. Deleted messages\\n// are excluded (tech-design §Mechanics' deleted-read rule, epic-fix-001):\\n// composition inputs and derivation reads never see deleted records, so a\\n// tool_call whose paired result has been deleted reads no pair and derives\\n// outcome `unknown` — never the dead result's outcome.\\nfunction findPairedBlock(\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\n  blockType: \\\"tool_call\\\" | \\\"tool_result\\\",\\n  toolCallId: string,\\n): Record<string, unknown> | undefined {\\n  const row = db\\n    .prepare(\\n      `SELECT b.content FROM message_block b\\n       JOIN message m ON m.message_id = b.message_id AND m.deleted_at IS NULL\\n       WHERE b.block_type = ? AND json_extract(b.content, '$.toolCallId') = ?\\n       ORDER BY m.source_event_order LIMIT 1`,\\n    )\\n    .get(blockType, toolCallId) as unknown as { content: string } | undefined;\\n  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\n  return JSON.parse(row.content) as Record<string, unknown>;\\n}\\n\\nexport function findPairedToolResult(\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\n  toolCallId: string,\\n): { content: string; isError: boolean } | undefined {\\n  const block = findPairedBlock(db, \\\"tool_result\\\", toolCallId);\\n  if (block === undefined) return undefined;\\n  return {\\n    content: typeof block[\\\"content\\\"] === \\\"string\\\" ? block[\\\"content\\\"] : \\\"\\\",\\n    isError: block[\\\"isError\\\"] === true,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function findPairedToolCall(\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\n  toolCallId: string,\\n): { toolName: string } | undefined {\\n  const block = findPairedBlock(db, \\\"tool_call\\\", toolCallId);\\n  if (block === undefined) return undefined;\\n  return { toolName: typeof block[\\\"toolName\\\"] === \\\"string\\\" ? block[\\\"toolName\\\"] : \\\"\\\" };\\n}\\n\\n// AC-2.8's intake-time lookup: does the paired call's summary sit landed with\\n// outcome \\\"unknown\\\"? Pending rows carry NULL metadata and never match, so the\\n// common case — call and result in one batch, summary not yet run — never\\n// triggers a requeue. Returns the call's message id and the form's current\\n// source version (the requeue enqueues at version + 1: the pair is the\\n// summary's source, and a source completing follows clear-and-regenerate).\\nexport function findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary(\\n  db: DatabaseSync,\\n  toolCallId: string,\\n): { messageId: string; sourceVersion: number } | undefined {\\n  const row = db\\n    .prepare(\\n      `SELECT df.subject_id, df.source_version FROM message_block b\\n       JOIN message m ON m.message_id = b.message_id AND m.deleted_at IS NULL\\n       JOIN derived_form df ON df.subject_kind = 'message'\\n         AND df.subject_id = b.message_id AND df.form = 'tool_call_summary'\\n       WHERE b.block_type = 'tool_call' AND json_extract(b.content, '$.toolCallId') = ?\\n         AND json_extract(df.metadata, '$.outcome') = 'unknown'\\n       LIMIT 1`,\\n    )\\n    .get(toolCallId) as unknown as\\n    | { subject_id: string; source_version: number | bigint }\\n    | undefined;\\n  if (row === undefined) return undefined;\\n  return { messageId: row.subject_id, sourceVersion: Number(row.source_version) };\\n}\\n\",\"numLines\":231,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":231}}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:162:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_017GcXhzz2RqjrhAruEQkMHS\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"78:export interface FormReportEntry extends DerivedForm {\\n79-  queue?: {\\n80-    status: \\\"queued\\\" | \\\"claimed\\\";\\n81-    attempts: number;\\n82-    lastError?: string;\\n83-    eligibleAt?: string;\\n84-  };\\n85-}\\n86-\\n87-// ── provider seam (DD-7) ─────────────────────────────────────────\\n88-// Every operation returns content or a structured failure carrying\\n89-// retryable-or-not; classification is the adapter's duty.\\n90-export type ProviderResult =\\n91-  | { ok: true; text: string }\\n92-  | { ok: false; retryable: boolean; reason: string };\\n93-\\n94-// Message kinds a rendering part can carry — mirrors the intake event-kind\\n95-// vocabulary minus turn_end (turn_end never projects a message). Mirrored\\n96-// rather than imported: shared/ may not import domains/.\\n97-export type RenderingPartKind =\\n98-  | \\\"user_prompt\\\"\\n99-  | \\\"assistant_text\\\"\\n100-  | \\\"assistant_thinking\\\"\\n101-  | \\\"runtime_note\\\"\\n102-  | \\\"tool_call\\\"\\n103-  | \\\"tool_result\\\";\\n104-\\n105-export interface RenderingPart {\\n106-  messageId: string;\\n107-  kind: RenderingPartKind;\\n108-  text: string; // ready form content, or raw/truncated fallback\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"92b30fef-4ad7-45bb-a8e9-4c6f66be56bf\",\"uuid\":\"805dc902-7e60-4bdd-a70f-96306795e2df\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-12T12:48:26.509Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"78:export interface FormReportEntry extends DerivedForm {\\n79-  queue?: {\\n80-    status: \\\"queued\\\" | \\\"claimed\\\";\\n81-    attempts: number;\\n82-    lastError?: string;\\n83-    eligibleAt?: string;\\n84-  };\\n85-}\\n86-\\n87-// ── provider seam (DD-7) ─────────────────────────────────────────\\n88-// Every operation returns content or a structured failure carrying\\n89-// retryable-or-not; classification is the adapter's duty.\\n90-export type ProviderResult =\\n91-  | { ok: true; text: string }\\n92-  | { ok: false; retryable: boolean; reason: string };\\n93-\\n94-// Message kinds a rendering part can carry — mirrors the intake event-kind\\n95-// vocabulary minus turn_end (turn_end never projects a message). Mirrored\\n96-// rather than imported: shared/ may not import domains/.\\n97-export type RenderingPartKind =\\n98-  | \\\"user_prompt\\\"\\n99-  | \\\"assistant_text\\\"\\n100-  | \\\"assistant_thinking\\\"\\n101-  | \\\"runtime_note\\\"\\n102-  | \\\"tool_call\\\"\\n103-  | \\\"tool_result\\\";\\n104-\\n105-export interface RenderingPart {\\n106-  messageId: string;\\n107-  kind: RenderingPartKind;\\n108-  text: string; // ready form content, or raw/truncated fallback\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:187:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01DcXDGaGSjKK5fKTz35SSbV\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\texport type ErrorClass = \\\"caller_error\\\" | \\\"state_corruption\\\" | \\\"system_error\\\";\\n2\\t\\n3\\texport type ErrorCode =\\n4\\t  | \\\"path_exists\\\"\\n5\\t  | \\\"thread_not_found\\\"\\n6\\t  | \\\"invalid_thread_ref\\\" // empty/blank file path or otherwise unusable reference\\n7\\t  | \\\"invalid_event\\\"\\n8\\t  | \\\"empty_batch\\\"\\n9\\t  | \\\"empty_stdin\\\" // CLI adapter only, emitted before any SDK call\\n10\\t  | \\\"turn_state_corrupt\\\"\\n11\\t  | \\\"storage_failure\\\"\\n12\\t  // Epic 02 (tech design §Interfaces, issue 4):\\n13\\t  | \\\"turn_open\\\" // caller_error — mutation against an open turn\\n14\\t  | \\\"message_initiates_turn\\\" // caller_error — delete refused toward turns.delete\\n15\\t  | \\\"message_not_found\\\" // caller_error\\n16\\t  | \\\"turn_not_found\\\" // caller_error\\n17\\t  | \\\"unknown_work_kind\\\" // state_corruption — unregistered kind at dispatch\\n18\\t  | \\\"provider_not_configured\\\" // caller_error — CLI drain without --provider / LHC_PROVIDER (DD-11)\\n19\\t  | \\\"provider_failure\\\" // system_error — exhausted retries; form.reason carries detail\\n20\\t  | \\\"source_damaged\\\" // state_corruption — handler found corrupt source; form blocked\\n21\\t  // Epic 03 (tech design §Interface Definitions): the surface-skeleton stub\\n22\\t  // contract — machine-readable, never a throw on the thread-view surface.\\n23\\t  | \\\"not_implemented\\\" // system_error — operation's story has not landed yet\\n24\\t  // Epic 03 Story 2 (AC-2.2/2.3): compact-time config rejection — unlike SDK\\n25\\t  // construction (programmer error, throws), a bad compact invocation is an\\n26\\t  // operational caller error returned as a result.\\n27\\t  | \\\"unknown_profile\\\" // caller_error — named profile not configured\\n28\\t  | \\\"invalid_view_config\\\" // caller_error — band sum / bound violation, named\\n29\\t  // Epic 03 Story 5: materialize accepts pi-session only; an unknown format\\n30\\t  // is a caller error naming the accepted values (story Scope).\\n31\\t  | \\\"unknown_format\\\"; // caller_error — materialize format not supported\\n32\\t\\n33\\texport interface ErrorResult {\\n34\\t  errorClass: ErrorClass;\\n35\\t  code: ErrorCode;\\n36\\t  reason: string; // human-readable; machine logic switches on code\\n37\\t  eventIndex?: number; // present on batch validation failures\\n38\\t}\\n39\\t\\n40\\t// Expected operational failures — caller errors, corruption, environment\\n41\\t// failures — are always returned as OpResult errors, never thrown.\\n42\\t// Programmer bugs inside lhc may still throw; callers are not expected\\n43\\t// to handle throws as contract outcomes.\\n44\\texport type OpResult<T> =\\n45\\t  | { ok: true; value: T }\\n46\\t  | { ok: false; error: ErrorResult };\\n47\\t\\n48\\t// Infrastructure failures (SQLite, fs) are expected operational outcomes,\\n49\\t// caught at the operation boundary and wrapped with the underlying detail.\\n50\\texport function storageFailure(reason: string): { ok: false; error: ErrorResult } {\\n51\\t  return {\\n52\\t    ok: false,\\n53\\t    error: { errorClass: \\\"system_error\\\", code: \\\"storage_failure\\\", reason },\\n54\\t  };\\n55\\t}\\n56\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"92b30fef-4ad7-45bb-a8e9-4c6f66be56bf\",\"uuid\":\"9a79d931-0fe1-4cc0-b560-f26572605ca0\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-12T12:48:33.503Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/shared/errors.ts\",\"content\":\"export type ErrorClass = \\\"caller_error\\\" | \\\"state_corruption\\\" | \\\"system_error\\\";\\n\\nexport type ErrorCode =\\n  | \\\"path_exists\\\"\\n  | \\\"thread_not_found\\\"\\n  | \\\"invalid_thread_ref\\\" // empty/blank file path or otherwise unusable reference\\n  | \\\"invalid_event\\\"\\n  | \\\"empty_batch\\\"\\n  | \\\"empty_stdin\\\" // CLI adapter only, emitted before any SDK call\\n  | \\\"turn_state_corrupt\\\"\\n  | \\\"storage_failure\\\"\\n  // Epic 02 (tech design §Interfaces, issue 4):\\n  | \\\"turn_open\\\" // caller_error — mutation against an open turn\\n  | \\\"message_initiates_turn\\\" // caller_error — delete refused toward turns.delete\\n  | \\\"message_not_found\\\" // caller_error\\n  | \\\"turn_not_found\\\" // caller_error\\n  | \\\"unknown_work_kind\\\" // state_corruption — unregistered kind at dispatch\\n  | \\\"provider_not_configured\\\" // caller_error — CLI drain without --provider / LHC_PROVIDER (DD-11)\\n  | \\\"provider_failure\\\" // system_error — exhausted retries; form.reason carries detail\\n  | \\\"source_damaged\\\" // state_corruption — handler found corrupt source; form blocked\\n  // Epic 03 (tech design §Interface Definitions): the surface-skeleton stub\\n  // contract — machine-readable, never a throw on the thread-view surface.\\n  | \\\"not_implemented\\\" // system_error — operation's story has not landed yet\\n  // Epic 03 Story 2 (AC-2.2/2.3): compact-time config rejection — unlike SDK\\n  // construction (programmer error, throws), a bad compact invocation is an\\n  // operational caller error returned as a result.\\n  | \\\"unknown_profile\\\" // caller_error — named profile not configured\\n  | \\\"invalid_view_config\\\" // caller_error — band sum / bound violation, named\\n  // Epic 03 Story 5: materialize accepts pi-session only; an unknown format\\n  // is a caller error naming the accepted values (story Scope).\\n  | \\\"unknown_format\\\"; // caller_error — materialize format not supported\\n\\nexport interface ErrorResult {\\n  errorClass: ErrorClass;\\n  code: ErrorCode;\\n  reason: string; // human-readable; machine logic switches on code\\n  eventIndex?: number; // present on batch validation failures\\n}\\n\\n// Expected operational failures — caller errors, corruption, environment\\n// failures — are always returned as OpResult errors, never thrown.\\n// Programmer bugs inside lhc may still throw; callers are not expected\\n// to handle throws as contract outcomes.\\nexport type OpResult<T> =\\n  | { ok: true; value: T }\\n  | { ok: false; error: ErrorResult };\\n\\n// Infrastructure failures (SQLite, fs) are expected operational outcomes,\\n// caught at the operation boundary and wrapped with the underlying detail.\\nexport function storageFailure(reason: string): { ok: false; error: ErrorResult } {\\n  return {\\n    ok: false,\\n    error: { errorClass: \\\"system_error\\\", code: \\\"storage_failure\\\", reason },\\n  };\\n}\\n\",\"numLines\":56,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":56}}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:238:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_017yGxDXv6jEesBtmErrxRzY\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/:\\nartifacts\\nepic.md\\nimpl-run.config.json\\nstories\\nteam-impl-log.md\\ntech-design.md\\ntest-plan.md\\n\\n/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/:\\n01-message-read-surface.md\\n02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md\\n03-view-contents-report.md\\n04-lifecycle-exercise.md\\ncoverage.md\\n47:- Message read completion on the `messages` surface: listing options (bounds, include-deleted) and single-message view with blocks and derivation form states\\n174:**List options**: bounded listing (range/limit) and includeDeleted; exact option names are tech design's, the *existence* of bounds and the deleted default are contract.\\n176:**CLI**: `lhc inspect overview|view|health`, `lhc messages list [--include-deleted] [bounds]`, `lhc messages show --message-id <id>` — JSON to stdout, SDK-parity, same error classes as every epic (`caller_error`, `state_corruption`, `system_error`).\\n192:6. Listing bounds: offset/limit vs event-order range — pick from CLI ergonomics; both bounded.\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"92b30fef-4ad7-45bb-a8e9-4c6f66be56bf\",\"uuid\":\"da28e9e2-eccd-4d4c-bdee-8840a86df33e\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-12T12:48:57.177Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/:\\nartifacts\\nepic.md\\nimpl-run.config.json\\nstories\\nteam-impl-log.md\\ntech-design.md\\ntest-plan.md\\n\\n/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/:\\n01-message-read-surface.md\\n02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md\\n03-view-contents-report.md\\n04-lifecycle-exercise.md\\ncoverage.md\\n47:- Message read completion on the `messages` surface: listing options (bounds, include-deleted) and single-message view with blocks and derivation form states\\n174:**List options**: bounded listing (range/limit) and includeDeleted; exact option names are tech design's, the *existence* of bounds and the deleted default are contract.\\n176:**CLI**: `lhc inspect overview|view|health`, `lhc messages list [--include-deleted] [bounds]`, `lhc messages show --message-id <id>` — JSON to stdout, SDK-parity, same error classes as every epic (`caller_error`, `state_corruption`, `system_error`).\\n192:6. Listing bounds: offset/limit vs event-order range — pick from CLI ergonomics; both bounded.\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:268:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"Exit code 1\\n# Team Impl Log — Epic 04: Inspection\\n\\nState: STORY_ACTIVE\\nSpec-pack root: /Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection\\nCurrent Story: 01-message-read-surface\\nCurrent Phase: implement (story-orchestrate)\\n\\n## Run Configuration\\n\\n- Date: 2026-06-12\\n- Caller harness: Claude Code (Fable 5) acting as impl-lead.\\n- Primary harness: claude-code. Secondary harness probe: codex-cli 0.139.0 available.\\n- Defaults table applied: \\\"Codex available\\\" (operations/31-provider-resolution.md), no deviations.\\n- Roles: story_lead_provider=codex gpt-5.5 high; story_implementor=claude-fable-5 medium; quick_fixer=claude-opus-4-8 xhigh; story_verifier=codex gpt-5.5 xhigh; epic-reviewer-1=claude-fable-5 xhigh; epic-reviewer-2=codex gpt-5.5 xhigh; epic_reverifier=claude-fable-5 xhigh.\\n- Self-review passes: 3 (default).\\n- Degraded-diversity: none (Codex available).\\n- Prompt inserts: both absent (non-blocking).\\n\\n## Verification Gates\\n\\n- Story gate: `pnpm verify` — source: package scripts (packages/lhc/package.json). Candidates considered: `verify`, `green-verify` (adds check-test-immutability guard), `verify-all`. `verify` selected per skill rule: prefer plain `verify` during story work because stories legitimately add tests; guarded `green-verify` reserved for hygiene/explicit policy.\\n- Epic gate: `pnpm verify-all` (runs red-verify + LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 vitest) — source: package scripts; matches spec-pack Verification sections (`LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all`). Process suite must report `ran`.\\n- Gate working directory: packages/lhc.\\n\\n## Spec Pack\\n\\n- inspect: ready. Shape: two-file (tech-design.md + test-plan.md). artifacts/ created.\\n- Stories in order: 01-message-read-surface, 02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health, 03-view-contents-report, 04-lifecycle-exercise. coverage.md ignored as non-story.\\n- Coverage gate (coverage.md): PASS — all 23 ACs owned, one primary owner per TC.\\n\\n## Retained Spec Notes (compaction-safe)\\n\\n- Epic 04 builds the inspection surface for the LHC SDK (in-process long-horizon-context system for PI CLI extensions; thin CLI for testing/integration).\\n- S1 message reads: listMessages bounds {from,to,limit,includeDeleted} in source-event order; show returns FULL record blocks + owner-reported form states (never view-shortened, never synthesized); deleted excluded by default, auditable, show on deleted = ok+flag, missing id = message_not_found; CLI deep-equal parity. Search deferred post-v1, no placeholder. Strategy: simple-risk-reminders.\\n- S2 inspect domain: overview (identity, event/message/turn/chunk counts, derivation states, view summary or null, boundary + zone tokens; deleted contract; all 5 thread shapes; pure read) + health (owner/kind/state counts via owner report surfaces ONLY — no direct derived_form/work_item reads; failure detail; repair preview = failed∧¬blocked, never executed; queue visibility; rebuild bracket edit→pending→drain→ready). Read-only delta helper lands here, wraps S1 ops retroactively. Mutation-in-flight fixture via production mutate + partial drain, never hand-written rows. Strategy: tdd-lite.\\n- S3 view report: threadView.describe = stored snapshot only (null when absent, never recompute); inspect.view = describe + measured pull tail; governing contract loadCost.total == actual pull served content (incl. never-compacted: meta null, bands [], tail-only). No new storage/migration. Strategy: tdd-lite.\\n- S4 lifecycle capstone: test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts scripted PI-extension order (create→intake→drain→status→compact→pull→inspect→edit+delete→rebuild drain→health→compact2→pull→materialize); deterministic provider only, zero network; replay byte-identical; SDK teardown/recreate continuity; spawned-CLI checkpoint parity; receipt-vs-health cross-check. Process suite must report ran, never silently skip. Strategy: full-staged-risk.\\n- Test plan: ~26 default tests across messages-read/inspect-overview/inspect-view/inspect-health/lifecycle + cli-process-inspect (process: TC-3.4, TC-5.4). Architecture-risk: read-only delta assert on every new op; throwing-provider suite-wide assert; loadCost parity two independent measurements; check-boundaries + source check against raw SQL into other domains from domains/inspect/**.\\n\\n## Operating Reminders\\n\\n- Impl-lead owns acceptance, final gates, fix routing, recovery. CLI never accepts.\\n- Story cycle: story-orchestrate validate → run (background) → monitor via runtime progress artifacts + 5-min Monitor cadence → review final package → run story gate myself → receipt → advance.\\n- Receipt before acceptance: implementor evidence, verifier evidence, gate result, dispositions, baseline before/after.\\n- Cumulative baseline tracking: total test count must not regress story-over-story.\\n\\n## Cumulative Baseline\\n\\n- Pre-run baseline (2026-06-12, before Story 1): `pnpm verify` PASS — 290 tests / 27 files.\\n\\n## Story Sequence Status\\n\\n| Story | Status |\\n|---|---|\\n| 01-message-read-surface | pending |\\n| 02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health | pending |\\n| 03-view-contents-report | pending |\\n| 04-lifecycle-exercise | pending |\\n\\n## Transitions\\n\\n- 2026-06-12: Run created. State: SETUP. inspect ready; config authored; gates resolved from package scripts.\\n- 2026-06-12: preflight ready (002-preflight.json). Gates persisted into impl-run.config.json by preflight (expected side effect). Baseline 290/27 recorded. State → STORY_ACTIVE, Story 01, phase implement.\\n(eval):1: == not found\",\"is_error\":true,\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01KsBs6Nhq2ZaapNyvwWbTJi\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"92b30fef-4ad7-45bb-a8e9-4c6f66be56bf\",\"uuid\":\"6ddcb74b-f806-462b-8934-67c6bb87a986\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-12T12:49:12.202Z\",\"tool_use_result\":\"Error: Exit code 1\\n# Team Impl Log — Epic 04: Inspection\\n\\nState: STORY_ACTIVE\\nSpec-pack root: /Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection\\nCurrent Story: 01-message-read-surface\\nCurrent Phase: implement (story-orchestrate)\\n\\n## Run Configuration\\n\\n- Date: 2026-06-12\\n- Caller harness: Claude Code (Fable 5) acting as impl-lead.\\n- Primary harness: claude-code. Secondary harness probe: codex-cli 0.139.0 available.\\n- Defaults table applied: \\\"Codex available\\\" (operations/31-provider-resolution.md), no deviations.\\n- Roles: story_lead_provider=codex gpt-5.5 high; story_implementor=claude-fable-5 medium; quick_fixer=claude-opus-4-8 xhigh; story_verifier=codex gpt-5.5 xhigh; epic-reviewer-1=claude-fable-5 xhigh; epic-reviewer-2=codex gpt-5.5 xhigh; epic_reverifier=claude-fable-5 xhigh.\\n- Self-review passes: 3 (default).\\n- Degraded-diversity: none (Codex available).\\n- Prompt inserts: both absent (non-blocking).\\n\\n## Verification Gates\\n\\n- Story gate: `pnpm verify` — source: package scripts (packages/lhc/package.json). Candidates considered: `verify`, `green-verify` (adds check-test-immutability guard), `verify-all`. `verify` selected per skill rule: prefer plain `verify` during story work because stories legitimately add tests; guarded `green-verify` reserved for hygiene/explicit policy.\\n- Epic gate: `pnpm verify-all` (runs red-verify + LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 vitest) — source: package scripts; matches spec-pack Verification sections (`LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all`).