{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '90,130p' packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md && rg -n \\\"Block|MessageRecord|listMessages|block summary|blocks\\\" packages/lhc/docs/02-specs -g '*.md'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '90,130p' packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md && rg -n \\\"Block|MessageRecord|listMessages|block summary|blocks\\\" packages/lhc/docs/02-specs -g '*.md'\"","aggregated_output":"\n- **AC-2.1**: The report names the active view — viewId, createdAt, profile name and resolved config, compactPoint, coveredFrom — and lists every band entry in served order (brief → detailed → smooth): subject kind and id, form used, degraded flag; plus every gap with its reason; plus per-band stored token counts. All of it from the stored snapshot, not recomputed.\n- **AC-2.2**: The tail section reports message count and token cost *as currently served*: tool results at-or-behind the visibility boundary are costed at their short form, everything else full.\n- **AC-2.3**: `loadCost` totals what `pull` serves now — bands plus tail — and a test asserts equality against an actual pull's measured content. The report never disagrees with the surface it describes.\n- **AC-2.4**: A never-compacted thread reports view: null with a tail-only loadCost under the same equality contract (the whole record served as tail).\n- **AC-2.5**: The report carries the view's recorded source-state provenance (what the compact saw: max event order, form counts) and is a pure read under AC-1.4's contract.\n\n#### Test Conditions\n\n- **TC-2.1** (AC-2.1, AC-2.5): On a compacted fixture with one degraded entry and one gap → report matches the stored arrangement exactly: subjects, forms used, degraded flags, gap reasons, band token counts, config, provenance.\n- **TC-2.2** (AC-2.2, AC-2.3): On a boundary-advanced fixture → tail cost counts short forms short; `loadCost.total` equals the token measure of an actual `pull`'s messages using the same estimator.\n- **TC-2.3** (AC-2.4): Never-compacted thread → view null, tail spans the record, cost-parity assertion holds.\n\n## Flow 3: Message Listing and Viewing\n\nThe drill-down floor. Every report names subjects; this flow is where an operator or agent reads the actual record. Epic 01 shipped `listMessages` bare; this flow completes it and adds the single-message view.\n\n#### Acceptance Criteria\n\n- **AC-3.1**: Listing returns messages in record order with kind, block summary, token estimate, turn membership, and deleted status, with bounded-listing options (range/limit) so large threads list without loading everything.\n- **AC-3.2**: `messages.show` returns one message in full: every block with complete content (the record — full tool results, not view-shortened forms), token estimate, turn membership, and the message's derivation forms with their states and metadata (joined from the owner's report, including tool-outcome metadata where present).\n- **AC-3.3**: Deleted messages are excluded by default and listable with an explicit include-deleted option, marked deleted — never silently mixed in. `show` on a deleted message returns the record marked deleted (audit is the point), never a not-found.\n- **AC-3.4**: CLI parity: `lhc messages list` and `lhc messages show` mirror the SDK operations — same options, same result JSON.\n\n#### Test Conditions\n\n- **TC-3.1** (AC-3.1): List on the fixture → record order, kinds, token estimates, turn ids correct; range and limit options honored exactly.\n- **TC-3.2** (AC-3.2): Show on a drained tool-result message → full original content present, forms listed with states, outcome metadata present.\n- **TC-3.3** (AC-3.3): Delete one message → default list excludes it; include-deleted lists it marked; show on its id → record with deleted flag.\n- **TC-3.4** (AC-3.4): Spawned-CLI list and show on a fixture thread → JSON equals the in-process SDK results (process suite).\n\n## Flow 4: Derivation Health and Rebuild Visibility\n\nThe state of every derived form, aggregated to act on. This is also where a mutation's rebuild is watched: cleared forms show pending with queued work, then land ready.\n\n#### Acceptance Criteria\n\n- **AC-4.1**: `inspect.health` aggregates across owners — counts by owner, form kind, and state (ready, pending, retrying, failed, blocked) — assembled entirely from the owners' report surfaces, never from direct `derived_form` or `work_item` reads.\n- **AC-4.2**: Failures carry actionable detail: subject id, form kind, reason, attempts, last error — enough to decide and target a requeue without raw SQL.\n- **AC-4.3**: The report previews repair: which forms a requeue pass would touch (failed and not blocked), reported and never executed.\n- **AC-4.4**: Rebuild visibility: after an edit or delete, health shows the cascade-cleared forms as pending with their queued work visible; after the queue drains, the same forms report ready. Two reads bracket a rebuild.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/team-impl-log.md:166:- Epic: LHC thread record + intake. Six stories = tech-design chunks 0-5, strictly linear deps, all extending one `messageEvents` walk: resolveThreadRef(S1) -> 3-layer closed validation(S2) -> BEGIN IMMEDIATE + corruption check(S2/S4) -> per-event walk [dedup(S2) -> record(S2) -> project message+blocks+estimate(S3) -> turn transition+stamp(S4) -> queue work(S5)] -> result -> COMMIT.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/team-impl-log.md:179:- Baseline rule: compare test totals before/after each story; a drop blocks acceptance.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:18:- **Message**: the readable form of a message-producing event. A message holds one or more **blocks** (text, tool payloads) and a token estimate.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:26:A harness integration creates a thread, then streams conversation activity into it as event batches. Each batch lands atomically: events are recorded in order, messages and blocks are projected with token estimates, turn state advances through a small fixed rule set, and derivation work queues durably — all synchronously, before the call returns. Resends are safe through per-event idempotency keys. Incoherent batches are rejected whole, leaving the thread untouched.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:137:- **AC-2.2**: Each message-producing event yields exactly one message carrying that event's content verbatim, structured as one or more typed blocks.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:149:- **TC-2.2** (AC-2.2, 2.3): A batch with one of each event kind → six messages with kind-appropriate blocks and verbatim content; `turn_end` present in events, absent from messages.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:362:- **Message**: `{ messageId, sourceEventOrder, kind, blocks[], tokenEstimate, actor, harness, turnId? }`\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:363:- **Block**: `{ blockType, content }`\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/epic.md:428:**Delivers:** Messages and blocks projected from recorded events in the same operation, token estimates stamped, actor/harness carried, message read-back.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/coverage.md:92:    project message + blocks + estimate ....... S3\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/coverage.md:97:read-back: listEvents S2 · listMessages S3 · listTurns S4 · listQueuedWork S5\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/03-message-projection-tokens.md:6:Messages and blocks projected from recorded events inside the batch transaction; token estimates stamped at creation; message read-back.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/03-message-projection-tokens.md:13:**Objective:** Everything recorded becomes readable, with its size known. Each message-producing event yields exactly one message with kind-appropriate typed blocks, verbatim content, the actor/harness carry, and a deterministic base-unit token estimate — written in the same walk iteration that records the event, so projection can never drift from its source.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/03-message-projection-tokens.md:20:- `messageId` in batch result entries; `listMessages` read-back; CLI `messages list`\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/03-message-projection-tokens.md:30:- **AC-2.2**: Each message-producing event yields exactly one message carrying that event's content verbatim, structured as one or more typed blocks.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/03-message-projection-tokens.md:31:  - **TC-2.2** (AC-2.2, 2.3): A batch with one of each event kind → six messages with kind-appropriate blocks and verbatim content; `turn_end` present in events, absent from messages.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/03-message-projection-tokens.md:48:This story adds projection to Story 2's walk: each recorded message-producing event yields its message, blocks, and token estimate in the same iteration that recorded it, inside the same transaction — projection cannot drift from its source because they are never separated. The risk profile is fidelity, not logic: kind-correct block shapes, verbatim content, and the absence of any code path that could shorten a tool result. `messages.createFromEvent` is the first cross-domain surface call through the operation context, establishing the pattern `turns.applyEvent` follows in Story 4.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/03-message-projection-tokens.md:66:| Projection | `src/domains/messages/internal/project.ts` (event → message + blocks per kind) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/03-message-projection-tokens.md:68:| Surface | `src/domains/messages/index.ts` (createFromEvent, listMessages) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/03-message-projection-tokens.md:85:| TC-2.2 | `test/projection.test.ts` | all seven kinds → six messages, kind-correct blocks, verbatim; turn_end absent |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/03-message-projection-tokens.md:100:- Message read-back: `{ messageId, sourceEventOrder, kind, blocks[], tokenEstimate, actor, harness, turnId? }` — `turnId` null until Story 4.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/03-message-projection-tokens.md:101:- Block shapes: text kinds → one text block; `tool_call` → `{ toolCallId, toolName, arguments }`; `tool_result` → `{ toolCallId, content, isError }`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/03-message-projection-tokens.md:108:- Block-shape assertions check full structure per kind, not just block count.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/03-message-projection-tokens.md:133:- [ ] `listMessages` ordered and deterministic; CLI `messages list` live\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:90:      index.ts              // surface: createFromEvent, listMessages, listQueuedWork\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:92:        project.ts          // event → message + blocks projection\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:128:| `messages/internal/project.ts` | Event → message + typed blocks, verbatim content, token estimate stamping, actor/harness carry, full tool-result preservation | AC-2.2, AC-2.3, AC-2.4, AC-2.5, AC-2.6 |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:149:**Batch intake is one SQLite transaction on the thread file.** `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` → record events → project messages/blocks → apply turn transitions → write work items → `COMMIT`. Any failure anywhere rolls back everything: AC-4.6's \"thread unchanged\" is the transaction's rollback, verified at the read-back level (Issue 4: logical equality, not file bytes). `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` takes the write lock up front, so the single-writer assumption failing loudly (SQLITE_BUSY after the busy timeout) rather than deadlocking mid-batch.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:264:The walk is where most of this epic's behavior lives. Each recorded event takes its order number from a counter initialized at `MAX(event_order)` when the transaction begins — skipped duplicates do not consume numbers, so the stream stays dense and AC-2.1's continuity holds across batches and across skips. Projection happens in the same iteration as recording: the message row, its blocks, the token estimate, and the actor/harness carry are written while the event is in hand, and the message id is the event's order number with an `m` prefix (Design Decision 7), so projection cannot drift from its source.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:279:    I->>M: createFromEvent(ctx, event) — message + blocks + estimate (AC-2.2–2.6)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:288:Two projection details are contractual rather than implementation-free. Block structure by kind: text-bearing kinds (`user_prompt`, `assistant_text`, `assistant_thinking`, `runtime_note`) project one text block; `tool_call` projects one block carrying `toolCallId`, `toolName`, and `arguments`; `tool_result` projects one block carrying `toolCallId`, the full `content`, and `isError`. Nothing splits, summarizes, or normalizes content at intake — AC-2.5's full preservation is the absence of any code path that could shorten it, which is why TC-2.4's hundreds-of-KB round-trip is a meaningful regression tripwire rather than a formality. Token estimates count each message's text content (for tool calls, the serialized arguments; for tool results, the full content string) through the one `token-counting` util, and the estimate lands on the message row in the same insert.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:295:| TC-2.2 | Per-kind projection, turn_end exception | Block mapping table; no-message path |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:490:export type BlockType = \"text\" | \"tool_call\" | \"tool_result\";\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:491:export interface Block {\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:492:  blockType: BlockType;\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:495:export interface MessageRecord {\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:499:  blocks: Block[];\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:506:export function listMessages(thread: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<MessageRecord[]>>;\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:619:**Delivers:** `createFromEvent` wired into the walk; per-kind block projection; token stamping via the Chunk 0 util; actor/harness carry; `listMessages`; deterministic `m<order>` ids; messageId in batch results.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-tech-arch.md:74:| `thread-view` | SDK + CLI | View assembly, smart compact, band locking, tool-result visibility policy (source-event-order boundary, whole-message protection floor), readiness sweep, rendering (message array + provider file) | `threads`, `messages`, `turns` | Views are derived and disposable; assembly is read-and-assemble only; missing derivations degrade, never block; source corruption blocks; thread-view drives repair through owning domains' surfaces and derives nothing itself |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-tech-arch.md:119:**Consequence:** Every derived artifact records its state, a reason on failure, and timestamps. Consequence-of-absence is a separate axis decided by the consumer: derivation gaps degrade and report; only damage to the source record blocks. A degraded view marks its gaps; thread-view never silently omits a span of history because its material was missing.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-tech-arch.md:157:  IS->>MS: create messages + blocks (ctx)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/00-prd.md:23:Each thread lives in its own SQLite file. A harness streams events in; synchronous intake records them, projects messages, and settles turn membership on the spot. Slow derivation runs through a durable work queue along three ownership paths: message-level forms (prompt smoothing, tool-call and tool-result summaries) queue when the message lands and belong to `messages`; turn and chunk derivations queue at close and belong to `turns`; view assembly consumes both and belongs to `thread-view`, which derives nothing itself. Thread views assemble locked summary bands plus a live full-fidelity tail, and render as an in-memory message array or a provider-format file. Missing derivations degrade a view, marked and reported; only damage to the source record blocks.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/00-prd.md:41:- AC-1.3: An event batch is recorded in stream order; each message-producing event yields a message with its blocks and a token estimate\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/00-prd.md:77:**Scenario 2: Inference fails mid-derivation.** The summarization provider errors or is unavailable. The artifact records a retryable failure; nothing downstream blocks on it. Retry succeeds later, or exhausts into a terminal failure that repair can re-queue.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/00-prd.md:82:**Scenario 3: A message is edited.** An operator or agent edits a message in a closed turn through the messages surface. The deterministic parts update synchronously — content, blocks, token estimate — and every derivation built from the old content clears and re-queues: the message's own forms, its turn's composed rendering and projection, and the containing chunk's summaries. Ordering guarantees that re-queued work lands after any in-flight work on the old content.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/00-prd.md:87:**Scenario 4: A message or turn is deleted.** A noisy message, or a whole dead-end exchange, is removed from the readable record. Delete is a projection-level operation: the message and its blocks drop from the readable view and from turn membership, while the source event log retains the original. Deleting a turn removes the exchange unit and everything in it. Dependent derivations clear and re-queue exactly as an edit's do; chunk boundaries stay where they were — a chunk shrinks, it is never re-cut.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/00-prd.md:144:- AC-4.2: Messages are listable and viewable in order with blocks, token estimates, turn membership, and derivation states\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/team-impl-log.md:34:- S1 message reads: listMessages bounds {from,to,limit,includeDeleted} in source-event order; show returns FULL record blocks + owner-reported form states (never view-shortened, never synthesized); deleted excluded by default, auditable, show on deleted = ok+flag, missing id = message_not_found; CLI deep-equal parity. Search deferred post-v1, no placeholder. Strategy: simple-risk-reminders.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/team-impl-log.md:8:- (Story 3 history: PRIMITIVE PATH — story-lead run 001 terminal blocked after two transient provider failures (socket close after 51 turns, then 529 Overloaded); composed resume re-blocks without redispatching. Recovery: fresh story-implement primitive dispatched 2026-06-11T17:10Z against partial worktree completed the story: SV-03-001 closed (sweep.ts walk/classify/requeue + surface + compact embed landed by the partial worktree, verified against owners' contracts), SV-03-002 closed (test/view-sweep.test.ts added — 10 tests, TC-3.1–3.4, classification edges, five-op zero-provider; stale placeholder assertions in view-pull/view-compact amended under the sanctioned-amendment pattern, red-manifest re-recorded). Gates green 2026-06-11: green-verify (273 tests + immutability OK), verify-all (300 tests incl. process suite). Next: story-verify follow-up on retained verifier handle codex/019eb786-e7ae-7d92-84c3-8daefeb333c6 → receipt.)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/team-impl-log.md:136:  - EPIC-02-BLOCK-002: findPairedBlock reads deleted results (filter bug) + counterpart summary not cascaded. IMPL-LEAD RULING: pair is a source dependency per AC-2.8 symmetry — deleting/editing half a pair clears + requeues the counterpart summary; AC-6.2's bound applies across turns/chunks, not within the pair.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/team-impl-log.md:141:  - BLOCK-002a — `findPairedBlock` (and `findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary`) now `JOIN message … AND m.deleted_at IS NULL`: a tool_call whose paired result is deleted derives outcome `unknown`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md:68:Per-story: `pnpm verify` (lint, typecheck, default suites). Story 4 and epic close: `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all` — process suite must report `ran`. Red manifests regenerated per chunk per house discipline; no Epic 01–03 test amendments expected (additive surfaces only — list-opts default behavior is unchanged, existing `listMessages` callers see identical results).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/test-plan.md:83:| TC-5.1 | Edit prompt in closed turn | Content + blocks + token estimate updated synchronously; result names cleared forms and queued items |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:21:**Mental model:** \"inspect describes; it never changes. Every report reads the same state the serving surfaces read, so a report never disagrees with what the agent was actually served. When a report names a subject, I can drill to it — view entry → chunk → turn → message → blocks.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:47:- Message read completion on the `messages` surface: listing options (bounds, include-deleted) and single-message view with blocks and derivation form states\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:105:The drill-down floor. Every report names subjects; this flow is where an operator or agent reads the actual record. Epic 01 shipped `listMessages` bare; this flow completes it and adds the single-message view.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:109:- **AC-3.1**: Listing returns messages in record order with kind, block summary, token estimate, turn membership, and deleted status, with bounded-listing options (range/limit) so large threads list without loading everything.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:172:**`MessageDetail`** (show): the full `MessageRecord` (all blocks, full content, token estimate, turnId, deleted flag) plus forms: the owner's report entries for this message.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md:187:1. `messages.show` shape: new operation vs `listMessages` option — and whether the forms join reuses `messages.report(messageId)` internally or a shared internal read.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:27:**Key constraint:** no inference anywhere in this epic. Views assemble stored artifacts; they never create them. When material is missing, the view degrades visibly and reports the gap — it never blocks, never silently omits a span, and never fabricates.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:115:- Overview reads `listEvents`, `listMessages({ includeDeleted: true })`, `listTurns`, `listChunks`, `status`, and `describe`, then normalizes absent sections to zero/null.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:13:Terms this epic uses that Epic 01 established: **event** (ordered source record), **message** (readable projection of an event, holding blocks), **turn** (one exchange: a user prompt and what came back for it, membership stamped at intake and frozen at close), **work item** (a durably queued unit of derivation work: owner, kind, sourceRef, queued in the same transaction as the record that needs it).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:62:- Block-level delete (whole message plus its blocks is the deletion unit)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:221:Editing fixes what the record got wrong. The edit targets a message in a closed turn, updates content and blocks synchronously, re-stamps the token estimate, and cascades: every derived form built from the old content clears to `pending` and re-queues in the same transaction. Per-thread ordering guarantees the rebuilt forms land after any in-flight work on the old content; a straggler can never overwrite a post-edit artifact.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:225:3. Synchronous, one transaction: content and blocks updated, token estimate re-stamped, dependent forms cleared to `pending`, replacement work queued\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:233:- **AC-5.1**: An edit to a message in a closed turn updates content and blocks and re-stamps the token estimate in one synchronous transaction; the edit result reports the content change, cleared forms, and queued work.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:391:| # | Question | Blocks | Resolution path |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:380:        reason: \"Block/MessageRecord types and fail-closed listMessages/listQueuedWork stubs\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:27:Messages and blocks projected from recorded events inside the batch transaction; token estimates stamped at creation; message read-back.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:34:**Objective:** Everything recorded becomes readable, with its size known. Each message-producing event yields exactly one message with kind-appropriate typed blocks, verbatim content, the actor/harness carry, and a deterministic base-unit token estimate — written in the same walk iteration that records the event, so projection can never drift from its source.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:41:- `messageId` in batch result entries; `listMessages` read-back; CLI `messages list`\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:51:- **AC-2.2**: Each message-producing event yields exactly one message carrying that event's content verbatim, structured as one or more typed blocks.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:52:  - **TC-2.2** (AC-2.2, 2.3): A batch with one of each event kind → six messages with kind-appropriate blocks and verbatim content; `turn_end` present in events, absent from messages.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:69:This story adds projection to Story 2's walk: each recorded message-producing event yields its message, blocks, and token estimate in the same iteration that recorded it, inside the same transaction — projection cannot drift from its source because they are never separated. The risk profile is fidelity, not logic: kind-correct block shapes, verbatim content, and the absence of any code path that could shorten a tool result. `messages.createFromEvent` is the first cross-domain surface call through the operation context, establishing the pattern `turns.applyEvent` follows in Story 4.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:87:| Projection | `src/domains/messages/internal/project.ts` (event → message + blocks per kind) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:89:| Surface | `src/domains/messages/index.ts` (createFromEvent, listMessages) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:106:| TC-2.2 | `test/projection.test.ts` | all seven kinds → six messages, kind-correct blocks, verbatim; turn_end absent |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:121:- Message read-back: `{ messageId, sourceEventOrder, kind, blocks[], tokenEstimate, actor, harness, turnId? }` — `turnId` null until Story 4.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:122:- Block shapes: text kinds → one text block; `tool_call` → `{ toolCallId, toolName, arguments }`; `tool_result` → `{ toolCallId, content, isError }`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:129:- Block-shape assertions check full structure per kind, not just block count.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:154:- [ ] `listMessages` ordered and deterministic; CLI `messages list` live\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:344:    planSummary: \"Wired message projection into the Story 2 batch walk: each recorded message-producing event now yields one message with kind-appropriate typed blocks, verbatim content, actor/harness carry, and a deterministic o200k_base token estimate, written in the same transaction iteration that recorded the event (createFromEvent is the first cross-domain surface call through OperationContext). Added message/message_block tables to thread schema v1 (same extension pattern Story 2 used for the event table), deterministic m<eventOrder> ids, messageId in batch result entries, listMessages read-back, and a live CLI `messages list`. Followed Red→Green: projection.test.ts and cli-process-projection.test.ts written and manifest-recorded first (all 7 failing on assertions), then implemented to green. turnId stays null throughout (Story 4). Projection failure rejects the whole batch, proven by an induced real failure (walk-hook drops message_block mid-transaction) asserted via read-back, not the error result alone.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:369:        reason: \"Pure per-kind event→blocks+estimate projection; verbatim field copies, no shortening path; tool_call counts serialized arguments, tool_result counts full content; turn_end → null\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:375:        reason: \"createFromEvent (synchronous cross-domain surface, m<eventOrder> ids, throws on projection failure) and real listMessages replacing the stub; RecordedEvent/MessageCreated types\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:381:        reason: \"Exported MessageRecord/Block/BlockType types at the package surface\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:390:        - \"test/projection.test.ts: CLI in-process messages list returns projected messages with blocks and estimates as JSON\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:418:        - \"tool_result blocks project isError as payload.isError ?? false, making the block shape total per the design's block contract ({ toolCallId, content, isError }); the underlying event payload remains verbatim with isError absent when the caller omitted it\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:388:        reason: \"Top-level TurnRecord type export, matching the MessageRecord pattern\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/01-message-read-surface.md:21:- **AC-3.1**: Listing returns messages in record order with kind, block summary, token estimate, turn membership, and deleted status, with bounded-listing options (range/limit) so large threads list without loading everything.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/01-message-read-surface.md:41:This story extends the existing messages surface. `listMessages` gains optional bounds and deleted-audit options while preserving default visible-message behavior for existing callers. `show` returns the canonical record content, not the view-shortened content, and composes form state from the owner report surface.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/01-message-read-surface.md:53:- `show` returns full record blocks, including full tool results.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/01-message-read-surface.md:93:- `listMessages` option defaults must preserve existing callers: visible messages, unbounded, record order.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/01-message-read-surface.md:106:- Entrypoint: `messages.listMessages`, `messages.show`, `lhc messages list`, `lhc messages show`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:90:Seam isolation, both directions (a throwing advance never eats the poke — TC-4.6 carries the assert; a failing poke never blocks the advance — separate leg). Both-modes proof in-process: manual-mode SDK intake advances, background-mode SDK intake advances. The process-boundary CLI leg is Story 5's (named debt in DoD). Supplemental golden: **Boundary G1 trajectory** in `view-select-golden.test.ts` — committed positions after each scripted batch, floor legs included (not a TC; hand-derived expectations per the goldens discipline).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:481:        reason: \"Block/MessageRecord types and fail-closed listMessages/listQueuedWork stubs\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/01-queue-execution-drain.md:17:- Durable claim/lease: claim survives process exit; expired lease reclaimable with attempts incremented; live lease blocks a second drain (reports in-flight)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:27:Messages and blocks projected from recorded events inside the batch transaction; token estimates stamped at creation; message read-back.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:34:**Objective:** Everything recorded becomes readable, with its size known. Each message-producing event yields exactly one message with kind-appropriate typed blocks, verbatim content, the actor/harness carry, and a deterministic base-unit token estimate — written in the same walk iteration that records the event, so projection can never drift from its source.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:41:- `messageId` in batch result entries; `listMessages` read-back; CLI `messages list`\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:51:- **AC-2.2**: Each message-producing event yields exactly one message carrying that event's content verbatim, structured as one or more typed blocks.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:52:  - **TC-2.2** (AC-2.2, 2.3): A batch with one of each event kind → six messages with kind-appropriate blocks and verbatim content; `turn_end` present in events, absent from messages.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:69:This story adds projection to Story 2's walk: each recorded message-producing event yields its message, blocks, and token estimate in the same iteration that recorded it, inside the same transaction — projection cannot drift from its source because they are never separated. The risk profile is fidelity, not logic: kind-correct block shapes, verbatim content, and the absence of any code path that could shorten a tool result. `messages.createFromEvent` is the first cross-domain surface call through the operation context, establishing the pattern `turns.applyEvent` follows in Story 4.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:87:| Projection | `src/domains/messages/internal/project.ts` (event → message + blocks per kind) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:89:| Surface | `src/domains/messages/index.ts` (createFromEvent, listMessages) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:106:| TC-2.2 | `test/projection.test.ts` | all seven kinds → six messages, kind-correct blocks, verbatim; turn_end absent |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:121:- Message read-back: `{ messageId, sourceEventOrder, kind, blocks[], tokenEstimate, actor, harness, turnId? }` — `turnId` null until Story 4.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:122:- Block shapes: text kinds → one text block; `tool_call` → `{ toolCallId, toolName, arguments }`; `tool_result` → `{ toolCallId, content, isError }`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:129:- Block-shape assertions check full structure per kind, not just block count.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:154:- [ ] `listMessages` ordered and deterministic; CLI `messages list` live\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:344:    planSummary: \"Fixed F-03-002. openThreadDatabase now performs an identity check before any migration runs: a read-only probe (so the probe itself cannot mutate an invalid file) requires schema version >= 1, a thread_metadata table, and the metadata singleton row that thread creation writes transactionally. Files failing the check — an empty database, an unrelated SQLite database, a non-database file — are rejected as caller_error/thread_not_found ('exists but is not an lhc thread file') with no lhc tables created and user_version untouched; SQLite's 'not a database' refusal is classified as the same identity failure, while other open errors remain system_error. The opener's signature changed to OpResult<DatabaseSync> so the rejection flows through the standard result contract, and all three call sites (runMessageEvents, runListEvents, listMessages) propagate it. Valid Story 2 user_version=1 files pass the check (they carry the metadata row) and still migrate lazily to v2, so F-03-001 behavior is preserved — all prior migration tests stay green. Three focused tests prove rejection-without-mutation for an existing empty file (verifier's exact probe), an unrelated SQLite database with foreign data, and a plain text file.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:354:        reason: \"listMessages consumes the opener's OpResult, so read-back on a non-thread file fails instead of adopting the file\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:363:        - \"test/thread-migration.test.ts: listMessages against an existing empty database file fails with caller_error/thread_not_found, user_version stays 0, no tables created (the verifier's exact F-03-002 probe)\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:365:        - \"test/thread-migration.test.ts: a non-SQLite text file is rejected as caller_error/thread_not_found by both listMessages and messageEvents with its bytes byte-identical afterward\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:434:    planSummary: \"Wired message projection into the Story 2 batch walk: each recorded message-producing event now yields one message with kind-appropriate typed blocks, verbatim content, actor/harness carry, and a deterministic o200k_base token estimate, written in the same transaction iteration that recorded the event (createFromEvent is the first cross-domain surface call through OperationContext). Added message/message_block tables to thread schema v1 (same extension pattern Story 2 used for the event table), deterministic m<eventOrder> ids, messageId in batch result entries, listMessages read-back, and a live CLI `messages list`. Followed Red→Green: projection.test.ts and cli-process-projection.test.ts written and manifest-recorded first (all 7 failing on assertions), then implemented to green. turnId stays null throughout (Story 4). Projection failure rejects the whole batch, proven by an induced real failure (walk-hook drops message_block mid-transaction) asserted via read-back, not the error result alone.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:459:        reason: \"Pure per-kind event→blocks+estimate projection; verbatim field copies, no shortening path; tool_call counts serialized arguments, tool_result counts full content; turn_end → null\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:465:        reason: \"createFromEvent (synchronous cross-domain surface, m<eventOrder> ids, throws on projection failure) and real listMessages replacing the stub; RecordedEvent/MessageCreated types\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:471:        reason: \"Exported MessageRecord/Block/BlockType types at the package surface\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:480:        - \"test/projection.test.ts: CLI in-process messages list returns projected messages with blocks and estimates as JSON\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:508:        - \"tool_result blocks project isError as payload.isError ?? false, making the block shape total per the design's block contract ({ toolCallId, content, isError }); the underlying event payload remains verbatim with isError absent when the caller omitted it\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:582:        evidence: \"Story 3 adds `message` and `message_block` only by changing the version-1 creation migration in `packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:23-60`. `runMigrations` skips migrations whose version is already current in `packages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:28-31`, and existing thread opens in `runMessageEvents` and `listMessages` call only `openDatabase` (`pipeline.ts:101-104`, `messages/index.ts:89-92`). The accepted Story 2 schema at commit `7c8623d` has `thread_metadata` and `event` tables with `PRAGMA user_version=1` but no message tables. A TSX probe using that schema returned `messageEvents` `{ ok:false, code:\\\"storage_failure\\\", reason:\\\"... no such table: message\\\" }` and `messages.listMessages` `{ ok:false, reason:\\\"... no such table: message_block\\\" }`. That leaves the Story 3 dependency on real Story 2 thread files unsatisfied and blocks AC-2.2/listMessages on an existing valid thread file.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:593:          - \"Definition of Done: listMessages ordered and deterministic\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:601:        evidence: \"Story 3 adds `message` and `message_block` only by changing the version-1 creation migration in `packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:23-60`. `runMigrations` skips migrations whose version is already current in `packages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:28-31`, and existing thread opens in `runMessageEvents` and `listMessages` call only `openDatabase` (`pipeline.ts:101-104`, `messages/index.ts:89-92`). The accepted Story 2 schema at commit `7c8623d` has `thread_metadata` and `event` tables with `PRAGMA user_version=1` but no message tables. A TSX probe using that schema returned `messageEvents` `{ ok:false, code:\\\"storage_failure\\\", reason:\\\"... no such table: message\\\" }` and `messages.listMessages` `{ ok:false, reason:\\\"... no such table: message_block\\\" }`. That leaves the Story 3 dependency on real Story 2 thread files unsatisfied and blocks AC-2.2/listMessages on an existing valid thread file.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:612:          - \"Definition of Done: listMessages ordered and deterministic\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:617:        - \"AC-2.2 / TC-2.2 on current-schema threads: `projectEvent` maps six message-producing kinds to typed blocks, `turn_end` returns null, batch results include `m<eventOrder>`, and `test/projection.test.ts` verifies six messages with full block structures and verbatim content.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:641:      - \"F-03-001: Existing valid Story 2 thread files with `user_version=1` are not migrated before Story 3 message write/read paths, so `messageEvents` and `messages.listMessages` fail with missing-table storage errors.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:687:    planSummary: \"Fixed F-03-001 with a real migration path. Restored the v1 thread-file migration to the exact accepted Story 2 schema (thread_metadata + event) and moved the message/message_block tables into a new version-2 migration, so the schema is a versioned history rather than a rewritten creation script. Added threads.openThreadDatabase — open + runMigrations to current version — and routed every thread-file open through it: runMessageEvents (migration completes before the batch BEGIN IMMEDIATE), runListEvents, and messages.listMessages. An existing Story 2 file with user_version=1 now gains the message tables on its first open by Story 3 code, on both the write and read paths. Proven with a new fixture that reproduces the accepted Story 2 on-disk layout byte-for-byte (below-SDK writer, sanctioned like corrupt.ts because current code can no longer create that shape) and three focused tests: messageEvents on a legacy file (upgrade, order continuation, m2 projection, legacy event intact, user_version 1→2), listMessages on an untouched legacy file (read-path upgrade, empty list, records unchanged), and a Story 2-recorded idempotency key still skipping after upgrade with no message created.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:700:        reason: \"listMessages opens through openThreadDatabase, migrating a pre-Story-3 file before the message read\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:715:        - \"test/thread-migration.test.ts: messageEvents on a Story 2 file upgrades the schema (user_version 1→2), continues the event order from the legacy record, projects m2 with verbatim blocks, and leaves the legacy event byte-identical on read-back\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:716:        - \"test/thread-migration.test.ts: listMessages on an untouched Story 2 file migrates on read, returns an empty list, and changes no record content\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:737:        - \"F-03-001: Story 2 thread files (user_version=1, thread_metadata/event only) were not migrated before message write/read — message and message_block now land via a version-2 migration applied lazily by openThreadDatabase on every thread-file open (messageEvents, listEvents, listMessages), not by rewriting the v1 creation migration; verified against a fixture reproducing the accepted Story 2 on-disk schema, with the verifier's exact failing probes (messageEvents and listMessages on a legacy file) now passing\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:803:        rationale: \"Resolved. `packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:22-78` now keeps v1 as the accepted Story 2 schema and appends v2 for `message`/`message_block`; `openThreadDatabase` runs migrations before returning at `create.ts:85-93`. `runMessageEvents`, `runListEvents`, and `listMessages` now open through `openThreadDatabase` (`pipeline.ts:100-106`, `pipeline.ts:227-230`, `messages/index.ts:92-97`). `test/thread-migration.test.ts:35-130` verifies Story 2 user_version=1 files upgrade before write/read, preserve existing event content, continue event order with `m2`, return empty messages on read-only upgrade, and keep legacy idempotency keys skipping without duplicate messages. Focused `vitest run test/thread-migration.test.ts`, `test/projection.test.ts`, `green-verify`, and `verify-all` all passed.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:809:        evidence: \"`openThreadDatabase` unconditionally opens the supplied path and runs `runMigrations(db, buildThreadMigrations())` in `packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:85-89`. When no creation metadata is passed, v1 creates `thread_metadata` without inserting the required singleton row (`create.ts:25-44`). `messages.listMessages` then calls this opener and returns `ok: true` from `readMessages` (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:84-98`). A TSX probe against an existing empty file showed `messages.listMessages({ filePath })` returned `{ ok:true, value:[] }`, changed `PRAGMA user_version` from 0 to 2, and created `event`, `message`, `message_block`, and `thread_metadata` tables; a later `messageEvents` call failed with `thread file has no metadata row`. This is a newly introduced production-path regression: read-back succeeds and mutates a non-thread file instead of rejecting an invalid thread file without creating app schema.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:817:          - \"Definition of Done: listMessages ordered and deterministic\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:825:        evidence: \"`openThreadDatabase` unconditionally opens the supplied path and runs `runMigrations(db, buildThreadMigrations())` in `packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:85-89`. When no creation metadata is passed, v1 creates `thread_metadata` without inserting the required singleton row (`create.ts:25-44`). `messages.listMessages` then calls this opener and returns `ok: true` from `readMessages` (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:84-98`). A TSX probe against an existing empty file showed `messages.listMessages({ filePath })` returned `{ ok:true, value:[] }`, changed `PRAGMA user_version` from 0 to 2, and created `event`, `message`, `message_block`, and `thread_metadata` tables; a later `messageEvents` call failed with `thread file has no metadata row`. This is a newly introduced production-path regression: read-back succeeds and mutates a non-thread file instead of rejecting an invalid thread file without creating app schema.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:833:          - \"Definition of Done: listMessages ordered and deterministic\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:838:        - \"F-03-001 / existing Story 2 user_version=1 files: verified by `test/thread-migration.test.ts`; messageEvents and listMessages migrate valid legacy thread files before write/read, preserve existing events, continue dense event order, and keep legacy idempotency skips inert for messages.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:842:        - \"Production-path handling for existing non-thread files supplied as `{ filePath }`: the directly touched lazy-upgrade path currently creates LHC tables and can return successful `listMessages` output without a metadata row.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:857:      - \"F-03-002: the lazy schema-upgrade opener mutates arbitrary existing files into partial LHC thread databases and allows `messages.listMessages` to return success without a thread metadata row.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:18:| 1 | **Handoff gate (epic Assumptions):** Epic 02/03 final deviation tables vs the contracts this epic consumes | Reviewed all recorded deviations (Epic 02 impl log; Epic 03 impl log: `ViewProfileOverride[]` config typing, `view_boundary` strftime seed, `ViewCompactParams` nested partial, additive error codes, sweep-absent literal superseded by Story 3). None alter consumed shapes: `ViewStatus`, `PullResult`, `thread_view`/`thread_view_band`/`view_boundary` DDL, `messages.report`/`turns.report`, `FormReportEntry`, `MessageRecord.forms` all match spec as built. One *favorable* drift: Epic 02's AC-4.7 ruling attached `forms` to message reads (built for this consumer), so Flow 3's join is thinner than the epic assumed | Gate PASSED — recorded here |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:19:| 2 | AC-1.1 needs counts (events, messages by kind, tokens) that no surface exposes as counts; inspect may not read tables directly; epic sanctions only one surface addition (`describe`) | Overview composes *list* reads (`listEvents`, `listMessages`, `listTurns`, `listChunks`) and counts in inspect. Cost is linear in thread size — acceptable at v1 scale (NFR allows thread-proportional reads). Count-only surface ops are a deferred optimization, not a v1 need | Resolved — composition, no new surfaces |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:36:                        messages.listMessages(+opts)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:47:| `listMessages` → `MessageRecord[]` with `forms?` attached | messages (E01 + E02 AC-4.7) | overview, list/show |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:70:      index.ts          ← listMessages gains opts; gains show()\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:85:| `messages/show` | Single-record read (full blocks) + `report(messageId)` composition | View-form shortening (show returns the record — full tool results, never boundary-shortened) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:86:| `messages/listMessages` opts | Bounds, limit, deleted filter | Default-including deleted (audit is opt-in) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:92:- **DD-2 (show composes report):** `show` = internal single-message read (same store read as `listMessages`, by id, full blocks) + `messages.report(ref, {messageId})` for the queue-joined forms. No new join machinery; `FormReportEntry` is the forms shape `show` returns.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:108:`overview(ref)`: resolve thread (registry metadata) → `listEvents` (count, first/last order) → `listMessages({includeDeleted: true})` (visible/deleted split, kind counts, visible token sum — deleted detected per the read contract's flag) → `listTurns` (open/closed counts) → `listChunks` (count; unchunked = closed turns minus chunk-member turns) → `status` + `describe` (derivation counts, visibility, view summary). Each piece independent; fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted-with-record, compacted, and mid-rebuild shapes fall out of the same composition path: absent pieces are zeros/nulls; no shape-specific branch is allowed except normalizing null sections.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:141:`listMessages(ref, opts)`: existing read + WHERE bounds on `source_event_order`, LIMIT, deleted filter (default excluded; `includeDeleted` includes flagged). `show(ref, messageId)`: by-id read, full blocks verbatim from the record, `deleted` flag honest, forms from `report({messageId})`. Not-found → `message_not_found` (existing code). Deleted + show → `ok` with flagged record (AC-3.3: audit, never not-found).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:199:listMessages(ref: ThreadRef, opts?: { from?: number; to?: number; limit?: number; includeDeleted?: boolean }): Promise<OpResult<MessageRecord[]>>;\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:200:show(ref: ThreadRef, messageId: string): Promise<OpResult<MessageDetail>>;  // MessageRecord (full blocks, deleted flag) + forms: FormReportEntry[]\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/05-message-edit-cascade.md:13:**Objective:** The record's first sanctioned mutation ships whole. Edit changes a closed-turn message's content and blocks, re-stamps the token estimate, and in the same transaction walks the derivation chain upward — the message's own forms, its turn's rendering and projection, the containing chunk's summaries — clearing each to `pending` and re-queueing. The event log keeps the original (projection-level mutation; Epic 01's events remain immutable). The ordering guarantee makes the cascade safe: an in-flight pre-edit item that completes after the edit discards against the source-version check; the post-edit artifact wins regardless of completion order. Edit never touches a generated thread-view — visibility arrives at the next compact/rebuild (DD-12).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/05-message-edit-cascade.md:16:- `messages.edit` (SDK + CLI): validates target (closed turn, message exists, not deleted), updates content and blocks, re-stamps the token estimate, cascades, returns the `MutationResult` (changed / cleared / queued / superseded)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/05-message-edit-cascade.md:30:- **AC-5.1**: An edit to a message in a closed turn updates content and blocks and re-stamps the token estimate in one synchronous transaction; the edit result reports the content change, cleared forms, and queued work.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/05-message-edit-cascade.md:48:The first sanctioned mutation, and the test of everything underneath it. `messages.edit` runs one transaction (DD-8): validate against the deleted-filtered read (`turn_open` / `message_not_found` refusals), apply content + blocks + token re-stamp, then the cascade from `messages/internal/cascade.ts` — bump source version and set `pending` on every dependent form (the message's own, the turn's two, the chunk's two), supersede-delete still-queued old-version items (issue 1's tidy-up, ids reported on the result), enqueue replacements at the new source version, register the poke. Claimed old-version items may still finish; their results are discarded by the source-version check. One commit carries all of it; the operation returns `MutationResult`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/05-message-edit-cascade.md:89:| TC-5.1 | `test/mutations.test.ts` | content + blocks + estimate synchronous; result names cleared + queued |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/fix/001-epic-fix-batch.md:6:- **F-EPIC-002**: Read-back surfaces (`listEvents`, `listMessages`, `listTurns`, `listQueuedWork`) skip thread-reference validation present on the write path, so malformed references (e.g. empty path) reach storage open. Fix: route all read surfaces through the same `resolveThreadRef` validation used by writes; empty/invalid refs return `caller_error`/`thread_not_found` consistently at SDK and CLI layers. Add a small test per read surface for the empty-path and unknown-id legs.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:562:        reason: \"Block/MessageRecord types and fail-closed listMessages/listQueuedWork stubs\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:493:        reason: \"Top-level TurnRecord type export, matching the MessageRecord pattern\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/06-message-turn-delete.md:24:**Scope — out:** Restore/undelete (no requirement; the event log is the recovery substrate if ever needed). Block-level delete within a message (v1 boundary: whole message plus its blocks). Open-turn mutations (refused, as in Story 5).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:27:Messages and blocks projected from recorded events inside the batch transaction; token estimates stamped at creation; message read-back.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:34:**Objective:** Everything recorded becomes readable, with its size known. Each message-producing event yields exactly one message with kind-appropriate typed blocks, verbatim content, the actor/harness carry, and a deterministic base-unit token estimate — written in the same walk iteration that records the event, so projection can never drift from its source.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:41:- `messageId` in batch result entries; `listMessages` read-back; CLI `messages list`\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:51:- **AC-2.2**: Each message-producing event yields exactly one message carrying that event's content verbatim, structured as one or more typed blocks.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:52:  - **TC-2.2** (AC-2.2, 2.3): A batch with one of each event kind → six messages with kind-appropriate blocks and verbatim content; `turn_end` present in events, absent from messages.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:69:This story adds projection to Story 2's walk: each recorded message-producing event yields its message, blocks, and token estimate in the same iteration that recorded it, inside the same transaction — projection cannot drift from its source because they are never separated. The risk profile is fidelity, not logic: kind-correct block shapes, verbatim content, and the absence of any code path that could shorten a tool result. `messages.createFromEvent` is the first cross-domain surface call through the operation context, establishing the pattern `turns.applyEvent` follows in Story 4.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:87:| Projection | `src/domains/messages/internal/project.ts` (event → message + blocks per kind) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:89:| Surface | `src/domains/messages/index.ts` (createFromEvent, listMessages) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:106:| TC-2.2 | `test/projection.test.ts` | all seven kinds → six messages, kind-correct blocks, verbatim; turn_end absent |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:121:- Message read-back: `{ messageId, sourceEventOrder, kind, blocks[], tokenEstimate, actor, harness, turnId? }` — `turnId` null until Story 4.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:122:- Block shapes: text kinds → one text block; `tool_call` → `{ toolCallId, toolName, arguments }`; `tool_result` → `{ toolCallId, content, isError }`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:129:- Block-shape assertions check full structure per kind, not just block count.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:154:- [ ] `listMessages` ordered and deterministic; CLI `messages list` live\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:360:        rationale: \"Resolved. `validateThreadFile` opens a read-only handle and requires `user_version >= 1`, a `thread_metadata` table, and the singleton row before any migration (`packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:101-136`). `openThreadDatabase` now returns an `OpResult<DatabaseSync>` and runs migrations only after that identity check (`create.ts:145-160`). `runMessageEvents`, `runListEvents`, and `listMessages` propagate failed opens instead of migrating (`pipeline.ts:100-106`, `pipeline.ts:225-227`, `messages/index.ts:92-98`). `test/thread-migration.test.ts:151-218` verifies empty database, unrelated SQLite database, and text file rejection without schema mutation or byte/content loss. An independent TSX probe confirmed empty files keep `user_version: 0` and no tables, foreign DBs keep only `notes`, and text bytes stay unchanged.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:436:    planSummary: \"Wired message projection into the Story 2 batch walk: each recorded message-producing event now yields one message with kind-appropriate typed blocks, verbatim content, actor/harness carry, and a deterministic o200k_base token estimate, written in the same transaction iteration that recorded the event (createFromEvent is the first cross-domain surface call through OperationContext). Added message/message_block tables to thread schema v1 (same extension pattern Story 2 used for the event table), deterministic m<eventOrder> ids, messageId in batch result entries, listMessages read-back, and a live CLI `messages list`. Followed Red→Green: projection.test.ts and cli-process-projection.test.ts written and manifest-recorded first (all 7 failing on assertions), then implemented to green. turnId stays null throughout (Story 4). Projection failure rejects the whole batch, proven by an induced real failure (walk-hook drops message_block mid-transaction) asserted via read-back, not the error result alone.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:461:        reason: \"Pure per-kind event→blocks+estimate projection; verbatim field copies, no shortening path; tool_call counts serialized arguments, tool_result counts full content; turn_end → null\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:467:        reason: \"createFromEvent (synchronous cross-domain surface, m<eventOrder> ids, throws on projection failure) and real listMessages replacing the stub; RecordedEvent/MessageCreated types\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:473:        reason: \"Exported MessageRecord/Block/BlockType types at the package surface\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:482:        - \"test/projection.test.ts: CLI in-process messages list returns projected messages with blocks and estimates as JSON\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:510:        - \"tool_result blocks project isError as payload.isError ?? false, making the block shape total per the design's block contract ({ toolCallId, content, isError }); the underlying event payload remains verbatim with isError absent when the caller omitted it\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:584:        evidence: \"Story 3 adds `message` and `message_block` only by changing the version-1 creation migration in `packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:23-60`. `runMigrations` skips migrations whose version is already current in `packages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:28-31`, and existing thread opens in `runMessageEvents` and `listMessages` call only `openDatabase` (`pipeline.ts:101-104`, `messages/index.ts:89-92`). The accepted Story 2 schema at commit `7c8623d` has `thread_metadata` and `event` tables with `PRAGMA user_version=1` but no message tables. A TSX probe using that schema returned `messageEvents` `{ ok:false, code:\\\"storage_failure\\\", reason:\\\"... no such table: message\\\" }` and `messages.listMessages` `{ ok:false, reason:\\\"... no such table: message_block\\\" }`. That leaves the Story 3 dependency on real Story 2 thread files unsatisfied and blocks AC-2.2/listMessages on an existing valid thread file.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:595:          - \"Definition of Done: listMessages ordered and deterministic\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:603:        evidence: \"Story 3 adds `message` and `message_block` only by changing the version-1 creation migration in `packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:23-60`. `runMigrations` skips migrations whose version is already current in `packages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:28-31`, and existing thread opens in `runMessageEvents` and `listMessages` call only `openDatabase` (`pipeline.ts:101-104`, `messages/index.ts:89-92`). The accepted Story 2 schema at commit `7c8623d` has `thread_metadata` and `event` tables with `PRAGMA user_version=1` but no message tables. A TSX probe using that schema returned `messageEvents` `{ ok:false, code:\\\"storage_failure\\\", reason:\\\"... no such table: message\\\" }` and `messages.listMessages` `{ ok:false, reason:\\\"... no such table: message_block\\\" }`. That leaves the Story 3 dependency on real Story 2 thread files unsatisfied and blocks AC-2.2/listMessages on an existing valid thread file.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:614:          - \"Definition of Done: listMessages ordered and deterministic\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:619:        - \"AC-2.2 / TC-2.2 on current-schema threads: `projectEvent` maps six message-producing kinds to typed blocks, `turn_end` returns null, batch results include `m<eventOrder>`, and `test/projection.test.ts` verifies six messages with full block structures and verbatim content.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:643:      - \"F-03-001: Existing valid Story 2 thread files with `user_version=1` are not migrated before Story 3 message write/read paths, so `messageEvents` and `messages.listMessages` fail with missing-table storage errors.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:689:    planSummary: \"Fixed F-03-001 with a real migration path. Restored the v1 thread-file migration to the exact accepted Story 2 schema (thread_metadata + event) and moved the message/message_block tables into a new version-2 migration, so the schema is a versioned history rather than a rewritten creation script. Added threads.openThreadDatabase — open + runMigrations to current version — and routed every thread-file open through it: runMessageEvents (migration completes before the batch BEGIN IMMEDIATE), runListEvents, and messages.listMessages. An existing Story 2 file with user_version=1 now gains the message tables on its first open by Story 3 code, on both the write and read paths. Proven with a new fixture that reproduces the accepted Story 2 on-disk layout byte-for-byte (below-SDK writer, sanctioned like corrupt.ts because current code can no longer create that shape) and three focused tests: messageEvents on a legacy file (upgrade, order continuation, m2 projection, legacy event intact, user_version 1→2), listMessages on an untouched legacy file (read-path upgrade, empty list, records unchanged), and a Story 2-recorded idempotency key still skipping after upgrade with no message created.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:702:        reason: \"listMessages opens through openThreadDatabase, migrating a pre-Story-3 file before the message read\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:717:        - \"test/thread-migration.test.ts: messageEvents on a Story 2 file upgrades the schema (user_version 1→2), continues the event order from the legacy record, projects m2 with verbatim blocks, and leaves the legacy event byte-identical on read-back\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:718:        - \"test/thread-migration.test.ts: listMessages on an untouched Story 2 file migrates on read, returns an empty list, and changes no record content\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:739:        - \"F-03-001: Story 2 thread files (user_version=1, thread_metadata/event only) were not migrated before message write/read — message and message_block now land via a version-2 migration applied lazily by openThreadDatabase on every thread-file open (messageEvents, listEvents, listMessages), not by rewriting the v1 creation migration; verified against a fixture reproducing the accepted Story 2 on-disk schema, with the verifier's exact failing probes (messageEvents and listMessages on a legacy file) now passing\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:805:        rationale: \"Resolved. `packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:22-78` now keeps v1 as the accepted Story 2 schema and appends v2 for `message`/`message_block`; `openThreadDatabase` runs migrations before returning at `create.ts:85-93`. `runMessageEvents`, `runListEvents`, and `listMessages` now open through `openThreadDatabase` (`pipeline.ts:100-106`, `pipeline.ts:227-230`, `messages/index.ts:92-97`). `test/thread-migration.test.ts:35-130` verifies Story 2 user_version=1 files upgrade before write/read, preserve existing event content, continue event order with `m2`, return empty messages on read-only upgrade, and keep legacy idempotency keys skipping without duplicate messages. Focused `vitest run test/thread-migration.test.ts`, `test/projection.test.ts`, `green-verify`, and `verify-all` all passed.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:811:        evidence: \"`openThreadDatabase` unconditionally opens the supplied path and runs `runMigrations(db, buildThreadMigrations())` in `packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:85-89`. When no creation metadata is passed, v1 creates `thread_metadata` without inserting the required singleton row (`create.ts:25-44`). `messages.listMessages` then calls this opener and returns `ok: true` from `readMessages` (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:84-98`). A TSX probe against an existing empty file showed `messages.listMessages({ filePath })` returned `{ ok:true, value:[] }`, changed `PRAGMA user_version` from 0 to 2, and created `event`, `message`, `message_block`, and `thread_metadata` tables; a later `messageEvents` call failed with `thread file has no metadata row`. This is a newly introduced production-path regression: read-back succeeds and mutates a non-thread file instead of rejecting an invalid thread file without creating app schema.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:819:          - \"Definition of Done: listMessages ordered and deterministic\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:827:        evidence: \"`openThreadDatabase` unconditionally opens the supplied path and runs `runMigrations(db, buildThreadMigrations())` in `packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:85-89`. When no creation metadata is passed, v1 creates `thread_metadata` without inserting the required singleton row (`create.ts:25-44`). `messages.listMessages` then calls this opener and returns `ok: true` from `readMessages` (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:84-98`). A TSX probe against an existing empty file showed `messages.listMessages({ filePath })` returned `{ ok:true, value:[] }`, changed `PRAGMA user_version` from 0 to 2, and created `event`, `message`, `message_block`, and `thread_metadata` tables; a later `messageEvents` call failed with `thread file has no metadata row`. This is a newly introduced production-path regression: read-back succeeds and mutates a non-thread file instead of rejecting an invalid thread file without creating app schema.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:835:          - \"Definition of Done: listMessages ordered and deterministic\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:840:        - \"F-03-001 / existing Story 2 user_version=1 files: verified by `test/thread-migration.test.ts`; messageEvents and listMessages migrate valid legacy thread files before write/read, preserve existing events, continue dense event order, and keep legacy idempotency skips inert for messages.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:844:        - \"Production-path handling for existing non-thread files supplied as `{ filePath }`: the directly touched lazy-upgrade path currently creates LHC tables and can return successful `listMessages` output without a metadata row.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:859:      - \"F-03-002: the lazy schema-upgrade opener mutates arbitrary existing files into partial LHC thread databases and allows `messages.listMessages` to return success without a thread metadata row.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:905:    planSummary: \"Fixed F-03-002. openThreadDatabase now performs an identity check before any migration runs: a read-only probe (so the probe itself cannot mutate an invalid file) requires schema version >= 1, a thread_metadata table, and the metadata singleton row that thread creation writes transactionally. Files failing the check — an empty database, an unrelated SQLite database, a non-database file — are rejected as caller_error/thread_not_found ('exists but is not an lhc thread file') with no lhc tables created and user_version untouched; SQLite's 'not a database' refusal is classified as the same identity failure, while other open errors remain system_error. The opener's signature changed to OpResult<DatabaseSync> so the rejection flows through the standard result contract, and all three call sites (runMessageEvents, runListEvents, listMessages) propagate it. Valid Story 2 user_version=1 files pass the check (they carry the metadata row) and still migrate lazily to v2, so F-03-001 behavior is preserved — all prior migration tests stay green. Three focused tests prove rejection-without-mutation for an existing empty file (verifier's exact probe), an unrelated SQLite database with foreign data, and a plain text file.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:915:        reason: \"listMessages consumes the opener's OpResult, so read-back on a non-thread file fails instead of adopting the file\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:924:        - \"test/thread-migration.test.ts: listMessages against an existing empty database file fails with caller_error/thread_not_found, user_version stays 0, no tables created (the verifier's exact F-03-002 probe)\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:926:        - \"test/thread-migration.test.ts: a non-SQLite text file is rejected as caller_error/thread_not_found by both listMessages and messageEvents with its bytes byte-identical afterward\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:424:        reason: \"Block/MessageRecord types and fail-closed listMessages/listQueuedWork stubs\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/02-message-level-derivation.md:156:| 2026-06-11 | \"Form read-back on message reads\" (Implementation Targets, Surface row) initially deferred to Story 4; verifier finding 02F-001 ruled it in-scope. Implemented: `listMessages` attaches each message's stored `derived_form` rows as `MessageRecord.forms` (one grouped query, stored state verbatim — no read-time derivation; messages with no rows carry no key, preserving AC-2.7). TC-2.1 amended to prove readability through this production path; red manifest regenerated for the suite | Resolved per 02F-001 |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:27:Messages and blocks projected from recorded events inside the batch transaction; token estimates stamped at creation; message read-back.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:34:**Objective:** Everything recorded becomes readable, with its size known. Each message-producing event yields exactly one message with kind-appropriate typed blocks, verbatim content, the actor/harness carry, and a deterministic base-unit token estimate — written in the same walk iteration that records the event, so projection can never drift from its source.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:41:- `messageId` in batch result entries; `listMessages` read-back; CLI `messages list`\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:51:- **AC-2.2**: Each message-producing event yields exactly one message carrying that event's content verbatim, structured as one or more typed blocks.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:52:  - **TC-2.2** (AC-2.2, 2.3): A batch with one of each event kind → six messages with kind-appropriate blocks and verbatim content; `turn_end` present in events, absent from messages.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:69:This story adds projection to Story 2's walk: each recorded message-producing event yields its message, blocks, and token estimate in the same iteration that recorded it, inside the same transaction — projection cannot drift from its source because they are never separated. The risk profile is fidelity, not logic: kind-correct block shapes, verbatim content, and the absence of any code path that could shorten a tool result. `messages.createFromEvent` is the first cross-domain surface call through the operation context, establishing the pattern `turns.applyEvent` follows in 