 `{ toolCallId, content, isError }`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:129:- Block-shape assertions check full structure per kind, not just block count.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:154:- [ ] `listMessages` ordered and deterministic; CLI `messages list` live\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:363:        rationale: \"Resolved. `packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:22-78` now keeps v1 as the accepted Story 2 schema and appends v2 for `message`/`message_block`; `openThreadDatabase` runs migrations before returning at `create.ts:85-93`. `runMessageEvents`, `runListEvents`, and `listMessages` now open through `openThreadDatabase` (`pipeline.ts:100-106`, `pipeline.ts:227-230`, `messages/index.ts:92-97`). `test/thread-migration.test.ts:35-130` verifies Story 2 user_version=1 files upgrade before write/read, preserve existing event content, continue event order with `m2`, return empty messages on read-only upgrade, and keep legacy idempotency keys skipping without duplicate messages. Focused `vitest run test/thread-migration.test.ts`, `test/projection.test.ts`, `green-verify`, and `verify-all` all passed.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:369:        evidence: \"`openThreadDatabase` unconditionally opens the supplied path and runs `runMigrations(db, buildThreadMigrations())` in `packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:85-89`. When no creation metadata is passed, v1 creates `thread_metadata` without inserting the required singleton row (`create.ts:25-44`). `messages.listMessages` then calls this opener and returns `ok: true` from `readMessages` (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:84-98`). A TSX probe against an existing empty file showed `messages.listMessages({ filePath })` returned `{ ok:true, value:[] }`, changed `PRAGMA user_version` from 0 to 2, and created `event`, `message`, `message_block`, and `thread_metadata` tables; a later `messageEvents` call failed with `thread file has no metadata row`. This is a newly introduced production-path regression: read-back succeeds and mutates a non-thread file instead of rejecting an invalid thread file without creating app schema.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:377:          - \"Definition of Done: listMessages ordered and deterministic\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:385:        evidence: \"`openThreadDatabase` unconditionally opens the supplied path and runs `runMigrations(db, buildThreadMigrations())` in `packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:85-89`. When no creation metadata is passed, v1 creates `thread_metadata` without inserting the required singleton row (`create.ts:25-44`). `messages.listMessages` then calls this opener and returns `ok: true` from `readMessages` (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:84-98`). A TSX probe against an existing empty file showed `messages.listMessages({ filePath })` returned `{ ok:true, value:[] }`, changed `PRAGMA user_version` from 0 to 2, and created `event`, `message`, `message_block`, and `thread_metadata` tables; a later `messageEvents` call failed with `thread file has no metadata row`. This is a newly introduced production-path regression: read-back succeeds and mutates a non-thread file instead of rejecting an invalid thread file without creating app schema.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:393:          - \"Definition of Done: listMessages ordered and deterministic\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:398:        - \"F-03-001 / existing Story 2 user_version=1 files: verified by `test/thread-migration.test.ts`; messageEvents and listMessages migrate valid legacy thread files before write/read, preserve existing events, continue dense event order, and keep legacy idempotency skips inert for messages.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:402:        - \"Production-path handling for existing non-thread files supplied as `{ filePath }`: the directly touched lazy-upgrade path currently creates LHC tables and can return successful `listMessages` output without a metadata row.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:417:      - \"F-03-002: the lazy schema-upgrade opener mutates arbitrary existing files into partial LHC thread databases and allows `messages.listMessages` to return success without a thread metadata row.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:465:    planSummary: \"Wired message projection into the Story 2 batch walk: each recorded message-producing event now yields one message with kind-appropriate typed blocks, verbatim content, actor/harness carry, and a deterministic o200k_base token estimate, written in the same transaction iteration that recorded the event (createFromEvent is the first cross-domain surface call through OperationContext). Added message/message_block tables to thread schema v1 (same extension pattern Story 2 used for the event table), deterministic m<eventOrder> ids, messageId in batch result entries, listMessages read-back, and a live CLI `messages list`. Followed Red→Green: projection.test.ts and cli-process-projection.test.ts written and manifest-recorded first (all 7 failing on assertions), then implemented to green. turnId stays null throughout (Story 4). Projection failure rejects the whole batch, proven by an induced real failure (walk-hook drops message_block mid-transaction) asserted via read-back, not the error result alone.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:490:        reason: \"Pure per-kind event→blocks+estimate projection; verbatim field copies, no shortening path; tool_call counts serialized arguments, tool_result counts full content; turn_end → null\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:496:        reason: \"createFromEvent (synchronous cross-domain surface, m<eventOrder> ids, throws on projection failure) and real listMessages replacing the stub; RecordedEvent/MessageCreated types\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:502:        reason: \"Exported MessageRecord/Block/BlockType types at the package surface\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:511:        - \"test/projection.test.ts: CLI in-process messages list returns projected messages with blocks and estimates as JSON\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:539:        - \"tool_result blocks project isError as payload.isError ?? false, making the block shape total per the design's block contract ({ toolCallId, content, isError }); the underlying event payload remains verbatim with isError absent when the caller omitted it\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:613:        evidence: \"Story 3 adds `message` and `message_block` only by changing the version-1 creation migration in `packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:23-60`. `runMigrations` skips migrations whose version is already current in `packages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:28-31`, and existing thread opens in `runMessageEvents` and `listMessages` call only `openDatabase` (`pipeline.ts:101-104`, `messages/index.ts:89-92`). The accepted Story 2 schema at commit `7c8623d` has `thread_metadata` and `event` tables with `PRAGMA user_version=1` but no message tables. A TSX probe using that schema returned `messageEvents` `{ ok:false, code:\\\"storage_failure\\\", reason:\\\"... no such table: message\\\" }` and `messages.listMessages` `{ ok:false, reason:\\\"... no such table: message_block\\\" }`. That leaves the Story 3 dependency on real Story 2 thread files unsatisfied and blocks AC-2.2/listMessages on an existing valid thread file.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:624:          - \"Definition of Done: listMessages ordered and deterministic\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:632:        evidence: \"Story 3 adds `message` and `message_block` only by changing the version-1 creation migration in `packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:23-60`. `runMigrations` skips migrations whose version is already current in `packages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:28-31`, and existing thread opens in `runMessageEvents` and `listMessages` call only `openDatabase` (`pipeline.ts:101-104`, `messages/index.ts:89-92`). The accepted Story 2 schema at commit `7c8623d` has `thread_metadata` and `event` tables with `PRAGMA user_version=1` but no message tables. A TSX probe using that schema returned `messageEvents` `{ ok:false, code:\\\"storage_failure\\\", reason:\\\"... no such table: message\\\" }` and `messages.listMessages` `{ ok:false, reason:\\\"... no such table: message_block\\\" }`. That leaves the Story 3 dependency on real Story 2 thread files unsatisfied and blocks AC-2.2/listMessages on an existing valid thread file.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:643:          - \"Definition of Done: listMessages ordered and deterministic\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:648:        - \"AC-2.2 / TC-2.2 on current-schema threads: `projectEvent` maps six message-producing kinds to typed blocks, `turn_end` returns null, batch results include `m<eventOrder>`, and `test/projection.test.ts` verifies six messages with full block structures and verbatim content.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:672:      - \"F-03-001: Existing valid Story 2 thread files with `user_version=1` are not migrated before Story 3 message write/read paths, so `messageEvents` and `messages.listMessages` fail with missing-table storage errors.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:718:    planSummary: \"Fixed F-03-001 with a real migration path. Restored the v1 thread-file migration to the exact accepted Story 2 schema (thread_metadata + event) and moved the message/message_block tables into a new version-2 migration, so the schema is a versioned history rather than a rewritten creation script. Added threads.openThreadDatabase — open + runMigrations to current version — and routed every thread-file open through it: runMessageEvents (migration completes before the batch BEGIN IMMEDIATE), runListEvents, and messages.listMessages. An existing Story 2 file with user_version=1 now gains the message tables on its first open by Story 3 code, on both the write and read paths. Proven with a new fixture that reproduces the accepted Story 2 on-disk layout byte-for-byte (below-SDK writer, sanctioned like corrupt.ts because current code can no longer create that shape) and three focused tests: messageEvents on a legacy file (upgrade, order continuation, m2 projection, legacy event intact, user_version 1→2), listMessages on an untouched legacy file (read-path upgrade, empty list, records unchanged), and a Story 2-recorded idempotency key still skipping after upgrade with no message created.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:731:        reason: \"listMessages opens through openThreadDatabase, migrating a pre-Story-3 file before the message read\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:746:        - \"test/thread-migration.test.ts: messageEvents on a Story 2 file upgrades the schema (user_version 1→2), continues the event order from the legacy record, projects m2 with verbatim blocks, and leaves the legacy event byte-identical on read-back\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:747:        - \"test/thread-migration.test.ts: listMessages on an untouched Story 2 file migrates on read, returns an empty list, and changes no record content\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:768:        - \"F-03-001: Story 2 thread files (user_version=1, thread_metadata/event only) were not migrated before message write/read — message and message_block now land via a version-2 migration applied lazily by openThreadDatabase on every thread-file open (messageEvents, listEvents, listMessages), not by rewriting the v1 creation migration; verified against a fixture reproducing the accepted Story 2 on-disk schema, with the verifier's exact failing probes (messageEvents and listMessages on a legacy file) now passing\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:42:- **AC-3.1**: Listing returns messages in record order with kind, block summary, token estimate, turn membership, and deleted status, with bounded-listing options (range/limit) so large threads list without loading everything.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:62:This story extends the existing messages surface. `listMessages` gains optional bounds and deleted-audit options while preserving default visible-message behavior for existing callers. `show` returns the canonical record content, not the view-shortened content, and composes form state from the owner report surface.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:74:- `show` returns full record blocks, including full tool results.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:114:- `listMessages` option defaults must preserve existing callers: visible messages, unbounded, record order.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:127:- Entrypoint: `messages.listMessages`, `messages.show`, `lhc messages list`, `lhc messages show`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:222:Per-story: `pnpm verify` (lint, typecheck, default suites). Story 4 and epic close: `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all` — process suite must report `ran`. Red manifests regenerated per chunk per house discipline; no Epic 01–03 test amendments expected (additive surfaces only — list-opts default behavior is unchanged, existing `listMessages` callers see identical results).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:265:    planSummary: \"Extended the messages surface per DD-2/DD-3: listMessages gained optional {from, to, limit, includeDeleted} bounds in source-event-order coordinates (defaults preserve all existing callers; bad bounds refused as caller_error/invalid_bounds before any read), the store gained a bounded read plus an unfiltered by-id read, and a new messages.show composes the canonical full-block record (deleted flag always present and honest) with the owner report's queue-joined FormReportEntry rows via the same reportMessageForms read messages.report serves — never synthesized. Deleted records are excluded by default, listed flagged under includeDeleted, and show on a deleted id returns ok+flag (audit), missing id returns message_not_found. CLI gained lhc messages list/show in a new cli/messages-read.ts thin wrapper (numeric conversion at the argv boundary, semantic validation left in the SDK so refusal JSON has parity); sdk.ts exports MessageDetail/MessageListOptions. Tests: 8 default-suite tests in test/messages-read.test.ts covering TC-3.1–3.3 plus the DD-6 read-only delta legs (observable-state snapshot deep-equal around every read mode) and a zero-provider capture assert; 2 process-suite scenarios in test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts covering TC-3.4 spawned-CLI deep-equal parity across default/bounded/include-deleted/refused list options and live/deleted/missing show targets. Default suite 290→298; verify-all (process suite ran) 335 passing.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:269:        reason: \"MessageListOptions + bounds validation on listMessages (invalid_bounds caller errors), MessageDetail shape, new show() composing the by-id record read with reportMessageForms({messageId}) per DD-2, MessageRecord.deleted audit marker\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:328:        - \"Bounded listing still loads all message_block rows before windowing (the pre-existing grouped-blocks read); linear in thread size, consistent with the v1 NFR and tech-design Spec Validation #2's deferred-optimization stance\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:269:| TC-5.1 | Edit prompt in closed turn | Content + blocks + token estimate updated synchronously; result names cleared forms and queued items |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:42:- **AC-3.1**: Listing returns messages in record order with kind, block summary, token estimate, turn membership, and deleted status, with bounded-listing options (range/limit) so large threads list without loading everything.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:62:This story extends the existing messages surface. `listMessages` gains optional bounds and deleted-audit options while preserving default visible-message behavior for existing callers. `show` returns the canonical record content, not the view-shortened content, and composes form state from the owner report surface.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/01-message-read-surface/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:74:- `show` returns full record blocks, including full tool results.\npackages/lhc/docs/