eadable alongside messages.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:641:      - \"02F-001: production `messages.listMessages` does not expose stored derived forms; TC-2.1 uses raw test fixture reads for the form state/content proof.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:686:    planSummary: \"Fix for verifier finding 02F-001 only: production form read-back on message reads. Added readMessageForms to messages/internal/forms.ts (one grouped query over message-owned derived_form rows, returned exactly as stored — no read-time derivation); listMessages now attaches each message's stored forms as MessageRecord.forms, with the key absent for messages that have no rows so AC-2.7's no-state-rows contract stays visible on the read surface. The CLI's list-messages inherits the field through the same surface. TC-2.1 amended so the AC-2.1 proof reads the ready smoothed form through sdk.messages.listMessages (the production path) with the raw fixture read retained only as a stored-state cross-check; red manifest regenerated for the suite. No other surfaces, handlers, or intake paths touched.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:690:        reason: \"NEW readMessageForms: message-owned derived_form rows grouped by message id for the listMessages join, stored state verbatim\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:693:        reason: \"MessageRecord gains optional forms: DerivedForm[]; listMessages attaches stored forms per message — the AC-2.1 'readable alongside the message' production path\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:696:        reason: \"TC-2.1 now proves the smoothed form through sdk.messages.listMessages (message.forms carries state/content/sourceVersion), raw derived_form read kept as agreement check\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:707:        - \"test/derivation-messages.test.ts: TC-2.1 — smoothed form asserted through the production message read path (listMessages → MessageRecord.forms), not only the raw fixture reader\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:725:        - \"02F-001: stored derived forms are now readable alongside messages through messages.listMessages, and TC-2.1's proof uses that production path\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:728:        - \"Swept all listMessages consumers before changing the shape: no whole-record toEqual assertions exist (field-mapped and symmetric twin comparisons only), confirmed by the full 182-test pass with no further amendments needed\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:810:      rationale: \"All five deviations approved: (1) intake touches in messages/index.ts follow Epic 01's actual placement of the kind map — semantics (deterministic, local, batch transaction) unchanged; (2) call-id index added in-place to migration v5 honors the 'one migration per epic' rule and the pinned version-5 tests; (3) outcome metadata on result summaries matches the Story 0 multi-state fixture contract (FC-0.3); (4) form read-back deferral was superseded by the 02F-001 fix, which landed listMessages form attachment anyway; (5) extending the sanctioned mechanical amendment sweep to Epic 02 Story 0/1 test files is the same amendment class (tool_call now queues work), each edit recorded and red manifest regenerated. None alter epic contracts.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:829:rationale: \"All five deviations approved: (1) intake touches in messages/index.ts follow Epic 01's actual placement of the kind map — semantics (deterministic, local, batch transaction) unchanged; (2) call-id index added in-place to migration v5 honors the 'one migration per epic' rule and the pinned version-5 tests; (3) outcome metadata on result summaries matches the Story 0 multi-state fixture contract (FC-0.3); (4) form read-back deferral was superseded by the 02F-001 fix, which landed listMessages form attachment anyway; (5) extending the sanctioned mechanical amendment sweep to Epic 02 Story 0/1 test files is the same amendment class (tool_call now queues work), each edit recorded and red manifest regenerated. None alter epic contracts.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:834:Latest note highlight: After continuation returns, verify 02F-001 specifically: production messages.listMessages/read path exposes stored derived forms alongside messages and TC-2.1 proves it through that surface.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:838:- sequence=11; actionSequence=10; createdAt=2026-06-11T04:36:37.914Z; note=\"After continuation returns, verify 02F-001 specifically: production messages.listMessages/read path exposes stored derived forms alongside messages and TC-2.1 proves it through that surface.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/02-message-level-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:951:    selfNote: \"After continuation returns, verify 02F-001 specifically: production messages.listMessages/read path 