mains/messages/internal/store.ts:48-79), and messages.edit only refuses target.turnStatus === 'open' before applying the edit (packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:411-434). I verified the production path with an ad hoc runtime scenario: a thread containing only a runtime_note before any prompt produced m1 with no turnId; messages.edit({ messageId: 'm1', content: 'edited gap' }) returned ok:true with changed.messageIds ['m1'] and an empty cascade, and listMessages showed the content mutated. That changes sanctioned record state outside the required closed-turn class.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:599:        evidence: \"Story scope requires messages.edit to validate a closed-turn target (story lines 15-20), and AC-5.1 is scoped to editing a message in a closed turn. In code, readMutableMessage explicitly allows turnStatus null for a gap/no-membership message (packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/store.ts:48-79), and messages.edit only refuses target.turnStatus === 'open' before applying the edit (packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:411-434). I verified the production path with an ad hoc runtime scenario: a thread containing only a runtime_note before any prompt produced m1 with no turnId; messages.edit({ messageId: 'm1', content: 'edited gap' }) returned ok:true with changed.messageIds ['m1'] and an empty cascade, and listMessages showed the content mutated. That changes sanctioned record state outside the required closed-turn class.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:611:        - \"TC-5.1 positive closed-turn edit: packages/lhc/test/mutations.test.ts:141-189 verifies content, blocks, token estimate, cleared/queued result, and rebuild from edited content.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/04-tool-result-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:111:Seam isolation, both directions (a throwing advance never eats the poke — TC-4.6 carries the assert; a failing poke never blocks the advance — separate leg). Both-modes proof in-process: manual-mode SDK intake advances, background-mode SDK intake advances. The process-boundary CLI leg is Story 5's (named debt in DoD). Supplemental golden: **Boundary G1 trajectory** in `view-select-golden.test.ts` — committed positions after each scripted batch, floor legs included (not a TC; hand-derived expectations per the goldens discipline).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/01-queue-execution-drain/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:38:- Durable claim/lease: claim survives process exit; expired lease reclaimable with attempts incremented; live lease blocks a second drain (reports in-flight)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/01-queue-execution-drain/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:282:| TC-5.1 | Edit prompt in closed turn | Content + blocks + token estimate updated synchronously; result names cleared forms and queued items |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/04-derivation-state-report-repair/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:41:- Blocked semantics: a handler reading damaged source (per Epic 01's corruption definitions) lands the form `blocked` with a reason naming the damage; the drain continues past it; re-queue requests for a `blocked` form are refused with that reason\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/04-derivation-state-report-repair/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:94:| Blocked path | handler outcome `{ blocked }` → form `blocked` write + item row deleted (drain-side, small extension of Story 1's completion) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/04-derivation-state-report-repair/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:126:| Blocked is not failed | TC-4.6 | requeue refused for blocked but allowed for failed | A single `failed`-style handling passes TC-4.4 and silently retries against damage |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/04-derivation-state-report-repair/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:135:**Blocked truth table row** (tech design §Mechanics): handler found source damage → work item `failed_terminal`/`failed_terminal`, form `blocked` with damage reason. Terminal by necessity — blocked forms refuse requeue, so a live item could only retry pointlessly against damage. Source repair is Epic 01's territory; this epic's contract stops at the refusal.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/04-derivation-state-report-repair/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:264:| TC-5.1 | Edit prompt in closed turn | Content + blocks + token estimate updated synchronously; result names cleared forms and queued items |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:34:**Objective:** The record's first sanctioned mutation ships whole. Edit changes a closed-turn message's content and blocks, re-stamps the token estimate, and in the same transaction walks the derivation chain upward — the message's own forms, its turn's rendering and projection, the containing chunk's summaries — clearing each to `pending` and re-queueing. The event log keeps the original (projection-level mutation; Epic 01's events remain immutable). The ordering guarantee makes the cascade safe: an in-flight pre-edit item that completes after the edit discards against the source-version check; the post-edit artifact wins regardless of completion order. Edit never touches a generated thread-view — visibility arrives at the next compact/rebuild (DD-12).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:37:- `messages.edit` (SDK + CLI): validates target (closed turn, message exists, not deleted), updates content and blocks, re-stamps the token estimate, cascades, returns the `MutationResult` (changed / cleared / queued / superseded)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:51:- **AC-5.1**: An edit to a message in a closed turn updates content and blocks and re-stamps the token estimate in one synchronous transaction; the edit result reports the content change, cleared forms, and queued work.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:69:The first sanctioned mutation, and the test of everything underneath it. `messages.edit` runs one transaction (DD-8): validate against the deleted-filtered read (`turn_open` / `message_not_found` refusals), apply content + blocks + token re-stamp, then the cascade from `messages/internal/cascade.ts` — bump source version and set `pending` on every dependent form (the message's own, the turn's two, the chunk's two), supersede-delete still-queued old-version items (issue 1's tidy-up, ids reported on the result), enqueue replacements at the new source version, register the poke. Claimed old-version items may still finish; their results are discarded by the source-version check. One commit carries all of it; the operation returns `MutationResult`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:110:| TC-5.1 | `test/mutations.test.ts` | content + blocks + estimate synchronous; result names cleared + queued |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:268:| TC-5.1 | Edit prompt in closed turn | Content + blocks + token estimate updated synchronously; result names cleared forms and queued items |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-