ckages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:556:        evidence: \"Story scope requires messages.edit to validate a closed-turn target (story lines 15-20), and AC-5.1 is scoped to editing a message in a closed turn. In code, readMutableMessage explicitly allows turnStatus null for a gap/no-membership message (packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/store.ts:48-79), and messages.edit only refuses target.turnStatus === 'open' before applying the edit (packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:411-434). I verified the production path with an ad hoc runtime scenario: a thread containing only a runtime_note before any prompt produced m1 with no turnId; messages.edit({ messageId: 'm1', content: 'edited gap' }) returned ok:true with changed.messageIds ['m1'] and an empty cascade, and listMessages showed the content mutated. That changes sanctioned record state outside the required closed-turn class.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:568:        - \"TC-5.1 positive closed-turn edit: packages/lhc/test/mutations.test.ts:141-189 verifies content, blocks, token estimate, cleared/queued result, and rebuild from edited content.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/04-tool-result-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:111:Seam isolation, both directions (a throwing advance never eats the poke — TC-4.6 carries the assert; a failing poke never blocks the advance — separate leg). Both-modes proof in-process: manual-mode SDK intake advances, background-mode SDK intake advances. The process-boundary CLI leg is Story 5's (named debt in DoD). Supplemental golden: **Boundary G1 trajectory** in `view-select-golden.test.ts` — committed positions after each scripted batch, floor legs included (not a TC; hand-derived expectations per the goldens discipline).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/01-queue-execution-drain/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:38:- Durable claim/lease: claim survives process exit; expired lease reclaimable with attempts incremented; live lease blocks a second drain (reports in-flight)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/01-queue-execution-drain/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:282:| TC-5.1 | Edit prompt in closed turn | Content + blocks + token estimate updated synchronously; result names cleared forms and queued items |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:358:      - \"Blocking: background SDK `threadView.pull` and `threadView.status` can trigger scheduler first-touch drains through `openThreadDatabase`/`fireThreadTouch`, causing provider calls and work-row mutations in the real SDK path.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/01-queue-execution-drain/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:38:- Durable claim/lease: claim survives process exit; expired lease reclaimable with attempts incremented; live lease blocks a second drain (reports in-flight)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/01-queue-execution-drain/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:282:| TC-5.1 | Edit prompt in closed turn | Content + blocks + token estimate updated synchronously; result names cleared forms and queued items |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:293:        - \"The suppression is scoped to the thread-view ops, not to openThreadDatabase generally: other read surfaces (messages.listMessages, reports called directly) still announce opens, preserving Epic 02's first-touch catch-up behavior — only the Epic 03 reads carry the reads-only contract. If a later story wants all reads touch-free, the same scope function is the seam to apply.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:553:      - \"Blocking: background SDK `threadView.pull` and `threadView.status` can trigger scheduler first-touch drains through `openThreadDatabase`/`fireThreadTouch`, causing provider calls and work-row mutations in the real SDK path.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/01-queue-execution-drain/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:38:- Durable claim/lease: claim survives process exit; expired lease reclaimable with attempts incremented; live lease blocks a second drain (reports in-flight)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/01-queue-execution-drain/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:282:| TC-5.1 | Edit prompt in closed turn | Content + blocks + token estimate updated synchronously; result names cleared forms and queued items |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:559:      - \"Blocking: background SDK `threadView.pull` and `threadView.status` can trigger scheduler first-touch drains through `openThreadDatabase`/`fireThreadTouch`, causing provider calls and work-row mutations in the real SDK path.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/01-pull-and-status/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:639:        - \"The suppression is scoped to the thread-view ops, not to openThreadDatabase generally: other read surfaces (messages.listMessages, reports called directly) still announce opens, preserving Epic 02's first-touch catch-up behavior — only the Epic 03 reads carry the reads-only contract. If a later story wants all reads touch-free, the same scope function is the seam to apply.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/04-tool-result-visibility/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:111:Seam isolation, both directions (a throwing advance never eats the poke — TC-4.6 carries the assert; a failing poke never blocks the advance — separate leg). Both-modes proof in-process: manual-mode SDK intake advances, background-mode SDK intake advances. The process-boundary CLI leg is Story 5's (named debt in DoD). Supplemental golden: **Boundary G1 trajectory** in `view-select-golden.test.ts` — committed positions after each scripted batch, floor legs included (not a TC; hand-derived expectations per the goldens discipline).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:283:| TC-5.1 | Edit prompt in closed turn | Content + blocks + token estimate updated synchronously; result names cleared forms and queued items |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:283:| TC-5.1 | Edit prompt in closed turn | Content + blocks + token estimate updated synchronously; result names cleared forms and queued items |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:283:| TC-5.1 | Edit prompt in closed turn | Content + blocks + token estimate updated synchronously; result names cleared forms and queued items |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:283:| TC-5.1 | Edit prompt in closed turn | Content + blocks + token estimate updated synchronously; result names cleared forms and queued items |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:283:| TC-5.1 | Edit prompt in closed turn | Content + blocks + token estimate updated synchronously; result names cleared forms and queued items |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:283:|